3zPz led Historical [UEZ], one of only two [[concordia|Concordia]] member guilds known by name.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L133, L200–201, composed 19 Jan 2018}}

He took Historical out of Concordia and into [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], and on 8 November 2015 posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded"; it drew 27 replies and 4,049 views, was locked, and was last posted in by Ferne on 10 November 2015.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|Alliance-prefix thread index}} [[ezura|Ezura]] of [[validus|Validus]] contested the disbandment in the thread, without changing how it was read.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L203–204, composed 19 Jan 2018}}

A month later he founded [[vesta|Vesta]] out of what Concordia left behind, opening its alliance thread on 10 December 2015.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}} Vesta was the larger alliance at the time it formed — fourteen guilds against Ordo's dozen — and is remembered chiefly for having done nothing.

Aequitas [Aeq] is a Wynncraft guild created on 24 Nov 2019.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## Leadership and structure

The guild's forum recruitment thread was opened on 3 Jan 2021 by [[frozengalaxy|FrozenGalaxy]] and has been maintained by him since. Aequitas runs a courtroom-themed rank ladder - Justices, Judges, Attorneys, Advocates, Jury, Witnesses - at the top of which the thread lists 'Justice Frozenman [OWNER]' and 'Justice Lalatera [CHIEF]'; Lalatera also drew the guild's artwork, and recruitment ran through peter3536.{{cite:thread-280525|post #1, opened 3 Jan 2021}} Two weeks after opening the thread, on 17 Jan 2021, FrozenGalaxy added the guild to [[the-forum-megalist|the forum megalist]] as a level 48 community and war guild.{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #66, 17 Jan 2021}}

The bar for entry rose as the guild did. In January 2021 the form asked players above level 70 whether they would help war, and within two days put the same question to players above 95{{cite:thread-280525-p02|#21, 24 Jan 2021, and #24, 26 Jan 2021, reproducing the application form}}. By December 2022 it carried a formal combat-level minimum of 80 and addressed warring to players above 100{{cite:thread-280525-p20|#381, 19 Dec 2022, reproducing the form}}. The minimum moved three times after that: 75 from May 2023{{cite:thread-280525-p22|#421, 24 May 2023, reproducing the form}}, 90 from August 2024{{cite:thread-280525-p24|#472, 30 Aug 2024, reproducing the form}}, and 100 by March 2025{{cite:thread-280525-p25|#491, 9 Mar 2025, reproducing the form. Applicants sometimes copied a superseded version, so each date is a requirement's first appearance rather than the day it was set}}.

The thread's header reads 'Est. November 24th 2019',{{cite:thread-280525|post #1, opened 3 Jan 2021}} matching the API's creation date:{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Aequitas was a year old before it began recruiting publicly.

## History

### Goose and Khaos (2021-2022)

Aequitas belonged to [[Goose]] among the coalition's later additions by 30 Mar 2021, when [[drasalia|Drasalia]]'s Goose fanart thread drew it as a blindfolded Greek figure - 'their name is the Latin concept of justice, equality' - and both Lalatera and FrozenGalaxy replied.{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}} Aequitas also had a brief [[Artemis]] stint in the war's final week (early May 2021) while still with Goose; the overlap was never explained.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} At [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021 Aequitas co-founded [[Khaos]] with the Goose bloc's core, fighting the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war against Valhalla and Vanir]] that peaked in January 2022;{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Khaos was defunct by 26 Jun 2022 and its guilds were absorbed into [[Cucumber Company]].{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}

### The super-alliance years (2022-2023)

Aequitas appears in Cucumber Company's 14-guild megalist roster of 26 Jun 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} and carried through into [[smtn elf]] until the alliance's quiet end in mid-2023.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In September 2023 'TNL and AEQ were allied and warring together'{{cite:thread-280525-p22|p22 #427, 1 Sep 2023}} - the only named guild relationship of its era.

### The Long Raid and the great wars (2024-2026)

In late July 2024 Aequitas's claim in the Sky province endured [[the-long-raid|a roughly week-long siege]], recounted in the video 'Wynncraft Warring - The Long Raid' (premiered 4 Aug 2024).{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-rlrh14ns6ok|premiered 4 Aug 2024}}{{cite:thread-318070|post #1, 9 Aug 2024}} The attackers were never named. From 3 Nov to 21 Dec 2025 Aequitas fought [[Avicia]] in [[aequitas-avicia-war|the largest war ever recorded]] (15,710 territory exchanges).{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} After a one-week clash in August 2025 and spring 2026 skirmishes, [[aequitas-sequoia-war|full war with Sequoia]] erupted in the week of 24 Aug 2026 - 7,488 territory exchanges in its first week,{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|territory count, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} That war is ongoing.

![The in-game guild leaderboard for Season 23, which ended 13 April 2025: Aequitas second on 11,082,978 Season Rating behind Sequoia, ahead of Empire of TKW, TruthSworD, Avicia and Titans Valor. Published in Titan Times vol. 19, 2 August 2025.](/images/chronicles/media/aequitas-b0ea886d.webp){{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol19|vol. 19, 2 Aug 2025}}

## Alliances

- [[Goose]] - by 30 Mar 2021 - 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}}
- [[Artemis]] - early May 2021 - 11 May 2021 (brief overlapping stint, never explained)
- [[Khaos]] - 11 May 2021 - defunct by 26 Jun 2022 (co-founder)
- [[Cucumber Company]] - spring 2022 - Sep 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}
- [[smtn elf]] - Sep 2022 - Jun 2023

## History

### Formation
The pact was created on 25 March 2018 by [[Fantasy]], Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team as a bond of sister guilds within the map-dominant Federation.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} [[DiamondDeities]] was accepted into the pact on 18 July 2018.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} The pact's thread, posted by the Sins of Seedia leader lotuss on 5 June 2018, described Aesir as "an alliance, or if you will sister-ship pact, between 4 warring and growing community guilds". Fantasy and Sins of Seedia became friends during the War Syndicate era, were separated when Fantasy entered the [[Coalition]] and Sins of Seedia warred against it, and were reunited inside [[the-federation|the Federation]], where IceBlue Team and then DiamondDeities were added.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

### Leadership
Each member guild was represented by two leaders.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

| Guild | Tag | Leaders |
|---|---|---|
| [[Fantasy]] | Fux | [[viaire|Viaire]], SpaseCow |
| Sins of Seedia | SDU | [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]], Shy_Phoenix |
| IceBlue Team | IBT | [[vmark03|Vmark03]], Mpr100 |
| [[DiamondDeities]] | DDT | [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], Icey_Diamond |

New guilds were admitted by a vote of these leaders; the thread advised applicants to form friendships with them first "(for voting process)".{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} Several of the same names recur in the Federation's leadership: [[Drew1011]] credited simplyinfinity_ as the first to accept the merger proposal that created the Federation, called Viaire "perhaps the best mapmaker the alliance had", and counted Nitrogen2Oxygen and Icey_Diamond among its most trusted friends.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

### Fantasy on both sides of it
Fantasy left the Federation on 22 September 2018 and [[fantasy-turns-on-the-federation|fought it through October]], while Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team stayed in.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|9/22/2018}} For a month a founder of the pact was at war with the alliance the other two founders belonged to, and nothing records what they made of it.

It ended on 24 October, when the pact told its members that Fantasy had left on its own terms, that there were no tensions between them, that the guild wanted a different path and should be shown respect — adding, in the same message, that Aesir was not weakened and there was now room to consider a new member.{{cite:fantasy-leaving-and-returning-2018-discord-private|24 Oct 2018}} A departure, a reassurance and a vacancy in one announcement. Fantasy was readmitted to the Federation five days later, and left again the same night.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|10/29/2018}}

### Five, then three
The pact admitted guilds by announcement to its own membership through 2018. IceBlue Team was welcomed on 18 May, DiamondDeities congratulated on its acceptance on 18 July, and on 14 October 2018 [[the-divine-swords|The Divine Swords]] was announced as the fifth guild admitted.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|admission announcements, 18 May – 14 Oct 2018}} Five was as large as it ever got, and it held for ten days: Fantasy's departure was announced on 24 October and The Divine Swords went on 6 November.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|departures, 24 Oct and 6 Nov 2018}}

The second departure was announced as voluntary and had been settled in council first. On 1 November the pact's leader told the council that the guild appeared to want to stay and asked what the others thought.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|1 Nov 2018, the question}} They answered that it should be removed, one holding that its principal fighter now held rank in a guild outside the pact and that it was finished, another that he was evenly split and would leave it to the rest, since the guild's hostility to [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] could damage relations there.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|1 Nov 2018, the answers}} At 09:23 on 6 November the leader told the council that the guild's people had to go; at 09:25 he announced to the whole alliance that the guild had left on its own terms.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|6 Nov 2018}} The Federation had expelled the same guild a week before and its members were scattering, so nothing shows it did not also leave of its own accord.{{cite:federation-decline-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018}} The same formula had been used of Fantasy thirteen days earlier, and for that departure no internal decision was ever written down.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|24 Oct and 6 Nov 2018}}

The pact's alliance-information card, posted to its own server at 23:42 on 6 November 2018, lists five member guilds, and cannot be read as a statement of the membership on that date: on 6 November the pact had three, and did not have five again until [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]] joined on 17 November.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|the alliance-information card, posted 23:42 on 6 Nov 2018, export clock}}{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|membership, Oct–Nov 2018}} The card was edited at least twice after it went up. On 20 November a council member said the alliance information ought to be updated and the card's author answered three minutes later that it was done; the last edit the export carries, at 18:08 on 1 December, is accounted for in the council an hour earlier, when the pact's leader asked the author to replace one member guild's Discord invitation with a new one.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|20 Nov and 1 Dec 2018}} An edit date fixes only that the surviving text is not the posting date's, and it carries the last edit alone.

The morning Fantasy's departure went out, the pact put two proposals to its voting channel: that members name any guilds they personally thought would suit it, and that it reach out to guilds founded by friends of its members and cultivate them — not admitting them, but building them up so that they would be inclined to help.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|24 Oct 2018, the voting channel}} That is neither membership nor a truce but sponsorship, and it took effect four weeks later, when the pact told its membership that [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] was a friend of the alliance rather than a member.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|21 Nov 2018}} Reading the proposal and the arrangement together is this article's.

### The council, 30 October 2018
The pact's first institution was built eleven days before the withdrawal. A leadership channel was created in its server on the afternoon of 30 October 2018, at 21:31:53 UTC, and used forty-five seconds later, addressed to a role its author said he had just given the alliance's most trusted members and telling them that this was where the planning would be done.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|channel creation and first message, 30 Oct 2018}} The reason came in the next line: the group would serve as a council because the Federation's own leaders' channel could not be relied on, on account of The Divine Swords — the pact's characterisation of a guild the Federation expelled by a leaders' vote that same day.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018}}{{cite:federation-decline-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018}} One member asked that the arrangement be permanent; a quarter of an hour later another asked that it be kept very small.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018}}

Eleven minutes before that channel was created, [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s own leaders had proposed the same thing. At 21:21:36 UTC its map-maker told the leadership channel that they should probably set up a second, advisor-level place for serious military matters; a guild leader answered that the advisory channel was useless to him and that he used only the leaders' channel, the war channel and one other; and the map-maker added that there were several spies in the advisory channel.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 21:21:36 UTC, the Federation's proposal}} Nothing shows that the pact's founders had read that exchange, and the Federation's proposal was for a channel inside its own server. What the pair shows is that the same conclusion was reached twice in eleven minutes, and that only one of the two rooms acted on it.

Three minutes after the council opened, the Federation began an audit of its members' rosters: at 21:28:33 UTC a guild leader proposed that every member guild go through its own membership and confirm that everyone in it was legitimate.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 21:28:33 UTC, the audit proposed}} [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]] reported itself clean at 21:32:59 UTC, twenty-one seconds after the first message in the council its own leader was sitting in.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 21:32:59 UTC, the report}}{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|channel creation and first message, 30 Oct 2018}} The council was about territory and succession, it had been opened by a different guild, and nothing suggests anywhere that IceBlue Team had placed anybody in anybody's roster. The coincidence is one of two clocks.

The Canyon was settled in one room and asked for in the other inside half an hour. At 21:42:05 UTC that guild's leader told the council that the Air Temple was the bloc's main source of experience and that the yield from it had collapsed, and the member drawing the bloc's Canyon map said he wanted no Air Temple on it.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 21:42:05 UTC, the council}} At 22:07:25, in the Federation's leadership channel, she said her guild would rather stay low on territory count, and at 22:11:09 that she would accept an increase provided it kept its Canyon holdings.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 22:07:25 and 22:11:09 UTC, the Federation's leadership channel}} At 22:12:08, asked whether a share of the Air Temple was still to pass to Sins of Seedia, she answered that she had only ever offered the upper half.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, 22:12:08 UTC, the Air Temple share}} The two experience figures she gave in the two rooms inside half an hour were not the same pair of numbers, which is a reason not to treat any of them as measurements.{{cite:federation-two-rooms-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, the two pairs of figures}} What it shows is a guild answering in the same hour to the body it belonged to and the body it trusted, which had stopped being the same body.

Nine minutes in they began dividing the Canyon. A member asked whether anybody could produce a blank sheet of the region with its territories unassigned, said he meant to split it three ways, and asked again for the sheet greyed out.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|the Canyon division, 30 Oct 2018}} An IceBlue Team member answered that if it could be arranged he would rather not be given Sins of Seedia's portion.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018, the shares}} They meant to leave the Air Temple off the map altogether — it had caused far too much trouble with Fantasy, one said, and another that it ought to stay with that guild if that guild were reliable.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|the Air Temple, 30 Oct 2018}} It was the ground [[fantasy|Fantasy]] had named as its whole price for rejoining the Federation in the middle of October, and which it left again the following day.{{cite:federation-air-temple-2018-discord-private|October 2018}}

Then a member put the strategic problem plainly. They could form a community-level combination with [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]], he said; not a war arrangement, since both groupings existed for community rather than for fighting. The point of it was that it would preserve the Federation's core if the Federation fell.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|the Valkyrie proposal, 30 Oct 2018}} A fall was close, another answered, and they all knew the problems. Keeping the relationship, said the first, would leave whichever alliance beat the Federation facing a threat on the other side; a third said he was unsure and would rather simply stay friendly.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|the Valkyrie proposal, 30 Oct 2018}} Nothing shows the proposal being put to Valkyrie. A week earlier the Federation's founder had called Aesir a community pact rather than a war alliance, and a member had answered that if that did not count as one then nothing did; the pact used both descriptions of itself in the same half hour.{{cite:federation-blocs-within-2018-discord-private|23 Oct 2018}} In the same conversation it sketched a recruiting team, staffed by trusted officers outside the council and modelled, expressly, on the Federation's own arrangement of advisors, war role and guild leaders; nothing shows it was created.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|the recruitment proposal, 30 Oct 2018}}

Little of the eleven days that followed was scheming. On 5 November the pact's leader told the council that another member guild's people were talking his captains into changing guilds.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|5 Nov 2018, the complaint}} The two leaders agreed there and then that neither guild would recruit from an Aesir guild again, and that every guild outside the pact remained fair game.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|5 Nov 2018, the rule}} On the sixth, a member looking for the leaders' chat was told that this was the leaders' chat.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|6 Nov 2018}} On the eighth, two days before the withdrawal, a member was still arguing against it: the Federation falling would cost them their protection, reduce them to warring at unpredictable hours to hold their own ground, and might let the [[confederation|Confederation]] or whatever succeeded it rise.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|8 Nov 2018}}{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|8 Nov 2018}}

Setting the planning of 30 October beside the argument of 8 November is this article's.

### The last defence
When the Federation began to cascade apart on 10 Nov 2018, the Aesir guilds — Sins of Seedia, DiamondDeities and IceBlue Team — were its last defenders, quitting only after 14 hours of constant warring{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}} as [[the-federation-dies|the Federation fell]] on 10–11 November 2018. The community timeline records: "At this point Aesir died too."{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

### Independence, November 2018
The pact's own channels describe the same moment as a withdrawal rather than a death. On 10 November 2018 its three remaining guilds voted to leave the Federation, judging that alliance unstable and dying, the vote turning on a single holdout changing position, and announced the departure jointly and as peaceful.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|withdrawal vote, 10 Nov 2018}} The three were the residue of five rather than a founding core, and the same morning's announcement said that Fantasy had rejoined the pact.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|10 Nov 2018}} The Canyon was divided among them that day, each guild taking named clusters, along the three-way split begun in the council eleven days before.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|territory division, 10 Nov 2018}}{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-founded-2018-discord-private|30 Oct 2018}} On the same day it readmitted a guild that had collapsed and been operating informally under a different name, and absorbed another by merger.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|10 Nov 2018}}

It then recruited. [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] petitioned to affiliate on 12 November, citing the Federation's collapse, and [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]] joined formally on 17 November.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|admissions, 12–17 Nov 2018}} The ground rules put to it that evening were four: no leaking; a rule of conduct towards enemies and allies which named [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]], whose land could be taken but with whom no quarrels were to be started; respect for the pact's existing pacts; and an obligation to help when the Canyon was attacked, without waiting to be asked.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|ground rules, 17 Nov 2018}} In the same conversation the pact's leader told the new member that this was not exactly an alliance but close friends fighting for a common cause, without the ambition of a mega-alliance to take everything.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|17 Nov 2018}} A guild provisionally accepted on 12 November was, nine days later, offered a lesser follower status instead, to hold until it had shown itself beneficial.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|follower status, 12–21 Nov 2018}}

On 27 November the alliance formalised two standing lists — guilds marked for open attack, and guilds placed under its protection — making both hostility and friendship an alliance-level decision rather than each member's own.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|standing lists, 27 Nov 2018}} That month it also organised a coordinated multi-guild invasion campaign against [[hackforums|HackForums]], one of two separate declarations of war made on that guild in November 2018.{{cite:hackforums-guild-profile-discord-private|November 2018}}

### Six days against HackForums
On the evening of 11 November 2018, the day after the Federation dissolved, the pact's general channel watched [[hackforums|HackForums]] take the map and named the connection. That guild had been held back by the Federation and by nothing else, one member said, and there was nobody left to do it; another expected it to own the whole map because people were giving up on warring.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, the evening conversation}} Later the same evening a member observed that the strongest guilds would inevitably band together against that guild again before long.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, later that evening}} It is the same conversation, forty seconds on, in which members stated that stopping it was the literal reason the Federation had existed.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018}}

The pact answered within three days. On 13 November its leader announced to the whole alliance that members were free to attack HackForums wherever and whenever they liked, because it was attempting to take the entire map, would not be allowed to monopolise a province, and had threatened the pact more than once.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|13 Nov 2018}} Those grounds are the pact's own account of that guild. On the fourteenth the campaign was organised: a member guild reported that its Molten territories had been under attack for three days, offered to give the region up for a while purely to harass HackForums, and agreed with the leader that they should harry it continuously, harassment being worth more than experience.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|14 Nov 2018, the Molten offer}} The leader asked the council to pass the plan to their own guilds quietly, and two member guilds announced a joint attack in the warriors' channel for a stated hour some twenty-one hours ahead.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|14 Nov 2018, the scheduled attack}} Two months earlier the Federation had pinged its war role at midnight and raised nobody at all.{{cite:federation-nobody-came-september-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, 00:01}} Setting the two beside each other is this article's.

It came apart in three quarters of an hour on the morning of the sixteenth. Shortly before seven the member guild carrying the attacks told the council that the alliance had a deal with HackForums and that everyone was to stop. Pressed, he gave his reasons: his guild could not sustain the attack long enough, the target would reclaim everything so that the effort threatened nothing, and it would answer by coming for them so that nobody earned anything.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|16 Nov 2018, the member guild}} That is one guild's assessment of its own capacity. The pact's leader answered within the minute: HackForums was an alliance enemy, they had been telling him to attack it with everyone rather than alone, one does not hand that guild what it wants but waits and assembles a considered attack, and it was not reliable.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|16 Nov 2018, the reply}} At 06:44 he laid down a rule: no truces with HackForums, [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]], Wrath of Poseidon or Achte Shadow unless the pact's council approved them.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|the rule, 06:44 on 16 Nov 2018, export clock}} Two minutes later he posted it to the announcements channel, where the whole membership could read it.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|the rule reposted, 06:46 on 16 Nov 2018, export clock}}

At 07:22 the same leader announced an alliance-wide truce with HackForums. Its leaders had agreed it; whether the membership liked it or not it was to their benefit, since the two sides would stop chasing each other and could spend the effort on other threats; and nobody was to attack that guild until it was called off.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|the truce, 07:22 on 16 Nov 2018, export clock}} Thirty-six minutes separate the rule from the announcement. What passed between them was decided in a server made for the purpose at seven o'clock that morning, and nothing said in it was kept. In the council, a member had proposed at 06:58 that such a server be set up with the opposing guild's leader and a few named members of the pact in it; the leader agreed and named who should be in it, and the invitation went out at seven.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|16 Nov 2018, the new server}} Members in the council treated the outcome as a win.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|16 Nov 2018, the council's reading}}

The peace did not last a week. On 23 November a member guild reported in the council that HackForums had broken it by attacking, and set out three courses — do nothing, warn them, or mount another large attack; another said his guild had been attacked the day before.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|23 Nov 2018}} Those reports are the pact's account of the other guild's conduct. The rule outlasted the peace, and the two standing lists of 27 November implement it: on that day the pact's leader stated that the whole alliance was under truce with HackForums and with [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]], and put HackForums on the list of guilds not to be touched.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|27 Nov 2018, the truces and the protected list}} In the same exchange he ruled that any former Confederation guild without a treaty was open to being wiped.{{cite:aesir-and-hackforums-november-2018-discord-private|27 Nov 2018, the guilds open to attack}} Tracing the lists back to the rule of the sixteenth is this article's.

### The lists and the card
The two standing lists of 27 November were made in one conversation and were not written down for another week. A council member proposed that alongside a list of enemies there should be a second list of guilds to be left alone, because nobody could rescue a member who got into trouble there; the pact's leader answered with his own guild's arrangements, and the two lists were read out of that.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|27 Nov 2018, the morning}} They were restated that night and pinned at 01:25 the next morning; three people answered the question whether everyone agreed, and none dissented.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|27–28 Nov 2018, the restatement and the pin}} The protected list was less the pact's policy than one guild's obligations extended to everybody: two days earlier members of three Aesir guilds had spent the night attacking [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] together, and on the 27th that guild went onto the list because the pact's leader was personally truced with it.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|24–25 and 27 Nov 2018}}

The lists reached the pact's information channel on 5 December 2018 as a single card, which also carried its only written definition of the oligarchy and a residual rule that a guild on neither list might be attacked freely.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|the card, posted 08:35 on 5 Dec 2018, export clock}} The card cannot date its own contents: its last recorded edit was made at 05:02 on 1 January 2019, and one earlier change is fixed in the council on 5 December itself.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|5 Dec 2018 and 1 Jan 2019, the edits}} Both instruments are set out at [[the-aesir-oligarchy|The Aesir oligarchy]].

Member guilds also ran their own unpublished arrangements over named territories, agreed bilaterally with guilds outside the pact. On 16 November 2018 a member reported that his guild and Kingdom Foxes treated Thesead as free-for-all between the two of them while leaving each other's assigned ground alone, an arrangement he confirmed was still running on 28 December; the same day another member reported that HackForums was insisting Lava Lake be free-for-all while DiamondDeities claimed it.{{cite:aesir-enemy-and-truce-card-2018-discord-private|16 Nov and 28 Dec 2018}} The pact itself never published a list of open territories.{{cite:aesir-canyon-abandoned-january-2019-discord-private|free-for-all mentions across the pact's channels, whole life of the server}}

### Divided loyalties
The pull did not end with HackForums. When a rival later asked for peace in exchange for leaving the Canyon alone, the leader refused any pact outright while at least one member disagreed, and a different member subsequently tried to broker a treaty with the same guild on the alliance's behalf.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|peace terms, winter 2018–19}}

One member guild belonged to three alliances at once. It disclosed in December 2018 that it had joined a second alliance alongside several guilds on Aesir's own enemy list, and by 1 January 2019 was recorded as a member of three; it then declared war on two guilds of a fourth alliance in its own name, and was accused by another Aesir member of quietly favouring that alliance by letting its members fight under a different guild's banner.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|December 2018 – January 2019}} Another member recorded in January 2019 that it was being pressed by two rival blocs to pick a side and was declaring itself out of the dispute.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|January 2019}}

### The loss of the Canyon
The alliance was organised around a region and lost it. On 31 December 2018 it released part of the Canyon to [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] in exchange for a ceasefire, in a negotiation that ran three hours and eleven minutes in its warriors' channel rather than in the council.{{cite:aesir-canyon-conceded-december-2018-discord-private|31 Dec 2018}} Two days later the ground passed to [[imperial|Imperial]], which was no party to the agreement, and on 18 January 2019 the council member who kept the pact's territorial map struck DiamondDeities' four Canyon claims off it and marked the region lost.{{cite:aesir-canyon-abandoned-january-2019-discord-private|2 and 18 Jan 2019}} No vote was taken, nothing went to the voting channel, and the pact never told its membership either that it had conceded part of the region or that it had lost the rest.{{cite:aesir-canyon-abandoned-january-2019-discord-private|announcements and voting channels, 27 Nov 2018 – 23 Feb 2019}} The sequence is set out at [[the-canyon-concession|The Canyon concession]].

One member had already reclassified itself as a community guild rather than a competitive one after months of sustained targeting, while noting that it still meant to recover its territory later; it did so on 8 January 2019, and the reclassification was cited in the council the same day as a reason the pact could not fight for the Canyon.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|member guild reclassification, January 2019}}{{cite:aesir-canyon-abandoned-january-2019-discord-private|8 Jan 2019}} Members had seen the shape of it early: days after the alliance formed they were observing that the era of mega-alliances had broken into competing groupings, none of them strong enough to dominate the map.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|November 2018}}

### Without a leader
2 January 2019 is the last day on which the account that had issued every alliance-wide instruction since 6 November 2018 posted in any of the pact's channels; its final messages that evening were three emoji in the announcements channel beneath a member guild's advertisement for its own event.{{cite:aesir-council-after-the-concession-2019-discord-private|2 Jan 2019}} By 23 February members in the general channel were describing Aesir as an alliance of two guilds that warred and a third that did not, and saying Sins of Seedia would not be back unless its leader became active again.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|23 Feb 2019}}

A leader of DiamondDeities opened a leadership election in the voting channel on 22 February, the occasion given to the alliance being that the leader had gone from the game; he won it five votes to four the following afternoon and told the whole membership to join a different Discord server, the existing one being the old leader's and not his to take.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|22–23 Feb 2019}}{{cite:aesir-council-after-the-concession-2019-discord-private|22 Feb 2019}} A member returned to the abandoned council channel on 18 May 2019 to ask how the other Aesir was getting on.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|18 May 2019}} The ballot, the objection made to it and the move to a new server are at [[the-aesir-election|The Aesir election]]; the body that held the vote is at [[the-aesir-oligarchy|The Aesir oligarchy]].

### After the election

The vote did not dissolve the alliance; it moved it. Six days after the count the chief of [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] who had been visiting the council since New Year founded [[the-consortium|the Consortium]], and by the middle of March its founding circle was the Aesir leadership; its membership card of 24 March named all five Aesir guilds among twelve.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|1-24 Mar 2019}}

The pact went on acting meanwhile. On 22 March a Consortium guild leader said that the chief of [[fantasy|Fantasy]] who had stood against the winner in February had been removed from Aesir the day before — whether from the alliance or only from its server was never made clear — and in the same exchange pressed the Consortium's organiser for a vote specified as being held in Aesir rather than in the Consortium, and was answered that a stand-in account was being used for all of them.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|22 Mar 2019, the Consortium's leaders channel}} The objection of 26 February had been that an unlimited number of chiefs could be put into the oligarchy to inflate a vote; a month later a chief in no Aesir guild was being pressed to vote in an Aesir ballot through a stand-in account. Setting the two beside each other is this article's.

On 27 March a member of the Consortium proposed celebrating [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]]'s return to Aesir, addressing the proposal to the leaders the pact's card named for Fantasy and [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]], and IceBlue Team's leader agreed.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|27 Mar 2019}} That is the last the pact appears as a body a guild could join, and the Consortium outlasted it by six days.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|March 2019}}{{cite:consortium-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 2 Apr 2019}}

The guilds outlasted both. In the ten days from 28 March to 6 April 2019 the five took 743 territories between them, and four of the five were still capturing in December, Fantasy's last capture of the year falling on 30 November.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by attacker for Sins of Seedia, IceBlue Team, DiamondDeities, Fantasy and TheNoLifes, 28 Mar - 6 Apr 2019 and Dec 2019, UTC, raw counts}} No alliance declared any ground open between the Federation's list of 12 October 2018 and [[terra|Terra]]'s of 14 September 2019, so nothing has been subtracted from those figures.{{cite:free-for-all-amendments-2018-2019-discord-private|the declaration of 12 Oct 2018}}{{cite:terra-alliance-announcements-discord-private|14 Sep 2019}} The log itself stops twice in the interval, for twenty-eight days from 7 April 2019 and sixteen from 6 May.{{cite:territory-exchanges|days with no rows, Jan 2018 - Sep 2026: gaps of 28 days from 7 Apr 2019 and 16 days from 6 May 2019}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Aesir Pact}}

## Truces in place of an alliance

Its members spent the day after the Federation's dissolution establishing what was still in force, and concluded that very little was. They had agreed a non-aggression pact with [[imperial|Imperial]] while that guild was still a Federation member, and did not know whether it still held now that the alliance framing it had gone.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, the old pact}} Imperial had truced them that day, and they had been obliged to agree and to leave the guild alone in order to get a respite.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, the new truce}} They could not break it or they were dead, they said, because Imperial liked targeting them.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, the cost of breaking it}} One member called it the strongest warring guild.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018, strongest warring guild}} Both the assessment of Imperial and the judgement about what breaking the truce would cost are the pact's members' own, and nothing from Imperial's side stands beside them.

That was the whole of the bloc's security in its first days alone: one bilateral truce it could not afford to break, and one older pact whose status nobody could settle.

## The alliance that said it did not want the map

On 11 November 2018, the day after [[the-federation-dies|the Federation came apart]], an Aesir leader told the whole alliance that Valkyrie, the Confederation or anyone else was not above them; that the object was to hold the land richest in experience rather than to dominate the map; and that they wanted other guilds to prosper while they held the ground they cared about. What they wanted was the canyon, not the map.{{cite:after-the-federation-2018-discord-private|11 Nov 2018}}

No other alliance in this record states that it does not want the map. The [[the-federation|Federation]]'s own position, given by the man who drew its maps eleven weeks earlier, was that a map which adjusted itself to war activity would destroy an alliance — territory assignments being delicate enough that one mistake could kill one.{{cite:federation-territory-doctrine-2018-discord-private|23 Aug 2018}} The two doctrines sit a day apart in the record and neither side refers to the other.

## Legacy
The pact outlived the alliance it was formed inside by three and a half months, and was the first of the successor groupings of the winter of 2018–19.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|November 2018 – January 2019}}{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|22–26 Feb 2019}} Its guilds then scattered — DiamondDeities into [[SOL]] within weeks, while IceBlue Team and Fantasy resurfaced in [[Terra]] during the wars of 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## History

### Formation
On 17 February 2018 (16 February in some accounts){{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, [[HackForums]], [[Paladins United]], House of Sentinels, [[Emorians]] and Kangronomicon left the Coalition — also called "The 1st Coalition" — over map disputes.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Together with [[Fantasy]] and Necronomicon they formed Alliance Alliance and declared war on their former alliance, beginning the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} (The seventh guild, spelled "Necromonicon" in some records, was Necronomicon, a guild active on the map through 2018.)

Before the name Alliance Alliance settled, the departing guilds were recorded calling themselves the Astrafteri Affinity — a name [[astrafteri-affinity|an alliance of 2016]] had carried before them, though nothing records whether they knew it.{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]], the Coalition leader who published the disputed map, wrote that the alliance had divided Gavel but never Wynn, that a vote to divide Wynn was called by AscendedKitten of [[imperial|Imperial]] and passed, and that "within an hour of announcing the map, on February 16th, 2018, five guilds left Coalition. Hax, PUN, Snt, Fuq, and Emorians [ERN] left and made their own alliance combined with Fux and Feq."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}} He added that the new bloc "attacked the rest of the Coalition, and had the map before the night was over"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}. Alliance Alliance held 337 of 376 territories on 17 February, against [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s 28{{cite:territory-exchanges|337 of 376 territories, 17 Feb 2018}}.

![The proposed division of the province of Wynn, drawn over a territory map in coloured regions, from the ninth redraw of the Coalition's plan. Drew1011 identified its announcement on 16 February 2018 as the cause of the split.](/images/chronicles/storytime/57-Map9Wynn2_-_Copy.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|working map "Map9Wynn2", part 17}}

Whether the departing guilds tried to settle the dispute before leaving is contested. Drew1011 wrote that they did not — "there were no straightforward and direct attempts to solve the issues beforehand" — while noting that others had claimed the opposite; he described the contacts he received as offhand remarks rather than negotiations.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}} No account by any of the departing guilds survives.

### The Coalition Civil War
The war set Alliance Alliance against the Coalition remnant, which had merged with War Syndicate's remains into the new Federation. The Federation struck first and hardest: three days after forming, it attacked member guild HackForums' 111 territories and [[the-wipe-of-hackforums|wiped them to zero]] in under 12 hours, ending HackForums as a territorial power.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The war's first engagement was an attack on [[emorians|Emorians]]' Llevigar territories, opened by Snowythewolf of Hall of Fame on 17 February; Emorians was bankrupt within two days{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}. The bloc lost a guild on its second day. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] dated [[viaire|Viaire]]'s move of [[fantasy|Fantasy]] into the Federation — mid-battle, in exchange for keeping his canyon territories — to 18 February{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}, and the Federation's own week bears the date out: it voted the guild in on the 18th on terms requiring its leader's other guild to take part{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|18 Feb 2018}}, and gave it the mid canyon in the allocation announced on the 21st.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018 9:12 PM}} On 17 February Fantasy had been taking canyon and Air Temple ground off Federation guilds; from the 19th it was taking HackForums' and [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]]'s, and none of theirs.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Fantasy captures by defending guild, 17 and 19–20 Feb 2018 UTC}}

The bloc counterattacked twice. The first came on 27 and 28 February 2018, eleven days after the Federation formed and six after it had divided the map. A Federation member watching it in the small hours of the 27th reported that Corkus, the Sky Islands and the canyon had gone in about two hours — the assigned holdings of three separate Federation guilds under the allocation of the previous week.{{cite:federation-first-counterattack-2018-discord-private|27 Feb 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018 9:12 PM}} By the following night a member was telling the Federation's general channel that HackForums, Necronomicon and [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] were attacking at once, and asking for anyone willing to help; a member of a different guild asked whether the call was only for the guild under attack, and was told the alliance could use everyone.{{cite:federation-first-counterattack-2018-discord-private|28 Feb 2018}} A [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] member announced on the 27th that he would take every territory House of Sentinels gained, on the grounds that it was passing captured ground to HackForums.{{cite:federation-first-counterattack-2018-discord-private|27 Feb 2018, Hall of Fame}}

The second and larger counter-offensive came a fortnight later, after a Wynncraft mob update took effect on 1 March 2018: Alliance Alliance attacked Gavel from midnight "using broken defenses that the vast majority of players were unable to overcome", held the initiative for several days, and lost the map again by 5 March{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}. The Federation's founder called it the only break in the bloc's map control, "~3 days in March"{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}. Alliance Alliance held 308 of 383 territories on 3 March against the Federation's 43, and 236 on 4 March, before the Federation recovered to roughly 300 territories from 6 March{{cite:territory-exchanges|Alliance Alliance 308 of 383 territories, 3 Mar 2018}}.

The alliance then came apart guild by guild: Paladins United asked to join the Federation on 7 March and was admitted; House of Sentinels left Alliance Alliance on 12 March, briefly considered joining the Federation and instead returned to neutrality; and Kangronomicon largely stopped warring{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}.

### The end date
The bloc's member stints closed on 19–20 March 2018. Alliance Alliance fell from 72 territories to one on 19 March, while the Federation reached 380 of 383 territories, or 99%, on 20 March{{cite:territory-exchanges|Alliance Alliance from 72 territories to one, 19–20 Mar 2018}}. No formal dissolution was ever recorded, and all seven of the bloc's guilds carry that same closing date rather than departure dates of their own.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Three of them had gone before it: Fantasy on 18 February{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|18 Feb 2018}}, Paladins United admitted to the Federation on 8 March{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 3/8/2018 6:54 AM}}, and House of Sentinels leaving on 12 March for neutrality rather than for the Federation.{{cite:federation-march-2018-discord-private|participant's narrative, August 2018}} [[emorians|Emorians]] was voted into the Federation on 12 April, three weeks after the date the rolls give it.{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|12 Apr 2018}}

The Federation had taken the map earlier, on 21 February 2018, when it held 356 of 383 territories{{cite:territory-exchanges|356 of 383 territories, 21 Feb 2018}}. The 20 March date sometimes given for the Federation taking map control{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} marks the end of the war rather than the change of map control. Drew1011 dated the bloc's end as a fighting force earlier still, to the week of 7–12 March, when Paladins United joined the Federation and House of Sentinels returned to neutrality{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}; it went on holding territory in reduced numbers, around 75, until 19 March{{cite:territory-exchanges|Alliance Alliance holdings, 6–18 Mar 2018}}.

