- [[the-federation|Federation]] — 18 Feb 2018 to 22 Jul 2018{{cite:angels-of-eternal-discord-private|18 Feb 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/22/2018}}
- the Confederation — from around July 2018{{cite:angels-of-eternal-discord-private|21 Jul – Sep 2018}}

Angry_will was Emperator of the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] when the alliance fell on 17 October 2017, the date its thread's opening post was last rewritten to name him.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}} He held the office the day after [[drew1011|Drew1011]] held it for a single day; the sequence was never explained.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's forum profile title chain, 2016–2019}}

At the fall, Drew1011 was Shadow Advisor and [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] was among the alliance's four remaining member guilds.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}

He had stood for the Shadow Advisor post earlier that year. On 31 August 2017 [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] asked the alliance to choose between Shy_Phoenix, Angry_will, Drew1011 and Whimsicality; the tallies were 4, 5, 19 and 4.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|Shadow Advisor poll screenshot dated 08/31/2017, part 12}}

**Aphelion** [Aph] first appears in the territory record on 18 March 2018 and took 339 territories between then and November, 176 of them in August alone.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Aphelion captures by month, Mar–Nov 2018 UTC: 339 total, 176 in August}} It belonged to [[the-federation|the Federation]] from 22 July to 19 October 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/22/2018; mira, 10/19/2018}}

## The application

On 21 July 2018 the guild's leader posted a prepared address to the Federation's voting channel and put its membership to the guild leaders as a motion, naming the two reactions to vote with.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018}} It gave the guild's founding date that March and said joining the alliance had been its aim ever since; described it as small and dedicated; and recounted that it had begun as a sister guild rather than a subguild of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]], and that its leader had severed the tie over a lack of communication from the other side while the two remained on friendly terms.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018}} It undertook to do anything in the guild's power for the alliance, with the express reservation that its leader would step back from anything that endangered the guild, and claimed the guild was formidable when it or its allies were seriously slighted, whether it struck at once or waited — a point supported with a line from a novel.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018}}

Two things in it are about the alliance rather than the guild. An applicant thought it necessary to explain a broken relationship with an existing member before asking to join, and the loyalty offered was conditional on the alliance not asking for anything that would endanger the guild offering it.

The vote carried twelve to one on thirteen distinct accounts, with no account on both options and the mover on neither, so nothing comes off it.{{cite:september-2018-observations-verified-discord-private|the admission motion of 21 Jul 2018 and its tally}} On 22 July the Federation announced that Titans Valor and Angels of Eternal had left the alliance and that Aphelion had joined.

The application was pasted into the leadership channel again on 23 September, two months after it was made and answered.{{cite:september-2018-observations-verified-discord-private|23 Sep 2018, the pasted application}} The account that posted it said within four messages that it was a copy-paste which had tagged the leaders' role, and Aphelion's own leader asked forty minutes later why her speech was in the channel.{{cite:september-2018-observations-verified-discord-private|23 Sep 2018, the replies in the same channel}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/22/2018}}

## What membership was worth

The alliance published what its members wanted their territories defended with, and Aphelion's request was for no mobs above level 50.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/1/2018}} That is the whole of the guild's public record as a member, apart from the map.

Admission had settled less than it appeared to, because territory was assigned afterwards and could be assigned low. On 25 September 2018, two months in, the guild's leader asked the leadership channel whether Aphelion had been given three territories on the new map because of her own inactivity, and a leader confirmed that this was essentially the reason.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|25 Sep 2018}} Another said the guild needed to war more, and that a Federation guild had to be present for its allies and to work constantly; the leader accepted the point.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|25 Sep 2018}} It is the clearest statement anywhere in the alliance's records of what it expected in return for ground. Three territories was the bottom of its range, and the guild's captures had fallen from 176 in August to 43 in September.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Aphelion captures by month, Aug and Sep 2018 UTC}}

Its two leaders voted separately in the ballot that readmitted Titans Valor on 19 September, both in favour; a member noticed, checked whether it changed the result, found it did not, and let it stand.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|19 Sep 2018}}

## What Titans Valor offered it

What the guild got from [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] two months after its application had explained the broken tie between them was instruction rather than ground. On 23 September 2018 that guild's leader told the Federation's leadership channel that he would send war help to Aphelion, but that fighting on its behalf would put it back where it began the moment the help was withdrawn; the object was for its own members to learn how wars were fought and take over.{{cite:titans-valor-family-of-guilds-2018-discord-private|23 Sep 2018, help and what it was for}} He told it to relax its recruitment requirements, since the alliance's newer guilds could not afford to hold out for high-level players, and to build more than one layer of leadership so that it did not stop functioning whenever its leader was away.{{cite:titans-valor-family-of-guilds-2018-discord-private|23 Sep 2018, the two pieces of advice}} Aphelion's leader answered that teaching her members to manage without her was exactly the difficulty.{{cite:titans-valor-family-of-guilds-2018-discord-private|23 Sep 2018, the answer}}

## Removed from the argument, then gone

On 11 October a leader told the leadership channel, expressly without personal animus, that Aphelion should not remain in the alliance, because as far as he could see it had only one capable defender. Others answered that the guild had been trying and needed no change, and one proposed instead giving it an isolated territory that enemies would find awkward to attack.{{cite:federation-october-2018-discord-private|11 Oct 2018}} By then the alliance's territory arguments had stopped being about which guilds deserved ground and become arguments about which could still hold it.

Eight days later the guild resigned. Its announcement to the alliance said it was doing so after seeing the vote and considering, and thanked the Federation for hosting it that long.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|mira, 10/19/2018}} Which vote was meant was not recorded, and no reason beyond it was given. Aphelion made eight more captures that November and does not appear in the territory record again until 2021.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Aphelion captures by month, Nov 2018 – Jan 2021 UTC}}

