## Legacy
Artemis gave its name to the [[artemis-goose-era|Artemis-Goose era]]. Its final membership fed both successor blocs of [[the-great-collapse|The Great Collapse]]: Titans Valor went into [[Valhalla]], while the late joiners Aequitas and Wheres The Finish co-founded [[Khaos]] the same day.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The joint protection of Profession Heaven outlived both blocs, maintained by their successors until 2026.

AurumKitsune founded the guild KingdomPhoenixes [PHX], announcing it on the forums on 24 September 2017 under the title "Queen of the Phoenixes"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1 (OP); thread opened 24 Sep 2017}}. The guild was "officially established" on 23 September 2017 - "We arose from the ashes of a dead guild, and re-birthed the spark that was missing!"{{cite:thread-204381|post #9, 24 Sep 2017}} - with Whimsy and Thundderr as its first chiefs{{cite:thread-204381|post #1 (OP)}}. One month later KingdomPhoenixes stood among the founder guilds of the [[Coalition]] (created October 2017), making AurumKitsune's brand-new guild part of the founding circle alongside [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], Gilded Sparrows and House of Sentinels{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}.

The guild’s own records give a crowded first six months. She held the throne from the founding, with Iron as her viceroy and then Alhecks in his absence from 9 October 2017; [[elegantdeath|ElegantDeath]] held the title of King for part of 15 October, when she spent half a day in [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]].{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|"The History of the Kingdom of Phoenixes", monarch and viceroy table}} On 2 November she took [[drew1011|Drew1011]] into the guild on an alternate account and made him viceroy in Alhecks’ place{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|Kingdom of Phoenixes dated event log}}, a decision that cost her much of the guild within days: she and Whimsicality, her second-in-command, fell out over it, and she removed her from the guild.{{cite:thundderr-oral-history|on the November 2017 split}} Whimsicality and others founded the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]] from the break.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}} She stepped down on 22 November, telling the guild she had "been leading for 2 months now, but due to some complications I will be stepping down"{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-public-announcements|11/22/2017}}, took the throne back on her return on 12 January 2018, and crowned Drew1011 King Consort on 9 February. In between she twice offered the guild away, settling on making the recipient viceroy while she stayed "as more of a figurehead".{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|2/1/2018 and 2/2/2018}}{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|"The History of the Kingdom of Phoenixes", monarch and viceroy table}}

Her larger legacy came in the [[the-federation|Federation]] (2018). [[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s "Federation Tribute" credits AurumKitsune with building the alliance's Discord infrastructure and with establishing its two-thirds-majority voting rule - the governance mechanism by which the alliance that held the whole map made its decisions{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}. Her own reply in the tribute thread added: "I still can not believe that I made the logo for fed a meme and it was never changed. Deus Vult!"{{cite:thread-237070-p03|p3 #43, 14 Nov 2018}}

Avicia [AVO] is a Wynncraft guild created on 1 Aug 2018.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-avicia|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Its tag is an acronym of the Latin phrase "amor vincit omnia", "love conquers all".{{cite:thread-233859|post #1}}

## History

### Founding and leadership

Avicia was founded by birdiefly209, who led it as "Grand Avis" over a High Council of a High Archon and about a dozen Archons.{{cite:thread-233859|post #1}} On 1 Dec 2018 birdiefly209 posted on the guild's thread: "I have stepped down from my role as Guild Master and passed the position on to Norgari."{{cite:thread-233859|post #16, 1 Dec 2018}} The succession of later leaders was never published: [[urbymine]] was a former Chief by February 2021,{{cite:thread-286375|post #5, 20 Feb 2021}} and FlamingoBike held the Chief title in April 2020.{{cite:thread-265297-p02|p2 #30, 12 Apr 2020}} Which of them held the office during the guild's August 2019 revolt against [[Luna]] is not recorded.

The guild came out of another guild's leadership. On the morning of 1 August 2018 one of [[emorians|Emorians]]' leaders told [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s leadership channel that he was leaving to found and run his own guild, and signed the message as guild master of Avicia.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the valedictory}} He would stay neutral for the time being, he said, and if he warred at all it would be only on the free-for-all ground the alliance designated.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the neutrality}} Emorians' senior team went with him, its remaining leader saying he had not been told the decision was being made.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the reply}}

The neutrality held as long as the guild fought at all. The message is stamped at 09:38 on a clock seven hours behind the capture log's, and the first Avicia capture — Lava Lake, from [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] — followed twenty minutes later at 16:58.{{cite:territory-exchanges|first capture recorded for Avicia, 1 Aug 2018 16:58 UTC}} It made forty-nine captures in all, between 1 and 14 August 2018 and across fifteen territories, and every one of those territories but North Nivla Forest stood on the Federation's declared free-for-all pool on both the list published before the window and the list published after it.{{cite:territory-exchanges|every Avicia capture, 1–31 Aug 2018 UTC: 49 across 15 territories, last on 14 Aug, checked against the declarations of 4 Jun and 6 Aug 2018}}

### The Luna era (2019)

During [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the alliance wars of 2019]], when [[Luna]] wiped every other guild from the map, Avicia was the last power standing; by joining Luna on 17 Jul 2019 it completed Luna's full map control.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Six weeks later, on 29 Aug 2019, Avicia and [[Emorians]] left after a leadership dispute and declared war on [[Imperial]], spiralling into a large war over Gavel out of which [[Terra]] emerged.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Goose, Valhalla and Vanir (2020-2021)

Avicia belonged to the anti-[[Artemis]] coalition of 18 Dec 2020{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} that became [[Goose]] — 'BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now', Avicia's own urbymine wrote on 1 Feb 2021{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} — and stayed until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, when it co-founded [[Valhalla]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It also belonged to the community alliance [[Niflheim]] by July 2021.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} On 28 Nov 2021 it followed Valhalla into [[Vanir]] — and on 18 Dec 2021 it was one of the four guilds whose departure collapsed it, the same day Niflheim dissolved.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Super-alliances and the Avocado split (2022-2024)

Avicia joined [[Cucumber Company]] for Season 5 of 2022 and carried through into [[smtn elf]],{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} while also joining the community alliance [[Adonis]] by 12 Jun 2022.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol3|vol. 3, 12 Jun 2022}} In June 2023 it quit smtn elf with [[The Aquarium]] over claim-shrinking pressure;{{cite:thread-308780|Avicia guild season post, 10 Jun 2023}} the pair fought on as the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact into early 2024.{{cite:thread-310286|Avicia guild season post, 19 Aug 2023}} From 30 Oct 2023 Avicia waged [[avicia-sequoia-war|war on the young Sequoia]], with a second round in January 2024.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### The Aequitas war (2025)

From 3 Nov to 21 Dec 2025 Avicia fought [[Aequitas]] in [[aequitas-avicia-war|the largest war in the entire territory record]] — 15,710 territory exchanges, with a weekly peak of 4,736.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} It was over by Christmas.

