## The record

The conflict that defines this guild is known from the side it fought. Its opponents' channels were preserved and its own were not, so the guild's aims and conduct through 2018 come down almost entirely as its enemies described them.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation channels, March–September 2018}}

## History

### Emperium and War Syndicate (2017)
BuildCraftia sat in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] under the owner ItsAZZA, with Tntdestroyd as its representative to the alliance{{cite:emperium-announcements|guild and representative roster}}; Tntdestroyd was the Emperium's War Leader by mid-June 2017.{{cite:thread-188024-p05|p5 #82, 16 Jun 2017, quoting the opening post}} In July 2017 the guild's SnarbyDragon signed the Emperium's non-aggression pact with Knights of War on the alliance's behalf.{{cite:gdoc-1xnystdpu-spsjds|Emperium of Wynn non-aggression pact, 13 Jul 2017}} That same month BuildCraftia was one of two guilds to leave the alliance, in which it counted as one of the larger war guilds.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|July 2017}}

By that winter it was a [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] guild, and one of only two that fought back consistently through the Gavel Invasion — the guild the invaders attacked hardest, [[drew1011|Drew1011]] wrote, "since many guilds such had personal grudges against them".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}} It was named on the [[coalition|Coalition]]'s enemy list of 11 January 2018.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018}}

### The Federation (February–March 2018)
Five weeks later the same guilds were allies. BuildCraftia appears in the Coalition remnant's first list of new allies on 17 February 2018{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/17/2018}} and drew the West Swamp in [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s first territory assignment four days later.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018}} It took the rest of the swamp from Serpentem Empire almost at once, and nothing was done: the alliance was days old, several former War Syndicate guilds were loyal to BuildCraftia, and punishing it risked losing them.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 18, composed 20 Jun 2019}}

The quarrel began four days after it joined and never stopped. The founding map of 20 February gave BuildCraftia the western swamp and [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]] the eastern; within two days it was taking all of it.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|20–22 Feb 2018}} On 24 February its leader called the settlement unfair, demanded more and said he would leave for the enemy; three days later the alliance decided to keep him anyway, agreeing to praise the guild whether or not the praise was deserved — not because anyone liked him, but because losing him would hand the enemy what it wanted.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|24–27 Feb 2018}} Asked on 6 March to wait for the map to be finished like everyone else, he answered that he would take what he wanted, that three guilds did not get to tell him what he could have, and that they did not run things any more.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|6 Mar 2018}}

On 24 March four member guilds invaded it without a vote. The map published that afternoon gave three of the four more ground than a fortnight earlier and BuildCraftia one territory less.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|24 Mar 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018}} The alliance defended the invasion in its own general channel the following day, a member saying that the only reason BuildCraftia had been attacked was that it had attacked an ally first, and that had an ally attacked the complainant's assigned territories the alliance would have fought for him too; the complainant's charge was that the alliance applied its rules to some members and not to others.{{cite:federation-attacking-allies-march-2018-discord-private|25 Mar 2018, the defence of the invasion}} How the rule was applied in the month's other cases is at [[federation-attacking-allies-march-2018|attacking an ally]]. It was expelled by vote on 6 April with three other guilds, one of them Serpentem Empire, whose half of the swamp it had been taking since February.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|6 Apr 2018}}

The alliance gave its reason for the allocation on 24 February 2018: territories had been assigned while it was unconfirmed whether the guild would return at all, and setting good ground aside for a guild that might never come back would have served no one. Its leader answered that he had been unable to do anything during that period, and asked where the fairness in that lay.{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|24 Feb 2018}} The alliance allocated on availability; the guild arrived to find the map already drawn.

Its objections to the alliance were constitutional before they were territorial. In March 2018 its leader argued that the Federation's two-thirds majority rule handed permanent control to the guilds that had arrived together from the Coalition, and pressed to change it{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation leadership channels, March 2018}}, and that the alliance's territory policy kept awarding the most valuable ground to one guild in particular — both arguments made openly in the alliance's own channels before any breach.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation channels, March 2018}} What turned the argument into a war was a map. In late March the guild began taking another member's territory on the strength of a redistribution proposal that had been drafted but not voted through, treating the draft as already in force; when the alliance published the finished map immediately after retaliating, the guild accused it of having withheld the map deliberately.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|territory seizure and retaliation, late March 2018}} One other member guild's leader sided with it publicly against the rest of the alliance.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation channels, March 2018}}

Once the guild was outside, the alliance turned to its money. On 13 April 2018 the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]]' Viceroy told the leadership channel that he wanted BuildCraftia forced to defend its territories heavily so that it would lose money, and instructed members to find out what its defences cost and attack in a way that left it no profit.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|13 Apr 2018}} He had been told the week before that the guild's bank stood at five hundred thousand emeralds, and that its leader — banned by then — had been the only member who ever donated in quantity.{{cite:buildcraftia-guild-profile-discord-private|early Apr 2018}} No other plan of economic warfare was ever set out this explicitly, and it rests on the same arithmetic as everything else in this period: a guild driven off the map with a full bank could return, and one with an empty bank could not.

The Federation voted on 30 March 2018 to expel the guild for repeated attacks on allied territory.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|30 March 2018 entry}} The vote carried an opt-out for member guilds unwilling to fight its leader personally, and he withdrew before the count concluded, so that the record would show a departure rather than a removal.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|expulsion vote, 30 Mar 2018}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 18, composed 20 Jun 2019}}

No guild voted to keep it. The count declared eight minutes after the motion opened was ten abstentions, ten in favour and one against, and the leader who made it called the one against a placeholder.{{cite:federation-buildcraftia-expulsion-march-2018-discord-private|the count at 20:00 UTC, 30 Mar 2018}} The exported tally gives thirteen for, one against and eleven abstaining, and twelve, none and ten once the account sitting on every option comes out. A second account sits on two of the three, expel and abstain; taking that one out as well would give eleven, none and nine. An account on every option is a placeholder holding the emoji for others, which is what a participant said it was, and an account on two is not the same thing.{{cite:federation-buildcraftia-expulsion-march-2018-discord-private|exported and corrected tallies, 30 Mar 2018}} The motion was written so that no guild had to fight: it said in terms that a guild voting to expel could stay neutral towards BuildCraftia and would not be required to attack it.{{cite:federation-buildcraftia-expulsion-march-2018-discord-private|the opt-out clause, 30 Mar 2018}}

The clause was not decoration. The result was declared at 20:00 UTC and the first Federation capture of BuildCraftia ground followed at 20:16; in the two hours to 22:07 the guild lost eighteen territories, six to [[imperial|Imperial]], five to [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], three to [[the-hive|The Hive]], two to [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] and one each to [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]] and KingdomPhoenixes, only Molten Reach among them on the alliance's declared open list.{{cite:territory-exchanges|BuildCraftia's losses by attacker, 30 Mar 2018 20:16-22:07 UTC, against the free-for-all list of 24 March as amended 27 March}} [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] and [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]], whose leaders had abstained, took nothing from it that day.{{cite:territory-exchanges|every attacker of BuildCraftia, 30 Mar 2018 UTC}}

The answer came the next morning and did not outlast the day. Between 09:06 and 12:24 UTC on 31 March the guild took seventeen territories from Kingdom Foxes, the guild that had led the expulsion, across the canyon, the jungle and the city of Troms.{{cite:territory-exchanges|BuildCraftia captures from Kingdom Foxes, 31 Mar 2018 09:06-12:24 UTC}} IceBlue Team took eleven of them back, DragonsArise five and The Hive one, each within an hour or two of its loss, and by 13:06 not one of the seventeen was still the guild's.{{cite:territory-exchanges|recapture of the same seventeen territories, 31 Mar 2018 UTC}} The guild holds 21 territories in the alliance's published map of 24 March 2018 and is absent from the next one, of 22 April.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|territory maps of 3/24/2018 and 4/22/2018}}

### The war against the Federation (April–September 2018)
The fighting ran for six months, and it shows in the capture record: between 30 March and 8 October 2018 the guild made 11,270 territory captures, the second most of any guild in the game, while its own holdings never passed twenty-six territories.{{cite:who-fought-2018-discord-private|BuildCraftia: 11,270 captures made, 11,290 suffered, peak 26, 30 Mar – 8 Oct 2018}} It attacked constantly and consolidated nothing.

BuildCraftia attacked Federation guilds through April and May, at times with four or more allied guilds striking a single target at once{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation war channel, April–May 2018}}, and the alliance read the strategy as an attempt to remove its smaller guilds one at a time rather than confront it directly — a reading later matched by intelligence describing that plan.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation assessments, spring and summer 2018}} In April the guild demanded a weekly payment from another guild for every territory it held in exchange for peace, and was publicly refused.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|April 2018}} A later approach to a Federation officer, seeking a truce that would grant territory access without alliance membership, was rejected by the alliance's leadership.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|truce approach, 2018}} A co-owner left in April 2018 to found a splinter guild, taking a member with him, which Federation members read as distancing himself from the guild's tactics.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|April 2018}}

The guild fought the war for information as well. The Federation's leadership channel was found to be leaking to its leader, discovered because he was circulating screenshots of it, and the alliance answered by creating a restricted channel limited to trusted leaders in place of the open war channel.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|leak investigation, May 2018}}{{cite:espionage-and-infiltration-discord-private|Federation leak response, May 2018}} A trusted war captain of one Federation guild was separately found to have spent about a week passing information to the other side.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation leadership channels, 2018}}

The argument was pressed in public too. On the game's forums the guild accused the Federation of treating smaller guilds unfairly and argued that alliances should not exist at all; days later its leader announced an alliance of his own, framed as a revolution against the Federation's control of the map.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|forum post and alliance announcement, spring 2018}} An earlier attempt had already failed: Federation leaders learned he had drawn up a rival bloc with the guilds assigned to each side in advance, and that it collapsed because no guild would join him rather than stay neutral.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|Federation intelligence, 2018}} The bloc that did form changed names at least three times between spring and midsummer 2018, appearing first under one name while he was still nominally inside the Federation, then as the Round Table, and finally as the Confederate Guilds of Wynn.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|names of the rival alliance, spring and summer 2018}} The Round Table broke apart on 18 June 2018, and nothing the Federation did brought it down. Its leader reported to his own leadership channel that it had fallen apart after roughly two hours of continuous arguing, that one member guild had walked out because the arguing had turned so poisonous, and that the guild's leader was messaging him as he wrote — about rejoining the Federation.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|Federation leadership channel, 18 Jun 2018}} That guild had joined the Round Table only days earlier, and had been kept out of the Federation once before by its leader's threat to ensure it never got in.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|June 2018}}

Five days before the collapse its leader had proposed dissolving the distinction between the two alliances altogether — merging the Round Table and the Federation into one alliance with no assigned territory at all, opening the whole map to unrestricted competition.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|mid-June 2018}} Ten days before that, a coalition of more than fifteen guilds under his banner had attempted a coordinated attack meant to remove the Federation from the map entirely, and was mocked for the failure afterwards.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|8 Jun 2018}}

The successor alliance's first act was to disown him: within a day the Confederation grouping formally cut ties with him, and its guilds agreed to pause warring for about a week and a half.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|June 2018}} The successor its members founded excluded BuildCraftia.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|July 2018}}

Its leader lost the leadership of the guild in September 2018, six months after the expulsion vote and five after the fighting began.{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|September 2018}}

The Federation put its own account of the rupture into words on 3 September 2018, five months afterwards. Asked in the leadership channel what she thought had happened, a member guild's leader called it a complicated misunderstanding made worse by nobody being willing to be in the wrong.{{cite:federation-leaving-and-attacking-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018, the account}} New territory assignments were being prepared, she said, with one region to be opened to everyone, and BuildCraftia began acting on them before the announcement was made.{{cite:federation-leaving-and-attacking-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018, the assignments}} Federation guilds then set about driving the guild off the map because it kept taking what had been [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] assigned ground, and BuildCraftia asked everyone to stop and was ignored.{{cite:federation-leaving-and-attacking-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018, the escalation}} A rival alliance was then assembled behind the Federation's back in retaliation.{{cite:federation-leaving-and-attacking-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018, the retaliation}} She added that a guild leaving the alliance intending to attack its former allies was in itself acceptable to her and that she did not much mind an enemy; what had been wrong was the manner of it.{{cite:federation-leaving-and-attacking-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018, her view of it}} The region she said was to be opened she did not name.

### How the expulsion was remembered (August 2018)
Five months afterwards the alliance could not say what had happened. On 20 August 2018 a member asked [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s general channel why BuildCraftia had been voted out.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the question}} Three answers came in six hours. The first said the guild had left, and had been attacking territories before those territories were free-for-all, so everybody invaded it.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the first answer}} The second reported that its leader was calling those attacks accidental, a misunderstanding.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the second answer}} The third said the leader had told him the opposite — that two Federation guilds had attacked his ground before it was designated — and that he thought he had a screenshot somewhere.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the third answer}}

The fullest version came four hours later, from a member of the guild that had led the invasion. He said the leader had left before the vote to remove him was decided.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the fourth answer, the departure}} He had begun attacking territory assigned to [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] ahead of the new map, under which Fox would have lost it anyway, and had refused when told to stop.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the fourth answer, the attacks}} He had taken about three territories while Fox wiped his guild out in the same period.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|20 Aug 2018, the fourth answer, the arithmetic}}

None of the four matches the ballot. The alliance expelled the guild by a vote of its leaders on 30 March 2018{{cite:federation-buildcraftia-expulsion-march-2018-discord-private|the count at 20:00 UTC, 30 Mar 2018}} and began taking its territory sixteen minutes later.{{cite:territory-exchanges|BuildCraftia's losses by attacker, 30 Mar 2018 20:16-22:07 UTC, against the free-for-all list of 24 March as amended 27 March}} Every August account has it leaving rather than being removed.

Ten days later the rupture came back as an allegation of vote-rigging. On the morning of 30 August 2018, in an argument about how the alliance's votes should be run, a guild leader said he had been told of an occasion when everybody withdrew their votes to make it appear a free-for-all designation would not pass, after an attack by BuildCraftia in Rodoroc that came before the designation was announced.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|30 Aug 2018, the allegation as relayed}} He said twice that this was only how the story had reached him.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|30 Aug 2018, said twice}} Another member answered that he was running two incidents together, and separated them: one concerned Rodoroc, the other an admission vote.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|30 Aug 2018, the correction}} No withdrawal of votes was recorded at the time. Rodoroc lies in the Molten Heights, where the attack of 24 March was made, so the region in the story was right and nothing else in it was.{{cite:federation-buildcraftia-expulsion-march-2018-discord-private|the attack of 24 Mar 2018 and the region}}

The other incident belonged to a different guild. It was a vote on admitting a guild abbreviated NYN, which the founder had already had to explain once, on 1 July 2018: BuildCraftia's leader had opened it, a more urgent question arose, the founder asked whether it could be held over, several leaders agreed and he halted it — and the mover concluded that he had sabotaged it.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|1 Jul 2018, the halted vote}} He retold the episode on 30 August as a short satirical script, naming the urgent question as a deal offered by [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] and ending with the vote re-run and failing.{{cite:federation-remembering-buildcraftia-august-2018-discord-private|30 Aug 2018, the retelling}} It is a comic piece by the person it is about, not a set of minutes.

What the alliance had lost in five months was not the events but the machinery: who decided, by what procedure, and whether the guild jumped or was pushed.

### 2019
The guild outlived the alliance it had fought. It was named as a founding guild of [[luna|Luna]] on 14 February 2019{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Feb 2019}}, and still held territory in Wynn that September, when [[the-simple-ones|The Simple Ones]] attacked it hours after defecting to [[terra|Terra]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Sep 2019}}

## Alliances

- [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] — 2017{{cite:emperium-announcements|guild and representative roster}}
- [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] — to December 2017{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}}
- [[the-federation|Federation]] — February to March 2018{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/17/2018}}{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|expulsion vote, 30 Mar 2018}}
- [[luna|Luna]] — from February 2019{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Feb 2019}}

## Worn down

Attacking a guild until it gave in was a method, and the alliance's founder was precise about how well it worked. On 9 July 2018 he told the Federation's war channel that the leader of [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] believed that attacking a guild persistently would bring it over to him, and that it had worked with exactly one guild: Kasai Shinrai, during the [[coalition|Coalition]] period.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|9 Jul 2018, the method and the one guild it worked on}} A member in the same exchange said the man spent more effort harassing his own former and prospective allies than fighting his principal enemies.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|9 Jul 2018, the remark about his targets}}

Kasai Shinrai had gone from the Coalition by the afternoon of 27 January 2018, when it was reported attacking a member guild, and no reason for the departure was ever given.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|27–28 Jan 2018}} Nobody in either conversation joined the two, and this article does not.

## Outbid

Guilds were bid for with offers of protected ground. On 13 July 2018 the Federation's leadership channel went over one such transaction in detail. The guild Beast [BST] had been offered the Jungle by the Coalition, on terms meaning the Coalition would not attack it there; since the rival alliance was not fighting in that province at all, the guild would have faced nothing worse than small unaffiliated guilds.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|13 Jul 2018, the offer of the Jungle}} It joined, and about five minutes later told the man who had made the offer that the other alliance had bettered it, and left.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|13 Jul 2018, the five minutes}} The Coalition then attacked it in the Jungle continuously and the guild collapsed in a little under a month.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|13 Jul 2018, the month that followed}}

The whole of it is the losing bidder's account, told for laughs, and the direction of the offer is only recoverable from the middle of the conversation.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|13 Jul 2018, the account and its teller}} No part of it carries a date, and the guild was never written about anywhere else.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|13 Jul 2018, no date in the account}}

An offer could also be revoked quickly. On 18 July 2018, in a round of reminiscence about the early Coalition, the alliance's founder told the leadership channel that a guild had been a member for six days before its leader fell out with the alliance and it was put out.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|18 Jul 2018, the six days}} The guild was not named, and the six days is his figure.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|18 Jul 2018, the guild unnamed}}

## Pushed

The third way out was being made unwelcome. On 14 October 2018 a member of the war channel said that the leader of [[lunatic|Lunatic]] had faced an attempt to hire BuildCraftia against his guild, a motion to put the guild out of the alliance, and sustained criticism.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|14 Oct 2018, the three things listed}} The founder confirmed the attempted inducement and the motion, and was careful about the limit of the admission: one leader had acted alone rather than the leadership acting together, although several leaders had been openly critical of the guild and its leader.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|14 Oct 2018, the founder's qualification}} The leader who did it went unnamed.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|14 Oct 2018, nobody named}} What the alliance's channels said at the time is at [[lunatic|Lunatic]].

## The reason preserved in the mockery of it

No guild's own account of why it left the Coalition was ever written down. What was written down was the ridicule of one. On 29 August 2018 the founder told the leadership channel that a guild had left on the reasoning that it was being targeted and would be targeted less outside the alliance, even though the Coalition was the stronger side, and called the reasoning poor.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|29 Aug 2018, the reasoning and the judgement on it}} The guild was not named, and the paraphrase was produced in order to be laughed at.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|29 Aug 2018, the guild unnamed and the tone of it}}

## What was remembered and what was not

Every one of these episodes came with a duration and none with a calendar: six days in the alliance, five minutes before the guild left, a little under a month before it collapsed.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|the durations given across the four accounts}} That what people kept was elapsed time rather than dates is this article's observation, and nothing in the conversations explains it.

Chownick founded TheNoLifes [TNL] on 27 December 2014, days after the guild system was introduced, making it one of the oldest guilds in the game.{{cite:thread-306694|post #1 (OP)}}

He was still the guild's owner in 2017, when TheNoLifes joined the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]: the alliance thread's roster lists "The No Lifes (TNL) - Owner: chownick" among its twelve member guilds, beside [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] under [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] and [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] under simplyinfinity_{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster, 7 May 2017}}.

He also belonged to the Ordo Malleus circle of the mid-2010s. Replying to the Federation Tribute on 13 November 2018 with "ordo buddies"{{cite:thread-237070|post #5, 13 Nov 2018}}, he drew from [[drew1011|Drew1011]] the answer "Once an Ordo brother always an Ordo brother."{{cite:thread-237070|post #6, 13 Nov 2018}}

TheNoLifes long outlasted his tenure — recorded switching to [[goose|Goose]] in February 2021{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} and inside [[niflheim|Niflheim]] that July{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} — but no source records when or how Chownick left its leadership.

## History

### The founders
The Coalition never announced itself on the forums: no founding thread, roster or declaration was ever posted{{cite:archive-search-method|Wayback CDX sweep of forums.wynncraft.com thread slugs (19,659 URLs)}}. The guild subforum's run of Alliance-prefixed threads jumps straight from Amnesty (30 August 2017) and the Emperium of Wynn's second thread (4 September 2017) to Revolution (25 April 2018){{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}{{cite:thread-202167|post #1, 30 Aug 2017}}{{cite:thread-224905|post #1, 25 Apr 2018}}. By late 2017 alliance diplomacy had moved to Discord, and the Coalition is the first major Wynncraft alliance with no forum existence at all. The founding was never announced, and the guild-history timeline image gives only the month{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, DerpyEmerald24's guild-history timeline image (i.imgur.com/seklYAQ.png), 28 Jul 2020}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}. Its founder gave a day: asked in a leaders channel on 28 February 2018 when the Coalition had formed, he answered 18 October 2017.{{cite:gavel-invasion-2017-discord-private|28 Feb 2018}} [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s own history gives the same date, and both sit within a day of the start of planning implied by his sixty-seven-day reckoning of the campaign.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Oct 2017}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]], one of the founders, placed the proposal "in mid October"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}} and, closing his account of the Gavel Invasion on 25 December 2017, wrote that "67 days after the planning had begun, victory had been achieved"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}} — placing the start of planning at **about 19 October 2017**.

The four founders joined in order: "It was Fox and Phx that cofounded it, with Spr (the guild Fishie had made) being the third guild to join, and Snt being the fourth."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}} Drew1011 gave the alliance's purpose as his own design: "From there we would grow our alliance with the sole purpose of bringing down War Syndicate."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}} Writing again years later he gave a personal trigger for it: "After being insulted by the leader of the ruling alliance at the time, which bore the name War Syndicate, I founded my own alliance."{{cite:gdoc-1wrptmug9r1z8k1a|Drew1011's retrospective essay}} The same account calls the December war "The Great Invasion" and describes the alliance mechanics of the era plainly: an alliance "portions off the map to its members like a slice of cake, and each guild is responsible for holding the lands that they are assigned", a strategy he says only internal collapse can defeat.{{cite:gdoc-1wrptmug9r1z8k1a|Drew1011's retrospective essay}}

![A Discord message from the KingdomPhoenixes parliament channel, forwarded to Drew1011, in which the guild's leader raises "a temporary alliance" with Kingdom Foxes "purely for the sake of elimination of BCr". Drew1011 presented this as the proposal that produced the Coalition.](/images/chronicles/storytime/41-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|the mid-October 2017 proposal screenshot, part 13}}

The four founding guilds can be described from their own threads, and two of them were barely older than the alliance:

- **KingdomPhoenixes** [Phx], led by [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] as "Queen of the Phoenixes", was "officially established" on 23 Sep 2017 — one month before the Coalition — and described itself as having "arose from the ashes of a dead guild"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1, 24 Sep 2017}}. It was a splinter of Kingdom Foxes{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} and had been a [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] member, leaving that bloc weeks before co-founding the Coalition{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}}.
- **Gilded Sparrows**, founded by [[killerfish|Killerfish]] and announced on 17 Nov 2017, was newer still: "Founded in the midst of autumn... although the guild itself is taking its first steps, its leader is not a novice at what he does."{{cite:thread-208566|post #1, 17 Nov 2017}} Its founding thread postdates the Coalition's founding by a month, though guilds routinely predated their threads. Drew1011 wrote that he did most of its warring on its owner's account because "Fishie was the only one in the guild"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}}.
- **House of Sentinels**, founded 2 Jul 2016 by Pyrias, was led by Pretzule from at least Apr 2017; that spring it turned deliberately toward warring — "Due to a few reasons our guild will also be focusing on warring with other guilds and maintaining territory"{{cite:thread-187152|post #1}} — after a year as a community guild in the [[aurelion|Aurelion]] alliance{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}}.
- **[[Kingdom Foxes]]** is the oldest of the four, founded in 2014 and a co-founder of [[Valkyrie]] in 2015 under [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]]{{cite:thread-89529|post #1}}. It was also a member of the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] in the months before the Coalition formed{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}; Drew1011, its Viceroy and the Emperium's Shadow Advisor, wrote that by mid-October, when the Coalition was proposed, "the Emperium was completely dead at that point"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}}.

The founders were one social circle before they were an alliance. Killerfish sat on House of Sentinels' council alongside Pyrias and Pretzule{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as revised 29 Apr 2017}}, and had helped write the [[halcyon|Halcyon]] alliance thread that June alongside Drew1011{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; Drew1011 posted congratulations on both the KingdomPhoenixes and the Gilded Sparrows announcement threads{{cite:thread-208566|post #3, 17 Nov 2017}}.

### Rise to map dominance
The Coalition took control of the Wynn Province on 23 Nov 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} — in Drew1011's words, the day "the Coalition first took control of every territory on the **Wynn mainland**", not of the whole map{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}}. A labelled map of that day shows the mainland held entirely by Coalition guilds, with only Titans Valor's island territories and one other guild's holdings outside it.

![The Wynncraft territory map of 23 November 2017, every mainland territory labelled with a Coalition guild — Kingdom Foxes, KingdomPhoenixes, Gilded Sparrows, Necronomicon, Hall of Fame, House of Sentinels, LE Flowers, Dishonored and Immortalish — with only island territories held by others. From Drew1011's storytime account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/44-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|map of 23 Nov 2017, part 14}}

He attributed the alliance's growth to War Syndicate's standing rule against attacking the province of Wynn: "the War Syndicate had given us over 100 territories on a silver platter... they divided Gavel amongst themselves, and we divided Wynn amongst ourselves"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}}. Three events immediately preceded the invasion: [[fantasy|Fantasy]]'s defection from War Syndicate to the Coalition{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, 21 Jul 2018}}, Fantasy's capture of Corkus from [[paladins-united|Paladins United]], and the revival of [[hackforums|HackForums]], whose owner Drew1011 wrote he had personally recruited on the understanding that Hax would help "deal with War Syndicate" once revived{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}}.

That December the Coalition destroyed [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] in a four-day campaign beginning 21 Dec 2017 — "they wiped ws off the map on Christmas day," as a participant on the losing side put it{{cite:thread-265297-p02|post #34, 14 Apr 2020}} — and held "all 349 territories on the map" by the end of 25 December{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}}. The day-by-day course of that campaign is set out on the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] page. Another participant disputed the wipe, holding that the two blocs merged instead{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}}.

At the declaration of war on 21 December 2017 the alliance numbered fourteen guilds: DeathReapers [DxR], Dishonored [TOH], [[fantasy|Fantasy]] [Fux], [[hackforums|HackForums]] [Hax], Hall of Fame [HoF], Hippies of Snuggles [HOS], House of Sentinels [Snt], Immortalish [Smd], Kasai Shinrai [Two], [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] [Fox], KingdomPhoenixes [Phx], LE Flowers [LEF], Necronomicon [Feq] and Serpentem Empire [SNK]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|roster at the declaration of war, part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}}. [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] joined during the war — "the only addition to our roster during the war", negotiated with its owner Olinite and with [[slayne|Slayne]], "the one doing most of the warring for PUN", days after Coalition guilds had taken Corkus from them{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}} — and [[imperial|Imperial]] was admitted after it on a second vote{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}}.

A member of another Coalition guild, asking on 24 December 2017 when Paladins United had joined, was told it had joined shortly before the attack on Gavel — a few days earlier than the account that has it admitted during the fighting.{{cite:gavel-invasion-2017-discord-private|KingdomPhoenixes general channel, 24 Dec 2017}}

### Running the alliance
Its members traced the alliance's conception to two people who had arrived at the same idea independently within hours of each other before building it together.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|founding accounts}} One participant gave a narrower origin, saying it existed because he had demoted two members out of the ruling body his own guild called Parliament — an alliance produced, on his account, by a quarrel inside a single guild's council.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|founding accounts}}

The alliance admitted guilds by formal vote and ran a moderation layer distinct from guild leadership: an alliance moderator reminded members to document and report territory-sniping by a rival guild, and corrected a misstatement about the alliance's own waiting rules.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|admission votes and moderation, January 2018}} Territory served as internal support as well as reward — the alliance granted a region to one member specifically to help it recover after its treasury had been drained.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|territory grant}} Its leaders also discussed deliberately limiting how much of the map the alliance controlled, measuring the question explicitly against the alliance they had displaced.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|leadership discussion, early 2018}}

Rules were adopted reactively through January 2018: a formalisation of written guild rules proposed after a dispute over a member's conduct, a ban on alt guilds and multi-account warring with a grace period, and a ten-minute window for a guild to reclaim its own lost territory before allies could take it.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|rule changes, January 2018}}{{cite:alliance-governance-mechanics-discord-private|Coalition reclaim rule, late January 2018}} It also disciplined its own: in February 2018 it stripped a guild leader of his roles for leaking alliance information to enemies, and separately removed a member guild after a rival leader supplied evidence that it had leaked internal material.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|discipline, February 2018}}

Fighting continued throughout. Members identified one rival guild as consistently avoiding the alliance's strongest members and attacking its weaker ones instead{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|war channel assessments}}, and another as having misjudged an alliance member as weak, attacked it, been pushed back into its own territory and then asked for a truce.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|war channel, early 2018}} Attacks were timed to activity rather than to strength: one rival pushed deep into a member guild's territory overnight while the alliance's defenders were largely offline, forcing an organised recapture.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|overnight attack, early 2018}} Through the same weeks a guild leader outside the alliance assembled a run of multi-guild targeting arrangements against Coalition members — the first aimed at Hall of Fame, the second at the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] — described at [[alovilatious-treaty|the Alovilatious Treaty]].{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition general and war channels, January–February 2018}}

### Dividing the map, and the split
Two internal fractures followed. Necronomicon and Hippies of Snuggles left during the post-war division of territory in late December 2017, over their allocations; Drew1011 disputed both guilds' grounds for leaving, and neither guild's side was ever recorded{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}}. On the evening of 11 January 2018 the alliance's Discord server was deleted by the former monarch of [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], one of its two founding guilds, in the course of a quarrel inside that guild; a replacement server was created forty seconds later, she said so in her own guild's channel a minute after the deletion, and the alliance reorganised around the new server.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}}{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|12 Jan 2018, 04:19–04:20 UTC}} The episode is set out at [[the-coalition-discord-deletion|the Coalition Discord deletion]].

The fighting of that month had a name. Participants called it the Trench War, after the way [[fantasy|Fantasy]] fought it: attacking every territory the alliance had assigned and defending each with a single mob, taking ground everywhere and holding none of it.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|January 2018}} Few conflicts in this period were named at all, and this one names its own tactic.

The date Fantasy left cannot be read off the alliance's own membership card. The card lists fourteen member guilds and, beneath them, fourteen enemies with Fantasy among them, but it was posted on 11 January 2018 and last revised on 14 February, and an edited Discord message kept only its final text — so its contents belong to the February date rather than to January.{{cite:coalition-information|posted 1/11/2018 9:33 PM, last revised 14 Feb 2018}} Five days after the rebuild a member asked in the leadership channel whether Fantasy was still in the alliance, and three others confirmed it had left; one added that it had been attacking [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] for about twenty hours already, which on the export's winter clock of UTC-08:00 puts the start of the fighting on the evening of the 15th.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} The capture log has the first exchange between the two guilds at 01:43 UTC on the 16th, which is the same hour read on the other clock.{{cite:territory-exchanges|first Fantasy–Kingdom Foxes exchange, 16 Jan 2018 01:43 UTC}}

In the same exchange the alliance's leader said they needed to discourage them, and that the fastest way was to attack them with several guilds at once.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} The week that followed, its haggled and broken settlement and the two rules that came out of it are set out at [[the-trench-war|the Trench War]].

The alliance's fatal defect, in its founder's own words, was that it had divided Gavel but not Wynn: "In Wynn, Coalition guilds could attack enemies, but not allies. (This oversight would come back to cause major problems for the alliance, and eventually be the main reason for its demise.)"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}} A proposal to divide Wynn was first made by Drew1011 and dropped; AscendedKitten of Imperial then re-proposed it and called a vote, which passed{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}. A working map drawn during that exercise recorded the alliance's holdings guild by guild.

![A working map of Gavel from the February 2018 redivision, whose per-guild counts sum to all 377 territories and so set none aside as free-for-all, overlaid with a legend reading "Territory Counts (377/377)": HackForums 101, Paladins United 65, Kingdom Foxes 49, House of Sentinels 45, Hall of Fame 26, Kangronomicon 26, Holders of LE 19, Imperial 19, LE Flowers 19, Emorians 4, and four single-territory guilds. From Drew1011's storytime account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/56-Map9_-_Copy.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|working map "Map9" with territory-count legend, part 17}}

The final allocation ran: Hax ~64, PUN ~50, HoF 38, Fox 36, Snt 36, Imp 32, Fuq 25, Phx 24, LEF 20, HoL 19, ERN 17, SNK 9, Smd 3{{cite:drew1011-storytime|allocation list, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}. No other pre-2019 Wynncraft alliance's per-guild allocation was ever recorded.

### January: churn, not growth

The alliance is usually described as growing through January 2018 towards the fourteen guilds it had when it broke apart. Its own messages show churn instead. The information card posted on the evening of 11 January named fifteen member guilds and eleven enemies, and four of the fifteen were gone by the first days of February.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card as posted, 11 Jan 2018}} [[fantasy|Fantasy]] went first, on the 15th, and was fighting the alliance within a day; it was on the card's enemy list by the 20th.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the enemy list}} Knights Radiant announced its departure to the guild leaders on the morning of the 22nd.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|22 Jan 2018}} Kasai Shinrai had gone by the afternoon of the 27th, when it was reported attacking a member guild, and the leaders were still asking why the next morning; no reason was ever given.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|27–28 Jan 2018}} [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] left at the turn of the month, its own channel putting the date at 1 February.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 1 Feb 2018}}{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|2/1/2018}}

Three guilds came in against those four. [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]] was admitted and announced at 12:20 on 16 January, forty-six minutes before a territory list that had to be redrawn to make room for it.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018 12:20 PM and 1:06 PM}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 16 January allocation before and after the edit}} As Darkness Falls was refused on 27 January and admitted at a second attempt on the 29th.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|27–29 Jan 2018}} [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] followed on 1 February, brought in by a new owner the day after the guild changed hands.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 1 Feb 2018}}{{cite:thread-217600|post #2, Drew1011, 31 Jan 2018}}

The alliance could not always say who its members were. At 19:33 on 23 January a member of the general channel, asked who was in the Coalition, was told to check the server's roles, listed the guilds from memory instead and named eleven, then a twelfth; two others corrected him inside a minute, each supplying a guild he had missed.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, 19:33}} His list left out two guilds the alliance's own documents carried, and he said half the guilds on it were no longer to be seen.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, the list and the correction}} It was the second time in eleven days that the alliance's membership had had to be established by asking around.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} The two kinds of document it kept did not name the same alliance either, and neither works as a membership roll on its own — see [[coalition-standing-documents|the alliance's standing documents]]. How it took its decisions in the same weeks is at [[coalition-voting|voting in the Coalition]].

### The bottom of a dominant alliance

While it held the map the alliance's smallest guilds were being taken apart, and it knew the attacks were aimed at them in particular. On 17 January 2018 a member warned the war channel that [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s leader meant to take all their territories, and a member of another guild told LE Flowers it was being singled out as weak; LE Flowers' own members agreed, having two people reliably online who could fight.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|17 Jan 2018, the war channel}} On the 20th a [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] member said the other side had made a treaty with several guilds for the express purpose of targeting them, and another replied that the treaty was cover for an alliance.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the treaty}} By the 21st a member reported that alliance confirmed, [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] and [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] in it.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|21 Jan 2018, the confirmation}}

The capture log gives the fortnight its scale from outside. Hall of Fame lost 43 distinct territories on 20 January across 76 losing exchanges, to attackers led by PCB with 27, Sins of Seedia with 14, [[fantasy|Fantasy]] with 11, and Titans Valor and [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] with 7 each.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Hall of Fame losses by attacker, 20 Jan 2018 UTC, raw}} Over 17–31 January its heaviest were Sins of Seedia with 97 captures and Titans Valor with 46.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Hall of Fame losses by attacker, 17–31 Jan 2018 UTC, raw}} The guild's own figure at the time was forty-five territories to one in twenty-eight hours.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|24 Jan 2018, the low point}} No free-for-all ground can come out of these counts: the alliance marked its open ground on a map rather than naming it, so no enumerated list covers January 2018.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, free-for-all ground shown on the map only}}

Hall of Fame was courted while it was being stripped. On 21 January a member reported that Titans Valor's leader was working on the guild with the argument that [[hackforums|HackForums]] looked after itself alone, and said he would play along.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|21 Jan 2018, the approach}} By the 24th another put the pitch as a standing one always to the same effect — the attacks were for Hall of Fame's own good, and its interest lay in leaving the alliance for Sins of Seedia; a member answered that if they ever joined he would leave.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|24 Jan 2018, the pitch refused}}

LE Flowers was reduced to nothing. On 23 January members reported in the war channel that it held no territories, that [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] held the ground assigned to it, and that four of its members fought if a particular account were counted; its leader had stopped playing out of boredom and would not hand the guild on.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, LE Flowers}} Between 18 and 24 January the guild neither took nor lost a territory in the log, which ran unbroken on both sides of those five days.{{cite:territory-exchanges|LE Flowers, no exchanges 19–23 Jan 2018 UTC; no gap in the log}}

What the alliance owed such guilds was argued out on 21 January, when a member thanked another sarcastically for getting an enemy to focus Knights Radiant instead and asked why anybody would steer enemies onto a guild in his own alliance with less to fall back on. The member accused apologised.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|21 Jan 2018, the accusation}} A third answered that the alliance ought to be shielding its lesser guilds and pushing hostile attention onto members able to contest their own ground.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|21 Jan 2018, the answer}}

It had already asked itself whether to stop. On the morning of 16 January, hours before it published the allocation and free-for-all declaration that defined its January, a member asked the war channel whether there would ever be an area they did not interfere in; another answered that the Wynn province had been meant to become free-for-all and had not, and that handing ground over as the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] had done was what the Coalition owed its own rise to.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018, the question and the answer}} A third warned that stepping in whenever a guild grew too strong was precisely what the War Syndicate had done, and would make them its successor.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018, the warning}} Nobody in the conversation had the authority to decide it.

The adversary organising the attacks spent the fortnight in the alliance's own general channel. The account of Titans Valor's leader posted 2,184 messages there between 12 and 25 January, the fourth largest number by any account in a month carrying 31,961.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|12–25 Jan 2018, the general channel}} At 13:42 on the 25th a member asked the guild leaders to remove him; another proposed a mute instead, since a ban could be answered with a new account. At 13:47 the alliance's leader said he had banned him.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|25 Jan 2018, 13:42-13:47}}

The grouping stopped attacking in the second week of February. On the morning of the 8th a member said it no longer attacked them and another asked whether its organiser had given up; the following morning a member remarked in a single line that the pact was finished.{{cite:coalition-weakest-guilds-january-2018-discord-private|8-9 Feb 2018}}

### The last fortnight

The alliance spent its final two weeks admitting guilds. On 9 February 2018, in the alliance's private channel, its leader said they were not letting another guild in — answering a suggestion that an outside guild wanting territory should simply rejoin, and quoting in the same message that guild's complaint that the alliance kept every territory for itself and left none for anyone else.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|9 Feb 2018}}

Within days it admitted [[emorians|Emorians]], which had already been fighting alongside the alliance unofficially for some days, and told the membership on the 12th.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|9–11 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/12/2018 4:19 AM}} Two other guilds were confirmed as members in the same days and neither was a new arrival. [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] had been admitted on 1 February, nine votes to none, and held mid canyon on the map published that evening.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 1 Feb 2018, the motion closed at 12:59}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/1/2018}} LE Flowers had been a member for the whole month, named on the alliance's information card of 11 January and on all three of the territory lists from 16 January onward.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card as posted, 11 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018 and 2/1/2018}}

A fourth guild had come back before any of that. [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] rejoined on 8 February by ten votes to three, a week after leaving and four days after its own leader announced an intention to disband it, its territories having been held in the meantime by two other members.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|4–8 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 8 Feb 2018}}

The admissions outran the alliance's own bookkeeping. Two days before Emorians was admitted, a member asked in the war channel who they were and was told they were not in the alliance; on the 12th a member took a territory off them because they were not yet on the shared roster, and the map revision planned for the next day was postponed to accommodate the new arrival.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|10–12 Feb 2018}} By the final allocation that guild held seventeen territories. The alliance went from not recognising a guild's name to assigning it seventeen territories in five days, and then broke over the assignment.

Emorians then walked out with the other five on 16 February, four days after joining. No reason particular to that guild was ever given: the territory redistribution was the stated cause for the guilds that led the walkout, and Emorians was not among them.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

That postponed revision is the one the alliance broke over. Every guild admitted needed territory, every territory came from a member that already held one, and the final allocation gave KingdomPhoenixes 24, LE Flowers 20, Holders of LE 19 and Emorians 17 — eighty territories, more than a fifth of the map, to four guilds that had joined or rejoined inside the preceding fortnight.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|allocation list, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}} The alliance did not fall out over a principle so much as run out of map. The record documents each link in that chain and joins none of them; the connection is this article's.

The fortnight looked worse from underneath it. A coordinated multi-guild assault ran across 12 and 13 February, which members called a full-scale war, and the alliance's own war-frequency record marks a second sustained rise from about the 11th.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|11–13 Feb 2018}} On 14 February As Darkness Falls left, having been targeted continuously and needing allied help to hold its own ground; its leader gave the reason as stress, and another member said he did not blame them.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|14 Feb 2018}} Two days before the walkout, a member guild left because belonging to the alliance had stopped being protection.

Two smaller things from the same fortnight read differently in hindsight. [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] had offered [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] a peace treaty on condition that Fox hold no more than twelve territories, and Fox's officers laughed it off.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|February 2018}} And [[hackforums|HackForums]] — the guild that would lead the walkout — spent the start of the fortnight formally approving another guild's takeover of its remaining territories.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|early Feb 2018}} What that meant for its intentions two weeks later, the record does not say.

### The split
On 16–17 Feb 2018 (the community guild-timeline image dates the split to the 16th{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, DerpyEmerald24's guild-history timeline image (i.imgur.com/seklYAQ.png), 28 Jul 2020}}, the Timeline document to the 17th{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}), five member guilds — [[HackForums]], [[Paladins United]], House of Sentinels, [[Emorians]] and Kangronomicon — left over map disputes and formed [[Alliance Alliance]] together with [[Fantasy]] and Necronomicon, declaring war on their former alliance and beginning the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. The departures came within an hour of the allocation's announcement: "Hax, PUN, Snt, Fuq, and Emorians [ERN] left and made their own alliance combined with Fux and Feq. They attacked the rest of the Coalition, and had the map before the night was over."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}

Drew1011 disputed later claims that the departing guilds had tried to resolve the dispute first, writing that "there were no straightforward and direct attempts to solve the issues beforehand"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}.

The alliance's own channels record the walkout in more detail, and count six withdrawals rather than five: HackForums first, then Paladins United and House of Sentinels within minutes, then KingdomPhoenixes, Kangronomicon and Emorians, all within a few hours of the announcement.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}} Members catching up the next morning had to count the departures to establish their scale.

Five of the six left over the redistribution. [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] left the same evening for reasons of its own: its leader said in the guild-leaders channel that the alliance was finished, that she could not revive her guild, and that its war force amounted to little more than herself.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition guild-leaders channel, 16 Feb 2018}} It was inside the successor alliance within a day, and held the South Canyon in the Federation's first territory assignment five days later.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/17/2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018}}

The two sides gave different reasons for the same departure, within a day of each other. [[hackforums|HackForums]], which left first, criticised the alliance's voting system as weighted toward a majority of larger guilds at the expense of the guilds carrying the actual fighting{{cite:hackforums-guild-profile-discord-private|16 Feb 2018}}; a Coalition leader's account afterwards was that the departing guilds had simply been unwilling to surrender their share of territory.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}} Both were describing the same rule, under which the most valuable ground went to the guilds doing the most warring.{{cite:territory-economy-and-warfare-discord-private|allocation and contribution, 2018}}

The bloc had been assembled before it left. On the evening of the walkout the remaining members reported that one of the departing guilds had already been assigned territory across an entire province in a new and still-unnamed alliance{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}, and two of the departing guilds were taking territory from guilds that had stayed within hours of announcing they were leaving.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018}} The eight guilds left behind — [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], [[imperial|Imperial]], LE Flowers, [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]], [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] and Hall of Fame among them — recruited outside help rather than fold, drawing in Sins of Seedia and Avos Air as active participants against the departed bloc.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|16–18 Feb 2018}} Two of the departed guilds formed a new independent alliance and tried to recruit a third, whose leader declined on the stated grounds of keeping its membership small.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

The Coalition remnant merged with War Syndicate's remains — by then trading as the Illustratus alliance — into the new [[the-federation|Federation]], ending the Coalition as an entity{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}}{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}{{cite:guild-lineage-and-succession-discord-private|Illustratus}}; the civil war itself ran until the Federation took control of the map on 20 Mar 2018{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}.

Members of the new alliance described that origin — the surviving half of one alliance joined to another — as a defining fact about it.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

A participant described the sequence: "When Coalition was taking its toll, Fux and SDU were offered to join a new alliance together, The Federation."{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, 21 Jul 2018}}

Even the genealogy was disputed among participants. One held that "Coa and WS merged... this was a creation of fed"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}}, while [[slayne|Slayne]] wrote in 2018: "I created Fed because I (along with some others) created Double AA."{{cite:thread-237070-p03|post #45, 14 Nov 2018}}

### What its members said it had been

Members named a standing instrument covering the province of Wynn and called it the Wynn agreement. On 8 February 2018 one told the war channel that a rival could not take particular Wynn territories from them because of it, and on the 9th a captain of a member guild listed among his frustrations an earlier breach of it by [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]] over truced ground.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|8-9 Feb 2018, the instrument invoked}} After the split the former leader described it as having amounted to an instruction not to attack allies, which is the rule his own written account gives as the alliance's fatal defect.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|17 Feb 2018, what it had amounted to}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}} Whether it was ever set down in writing is not known.

The fullest description of it was given a week after the alliance ended. On 23 February a Fox war-leader set out in the successor alliance's war channel what the Wynn convention had been — ground held by an ally was not to be taken, and anything not held by an ally was open — and said it had worked badly, especially after the introduction of a rule under which a guild losing a Wynn territory had ten minutes to reclaim it before anyone else could.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|23 Feb 2018, the convention described}} That rule was why [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] ended up holding most of Wynn, he said, because they had the most people available to take ground at short notice; he had opposed it from the start, and its author was an officer associated with Paladins United.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|23 Feb 2018, the ten-minute rule and its author}} The alliance had approved the ten-minute rule five votes to nothing on 31 January.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan 2018}}

Its members defended the territorial system in merit terms. Answering an outside critic who called it exploitation, a member argued on 13 February that every guild was the alliance rather than serving a dominant one, that a guild which did not war had no reason to be given territory, and that heavy warring implied a treasury able to sustain it and therefore a capacity to hold ground — which was why HackForums held so much.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|13 Feb 2018, the defence}} The [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]], then resting, held nothing for the same reason and would have its ground returned when it came back; another member agreed that the guilds without territory were the ones not warring enough.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|13 Feb 2018, the guilds without territory}}

The leader carried a specific grievance about a guild that had gone. On 11 February a member explained that [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]] had once been a Coalition guild and had left because it contributed nothing and did not war; the leader added that it had been given the whole of Llevigar while contributing nothing, that across an entire in-game invasion it had taken a single Gavel territory, and that back when the alliance held only Wynn ground it had needed about a week to recover one territory.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|11 Feb 2018, the grievance}} Necronomicon was in [[alliance-alliance|Alliance Alliance]] five days later.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Members put the alliance's beginnings in Wynn alone: on 26 February the former leader told the successor alliance that the Coalition had tried and failed to recruit Achte Shadow back when it controlled only that province.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|26 Feb 2018, the recruitment attempt}}

The sizes they carried do not agree with each other. On 20 February a Fox war-leader put his guild's peak at ninety-one territories in the Coalition; the next day the guild's Viceroy put it at eighty, falling to about thirty when Gavel was assigned, and a leader of [[imperial|Imperial]] answered him in the same minute that HackForums had held a hundred and dropped to none after leaving.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|20-21 Feb 2018, the three figures}} On the 21st the former Coalition leader told the successor alliance's leaders that HackForums had held all of the Light Realm and around fifty territories in Wynn, and had left because those Wynn territories were being taken from it and it did not want to lose them to guilds it thought undeserving; the same Imperial leader replied that [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]]' own share had been disproportionate.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|21 Feb 2018, the leaders' channel}} On the 22nd he said the alliance had held every territory on the map and had held it that way for two months before it fell, and an officer of [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] said it had fallen out of greed.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|22 Feb 2018, the extent and the cause}} Members elsewhere put the alliance's whole life at about three months.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

### The record
The territory-exchange log begins in January 2018, after the Coalition formed; the guilds' real join dates were never recorded, and the membership of the five departing guilds rests on their documented February 2018 departures rather than on recorded joins{{cite:territory-exchanges|earliest row in the table, 3 Jan 2018 20:22:23 UTC; nothing precedes it}}. The alliance posted no founding thread, member list, takeover post, invasion thread or split thread. Most of its history — the planning date, the stated purpose, the rosters and the course of the split — rests on Drew1011's storytime account, written between March and July 2018 by a founder of the losing side of the split; beyond it and the community timeline, the Coalition's third-party trace is a handful of retrospective one-liners{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}}.

### The November 2017 allocation

A month before the invasion the alliance already divided the map. Drew1011 posted the allocation to KingdomPhoenixes on 22 November 2017, with a map, naming ten guilds and their regions: Dishonored at Ragni Main Entrance and Emerald Trail, Gilded Sparrows at the Nether and Detlas, Hall of Fame at Ragni, House of Sentinels in the canyon and at Ternaves, Immortalish in the jungle, Kasai Shinrai at Nivla, [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] at Nesaak and the mining base, KingdomPhoenixes across the desert and savannah, LE Flowers at Nivla and Time Valley, and [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]] at Nemract.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|11/22/2017}}

By 1 January 2018 the roster posted to the same channel had grown to thirteen, adding DeathReapers, [[hackforums|HackForums]], Knights Radiant, [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] and the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]].{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|1/1/2018}}

### The alliance’s own channels

What survives of the Coalition’s Discord is its second one. The first was deleted by its owner on 11 January 2018 in the course of [[the-coalition-discord-deletion|a quarrel inside a member guild]] and rebuilt the same day, so the record begins six weeks before the alliance ended and holds nothing of its founding or of the Gavel Invasion.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|1/11/2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|the rebuilt server, from 11 Jan 2018}} The rebuild carried a #storytime channel "for leaders to tell their Wynn stories" — the setting Drew1011’s serialised account came out of.{{cite:coalition-welcome|1/23/2018}}

On the day of the rebuild the alliance posted a card listing its member guilds and, separately, its enemies. It was last revised on 14 February 2018 and only the revised text was kept, so the fourteen and fourteen it names are the alliance's position two days before it broke rather than on the day the card went up: [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] and [[emorians|Emorians]] stand among the members, and both were admitted in February.{{cite:coalition-information|posted 1/11/2018 9:33 PM, last revised 14 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|9-11 Feb 2018}} The enemies were BuildCraftia, Funbari Onsen, Germany Elite, Magic Funhouse, Sins of Seedia, DogsAmongUs, TheOldKeepers, TheDivineSwords, Titans Valor, [[fantasy|Fantasy]], Beasts, Wrath of Poseidon, [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]] and Division Ragnarok.{{cite:coalition-information|enemy list as revised 14 Feb 2018}} Fantasy and Necronomicon had been Coalition guilds at the declaration of war in December, and both joined [[alliance-alliance|Alliance Alliance]] two days after the revision. As posted on 11 January the card had named fifteen member guilds and eleven enemies, with [[fantasy|Fantasy]] among the members and [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]] among the enemies; by 20 January Fantasy had been added to the enemy list and Necronomicon taken off it.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card as posted, 11 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the enemy list}}

Territory was reassigned four times in those six weeks — on 16 and 23 January, 1 February, and 16 February — each time as a list of guilds against regions, with maps.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018, 2/1/2018 and 2/16/2018}} The two January lists were rewritten in place afterwards, on 20 and 28 January, so neither carries the text it carried when it went up; what each said as posted, and what the edits changed, is set out at [[coalition-standing-documents|the alliance's standing documents]].{{cite:coalition-announcements|edit stamps: 16 Jan 2018 → 20 Jan 2018; 23 Jan 2018 → 28 Jan 2018}} By 12 February the alliance was "currently down a lot of territories and is getting attacked by many guilds", and Drew1011 was asking anyone who could log on to defend.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/12/2018}}

The last of those lists is the one that mattered. On 16 February 2018 Drew1011 posted "Territory change, we decided to assign Wynn" and gave thirteen guilds their regions — HackForums the Molten Heights, Sky Islands, Light Realm, savannah, jungle and Little Wood; Kingdom Foxes the north canyon and Nesaak; Emorians Llevigar, the Quartz Mines and the desert; Paladins United Corkus and the ocean, and so on.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/16/2018}} It is the announcement his account identifies as the cause of the split, and the split came within the hour.

The day after, a Coalition officer posted a new list to the same channel under the words "Hey people these are our new allies": Sins of Seedia, BuildCraftia, Kingdom Foxes, LE Flowers, PaT, TheDivineSwords, KingdomPhoenixes, Holders of LE, Imperial, DeathReapers and Immortalish.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/17/2018}} Three of those — Sins of Seedia, BuildCraftia and TheDivineSwords — had been on the alliance's enemy list three days earlier. That is [[the-federation|the Federation]] forming, recorded in the channel of the alliance it replaced.

## Membership
{{alliance:Coalition}}

## Legacy
Both of the great blocs of 2018 descend from the Coalition: Alliance Alliance from its defectors, and the Federation from its remnant{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. The Federation went on to hold the entire map for most of a year, defining the [[federation-era|Federation era]]{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} — and the Coalition's brief, total dominance became the template every later map-holding alliance would be measured against; a 2019 poster listed it alongside "Federation, Hax & Co" as one of the recurring mega-alliances of Wynn's history{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}}. It was also the last major alliance of the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]] to leave no thread of its own: from 2018 onward the blocs announced themselves on the forums again{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}.

## Documents kept current

The [[coalition|Coalition]] governed Gavel by publishing a list of guilds against regions with maps attached, and it published three such lists between the destruction of its Discord server on 11 January 2018 and the division of Wynn that broke the alliance: on 16 January, on 23 January and on 1 February.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018 and 2/1/2018}} A fourth, on 16 February, extended the same method to the province of Wynn, and the walkout that ended the alliance began within the hour.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/16/2018}} Alongside them stood the alliance-information card, a panel naming the alliance's members and its enemies, posted on the evening of the rebuild.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018}}

Three of the four were rewritten in place afterwards. The 16 January list was edited at 23:53 on 20 January, the 23 January list at 11:33 on the 28th, and the card at 06:01 on 14 February; the 1 February list carries no later edit.{{cite:coalition-announcements|edit stamps: 16 Jan 2018 → 20 Jan 2018; 23 Jan 2018 → 28 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018, revised 14 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|posting and edit timestamps, January–February 2018}} None of the three therefore dates its own contents to the day it went up. Two of them can be read as posted anyway, because the alliance's papers moved in both directions: members copied them out of the announcements channel to explain them to each other, and leaders had drafted them in other rooms first.

## The allocation of 16 January

At 03:41 on 20 January a member of the war channel, pointed at the announcements channel two minutes earlier, pasted the whole of the 16 January list back into the conversation and posted the announcement's own map image seconds afterwards.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the paste}} As posted, the document gave regions to thirteen guilds: the Light Realm to Knights Radiant, the Molten Heights with part of Llevigar and a share of the north canyon to [[hackforums|HackForums]], the rest of the north canyon to [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], the south canyon to [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], the ground around Cinfras to [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], the Dark Forest to Kasai Shinrai, the Light Forest to [[imperial|Imperial]], the fortress and Gelibord to Dishonored, the swamp to [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]], Llevigar to Immortalish, the north ocean to LE Flowers, the south ocean to the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]], and Corkus to [[paladins-united|Paladins United]].{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 16 January allocation as posted}}

The edit rewrote two lines and left the other eleven alone: Llevigar passed from Immortalish to [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]], Immortalish moved to the south ocean, and the Serpentem Empire came off the map altogether.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the two texts compared}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, revised 20 Jan 2018}} Thirteen guilds still held ground. The stamp gives the last revision rather than the only one, so the two lines could have moved at any point between the paste and the night of the 20th.

Kangronomicon had been admitted at 12:20 on 16 January, forty-six minutes before the list went up, and was not in it.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018 12:20 PM and 1:06 PM}} Ten minutes before that admission was announced, the alliance's leader had told the guild leaders that the new arrival meant ground had to be found, and had given any guild that had not yet taken the land already assigned to it until Saturday before its allocation was redrawn smaller; the message was pinned.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018, the deadline}} Saturday was 20 January, and the document was edited at four minutes to midnight that night. Reading the edit as the deadline being enforced is this article's: the alliance never said so, and what supports it is the substance of the change, a newly admitted guild written into a region that had been assigned to a guild under notice.

## The allocation of 23 January

The next list was drafted in a small leadership channel at 13:28, with a table of each guild's net gain or loss and a question whether everyone was satisfied; a leader pointed out within twelve minutes that a guild had been left off it.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, the drafting}} The same text went to the wider guild leaders' channel at 16:40, was put as a motion at 16:45, and was published at 17:33.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, the sequence}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018 5:33 PM}}

Both drafts gave Kander to Kasai Shinrai and gave Immortalish the west ocean, which the same document also assigned to Paladins United; the published text as it now stands gives Kander to the Serpentem Empire and moves Immortalish to the east ocean.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 23 January drafts}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018}} Kasai Shinrai left the alliance on 27 January and the document was edited on the 28th.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|27–28 Jan 2018}}

The substitution appears to have been made at that edit rather than before publication, though what circulated four hours and fifty-three minutes beforehand was the draft and not the published text.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, drafting and publication}} Three things support it: the drafts and the published text agree line for line everywhere else; the Serpentem Empire had no assigned region at all that afternoon; and at 17:24, nine minutes before publication, the leaders were choosing a single territory on the edge of the map to give it.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, the edge territory}}

## The allocation of 1 February

The list of 1 February was posted at 20:57 and never touched again. It gave ground to eleven guilds, among them [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] at mid canyon and As Darkness Falls in the east Dark Forest, both admitted within the previous four days; KingdomPhoenixes, Dishonored, Immortalish and DeathReapers hold nothing on it.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/1/2018}}

## The information card

The card went up at 21:33 on 11 January 2018, sixty-eight minutes after the alliance's leader pasted its text into the general channel of the replacement server, which was then minutes old; the material had been saved as soon as the first server was threatened.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|11 Jan 2018, 20:25 and 21:33}}{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|12 Jan 2018, 04:19:40 UTC}} That January text named fifteen member guilds and eleven enemies.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card as posted, 11 Jan 2018}} The fourteen members and fourteen enemies the card now carries are the text as last edited on 14 February 2018, five weeks later — which is why [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]], [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] and [[emorians|Emorians]] are on its member list, having been admitted on 16 January, 1 February and 12 February.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018, revised 14 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 2/1/2018 and 2/12/2018}}

A third state of the card is fixed between the two. At 03:39 on 20 January a member pasted its list of enemies into the war channel, two minutes before pasting the allocation: eleven guilds, with [[fantasy|Fantasy]] added after its departure on 15 January and [[necronomicon|Necronomicon]] taken off.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the enemy list}} That list is the February list without its last three entries, which are Wrath of Poseidon, Necronomicon and Division Ragnarok: the February text put Necronomicon back after a month off the list and added two names at the end. A document maintained by appending looks exactly like that, and reading it that way is this article's; the alternative, that the paste was cut short, sits badly with Necronomicon standing last on 11 January.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018, revised 14 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the three states of the enemy list}} The dates belong to the card and not to the hostilities: an entry says when the panel was brought up to date, not when a guild became an enemy.

## Two instruments, two memberships

The card and the allocations did not name the same alliance. DeathReapers is on the card in both its January and its February states and on none of the three territory lists. Dishonored holds ground on 16 and 23 January, is absent from the list of 1 February and from the February card, and no departure was ever announced. Immortalish holds ground on both January lists, is absent from the 1 February list, and is on the February card all the same.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card in both states}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018 and 2/1/2018}}{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018, revised 14 Feb 2018}}

Neither works as a membership roll by itself, and absence from an allocation is not a departure: the Serpentem Empire was a member for about a week at the end of January with no assigned region at all.{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|16–23 Jan 2018}}

## Free-for-all ground

The alliance opened territory to anyone who wanted it and never wrote down which. The declaration of 16 January defined the pool only as the black areas of the two attached maps.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018: "Free for all territories are in black."}} The list of 23 January did not mention it at all, and the list of 1 February said further territories would be opened without saying which.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018 and 2/1/2018}}

The version of the 1 February document put to the guild leaders went one step further, recording that some of the best territories around Ahmsord were to be made free for all once the official map existed.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|1 Feb 2018, the Ahmsord note}} That names a district and not a territory, and it is the nearest the alliance came to setting its open ground down in text. The three distributions the leaders voted on that month are at [[coalition-three-maps-february-2018|the Coalition's three maps]].{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the three motions, 1-16 Feb 2018}}

There had been a register. On 17 January the alliance announced a listing that sorted every territory it did not own into assigned ground, truced ground and free-for-all ground.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/17/2018 6:04 PM}} It lived in a channel members were already calling deleted three days later.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|17–20 Jan 2018}} The only January ground that can be placed in the pool from text is the black area beside Cinfras, which a member explained to a newcomer on the 20th as open to anyone and generally taken by Hall of Fame — practice rather than policy.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|20 Jan 2018, the Cinfras ground}} The alliance's free-for-all position for January 2018 cannot be recovered, and no capture figure for that month can be corrected for it. The first free-for-all list written out by name came from the [[the-federation|Federation]] on 10 March 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018}}

## The maps

The two images attached to the 23 January list are named as the seventh map and its ocean companion, so the alliance had drawn at least six before it — a numbering may skip or restart, and no more than that follows from it.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 23 January attachments}} Those earlier maps went with the alliance's first Discord on 11 January, which is why the series begins on the 16th.{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|12 Jan 2018, 04:19 UTC}} One earlier allocation had been posted elsewhere and outlasted them: on 22 November 2017 the alliance's leader gave ten guilds their regions, with a map, in a member guild's own announcement channel.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|11/22/2017}}

Times here are the alliance's own clock, which ran eight hours behind UTC that winter. Territory-exchange figures are UTC and say so.

## Three distributions in a fortnight

The [[coalition|Coalition]] put three complete territorial distributions to its guild leaders in the fourteen days before it broke apart, and carried all three.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the three motions, 1-16 Feb 2018}} The first was posted at 12:58:48 on 1 February 2018 and put to a vote seventy-two seconds afterwards; it closed at 11:21:39 on 3 February, seven in favour and one against.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|first motion, 1-3 Feb 2018}} The second went up at 19:33 on 9 February and closed at 12:31:09 the next midday, six in favour and three against.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|second motion, 9-10 Feb 2018}} The third was put at 12:22:59 on 14 February and closed at 18:18:50 on the 16th, seven in favour and one against.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|third motion, 14-16 Feb 2018}}

The second was a restart rather than a fresh question. The alliance's leader had opened a vote on the same subject about three hours earlier and, asked whether he meant to redo it, said he did.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|9 Feb 2018, the restarted motion}} Whether that abandoned attempt counts as a fourth motion is a judgement this article does not make.

Only two of the three reached the membership. Territory lists went to the alliance's announcements channel on 16 and 23 January, 1 February and 16 February, and none between the two February dates.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018, 2/1/2018 and 2/16/2018}} The distribution carried on 10 February was settled in the guild leaders' channel and never published to the alliance at large. How the alliance took its other decisions in the same weeks is at [[coalition-voting|voting in the Coalition]], and the documents it kept current are at [[coalition-standing-documents|its standing documents]].

## What moved between the first and the second

Both surviving documents can be read line for line, and the assignments move. The distribution of 1 February gave eleven guilds a region each: the Molten Heights, the Sky Islands and the Light Realm to [[hackforums|HackForums]]; the north canyon, the Quartz Mines, Leadin Fortress, the Llevigar entrance and the road to the Light Forest to [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]]; the south canyon to [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]]; the ground around Cinfras to [[imperial|Imperial]]; the east Dark Forest to As Darkness Falls; Kander to the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]]; the swamp and west Dark Forest to [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]]; the Light Forest to [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]]; the mid canyon to [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]]; Llevigar to LE Flowers; and Corkus with the ocean to [[paladins-united|Paladins United]].{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the distribution of 1 Feb 2018}}

The distribution of 9 February left seven of those alone — HackForums, Hall of Fame, Imperial, House of Sentinels, Kangronomicon, LE Flowers and Paladins United — and moved the rest.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the distribution of 9 Feb 2018, guilds unmoved}} [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] was added and took the mid canyon; Holders of LE, which had held it, went out to all nine jungle territories; and the Serpentem Empire and As Darkness Falls exchanged regions, the one moving into the east Dark Forest and the other into Kander.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the distribution of 9 Feb 2018, the moves}}

Llevigar appears twice on the second document, once against LE Flowers and once against Kingdom Foxes, and the two entries were never distinguished — either two places sharing a name or a mistake in the drafting.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the two Llevigar entries, 9 Feb 2018}} Whether either document was altered after it went up is not known: both were put to the guild leaders rather than announced, and only the announcement channel's messages carry edit stamps.{{cite:coalition-announcements|edit stamps on the announced lists: 16 Jan 2018 to 20 Jan 2018; 23 Jan 2018 to 28 Jan 2018}}

The 1 February document also said something about open ground: that some of the best territories around Ahmsord were to be made free for all once the official map existed.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|1 Feb 2018, the Ahmsord note}} That names a district and not a list, and it is as near as the alliance came to writing its free-for-all pool down — the ground was otherwise drawn in black on the maps and never set out by name.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, free-for-all ground shown on the map only}} No enumerated free-for-all list covers February 2018, so no capture figure for the month can have that churn taken out of it.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018, the first list written out by name}}

## The Wynn motion

Between the second distribution and the third the alliance voted separately on the province of Wynn — the ground its largest guilds held, and the one province its settlement had never divided.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the Wynn motion, 10-11 Feb 2018}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 16, composed 20 May 2018}} The motion was put at 12:31:54 on 10 February, forty-five seconds after the second map motion closed, and it closed at 17:53:14 the following afternoon, nine in favour and four against.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the Wynn motion put and closed, 10-11 Feb 2018}} Thirteen guilds voted on it, against eight on the map motion five days later.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the two counts, 11 and 16 Feb 2018}}

On the evening of the walkout the alliance's leader named the four guilds that had voted against: HackForums, Paladins United, Kangronomicon and House of Sentinels.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018, the four named}} Asked whether [[emorians|Emorians]] had been among them, he answered that the guild had not yet been a member when the motion ran.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018, the correction about Emorians}} He was right by under three hours: Emorians was admitted at 20:44:32 on 11 February, nine votes to nothing.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the Emorians motion, 11 Feb 2018}} A member in the same exchange gave a different set of dissenters including DeathReapers, and the recorded count matches the leader's four rather than his.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018, the competing list}}

## Fifty-three minutes

The third motion closed at 18:18:50 on the evening of 16 February, which is 02:18:50 UTC on the 17th.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the close, 16 Feb 2018}} Fifty-three minutes and fifty seconds afterwards the leader of HackForums announced in the alliance's general channel that his guild was formally withdrawing, and House of Sentinels, Paladins United and Emorians followed within ninety seconds.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018, 19:12:40 and after}} The successor alliance's Discord server was created fifty-two minutes and twenty-seven seconds after that message.{{cite:federation-founding-night-2018-discord-private|server creation computed from the Discord id, 16 Feb 2018}} Three of the four had voted against the Wynn assignment; the fourth had not been a member when that motion ran. The guilds that left gave the alliance's direction as their reason.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

Eight minutes before the first withdrawal a member had told the same channel that the map they were looking at was the one that had been discussed in another guild's server.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018, the map already seen}} The document was two days old and was being argued over in the channel that evening.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|14-16 Feb 2018, the map in circulation}}

Territory exchanges put the break in the same hour from outside. Those between the five guilds that left and the eight that stayed had run between twenty-two and sixty-four a day through 10 to 16 February; on 17 February there were 495, and the hour after the first withdrawal message carried 58 against thirteen in the hour before it.{{cite:territory-exchanges|exchanges both ways between the five withdrawing guilds and the eight that stayed, 10-20 Feb 2018 UTC, raw: no free-for-all list covers February 2018}} The first of them fell at 03:18:37 UTC, five minutes and fifty-seven seconds after the message.{{cite:territory-exchanges|House of Sentinels takes Gromblins Hideout from Serpentem Empire, 17 Feb 2018 03:18:37 UTC}} None of these figures can be corrected for free-for-all ground, because no list naming that ground was written down before 10 March 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018, the first list written out by name}}

## The third map, still being drawn

The third distribution was being revised while it was being voted on. Late on 14 February members told the war channel that the alliance's leader had made a new map and put it to a vote; that it would this time include KingdomPhoenixes and Emorians; and that it would have to be redrawn again because As Darkness Falls had already left the alliance.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|14 Feb 2018, the war channel}} That guild had gone on the 14th, two days before the walkout.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|14 Feb 2018}}

Whether the document that closed on the 16th was the one posted on the 14th or a revision of it was never established.{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|14-16 Feb 2018, the two versions}} What the announcements channel carried that evening named thirteen guilds and their regions, and the first withdrawal followed within the hour.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/16/2018}} The walkout itself is at [[coalition|the Coalition]] and the alliance it produced at [[the-federation-founding-night|the founding night]]. The fighting around the alliance in the same fortnight, most of which was not between alliances, is at [[coalition-under-attack-february-2018|the Coalition under attack]].

## Two rooms and a channel

The [[coalition|Coalition]] made its decisions in two rooms and published them from a third. Documents were drafted in a small leadership channel, put to the wider guild leaders' channel, voted there, and announced to the membership.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|the sequence, January 2018}} The territory list of 23 January 2018 is the worked example: drafted at 13:28 with a table of each guild's net gain or loss and a question whether everyone was satisfied, corrected within twelve minutes when a leader pointed out that a guild had been left off it, posted unchanged to the guild leaders at 16:40, put as a motion at 16:45, and published at 17:33.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018 5:33 PM}}

## The ten results

Every result was written into the guild leaders' channel as its motion closed, so the counts below are the counts the alliance acted on rather than a later reading.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|15 Jan – 8 Feb 2018, the recorded closes}}

[[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]] was admitted, eleven for and none against with six abstentions.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|15–23 Jan 2018}} The territory list of 23 January was approved eight to nothing with no abstentions.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|23–24 Jan 2018}} As Darkness Falls was refused admission on 27 January, eleven against and one for with six abstentions, and Legion of Tilks — put to the leaders as being in effect a sub-guild of [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] — was refused seven to five with one abstention.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|27 Jan 2018, the two refusals}} A motion to do away with abstention was defeated six to five with one abstention.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|27–28 Jan 2018}} As Darkness Falls was then put a second time and admitted, seven for and one against with six abstentions.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|28–29 Jan 2018}} A ten-minute waiting rule for the Wynn province was approved five to nothing and announced on the evening of 31 January.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/31/2018 9:08 PM}} [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] was admitted, nine for and none against with one abstention.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 1 Feb 2018}} The territory list of 1 February was approved seven to one, and [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] was readmitted on 8 February by ten votes to three.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|1–8 Feb 2018}}

## Announced before it was carried

The alliance published its decisions before its votes closed, and did so as a matter of course rather than by accident. Kangronomicon's admission was announced at 12:20 on 16 January; the motion admitting it had been open since the evening of the 15th, a leader had noted that morning that it had a majority, and nobody closed it until 16:45 on the 23rd, seven days later.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018 12:20 PM}}{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|15–23 Jan 2018, the admission}} The list of 23 January was published forty-eight minutes after its motion was put and approved nineteen hours after publication.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|23–24 Jan 2018}} The list of 1 February went up while its motion was still running and was approved two days afterwards.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|1–3 Feb 2018}} On 8 February the alliance's leader said a readmission had a majority and that the motion would be closed once other business was finished; it was closed nine minutes later.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018}}

Nothing set that out as a rule, and the alliance never wrote one down. What the four cases show is a practice of acting on a visible majority and recording the count afterwards, and the consequence matters more than the practice: the date a Coalition decision took effect is the date it was announced, not the date it was carried, and the two could be a week apart.

## More votes than there were guilds

The counts do not fit an alliance voting once per member guild. The ten recorded totals run from five to eighteen. Seventeen votes were cast on Kangronomicon's admission and eighteen on the first refusal of As Darkness Falls, against fifteen member guilds on the alliance's card of 11 January and fourteen by February.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|the recorded totals}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the card as posted, 11 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018, revised 14 Feb 2018}}

One guild named a second representative to the leaders' channel on 16 January.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} Whether both of a guild's representatives could vote was never settled here or anywhere else in the period; on 24 January enforcement amounted to one member telling another that they could only vote once.{{cite:who-gets-a-vote-discord-private|24 Jan 2018}} The longer argument is at [[alliance-governance|alliance governance]].

## The vote on voting

The one motion the alliance put about itself was whether to keep the right to abstain. It followed the two heaviest abstentions on the record — six of seventeen votes on one admission and six of eighteen on another — and a leader telling the channel that anyone who did not want to vote should simply not vote.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|January 2018, the abstentions}} Put on 27 January and closed on the 28th, it was defeated by six votes to five with one abstention, the narrowest of the ten results.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|27–28 Jan 2018}}

Abstention then disappeared anyway. Every motion put before 31 January offered it; the last that did was opened on the evening of the 31st and restarted without it by another leader two minutes later.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan 2018}} None of the motions that followed offered it — not the ten-minute rule, not the list of 1 February, not the readmission of 8 February, and neither of the two February redistributions.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|31 Jan – 14 Feb 2018}} The February counts are therefore counts under a two-answer regime: the redistribution that preceded the walkout carried seven to one, which is eight votes cast in an alliance of fourteen guilds.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|10 and 14 Feb 2018}} The alliance voted to keep the option and then stopped using it.

## A refusal reversed in two days

As Darkness Falls was refused on 27 January by eleven votes to one; the motion was put again on the 28th and carried on the 29th by seven to one.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|27–29 Jan 2018}} No reason for the reversal was ever given. The guild took the east Dark Forest on the territory list of 1 February and left the alliance on 14 February, two days before the walkout.{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/1/2018 and 2/14/2018 2:46 PM}}

## How a guild got in

The procedure had two entry points and one gate. A guild wanting to join asked the alliance's leader directly, or a member guild's leader proposed inviting one, and in either case the alliance then voted.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|9 Feb 2018, the procedure}} He set it out on 9 February 2018, and it matches the motions the leaders' channel actually carried.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|15 Jan - 8 Feb 2018, the recorded closes}} Asked in the same exchange what had persuaded the alliance to admit [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], he answered that it had held only about four guilds at the time and had needed more; the answer carries no date, and the alliance had been founded the previous autumn.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|9 Feb 2018, the Hall of Fame answer}}

Terms could run the other way. On the morning of 9 February an officer of Hall of Fame recounted in the war channel that her guild had left the alliance, had said it would come back if the alliance made a channel to hold muted members, that the alliance did so, and that this was how the guild rejoined.{{cite:coalition-explained-by-its-members-february-2018-discord-private|9 Feb 2018, the condition and the return}} No vote on that condition was recorded, and neither the departure nor the return was dated by anyone who spoke of them.

The February motions are not in the ten results above. Three complete territorial distributions, a separate decision on the province of Wynn and two more admissions went to the same channel between 1 and 16 February 2018, and they are set out at [[coalition-three-maps-february-2018|the Coalition's three maps]].{{cite:coalition-three-maps-february-2018-discord-private|the February motions, 1-16 Feb 2018}}

## Jurisdiction over conduct

The alliance claimed authority over how its guild leaders behaved towards members of other member guilds. After complaints about one of them, its moderation drafted a formal notice in the leadership channel on 25 January 2018, circulated it there for approval and posted it to the guild leaders' channel at 12:30. It reminded guild leaders that they represented the alliance as well as their own guilds, and warned that if the conduct continued the matter would be made public and those responsible would cease to be part of the alliance.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|25 Jan 2018, the notice}} Rules otherwise arrived after the event: written guild rules were proposed following a dispute over a member's conduct, alt guilds and multi-account warring were banned with a grace period after two such guilds were exposed, and the ten-minute reclaim window followed a month in which allied guilds had been taking each other's lost ground.{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|rule changes, January 2018}}{{cite:alliance-governance-mechanics-discord-private|Coalition reclaim rule, late January 2018}}

The **Confederation** was a war alliance of 2018, assembled against [[the-federation|the Federation]] and led from [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] after that guild's expulsion in April.

## Known only from its enemy

The Confederation ran a Discord server of its own and it was destroyed. The day it went was never written down: [[the-federation|Federation]] members were still speaking of it as a live server on 30 July 2018{{cite:confederation-side-of-the-archive-2018-discord-private|30 Jul 2018}}, and by 23 August one of them was calling it the old Confederation Discord.{{cite:confederation-side-of-the-archive-2018-discord-private|23 Aug 2018}} On 8 September a member said in the Federation's general channel that whoever had deleted it had taken a great deal of guild history down with it; a second named him and said he had by then destroyed two alliance servers, and a third that he had a history of interfering with roles and with Discord servers.{{cite:confederation-side-of-the-archive-2018-discord-private|8 Sep 2018}} No reason for it was ever given. A Confederation server was running again by October, gated so that a member had to be approved before he could see its channels.{{cite:confederation-side-of-the-archive-2018-discord-private|October 2018}}

The Federation had been inside the first one since midsummer. Its founder joined on 18 June 2018, told his leadership channel the next evening what the alliance had just decided, and produced a screenshot of its leaders' channel that day and another the day after.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|18–20 Jun 2018}} He kept a second account there through the summer that survived at least one round of bans, and was still asking in October whether it might be let back in.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|Jul – Oct 2018}} In September 2018 another Federation member said the Confederation had made him a moderator of its server in the knowledge that he did not belong to it.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|Sep 2018}}

Everything below was written down by the alliance it was attacking, in that alliance's own rooms, and almost all of it is in the accusative: things the Confederation did to somebody else.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|September 2018}}

One guild named as joining it kept a server that survived, and the alliance does not appear in the part of it that was collected. Across two channels of [[kingdomphoenixes|Kingdom Phoenixes]] between mid-August and mid-November 2018, a search for the alliance, its leader, its principal guild and the two guilds named alongside this one returns eleven messages, all of them jokes.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|two channels, 15 Aug – 15 Nov 2018}} Nine of the eleven fall on 9 October, when members noticed the enemy leader sitting in their own Discord with no roles, talking to himself.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|9 Oct 2018}} That is two channels of one guild, out of ten taken from a server that listed eighteen — and the channel the guild kept for alliance business is among the eight never collected. So the silence is bounded by what was gathered rather than by what was said, and members need not discuss alliance politics in a general channel in any case.

## Out of the Round Table (June–July 2018)

The bloc had a predecessor that destroyed itself without being beaten. On 18 June 2018 [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s leader reported to his own leadership channel that the Round Table — the alliance assembled to fight his — had just fallen apart after about two hours of continuous arguing, that a member guild had walked out because the arguing had turned so poisonous, and that its leader was messaging him at that moment about rejoining the Federation.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|18 Jun 2018}} Ten days earlier more than fifteen guilds under its banner had attempted a coordinated attack meant to remove the Federation from the map, and five days before the collapse its own leader had proposed merging the two alliances into one with no assigned territory at all.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|8 Jun and mid-Jun 2018}}

The successor's first act was to disown him. Within a day it formally cut ties with the Round Table's leader, and its member guilds agreed to stop warring for about a week and a half.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|June 2018}} By 20 June Federation members were recording the pieces as a new alliance, the Confederate Guilds of Wynn, and treating it as the main opposition from that point; a further grouping was announced under the Confederation name before July was out.{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|20 Jun – Jul 2018}} By September the Federation was again describing the alliance as led from [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]]{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018}}; how the disowning ended was never recorded.

It was fighting on the old scale within weeks. On 25 July 2018 the Federation told its membership that [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] and Verinian Trials had left it and partnered with the new bloc.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/25/2018}} In the last days of the month it put roughly fifteen guilds against the Federation's largest, five to seven attacking at once, over about sixteen hours — see [[the-federation-july-2018|the Federation in July 2018]].{{cite:enemy-alliances-2018-discord-private|late July 2018}}

## Something was already forming in April

One source from that side is public. On 25 April 2018 a thread went up on the Wynncraft forums calling for an uprising against "these tyrannical mega-guilds such as Imperial and Kingdom of Foxes", asking any guild "brave enough to fight against the largest armies known to Wynn" to reply with its tag.{{cite:thread-224905|post #1, 25 Apr 2018}} One guild was enlisted: the author's own.

The next morning [[tntdestroyd|Tntdestroyd]] told him they had already begun forming what he was looking to do, and invited him to join that instead.{{cite:thread-224905|post #3, 26 Apr 2018}} Four months before the offensive. Whether what he had begun became the alliance BuildCraftia led in September is stated by nobody; only his guild joins the two.

A member of one of the guilds named answered at length, and the alliance the recruiter had called a dictatorship described itself, unasked and in public, as a franchise with a property qualification: two votes per member guild, one per leader, on admissions and expulsions, with territory assignment kept by the veteran guilds and earnable by activity.{{cite:thread-224905|post #7, 26 Apr 2018}}

On 29 July 2018 the Federation's founder put a second thread, titled The Revolution 1.0, into his own channels, by a different author, and told them it was the work of a player his guild had removed.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|29 Jul 2018}} It has since gone from the forum, and what it said went unrecorded elsewhere.{{cite:https://forums.wynncraft.com/threads/231203/|Wynncraft forums thread 231203, no longer served}}

## What it did in its own name

It assigned territory to its guilds and passed the assignments round inside its own server rather than publishing them: on 20 June 2018 the Federation's leadership channel was shown a screenshot of a member handing them out there.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|20 Jun 2018}} What they named went unrecorded. The Federation published its own allocations in an announcement channel through the same months{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|the published allocations, Mar – Oct 2018}}; setting the two against each other is this article's.

On 16 July 2018 a member of the Federation's leadership channel who had herself belonged to the Confederation said the alliance had voted on whether to remain the Round Table or become the Confederate Guilds of Wynn, and that its leader found the winning name deeply objectionable on grounds unconnected with the game and tried to have it changed; two others present confirmed the vote and his reaction.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|16 Jul 2018}} When the vote fell was never written down, and no other decision of the alliance's own was either.{{cite:confederation-side-of-the-archive-2018-discord-private|Feb – Oct 2018}}

No pool of territory open to all comers was ever published on the Confederation's side.{{cite:confederation-instruments-2018-discord-private|no free-for-all declaration on that side, Feb – Oct 2018}} Every declaration and every argument about one belonged to the [[coalition|Coalition]], the Federation and their successors.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|free-for-all declarations, Mar – Oct 2018}} Reading that against the merger its leader had proposed in June — one alliance, no assigned land at all — as a position rather than an omission is this article's.

## The September offensive

It was felt hardest by the smallest guilds. On 2 September 2018 members of two of them reported in the Federation's war channel that they were being attacked three times in a minute, that the fighting was five against three, that two defenders were carrying it, and that the attackers were moving faster than they could answer.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|2 Sep 2018}}

A member watching the same fighting noticed that all the attacking guilds but one appeared to be operating alone rather than in concert.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|2 Sep 2018}}

## Dead on the fifteenth, rebuilt by the eighteenth

On 15 September a Federation member reported that the Confederation was finished and that every guild had left it except two.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|15 Sep 2018}}

Three days later another told the leadership channel that BuildCraftia's leader had confirmed to him directly that three further guilds — [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]], Fuq and [[kingdomphoenixes|Kingdom Phoenixes]] — had each agreed to enter the alliance he was assembling.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018}}

By 20 September a Federation member could say that the only alliances left standing were the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] and [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]].{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|20 Sep 2018}}

## Watched from inside as it broke up

Federation members spent September 2018 reading the other side's channels and reporting what they found. On the 6th one relayed what was being said there about [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], and the Federation's founder repeated a phrase from it about an offensive that had nearly emptied his guild.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|6 Sep 2018, the relay}} A second member confirmed it and a third said the attempt had cost the attackers more morale than the defenders.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|6 Sep 2018, the answers}} On the 7th a member spent about an hour and a quarter compiling screenshots of an argument he said had run two or three hours in the other alliance's Discord, and posted the lot as an album.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|7 Sep 2018}} On the 9th another reported a leak from a source inside it, and the founder said the two sides there had been arguing constantly since [[nethers-ascent|Nethers Ascent]] left them and had had a four-hour argument the day before.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|9 Sep 2018}}

The break-up reached the Federation before it reached the map. On 19 September its war channel noticed from [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]]'s public statistics page that the guild's leading figure had stepped down, and the alliance's territory coordinator observed that stepping down had obliged him to leave the guild altogether, forfeiting a contribution of about five million emeralds.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|19 Sep 2018, the statistics page}} Inside the hour the leadership channel had the rest: he had been banned from the game, the leadership had passed to a named member, and that member had described holding ownership jointly with a second person.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|19 Sep 2018, the leadership channel}} The ground given for the ban was abuse of a game glitch, reported at second hand by Federation members and confirmed by nobody, as was the emerald figure; members disagreed about whether it was his second ban or his fifth.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|19 Sep 2018, the war channel}} Half an hour after the ban was reported the Federation's founder said the other side had already made a new alliance.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|19 Sep 2018, the new alliance}}

The next day his leaders had the shape of it. The member who had been reading those channels said the split had been caused by two figures rather than by the banned leader, that the active guilds had all left to form a new alliance, and that what stood under the old name was two guilds — Achte Shadow and Wrath Of Poseidon — and the inactive members.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|20 Sep 2018}} Half an hour later he said the Confederation no longer existed and that it was now Zenith and the guilds of the [[sol|SOL]] pact.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|20 Sep 2018, the successors}} Another leader answered that the enemy-of-my-enemy principle held only so long as the friends did not fight each other.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|20 Sep 2018, the principle}} The two-guild count is the same one a Federation member had given five days earlier; the two names and the successors come from a different speaker in a different channel.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|15 Sep 2018}}

A guild formed out of the wreck was identified inside the Federation's war channel within a week of appearing, and the identification was disputed. On 19 September a member said Azeron [Zer] was a new BuildCraftia subguild, that he knew rather than guessed it, and that he had played with its owner when the owner was in BuildCraftia; the next afternoon a second member said instead that it was a subguild of Arisen, a Federation member.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|19–20 Sep 2018}} Which it was went unresolved. The alliance refused the guild's application a month later — see [[federation-last-motions-2018|the Federation's last motions]].

## The enemy list became the enemy's roster

On 22 September 2018 the Federation stopped keeping a list of its own enemies and adopted the successor alliance's membership roll in place of it. Its founder put to the leadership channel a roll of nineteen guilds he said he had taken directly from the new alliance's Discord and asked whether the leaders were content for it to replace the enemy list in the alliance's information channel; three agreed inside the minute and nobody objected.{{cite:federation-who-is-an-ally-september-2018-discord-private|22 Sep 2018}} The nineteen, given alphabetically: Achte Shadow, [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]], [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]], Faith, [[hackforums|HackForums]], [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], HardcoreGamerzThree, Kangronomicon, [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], [[libertas|Libertas]], Metric, Oceans Wrath, Sin of Wrath, The Mage Legacy, The Nezaract, TheOldKeepers, The Super Empire, TruthSworD and Wrath Of Poseidon.{{cite:federation-who-is-an-ally-september-2018-discord-private|22 Sep 2018, the roll}}

Two of the nineteen had been Federation guilds that same year. Hall of Fame left the alliance on 25 July{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|7/25/2018}}; Metric was removed from it on 2 September.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|9/2/2018}} The roll was what the Federation believed the other side to be, copied at second hand from a server it had no standing in: evidence of its own understanding rather than of the successor's membership.

Five days later the founder was trying to settle with the guild second on that list. On 27 September the territory coordinator told the war channel that a player had left BuildCraftia's Discord when Kingdom Foxes members joined it, that he had spoken to that player shortly before they did, and that BuildCraftia's new leader and the Federation's founder had reached an understanding that the two of them would try to mend the breach between their guilds.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|27 Sep 2018}} That is one member's account of an agreement between two people, neither of whom was in the conversation.

## The other side's account of the same collapse

On 5 November 2018 a war leader of the opposing alliance wrote a summary of her own history in a Federation channel and gave the same sequence: arguments between the same two figures and the banned leader until drama was routine; the alliance losing people and morale; a decision to split it in two, Zenith and the SOL pact, with every guild but Achte Shadow and Wrath Of Poseidon going into Zenith; Zenith renamed afterwards; the ban, described this time as permanent; difficulty transferring ownership; and joint leadership with a second person once the transfer went through.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|5 Nov 2018}} BuildCraftia had not been able to stay alive without him, she added, and had become nearly dead.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-after-confederation-2018-discord-private|5 Nov 2018, the guild afterwards}} It is a participant's account of her own alliance, written six weeks afterwards in the channels of the alliance she had been fighting; what it is worth is the agreement on the two figures blamed, the two guilds left behind and the two successors. On one point the two sides do not agree: the Federation understood on 19 September that BuildCraftia's leadership had passed to a particular member, and this account has its author taking ownership herself with a second person as co-leader. Whether those are the same person under two names went unresolved.

## What the capture log says about the rebuild

The three guilds named on the 18th were already at war with Federation members before the agreement was reported. [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]]'s heaviest day of the month was the 16th, two days earlier, with 114 captures off Federation guilds; [[kingdomphoenixes|Kingdom Phoenixes]] had begun on the 14th; [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] had taken territory on every day of the month, and up to the 18th never fewer than forty in a day.{{cite:territory-exchanges|daily captures by BuildCraftia, KingdomPhoenixes, Blacklisted and Kangronomicon, 1–25 Sep 2018, UTC}} The 18th shows no step change in any of them.{{cite:territory-exchanges|same series}} What it does show is a slackening after it: BuildCraftia's daily figure fell below forty four times in the following week, to a low of twenty-one on the 21st, having done so on no day before.{{cite:territory-exchanges|daily captures by BuildCraftia, 19–25 Sep 2018, UTC}}

How much of this fighting fell on ground open to anyone is not recoverable. The declaration in force was the one published on 8 September, and the text that came down from it is a revision made on the 11th, of a pool that was then altered twice in committee inside two days and again later without announcement, so it does not describe the map between 8 September and 12 October.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Viaire, 9/8/2018 1:46 AM}}{{cite:free-for-all-amendments-2018-2019-discord-private|the edit audit, 11 Sep 2018}} The counts here are raw: BuildCraftia made 130 captures in the three days from the 18th, Kingdom Phoenixes 73, [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] 39 and Kangronomicon [Fuq] 7.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by attacker, 18–20 Sep 2018 UTC, raw — no declaration in force for the window can be applied}} What the declarations can and cannot say is at [[federation-free-for-all-territories|the Federation's free-for-all territories]].

The agreement therefore did not start a war; it reported guilds already prosecuting one. In those three days BuildCraftia took 90 of its 130 territories off two guilds alone, Renegade and [[the-divine-swords|the Divine Swords]], while Kingdom Phoenixes spread 73 across twelve — one guild's campaign with others alongside it rather than a single operation.{{cite:territory-exchanges|BuildCraftia and KingdomPhoenixes captures by defender, 18–20 Sep 2018}}

## A guild that did not know which alliance it was in

In the early hours of 14 September 2018 a member asked the others whether the guild was still in [[the-federation|the Federation]]. About ten minutes later another answered that he did not think so, and that it was best to attack nothing until they could confirm it.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|14 Sep 2018, early hours}} Five hours later a third said flatly that they were not.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|14 Sep 2018, five hours later}}

Four days after that the Federation's leadership named the guild as joining the alliance opposite.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018}} The alliance's difficulty in saying who its members were has come down from the leadership's side; this is the same difficulty from the floor.

The attacking came first. Kingdom Phoenixes had taken no ground at all that month until that night, when it took ten territories between 06:04 and 07:42 UTC — six of them from [[fantasy|Fantasy]], which stayed a Federation member for another eight days, and the other four from [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]], [[odysseia|Odysseia]], Kingdom Foxes and a guild outside the alliance.{{cite:territory-exchanges|KingdomPhoenixes captures with defenders, 14 Sep 2018 UTC, raw — the declaration in force cannot be applied to the window}} The question about membership came at 10:07 and the counsel against attacking at 10:19, some two and a half hours after the last of them.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|14 Sep 2018, message times}} Nobody in the exchange mentions the seven.

The guild then took thirty-three territories on the 16th, forty-two on the 18th and thirty-one on the 20th.{{cite:territory-exchanges|KingdomPhoenixes captures by UTC day, September 2018, raw}}

## What the guilds did instead

Underneath all this, guilds were settling territory between themselves. On 18 September a member described an arrangement he had reached with two others: he would leave two named territories alone while they held them, and they would leave a third to him while he held it.{{cite:confederation-collapse-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018}} Bilateral, unwritten, and outside any alliance.

## History

### Formation
The Council formed on 15 Sep 2019, a week after [[Terra]] took the map from [[Luna]], by seven guilds: [[Kingdom Foxes]], [[DiamondDeities]], [[Titans Valor]], [[The Simple Ones]], [[Fantasy]], Phantom Hearts and Empire of Sindria.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|15 Sep 2019 entry}} Five had fought with Terra. Kingdom Foxes had co-founded Luna in February and did not leave it until 18 September, three days after the Council was founded, so the alliance spanned both sides of the war it followed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|14 Feb, 15 Sep and 18 Sep 2019 entries}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Course
Phantom Hearts left the Council around 1 October 2019{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}, and went on to join [[Artemis]] on 4 Nov. TheNoLifes joined on 29 Sep, BlueStoneGroup on 11 Oct and Vindicator on 15 Oct, bringing the Council to its peak of nine concurrent members.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Kingdom Foxes departed on 2 Nov, the day Terra formally fell.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2 Nov 2019 entry}}

### Collapse
The Council collapsed on 23 Nov 2019 after The Ascendancy bloc departed, two days after Titans Valor and DiamondDeities left.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The Ascendancy — created 27 Apr 2019{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} — never published a roster. A week later, on 1 Dec, DiamondDeities, Titans Valor and The Simple Ones regrouped as [[Horologium]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Council of Canyon Kingdoms}}

## Legacy
The Council was the first of the short-lived successor blocs that followed the [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|Alliance Wars of 2019]] — none of Terra's heirs held together for more than a few months, and the map stabilized only with [[Artemis]]'s rise from 30 Oct 2019. Its own direct successor, Horologium, lasted five weeks.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

DiamondDeities [DDT] existed for under two years but touched six chronicled alliances.

## History

### LE Flowers, and why it stopped (March–April 2018)

LE Flowers held ten territories around Llevigar on [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s map of 10 March 2018 and nine, in the same region, on the map of the 24th.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018}} On 22 March its leader told the alliance's leadership channel that he would be away for three weeks, that his co-leader had not been online for some time and that nobody was applying to the guild, and asked that the alliance's leader role be given to one of his members until he returned.{{cite:le-flowers-to-diamond-deities-2018-discord-private|22 Mar 2018}}

It stopped fighting before it stopped existing. Its last territory exchange either way falls on 19 March 2018, and it took and lost nothing in the twenty days that followed.{{cite:territory-exchanges|LE Flowers, last exchange 19 Mar 2018 UTC; none 20 Mar – 8 Apr 2018}} Only changes of ownership were logged, so what that shows is that nobody attacked its nine territories and it attacked nobody. On 4 April the alliance put it on a list of guilds to be expelled for not claiming their assigned land, and took it off again the same morning after the officer running the vote asked two guild leaders whether they would vote yes if he removed it.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4 Apr 2018}}

Two days later its leader gave the reason. The guild was trying to war, he said, but the members who warred could not kill the defending mobs; they would work on their builds over the weekend and try again within a day or two, and that was why it had been inactive.{{cite:le-flowers-to-diamond-deities-2018-discord-private|6 Apr 2018}}

### The re-founding (8 April 2018)

DiamondDeities was created on 8 April 2018 by the leadership of LE Flowers, who dissolved that guild the same day. It was not a rename. An officer told the alliance's general channel that morning that LE Flowers was inactive and that they meant to begin again from nothing, to draw in people who would play; that evening its leader told the leadership channel to expect nothing from LE Flowers ever again, named the new guild, said he was its leader, and told the alliance they would be back as soon as it was ready.{{cite:le-flowers-to-diamond-deities-2018-discord-private|8 Apr 2018, morning and evening}} The alliance twice proposed a merger instead, with [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] and then with [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]], and was refused both times on the ground that the new guild had already been created.{{cite:le-flowers-to-diamond-deities-2018-discord-private|8 Apr 2018, the merger proposals}}

The alliance's founder, listing its membership seven months afterwards, drew the same distinction: "37 guilds. 40 if you count guilds such as LEF and DDT to be entirely different ones."{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

The new guild was fighting inside five days and on the alliance's map inside a fortnight. It first took territory on 13 April 2018 and made nineteen captures in the rest of the month, fifteen of them of assigned ground under the free-for-all list of 24 March, almost all in the Detlas suburbs, holding what it took for a median of about eight and a half hours.{{cite:territory-exchanges|DiamondDeities captures 13–30 Apr 2018, FFA list of 24 Mar 2018 applied; median hold 522 minutes, UTC}} The Federation's allocation of 22 April gave it five territories in the Detlas area, the ground it had spent the previous nine days taking, and did not list LE Flowers at all.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|4/22/2018 2:34 PM}}

### Federation and Aesir (2018)

DiamondDeities served the Federation until the end,{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} having been accepted into the [[Aesir Pact]] on 18 Jul 2018;{{cite:thread-227373-p02|p2 #24, 18 Jul 2018}} the Aesir guilds were the Federation's last defenders on 10-11 Nov 2018, quitting after 14 hours of constant warring.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}}

### SOL and the wars of 2019

After the collapse, DiamondDeities appears to have joined [[SOL]], the war alliance born from the Federation's ashes; no roster of SOL was ever published.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Its peace with [[Kingdom Foxes]] — the Treaty of Rodoroc — took effect on 2 Mar 2019,{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} and in late 2018 it had made a deal to share Molten Heights with Fox.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} In March 2019 it held 15 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 3 Mar 2019}} That autumn it fought with [[Terra]] against [[Luna]] and joined the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]], leaving on 21 Nov 2019, two days before the alliance collapsed.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

The guild left the Federation on 10 November 2018 as part of the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]]'s joint withdrawal, and the pact then ran as an independent alliance for three and a half months.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|10 Nov 2018 – Jan 2019}} A DiamondDeities leader told the Aesir council on 25 December 2018 that the guild had also joined Olympus, an alliance whose members included the two guilds then taking Aesir's Canyon ground; it left Olympus on 5 January 2019.{{cite:aesir-canyon-conceded-december-2018-discord-private|25 Dec 2018}}{{cite:aesir-olympus-two-accounts-2019-discord-private|5 Jan 2019}} It was a DiamondDeities leader who gave the approval [[the-canyon-concession|the ceasefire of 31 December]] required, and asked afterwards what he had approved{{cite:aesir-canyon-conceded-december-2018-discord-private|31 Dec 2018, the approval}}, whose four Canyon claims the pact struck from its map on 18 January 2019{{cite:aesir-canyon-abandoned-january-2019-discord-private|18 Jan 2019}}, and who called the leadership election of 22 February 2019 and won it five votes to four.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|22–23 Feb 2019}}

### Horologium and the end (1 Dec 2019 - 8 Jan 2020)

On 1 Dec 2019 DiamondDeities co-founded [[Horologium]] with [[Titans Valor]] and [[The Simple Ones]]. On 8 Jan 2020 [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] disbanded the guild, taking Horologium down with it; most remaining members regrouped as Lux Nova the next day.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} A single-member guild under the name, with a creation date of 8 Apr 2018, still existed in September 2026;{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} how it relates to the 2020 disbandment is not known.

