**DogsAmongUs** [DAU] warred for eight months of 2018 and left the map under a different name. It appears in the capture log from 3 January to 6 August 2018, taking territory 1,155 times across 194 distinct pieces of ground and ending the run about where it started.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by DogsAmongUs across 194 distinct territories, 3 Jan – 6 Aug 2018 UTC}}

## From enemy to member

The guild is listed in the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] charter under WynnChairman, one of eleven member guilds.{{cite:gdoc-1kdasl6eq7y_zssy|War Syndicate charter, list of all allies}} When the [[coalition|Coalition]] rebuilt its Discord on 11 January 2018 and posted fourteen member guilds alongside fourteen enemies, DogsAmongUs was on the second list.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018}}

Five weeks later it was inside the alliance that replaced the Coalition. [[the-federation|The Federation]] admitted three guilds in three days while the fighting of its founding week was still running, and DogsAmongUs was the one that joined without ceremony, already helping with the attacks before its membership was settled.{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|17–20 Feb 2018}}

## Ragni

On 21 February 2018, five days into the alliance's existence, DogsAmongUs pressed the leadership to be assigned Ragni, a region it had left unallocated, arguing that the omission was a mistake given what the guild had contributed to the war.{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|21 Feb 2018}}

The capture log puts the guild in Ragni the same day, and shows it unable to stay there. Before that morning it had taken nothing in the region at all; at 00:12 it took Ragni from [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]], one of the guilds the alliance had broken two days earlier, then Ragni East Suburbs, Katoa Ranch and Emerald Trail from the same guild within twenty-one minutes. It lost Ragni to Eagle Talon at 03:29 and took it back four minutes later, took Ragni Main Entrance at 02:22 and lost it that evening, and closed the day taking the three Dernal Jungle territories from [[imperial|Imperial]] and Pigmen Ravines from [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]. It was its largest day of the founding week: 46 captures across 38 territories, 37 of them outside the fourteen the alliance declared free-for-all that same day.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures and losses, DogsAmongUs, 21 Feb 2018, with declared free-for-all territories marked}}{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|free-for-all list, 21 Feb 2018}}

It got what it asked for that evening. The Federation's founding allocation, announced to the alliance at 9:12 PM on 21 February 2018, assigned DogsAmongUs the Jungle and Ragni.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018 9:12 PM}} The guild had spent the day taking Ragni and failing to hold it, argued in the leadership channel that the omission was a mistake, and was allocated the region before the day was out.

It paid for the region in ground elsewhere. A draft of the map circulated on 20 February had left Ragni unassigned, in reserve for guilds that might join later; between that draft and the announcement DogsAmongUs gave up Little Wood and the Pigmen Ravines and received Ragni instead.{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|draft and announced maps compared, 20–21 Feb 2018}}

The request and the fighting were the same claim made in two places. It was also the first of its kind inside the alliance — a member arguing for ground on the strength of its war record before the membership itself was settled — and the argument outlasted the guild that started it, running through [[the-federation-june-crisis|the June crisis]] to [[the-federation-dies|the alliance's dissolution]] in November.

## The region it kept fighting for

DogsAmongUs went on warring in the Ragni area for the rest of its recorded life. Its captures ran 380 in February 2018, 137 in March, then almost nothing through April and May before 69 in June and 544 in July — its heaviest month by a wide margin.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by month, DogsAmongUs, Jan–Aug 2018}} The July fighting concentrated on the ground it had given up to get Ragni: Pigmen Ravines Entrance 49 times, South Pigmen Ravines 45, Pigmen Ravines 37 and Abandoned Farm 34.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by territory, DogsAmongUs, July 2018}} Having traded the Pigmen Ravines away in February for the region it had argued for, it spent its heaviest month of the war taking them back. Ragni itself it took 38 times between 21 February and 2 July 2018.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Ragni captures by DogsAmongUs, 21 Feb – 2 Jul 2018}}

## White Lotus

Under the new name it stopped mattering to the alliance. On 10 September 2018 [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s territory coordinator asked the leadership channel whether he should be assigning White Lotus any land at all, and said that he had not been.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|10 Sep 2018, assignments withheld}} He asked its representative whether a revival was expected within a fortnight or whether the guild should be left suspended.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|10 Sep 2018, suspension put to the guild}} Membership and territory had come apart: a guild could keep its seat, its roles and its place on the roster and be left off the map.

Eight days later the guild leaders voted on expelling it for prolonged inactivity.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the expulsion vote}} The argument that mattered was about the price of removing a guild rather than about this one. A leader said he was voting against removal purely to prevent the pattern in which the alliance kicked a guild and it then became active and attacked them; that had happened too many times, and he did not enjoy taking chances.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the argument against removal}} Another answered that it had happened with the others because those guilds had a fighting force beforehand, and this one had never had anybody beyond its leader.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the counter}} A middle course was proposed — expel it but place it under a truce, so its leader could return when he had time.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the truce proposal}} The guild's own representative asked what the point of expelling it would then be, and nobody answered him.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the unanswered question}}

The evidence for the inactivity was that people had not seen it. A member said he had not seen the guild in the channel or in the game since another guild joined the alliance, and allowed that he might have missed something.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the evidence}} Two members had opened the discussion by asking what the guild in question even was.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, who is this guild}} All of it is the Federation's account of a member it was removing, and the guild left nothing beyond that one question.

The vote carried, and the reason was given plainly a week afterwards. Asked in the general channel on 27 September why White Lotus had been kicked, and pressing again after a joke, a member was told that it had been inactive and had done nothing, that it was only taking up space, and that it had been dead weight.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|27 Sep 2018}}

The alliance was running a capture log throughout and did not consult it. Between 1 September 2018 and its last capture on 8 January 2019 the guild took territory 46 times and never held anything longer than an hour and three quarters.{{cite:territory-exchanges|White Lotus exchanges, 1 Sep 2018 – 8 Jan 2019 UTC: 46 captures, longest hold 105 minutes}} It took Rodoroc from [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]] at 17:17 UTC on 23 September and lost it at 17:31, and took Cinfras at 22:14 on the 25th and lost it by 23:42, both between the vote to remove it and the removal being remarked on.{{cite:territory-exchanges|White Lotus captures and losses with times, 23 and 25 Sep 2018 UTC}} One of the two was on the free-for-all list then in force, so the log does not show the alliance wrong — only that it decided from impressions when it had something better.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|9/8/2018}}

Then it came back. Through the second half of November it attacked ground held by the bloc that had succeeded the Federation, taking eight territories off [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] in the Light Realm on 28 November alone and losing all eight inside the hour.{{cite:territory-exchanges|White Lotus captures against DiamondDeities, 28 Nov 2018 UTC}} Members of that bloc recorded on 22 November that White Lotus had attacked the Molten Heights and lost, one of them supposing it wanted the Light Realm because it used to own it.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|22 Nov 2018}} On the 26th somebody called for help in the warriors' channel because it was trying to take their Light Realm assignment.{{cite:federation-inactive-members-2018-discord-private|26 Nov 2018}} The attack it lost moved no ground and so produced no capture; the Light Realm fighting is in the log at 00:01 UTC on 23 November and at 23:41 UTC on the 26th, and the messages are timed eight hours behind that, daylight saving having ended on the 4th, which puts the first at 16:01 on the 22nd and the second at 15:41 on the 26th — inside the days the members were writing about.{{cite:territory-exchanges|White Lotus captures, 22–27 Nov 2018 UTC}}

That is the outcome the dissenting leader had named in general terms nine weeks earlier. Nobody at the time connected the two.

The guild renamed to White Lotus in August 2018, one of three renames among the Federation's roster guilds.{{cite:territory-exchanges|first and last exchange under each name, either side: DogsAmongUs 3 Jan 2018 21:09 – 6 Aug 2018 20:28 UTC, White Lotus 3 Aug 2018 22:27 UTC – 8 Jan 2019 18:08 UTC; a name-appearance check, so no free-for-all subtraction applies}} The capture log dates the change to the first week of that month: DogsAmongUs last appears on 6 August 2018 and White Lotus first appears on 3 August, the two names overlapping for four days. Under the new name the guild made 221 captures before its last on 8 January 2019, 175 of them in August.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures, DogsAmongUs and White Lotus, Aug 2018 – Jan 2019}}

