## Guild and alliance career

He joined the guild Pirates of Wynn — otherwise unrecorded — in early January 2015, and returned from a hiatus in late May 2015 to join Holders of LE{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L13–16, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}. He rose to co-leader and took ownership of the guild on 16 December 2015{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile (member 2157): title chain with dates}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L312, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}, and held it until 31 January 2018, when he passed it to Thundderr with the post "Make me proud."{{cite:thread-217600|post #2, Drew1011, 31 Jan 2018}}

From 6 November 2015 he sat in the leader chat of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] as one of its seven founding guild leaders, and in the senior chat its members called the "Shadow Government"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178, L248–257, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}. He withdrew Holders of LE from the alliance on 9 March 2016, the departure that ended it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L454, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}}, and later wrote: "many people began naming me as its destroyer. Did I truly deserve that title? To this day I'm still not sure."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L457, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}

Holders of LE joined [[Valkyrie]] on 18 March 2016{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}}, left on 5 June 2016 to co-found the [[halcyon|Halcyon]] Alliance with Yamipanda's ToastedPandas{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}, and rejoined on 3 September 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L554, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}. His leadership of Valkyrie was taken rather than inherited: by his own account he drafted the messages by which the other guild leaders asked Yuno F Gasai to stand down in the autumn of 2016, Yuno withdrew [[Imperial]] and deleted the alliance thread, and Drew1011 reposted it with permission on 15 October 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L562–580, composed 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1 (OP); thread opened 15 Oct 2016}}. He held "Leader of the Valkyrie Alliance" from that day until 10 March 2018{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile (member 2157): title chain with dates}}. In [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] he was "King of the Foxes" from the guild's revival as Foxton Legacy [Eon] on 24 November 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L602–604, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}, then stepped down on 7 February 2017 when [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] resumed the throne, becoming "Viceroy of the Foxes"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L652, composed 15 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile (member 2157): title chain with dates}}.

## The Emperium and the one-day title

Drew1011 was the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]'s **Shadow Advisor**, the post the alliance's thread defines as "the co-leader of the alliance"{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya, 5 Sep 2017, quoting the opening post}}. He won it in a poll run by Emperator [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] on 31 August 2017, taking 19 votes to 5, 4 and 4 for Angry_will, Shy_Phoenix and Whimsicality, after Paladin A'renos left the post{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L797–798 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, and the thread's opening post names him as Shadow Advisor from 5 September 2017 onward{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya, 5 Sep 2017, quoting the opening post}}{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}.

![The Emperium of Wynn's Shadow Advisor poll of 31 August 2017, run by Nitrogen2Oxygen: Drew1011 19 votes, Angry_will 5, Shy_Phoenix 4, Whimsicality 4. Screenshot from Drew1011's own account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/38-image.webp)

His profile also records "Emperator of the Emperium of Wynn (15 October 2017 — 16 October 2017)", and the one-day reign is unexplained{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile (member 2157): title chain with dates}}. Three sources bear on it and no two agree. The profile claims the title; Drew1011's own narrative says he **ran for Emperator and lost**, 30 votes to 31, to Nitrogen2Oxygen, and never claims to have held the office{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L788–794, composed 26 Feb 2018}}; and the alliance's thread names Nitrogen2Oxygen as Emperator on 5 September 2017 and Angry_will as Emperator in the opening post as it was last edited on 17 October 2017, with Drew1011 as Shadow Advisor in both{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya, 5 Sep 2017}}{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}. No Emperator election was ever recorded on the forums. A succession between one Emperator's exit and another's installation, falling to the co-leader, would fit every date, but whether it happened is not known.

## The Coalition and the Federation

Drew1011 co-founded the [[Coalition]] with [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and KingdomPhoenixes in October 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2017 entries}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L865–870, composed 4 Mar 2018}}. When the Federation formed in February 2018 from the Coalition's fracture and merger with the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] remnant, he founded and led it (his profile: "Founder of the Federation", 16 Feb - 10 Nov 2018){{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile (member 2157): title chain with dates}} — though not without a rival claim: [[slayne|Slayne]] asserted a causal founder's role via [[alliance-alliance|Alliance Alliance]]'s creation{{cite:thread-237070-p03|p3 #45, 14 Nov 2018}}. Asked publicly in November 2018 how he had made three alliances in a year, he corrected the count to two{{cite:thread-236914|post #19, Drew1011, 10 Nov 2018}}.

Three days after [[the-federation-dies|the Federation's collapse]] on 10 November 2018, he posted the "Federation Tribute" - a full roster of its member guilds and the alliance's epitaph: "What killed Federation was... internal affairs."{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

He also maintained on Discord "a massive ongoing written history of the guild community from May 2015 onwards"{{cite:thread-251543|post #6, 27 Jun 2019}}. That history, or a large part of it, survives as a serialised account posted between 22 February 2018 and 1 February 2021, covering January 2015 to June 2018 and beginning in May 2015 exactly as described{{cite:drew1011-storytime|composed 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}}. For the 2015-2016 chapters he worked from the [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] forum thread, which he had asked Paladin A'renos to have restored: "many of the dates and minor events during the Ordo parts of this story would have been educated guesses without it."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L695, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} He is a participant in nearly everything the document narrates and set out his own standard for it — "I strive to tell a factually accurate story… If you ask others who were here, they might give a completely different perspective."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L393–397, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} It is the single largest source for the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]].

Asked in July 2018 whether he wrote from a draft, he answered that he wrote from memory, fixed his dates against his guild's own timeline document and went back through old logs, and that anything finer than that was memory.{{cite:storytime-as-a-source-discord-private|method, 12 Jul 2018}} That timeline was maintained by somebody else and revised after the fact: in August 2018 he noticed that the Federation had first been entered on it as the Second Coalition, and that its maintainer had since changed the entry.{{cite:storytime-as-a-source-discord-private|22 Aug 2018}} The account is examined at [[guild-histories|Guild Histories]].

![The portrait Drew1011 used as his own chapter header in the account, matching the Discord avatar visible in its other screenshots.](/images/chronicles/storytime/60-image0.webp)

## Doctrine

Before he stepped down, Drew1011 began a document applying Robert Greene's *48 Laws of Power* to Wynncraft guild politics, written to train [[goden|Goden]] as his successor. He abandoned it after ten laws.{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|"The 48 Laws and how they have been applied on Wynn"}} It is an interested party's account of his own conduct throughout, and it is candid.

Two of the laws describe what he did rather than what he believed. Under "Never outshine the master" he explains the arrangement his farewell address also describes: he ran foreign affairs while giving up internal ones, on the reasoning that the Queen "loves attention and authority, do not take too much away from her or she will grow jealous and want to replace you."{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 1}} Under "So much depends on reputation, guard it with your life" he casts the quarrel with Tntdestroyd as a contest of standing rather than of force: "My struggle against Tnt was a war of reputation. I always prevailed because I was better at protecting mine than he was. If he had been better at guarding his reputation, he might have actually been able to overcome my own and steal the top Federation guilds like he wanted."{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 5}} He also mentions a spy inside the guild's Royal Dragoons, identified through Tntdestroyd's own handling of spies.{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 2}}

The rest is method. He treats unpredictability as an asset — "Did anyone expect me to ally with War Syndicate when AA left?"{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 3}} — says he stayed out of debates in the Federation leader chat by policy{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 4}}, and, under "Get others to do the work for you, but always take the credit", asks: "Notice how I never even warred for Federation or did more than talk to the leaders but I was still seen by everyone as the mastermind behind it?"{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 7}} The one law he says he could not keep is the tenth, on avoiding the unhappy and the unlucky, which he wrote had backfired on him repeatedly.{{cite:gdoc-1wtvbezh8o7ikiba|Law 10}}

The Emperator contest he lost is now dated to the day: A’renos opened it on 2 August 2017 for three days of voting, and the reaction counts under the announcement read 30 for him against 31 for Nitrogen2Oxygen.{{cite:emperium-announcements|marker 12, screenshot of the #voting channel, 2 Aug 2017}} He was elected Shadow Advisor four weeks later and still held the post when the alliance fell.{{cite:emperium-info|9/21/2017}}

## The Phoenix viceroyalty

He held office in a second guild at the same time. On 2 November 2017 [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] took him into [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] on an alternate account and made him Viceroy of the Phoenixes in place of Alhecks{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|Kingdom of Phoenixes dated event log}}. Three of the guild’s officers moved against the appointment and were gone within two days, and the Phoenix crown passed to [[thundderr|Thundderr]] three weeks later{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|"The History of the Kingdom of Phoenixes", monarch and viceroy table}}. He was crowned King Consort on 9 February 2018, a fortnight before the [[the-federation|Federation]] formed.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|"The History of the Kingdom of Phoenixes", monarch and viceroy table}}

## The farewell address

Drew1011 gave up the viceroyalty on 7 February 2019, two years to the day after LoveLusting resumed the throne, and marked it with a written address to the guild.{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}} It is his own account of his motive throughout, and the motive he gives is not a noble one: after the first revival council gave up on the guild, "the only thing I desired was to prove the former council wrong", and he repeats the pattern at each later crisis.{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}} He gives spring 2017 as the height of the revival, when "we would see upwards of 13 people online during the weekends" — a figure he offers as high for a period when, by his account, no guild in the community was truly active.{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}}

He dates his own turn to warring to the departure of "almost the entire gentry" that founded [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], and says he quit other games to make time for it.{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}} On the December 2017 war he wrote: "We built up Coalition for two months, and on December 21st, 2017, we launched our attack. Coalition took the initiative, and we swept Gavel with a fury that the server had never before seen. By Christmas Day, the war was won."{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}}

The address also records what the office cost him. To keep control of external affairs once LoveLusting became active again, he gave up his influence inside the guild and stopped leading its Parliament; the result, he wrote, was that "I became so consumed with Federation and Coalition, with enemies and allies, with wars and politics, that I lost all connection to the guild itself", and that many active members had never spoken to him.{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}} He handed the office to [[goden|Goden]] and signed himself, for the last time, "His Excellency, / Drew Holderson / Viceroy of the Foxes"{{cite:gdoc-16kljroe67z_p80r|"Drew's Farewell Address", 7 Feb 2019}}

{{map:2018-01-07|The earliest weeks of the recorded territory map, days after the era's close}}

The early guild era is the least documented period of Wynncraft guild warfare: the continuous territory-exchange log begins only on 3 January 2018, no exchange-level war data was ever published for the years before it{{cite:territory-exchanges|earliest row in the table, 3 Jan 2018 20:22:23 UTC — HackForums taking Molten Heights Portal from Magic Funhouse; nothing precedes it}}, and the era is documented mainly by forum threads, a community-maintained timeline{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Wynncraft guild history timeline, community document}}, a first-person memoir written between 2018 and 2021 by [[drew1011|Drew1011]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|composed 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}}, and two captures of the guild leaderboard{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 16 Apr 2018}}.

## The first guilds (December 2014 – 2015)

Guilds and guild wars arrived together in [[the-guild-update|the Guild Update]] — version 1.13, the "Wynnter Update" of 22 December 2014{{cite:https://wynncraft.fandom.com/wiki/Version_1.13|Version 1.13 — Wynncraft Wiki}}. The first foundings came that same week: Holders Of LE [HoL] by PillowPet and Nethers Ascent [TNA] by Francis12qwasyx on 21 December, Kingdom Foxes [Fox] registered in-game by [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] on 22 December, Kangronomicon [Fuq] on 23 December, and [[HackForums]] [Hax] by [[thedarksoul|TheDarkSoul]] on 24 December.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2014 entries}} Kingdom Foxes had existed as "the first 'guild'" since 2 June 2014, six months before the mechanic{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jun 2014 entry}}. Holders of LE described itself as "Founded upon the advent of the official release of guilds"{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}, and PillowPet was still a chief of it in 2018{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}. [[Imperial]] followed on 14 January 2015 under darkbio99 and KnightOfValor [KnV] on 16 January under Nozomi.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jan 2015 entries}}

The first alliance was **Legio Praetoria**, founded in early March 2015 by KnightOfValor, Imperial, Nethers Ascent and Kangronomicon; Imperial and KnightOfValor left it on 5 June 2015, and the alliance collapsed a month later "due to internal strife".{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2015 entries}} Contemporaries gave the same diagnosis in 2016 — "Legio fell because of internal affairs"{{cite:thread-133666|post #15, 28 Jun 2016}} — and Drew1011 treated the split as the origin of [[Valkyrie]]: "much like Imp leaving Legio to create Valkyrie with Fox".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L499 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

By mid-2015 two guilds held the map between them. "Kangronomicon [Fuq] and Nether's Ascent [TNA] were essentially the Hax of mid 2015," Drew1011 wrote{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L32, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}, and a June 2016 forum post named "the ancient guilds of 'The Nether's Ascent' and 'Kangronomicon'"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}. Kangronomicon, led by Spham and then by Dar_Krusos, ran a system of subguilds. Holders of LE became one in August 2015 and, during a period when "a major war glitch" prevented Kangronomicon itself from attacking{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, took and held about fifty territories on its behalf.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L34–41, L100–101, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}

Within six months of the Guild Update the era's most durable institution appeared: [[Valkyrie]], founded on 2 June 2015 by Kingdom of Foxes and [[Imperial]] "not established for the purpose of war" and governed by an Electorate of guild masters{{cite:thread-89529|post #1}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jun 2015 entry}}. It outlived every war alliance around it, lasting into 2022{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. It also set the constitutional template the period reused: internal affairs left to each guild, foreign policy pooled in a unanimous council of guild masters{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, 15 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1}}.

!['Visualized History of the Kingdom Foxes', an infographic timeline running January 2014 to December 2015: nine government sessions and their leaders plotted against the guild's founding, the merger and detachment of Nether's Ascension, the Wynnter War, the founding of Imperial in January 2015 and the incorporation of Valkyrie. Posted by LoveLusting in the Kingdom of Foxes thread.](/images/chronicles/media/early-guild-era-c45cf1a5.webp){{cite:thread-89227|post #1, timeline graphic}}

## Concordia and Ordo Malleus (autumn 2015 – March 2016)

The first bloc assembled against the Kangronomicon–Nether's Ascent duopoly was **Concordia**, founded by the guild Validus under Ezura, with a chief named tangler as its recruiter. It grew through the autumn of 2015 by absorbing guilds that resented the duopoly, destroyed "the remnants of Legio", and peaked in October 2015.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L119–147, composed 22 Feb 2018}} The Concordia Wars began in late 2015.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Contemporary opponents accused the Validus leadership of hostile conduct in game and on the forums; Drew1011, who was among the accusers, later wrote that he had campaigned to persuade another guild's leader that Ezura "was a bad person", and that he considered Ezura's conduct to have cost Validus allies.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L138–143, L194, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}} Nothing else about Ezura was recorded.

![A territory map dated to late September or early October 2015, showing Concordia at its peak: Validus and Travellers hold most of the province, Holders of LE are reduced to a Detlas pocket, Nether's Ascent keeps its eastern block, and Kangronomicon appears nowhere on the map. From Drew1011's account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/06-image.webp)

The counter-bloc was [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], the Order of the Hammer, created on 6 November 2015 by seven guilds — Kangronomicon, Holders of LE, Ha Ha United, End of Everything, HackForums, ToastedPandas and Sinners — and, in Drew1011's words, "created for the sole purpose of defeating Concordia".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–179, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "-= Ordo Malleus =-", Paladin A'renos, Nov 6, 2015}} It won by assigning each member guild a block of territories to hold, and Concordia was effectively finished within days: on 8 November 2015 the leader of Historical [UEZ], 3zPz, posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded", which Ezura contested in the thread itself.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "Concordia Disbanded", 3zPz, Nov 8, 2015, 27 replies, locked}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L197–204, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}} By February 2016 Ordo Malleus counted twelve guilds, bound by a single rule — "Don't attack the territories that ally guilds own" — and coordinating over Skype{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}. It fell "from the inside because of guilds fighting"{{cite:thread-143392|post #10, 9 Aug 2016}} on 9 March 2016 — 11 March by the community timeline, which traces the collapse to "a chain of leaves started by Holders Of LE [HoL] approximately 2 days before"{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}} — with Holders of LE withdrawing on 9 March{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L454, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}.

### Vesta

The last alliance of the period was **Vesta**, built by 3zPz out of what remained of Concordia. It counted fourteen member guilds — Historical [UEZ], Validus [Val], Travellers [TVL], TheNoLifes [TNL], Super Crafters [SPC], Wynn Try Hards [WTH], Da Classy Goats [CLG], NightStriders [CGO], BOOM [BOO], Frosted Pants [FPS], Omegamine [OMM], Silver of Anarchy [SOA], IceBlue Team [IBT] and Artifact [UPZ] — and was larger than Ordo Malleus at the time, but, in Drew1011's words, "Aside from a few small skirmishes, Vesta barely even existed." It was declared dead one month after its creation, on 10 January 2016.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L289–311, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} A Holders of LE member recalled that the guild "we were at war with Vesta" before Gavel was released.{{cite:thread-217600|post #17, PikaLegend}}

Both the community timeline and Drew1011 date Vesta's creation to **December 2016**{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L289, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}, a year late: 3zPz opened the Vesta alliance thread on 10 December 2015{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "-*-vesta Alliance-*-", 3zPz, Dec 10, 2015}}, and Drew1011's own chronology agrees — an alliance built from the remnants of a bloc that died in November 2015, dead by January 2016, with Gavel's release following.

Gavel's release closed the period with a territory lock. Drew1011 dates the release to 21 December 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L315–325, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, the community timeline to 14 December{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}. The whole map was frozen for roughly two weeks afterwards, so that guilds holding good territory when it landed kept it; ToastedPandas, which had captured the entire jungle days earlier, rose to guild level 51 during the freeze.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L315–325, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

The release of the Gavel province on 21 December 2015 shaped what followed. Every territory was locked against attack for a fortnight, which froze ownership at the moment of release and handed a lasting advantage to whichever guild happened to hold the best ground when the lock came down.{{cite:ordo-malleus-and-the-first-alliances-discord-private|Gavel release, 21 Dec 2015}}{{cite:territory-economy-and-warfare-discord-private|Gavel release, December 2015}}

[[the-rank-and-file|A second history of the period]], written in April 2018 by a member of [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]], gives the same date of 21 December{{cite:holders-of-le-storytime-2018-discord-private|the Gavel release}} — a second telling that agrees rather than a check on the first, its author having read the older account before he wrote his own.{{cite:holders-of-le-storytime-2018-discord-private|2 and 7 Apr 2018, the comparison with the other narrator}} He described the guild system failing around the release, with guild wars not working for the first week and the guild chat broken with them{{cite:holders-of-le-storytime-2018-discord-private|the week after the release}}, and listed faults he said had predated the update and been made worse by it: players not teleported into wars they had started, war mobs failing to spawn, and whole servers stalling when a territory was defended.{{cite:holders-of-le-storytime-2018-discord-private|the faults he described}} His judgement was that the update brought the wider player community back and killed the guild community with it.{{cite:holders-of-le-storytime-2018-discord-private|his judgement on the update}}

## The alliance scatter (2016)

What followed Ordo's collapse was not another war bloc but a scatter of small community alliances, formed while one guild held most of the map and open warring paid poorly. The **Astrafteri Affinity** is the exception that mattered: founded around January 2016, apparently by coralialia, a former Holders of LE officer{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L352–358, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}, it appears from 11 February 2016, when HackForums' recruitment thread listed "Astrafterí-affinity" as its alliance{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}, and it only acquired a forum thread of its own on 3 April 2016, posted by LordMuttonChops rather than by coralialia{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "✯ Astrafterí Affinity ✯", LordMuttonChops, Apr 3, 2016}}. The rest were social: [[halcyon|Halcyon]] (June 2016) paired ToastedPandas and Holders of LE in an "agreement for whenever help is needed"{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; [[seraphim|Seraphim]] (August 2016) declared itself "100% community based" with "no intention of actively providing support for guild wars"{{cite:thread-143392|post #1}}; [[lux-imperius|Lux Imperius]] (September 2016) was invite-only and refused applicants to stay small{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016}}; and [[aurelion|Aurelion]] (February 2017) gathered House of Sentinels, Hippies of Snuggles, The Dark Phoenix and Dragons Arise{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}}. Membership overlapped freely — Seraphim's rules expressly allowed guilds to belong to several at once{{cite:thread-143392|post #1}} — and Holders of LE was in three of them within five months.

## The HackForums dominance

By 2016 the map belonged to [[HackForums]]. In June 2016 an anti-Hax alliance thread put the guild at 94 territories{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; by September 2016 Hax held 146 of roughly 332 territories, ahead of [[Libertas]] with 60 and UltimateXeons with 53{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}. Hax was not acting alone. A June 2016 thread described a "rule of two" with Libertas — "The two guilds crushed all opposition and still rule with an iron fist"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} — and a member of UltimateXeons named his own guild as a third party: "our alliance with Hax and Lir (we are UXs)"{{cite:thread-133666|post #13, 27 Jun 2016}}. "Hax has not been a one man army in ages," a poster objected in August 2016. "They work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories."{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, 9 Aug 2016}} With Libertas' 60 and Blacklisted's 22 beside Hax's 146, the bloc held 228 of the map's 332 territories in September 2016{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}, and Blacklisted's own thread stated the arrangement plainly: "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}}

The bloc was never named at the time. A contemporary called it "a mutual land agreement" rather than an alliance{{cite:thread-133666|post #16, 28 Jun 2016}}; a Libertas member who asked his guild owner for "the name of our alliance" in August 2016 got no reply{{cite:thread-119596-p08|post #152, 9 Aug 2016}}; and no Alliance-prefixed thread was ever opened for it{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}. The name "Hax & Co" was coined only in retrospect: Drew1011 used it in a chapter written on 30 August 2018{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1086, L1097, composed 30 Aug 2018}}, and its earliest public use is a July 2019 post listing "Federation, Hax & Co, Coalition" among Wynn's mega-alliances{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}}.

Resentment was public and futile, and in June 2016 it produced two named alliances in three weeks. The Banhammer, opened by Mr_Robin_Hood on 8 June, argued that Hax "are too strong for a single guild to fight / and the only way for us to be able to beat them / is if all of the guilds unite!" and listed World of Crafters [WoC], The Wynn Guard [TwG] and MythicZodiac [MZS]{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; a Hax-side poster replied that "I will not stop till every inch of wynncraft is mine or my allies"{{cite:thread-130386|post #5, 8 Jun 2016}}. The Separatists, founded by Tapu_Fini on 26 June around the guild The Anarchy under supermariowifi, took open enrolment — "You could pledge your guild to The Separatists, and you way withdraw that allegiance whenever you feel the need"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}. "Right now there is 2 anti hax alliances," a Hax chief noted at the end of the month{{cite:thread-134638|post #13, 30 Jun 2016}}; both failed, as an UltimateXeons member had already predicted from the earlier attempts — "It didn't work, all those guilds no longer have any territory."{{cite:thread-133666|post #10, 27 Jun 2016}}

In March 2017 a thread demanding that "Haxforums Should Be Limited On Territory Influence" charged that Hax held "100+ territories" by "taking advantage of the broken guild system"{{cite:thread-179383|post #1, 1 Mar 2017}} and "cheat the game with there control"{{cite:thread-179383|post #5, 1 Mar 2017}}; the thread's respondents, including Drew1011, uniformly rejected the idea of a cap — "Their success should not be limited just because other people are upset"{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} — and one asked pointedly "are Lir, BLA, UXs somehow exempt?"{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}}. Drew1011's diagnosis was that Hax's position was an artefact of the era rather than of strength: "The reason that Hax is able to hold so much is because, to put it simply, nobody is trying to challenge them."{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} By May 2017 a forum thread title was asking why Hax had "MORE THAN 300 TERRITORIES"{{cite:thread-189768|post #1, thread title, Hide007, 22 May 2017}}, and a 2020 recollection put the peak "closer to 350", "when they owned the whole map"{{cite:thread-265297|post #18, 4 Apr 2020}}.

Members of the [[coalition|Coalition]] put it higher still while the guild was being destroyed. On 17 February 2018 they had Hax holding every territory in every province, one of them placing that before the Corkus province was added to the game.{{cite:undated-observations-verified-discord-private|17 Feb 2018}} No year was attached to the claim.

## 2017: Emperium, War Syndicate and the Coalition

The [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]], founded on 21 April 2017 under Emperator [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], was the era's most elaborate institution: twelve member guilds with named leaders, a High Council of guild representatives, portfolio leaders for war, community and economy, judges whose word could not be over-ruled, and an oath for incoming members{{cite:thread-188024|post #1}}. It fell on 17 October 2017, with Angry_will as its last Emperator{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}, the day after [[drew1011|Drew1011]] held the title of Emperator for a single day{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's forum profile title chain, 2016–2019}}; the sequence was never explained.

[[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] was created on 17 July 2017{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}; its roster and leadership were never published, and it had no thread of its own{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}. In October 2017 Kingdom Foxes, KingdomPhoenixes, Gilded Sparrows and House of Sentinels founded the [[Coalition]]{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2017 entries}}. It took control of the Wynn province on 23 November 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Nov 2017 entry}} and ended War Syndicate that December — "They wiped ws off the map on Christmas day", a veteran recalled in 2020{{cite:thread-265297-p02|post #34, 14 Apr 2020}}, while another insisted the two blocs instead merged{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}} — entering 2018 with full map dominance.

## The state of the record

Nothing like a war log exists for these years. Archived 2015-era guild pages on wynncraft.com carry no territory counts, and 2016–2017 war events survive only as forum-thread imagery and written accounts. The two leaderboard captures — September 2016 and April 2018 — bracket the era{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 16 Apr 2018}}; everything between them is narrative. How HackForums fell from roughly 350 territories to the 111 it held in February 2018 is recorded in no contemporaneous source: no thread names the attackers, the dates or the sequence. The end itself, however, is dated. A 2020 participant called the fall of Hax "probably the biggest event that happened in 2017"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}}, but a contemporaneous thread of 22 February 2018 records that "HaxForums has lost all its territories" and that the largest guild on the map then held only 43{{cite:thread-219744|post #1, 22 Feb 2018}} — placing the fall about two months later than the recollection, in the week after [[the-federation|the Federation]] was founded. The era closed in mid-February 2018, when five guilds split from the Coalition over map disputes and opened the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]], beginning the [[federation-era|Federation era]]{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}.

The single largest addition to the record for these years is a memoir rather than an archive: a serialised chat history posted by Drew1011 between February 2018 and February 2021, covering January 2015 to June 2018, written by a participant in most of what it describes.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|composed 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}} He set out his own standard for it — "I strive to tell a factually accurate story, with no lies or complete falsities. Along with this factually accurate story, I interweave my own perspective and opinions… If you ask others who were here, they might give a completely different perspective"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L393–397, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} — and his own limits, writing of the rise of HackForums that "even my timelines and knowledge of guild history has its limits, and I know no exact dates for any of this."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L518, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} Where his dates for late 2015 and early 2016 can be checked against the forum-thread census, several of them are correct to the day; his 2017 and 2018 dates are from memory, and he says so.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L695, L1153}}

One stretch of the period was written down by the people in it as it happened. Between 3 December 2016 and March 2017 [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] governed itself in a Discord server of roughly eighty thousand messages across eight channels — a private leaders' room of about thirteen and a half thousand, a Parliament room opened in February 2017, and an announcements channel of forty-two posts that was the guild's own formal record.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|the server, December 2016 – March 2017}} The server stopped in March 2017 because the guild built itself a new one and cleared the first out on the 21st, and for no other reason.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|8–21 Mar 2017}}

Eden's own recruitment thread describes it as having 'a deep history, both in guild politics and community relations' and states an aim 'to be a strong, independent force in Wynncraft politics'.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}} In the winter of 2020-21 it was one of the guilds that broke [[Artemis]]'s hold on the map,{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} and in May 2021 it was a founding member of [[Khaos]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Government

Eden governs itself as an 'Empire' with an unusually formal constitution for a Wynncraft guild, set out in its recruitment thread. Three institutions sit under the Emperor, the guild's leader, whose principal power is a veto: the Agora, of which every member is part and where non-binding votes are taken; the Legion, the guild's military, open to any member who applies for an army rank; and the Senate, which votes on decisions affecting the whole guild. Senate ranks run Consul (two, one permanent and one elected monthly, handling foreign relations), Dux (senior officers below the Consuls), and Senate; below them come Legate, Legionnaire and Citizen. An Emperor can only be replaced when the incumbent steps down and hands over.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

In 2020-21 [[yugito|Yugito]] led Eden - he opened the guild's forum thread on 1 January 2020 and answered on it throughout that year - with Lev98bug, Asthae and Rothboy among its chiefs and senators. By the time the thread was last revised, in January 2025, the Senate had turned over completely: it listed FadeDave as Emperor, Asthae as a Consul and Yugito as one of six Duxes, in a body of fourteen.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

## History

### Against Artemis (2020-21)

In March 2020 Asthae, an Eden chief, posted as an involved party in the thread attacking the Artemis alliance, replying to a critic that 'clearly I am the chief who messaged you'.{{cite:thread-263975|post #15, 9 Mar 2020}} Nine months later Eden was on the other side of the map from Artemis. The 'Guild Moderators' thread of 18 December 2020 - the flashpoint of the Dec 2020 moderation crisis - names Eden among the then-unnamed anti-Artemis coalition,{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} and Asthae posted in support of it within three minutes of publication.{{cite:thread-279337|post #2, 18 Dec 2020}}

That coalition acquired a name the following month: on 19 January 2021 Eden's chief Lev98bug wrote to [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]], 'Eden is in Goose if you could add that.'{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #72, 19 Jan 2021}} Eden's standing inside [[Goose]] was substantial. In February 2021, arguing about the 1.20 war rework, Rothboy and Lev98bug spoke for the Goose side against a critic,{{cite:thread-286375|posts #8, #9, #13 and #16, 20 Feb 2021}} and a third poster cited 'EDN who had to literally try crawl through ERN terrs' as an example of what warring against fortified [[Emorians]] territory cost.{{cite:thread-286375|post #10, 20 Feb 2021}} When [[drasalia|Drasalia]] of ChinaNumberOne drew the Goose alliance in April 2021, Eden led the second thread: 'Eden, the big bois who own a whole lotta territory. Really cool guys but I get a military vibe from them since I see them helping out other guilds during wars a lot.'{{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}}

### Khaos (2021-22)

At [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, Eden was one of the nine guilds that founded [[Khaos]] rather than [[Valhalla]], alongside [[Aequitas]], Wheres The Finish, Nerfuria, Tartarus Wrath, Ultra Violet, Fuzzy Spiders, ChinaNumberOne and Cyphrus Code. It fought the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war against the ex-Valhalla guilds]] that peaked in January 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Khaos was defunct by 26 June 2022; Eden does not appear in [[Cucumber Company]]'s roster of that date,{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} and no later alliance membership is recorded for it.

### The coup

At some point before April 2023, Eden was overthrown from within. The only account is by xK6TA, a former member describing his own past in an April 2023 guild application to [[Titans Valor]]: 'I was a part of Eden when it was #1 and slightly after it got couped.' The application repeats the claim once - 'Eden when it was #1, it got couped when I was a player lol'.{{cite:thread-206094-p97|p97 #1922, 16 Apr 2023}}

The coup's actors and date were never recorded, and what '#1' meant is not known: Eden never won a [[guild-seasons|guild season]],{{cite:wynncraft-wiki-gg-wiki-guild-seasons|season winners table}} and no other ranking of the period placed Eden first. The guild survived the coup: its recruitment thread was still being maintained in 2025, with a full Senate and an Emperor who was not Yugito.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

## Alliances

- [[Goose]] - by 18 Dec 2020 - 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}
- [[Khaos]] - 11 May 2021 - defunct by 26 Jun 2022 (founding member)

ElegantDeath stood in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]'s Emperator election of 2017 under a different handle. When [[arenos|Paladin A'renos]] announced he no longer had time to run the alliance, three candidates came forward — [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], ElegantDeath and [[drew1011|Drew1011]] — and he withdrew to act as Drew1011's campaign manager in exchange for the promise of the Community Leader post.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The vote ended 31–30 in Nitrogen2Oxygen's favour.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} It ran three days rather than the week that account gives it, closing on 4 August 2017.{{cite:emperium-announcements|8/4/2017, the close}}

In early October 2017 [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] handed [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] to him and briefly rejoined [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] before taking the guild back.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L853–863}} A message from the guild's parliament channel is signed "King ElegantDeath".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|KingdomPhoenixes parliament channel screenshot}}

His forum account was registered on 10 August 2016 and shows the guild Hall of Fame.{{cite:wynncraft-forum-profiles|ElegantDeath, member 69528}}

Emorians [ERN] was created on 17 Dec 2017{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} and was in the thick of alliance politics within weeks. Its recruitment thread records: "The Emorians started their journey on December 17th, 2017, under command of AzanderK and Hazeful, with Kanafarmari as second in command."{{cite:thread-248101|post #1, opened 21 Apr 2019, revised in place}} The guild's earlier thread, opened on 12 June 2018, carries the same founding claim and names AzanderK, KeyTheKhaos and OliviaLime at the head of a roster of about twenty-five, ranked by chess piece and annotated with award abbreviations.{{cite:thread-221386|post #1, AzanderK, 12 Jun 2018}}

## History

### Coalition to Federation (2017-2018)

Emorians joined the [[Coalition]] on 12 February 2018 and left it four days later. On 17 Feb 2018 it left with four other guilds to co-found [[Alliance Alliance]], fighting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]; when the war ended it was absorbed into [[the-federation|the Federation]], where it stayed until [[the-federation-dies|the collapse of 10 Nov 2018]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It also joined the [[Valkyrie]] community alliance on 23 May 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Drew1011's Federation tribute thanked OliviaLime — whose forum title read "Retired Lady of Emoria" — "for slapping the sense in to people when nobody else wanted to".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

The guild assisted the Coalition for about three days before belonging to it. On 10 February 2018 a member asked in the alliance's war channel who the Emorians were and was told they were not in the alliance; another noted that they had attacked no Coalition guild, only smaller ones, and wondered whether that was deliberate.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|Coalition war channel, 10 Feb 2018}} The admission was announced on the 12th, one member putting the guild's involvement at about three days and another saying he had not seen them the day before.{{cite:coalition-last-fortnight-discord-private|12 Feb 2018}}

Emorians was the last of the six guilds recorded leaving the [[coalition|Coalition]] on the evening of 16 February 2018.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

### Bankrupt to twenty-seven territories (2018)

Three days after leaving the Coalition the guild was broke. On 19 February 2018 members noted that its bank was empty, drained in the fighting, while it was still trying to take ground it could not hold and defending territories with about a hundred mobs apiece.{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|19 Feb 2018}}

Ten weeks later it was among the largest guilds on the map. It helped [[the-federation|the Federation]] retake Corkus from [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] on 11 and 12 April and was voted into the alliance immediately afterwards,{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|11–12 Apr 2018}} and the allocation published on 22 April gave it twenty-seven territories.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|4/22/2018}} On 16 May it held Llevigar — by its leader's own account the first territory the guild had ever been assigned — against BuildCraftia and [[hackforums|HackForums]] together.{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|16 May 2018}} The next day he told the other guild leaders that he had been thinking of standing down, or of disbanding the guild.{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|17 May 2018}}

### Losing its leadership (August 2018)

The guild lost most of the people who ran it inside an hour on 1 August 2018, in [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s leadership channel. At 09:38 one of its leaders posted a valedictory: he was leaving to found and run his own guild, and had already spoken to the alliance's founder about it.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the valedictory}} He intended to stay neutral for the time being, and if his guild warred at all it would be only on the free-for-all ground the Federation designated.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the neutrality}} He asked the other guild leaders to stand by Emorians through the transition, and signed the message as guild master of [[avicia|Avicia]].{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the signature}}

Fifty-six minutes later the guild's principal leader answered him in the same channel. He was resuming his place as its main leader; he had not been told the decision was being made and had not been consulted; his senior team had been told beforehand and had gone with the departing leader.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the reply}} The two of them remained friends and would stay so, he said, and he had a great deal to rebuild.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, what was left}} His guild would go on carrying its share of the alliance's warring, but he would probably stop reading the leadership channel closely and would not be able to help write the rules the alliance had been planning.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|1 Aug 2018, the withdrawal}} Both messages are courteous, and between them they describe a member guild hollowed out overnight.

Twelve days later the guild changed its representative in the leadership channel. On the morning of 13 August 2018 its leader asked the alliance's Discord managers to replace one member with another, giving as the reason an understanding reached with a party he named, and the map-maker made the change within three minutes.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|13 Aug 2018, the replacement}} What the understanding was went unrecorded.

The rest of the month went on defence. On 19 August 2018 the guild's leader was challenged over the alliance's arrangements for defending allied territory, and answered that the point was efficiency and streamlining between guilds.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|19 Aug 2018, the answer}} Asked on the spot, he could name only one guild that wanted its ground lightly defended, and only because that guild's representative kept raising it and shouting at other members.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|19 Aug 2018, the one guild}} His challenger asked whether remembering four guilds was really so hard.{{cite:emorians-august-2018-discord-private|19 Aug 2018, four guilds}} The audit of the noticeboard that prompted the exchange is at [[allied-defence|defending an ally's territory]].

### The map round of September 2018

On 25 September 2018 the guild's leader pressed [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s map-maker in the leadership channel: he had been told minutes earlier that a particular region was assumed to yield less experience and had chosen a different one for that reason, and he had been told the map-maker was vouching for his guild.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|25 Sep 2018, the complaint}} The map-maker answered that he was aware his own guild had been doing worse and that he had cut territories from it too.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|25 Sep 2018, the answer}} A member observed that there was a large difference between one of the alliance's leading guilds and one that had only just joined, inactivity in the former mattering much less.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|25 Sep 2018, leading guilds and new ones}}

The next morning the leader posted a public apology to the channel on his own behalf and the guild's, said that both of them had gone too far and took the blame for it.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|26 Sep 2018, the apology}} He announced that he would step back from the Federation to concentrate on Emorians, in the hope of settling the tension between his guild and some of the other leaders.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|26 Sep 2018, the withdrawal}} The map-maker resigned later the same day.{{cite:federation-mapmakers-2018-discord-private|26 Sep 2018}}

On the 27th the map-maker told the channel that he had given Emorians a named eastern region as a last chance to raise its war activity so that it might recover its position on the map.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|27 Sep 2018, the grant}} The guild's leader had then accused him of having lied about what the region was worth.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|27 Sep 2018, the accusation}} Both are his account, and the guild left no answer to either. It is the only occasion in the alliance's channels of territory being issued as a remedy rather than as a reward — see [[federation-territory-committee|the territory committee]].

A month later the same man, by then advising rather than drawing, told the leadership channel that map-makers approached each guild about to lose ground beforehand so that it would not call on its bloc for support.{{cite:federation-blocs-within-2018-discord-private|24 Oct 2018, pre-consultation}} The procedure had failed exactly once, he said — with Emorians, and after the vote rather than before it.{{cite:federation-blocs-within-2018-discord-private|24 Oct 2018, the one failure}} Going through the alliance's voting record, he added, Emorians was the only one of the four guilds in the grouping he was examining that ever voted against the other three.{{cite:federation-blocs-within-2018-discord-private|24 Oct 2018, the voting record}}

### The move to Audux (October–November 2018)

On 22 October 2018 a leader asked [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s leadership channel whether Emorians was relocating to another guild account, and the alliance's former map-maker answered that there were internal struggles within it and an absence of its actual leader.{{cite:federation-guild-swap-2018-discord-private|22 Oct 2018}} That is one Federation member's second-hand account of another guild's internal state, and it is the only reason recorded anywhere; the guild gave none of its own. The alliance agreed that the swap to the new account, Audux, would not need a vote.{{cite:federation-guild-swap-2018-discord-private|2 Nov 2018}}

The move was still unfinished on 2 November, and the alliance could not say what the new account was. Asked whether it was technically a member, a leader said that nothing would stop anyone wiping it and that anything outside the Federation was in reality an enemy; asked whether that made it one, he said the position was extremely complicated, because the old guild was still in use and the guild's official identity had not yet moved.{{cite:federation-guild-swap-2018-discord-private|2 Nov 2018}} The alliance dissolved eight days later.

### Luna and the revolt (2019)

Emorians was a founder of [[Luna]] on 14 Feb 2019.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} In March 2019 it was the map's second-largest holder at 61 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 3 Mar 2019}} On 29 Aug 2019, after a leadership dispute, Emorians and [[Avicia]] left Luna and declared war on [[Imperial]] — the revolt that spiralled into a large war over Gavel, out of which [[Terra]] formed and Luna ultimately fell.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

[[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]], writing from the opposing side on 14 September 2019 while the war was still running, stated that the Emorians left "supposedly frustrated with the actions of other prominent guilds", that in response "Luna seized all of its lands", and that this was "a large mistake", because "the Emorians became more sympathetic to our efforts against Luna".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} The seizure is recorded nowhere else.

GrandpaLee later led the guild as Lord of the Emorians, over a council styled "The Parly" — DerpyEmerald24, KittySenpai_, BurntPancakes, Splintered and IzzSt; when that leadership took over is not recorded.{{cite:thread-248101|post #1, opened 21 Apr 2019, revised in place}} DerpyEmerald24 later became Chief of Emorians and, in April 2020, compiled the community guild timeline.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, DerpyEmerald24}}

### The blocs of the 2020s

Emorians appears in the 18 Dec 2020 anti-[[Artemis]] coalition list that became [[Goose]],{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} staying until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, then joined [[Valhalla]] at its founding and followed it into [[Vanir]]. On 18 Dec 2021 it was one of the four guilds whose departure collapsed Vanir after twenty days.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It had also joined the community alliance [[Hestia]] by 6 Jun 2021,{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #140, 6 Jun 2021}} and was still a member when Hestia was last recorded in September 2022.

