An alliance of the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]], it was governed under a written constitution of offices, and its membership — twelve guilds at its August 2017 peak — turned over almost completely between May and October.

## History

The first alliance thread (Wynncraft forums thread 188024) was opened on 7 May 2017 by Paladin A'renos: "The Emperium of Wynn (TEoW) is a Dynamic alliance that was formed on the 21st of April with the goal of uniting guilds of all levels and experience to create a more user-friendly experience."{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}} Its stated order of business put community ahead of war — "As a fairly new alliance, our first goal is to get connected with our community. Events, giveaways, dungeon runs... After that, we plan on bringing in the war aspect of any alliance" — though the rules also provided for "aggressive extermination" of guilds found to be bullying members, and asked members to "refrain from taking lands from small guilds".{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}}

The May 2017 roster listed ten guilds — [[libertas|Libertas]], UltimateXeons, NeoPancakes, Sinners, The Mage Legacy, Wynn Theory, Boom, BuildCraftia, Shadow Kittens and LE Flowers — with Beasts and Jaguars pending, and only one filled leadership portfolio (War Leader DownDeeper).{{cite:thread-188024|post #4, Yuno F Gasai, 7 May 2017}} By the time the opening post was last revised in August 2017 the roster had turned over almost completely and every office was staffed; the War Leader by mid-June was TnTdestroyd, who was also named the alliance's member of the month for his warring.{{cite:thread-188024-p05|p5 #82, 16 Jun 2017, quoting the opening post}}

A second thread (202724) was opened on 4 September 2017 by Nitrogen2Oxygen, posting as "Cloud Man", after A'renos left the alliance.{{cite:thread-202724|post #2, Drew1011, 4 Sep 2017}} By 5 September 2017 the alliance had a ten-guild roster, Nitrogen2Oxygen as Emperator and Drew1011 already installed as Shadow Advisor;{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya quoting the opening post, 5 Sep 2017}} by 17 October 2017 it was much reduced.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

## Government

The alliance's constitution, "The Emperial Truth", set out five tiers and gave several of them Latin names borrowed from *Warhammer 40,000*. It opened with the same sentence as the forum thread — the alliance was formed on 21 April "with the goal of uniting guilds of all levels and experience to create a more user-friendly experience" — and closed the introduction with a motto: "We, together, will become Unitum Populo."{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", introduction}}

Tier one was the Triarch. A War Leader, styled Ordo Malleus, allocated territory and taught bank management and post-war defence buying{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1, War Leader}}; a Community Leader, styled Ordo Ministorum, ran events and policed members' conduct{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1, Community Leader}}; and an Economy Leader supplied members with builds and equipment and was cast as the tie-breaker "between the Community and War Leaders"{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1, Economy Leader}}. All three were elected monthly.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1}} Beside them sat the Shadow Advisor, who took no part in decisions but knew everything and could "in extreme emergency situations take control of the whole alliance"; the constitution added that "This Role is Fixed and cannot be changed."{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1, Shadow Advisor}} An optional merchant rank, the Tithe, was to buy equipment for members and sell it to them cheaply or give it away, and to raise the prizes for alliance events.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 1, The Tithe}}

Tier two was the bench of Judges, "THE BLIND JUDGEMENT", under a High Judicator{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 2, The High Judicator}}, with Exemplars handling relations with guilds outside the alliance and recruitment{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 2, Exemplars}} and Inquisitors enforcing the rules{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 2, Inquisitors}}. "All members of the alliance must listen to the judgment of the Judges, and follow what they put out, that includes all leadership, as well as the Emperator."{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 2}}

Tier three was the High Council, "THE LIFEBLOOD OF THE ALLIANCE": one to three representatives per guild, a maximum of forty-five in an alliance capped at fifteen guilds.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 3}} It chose the three leaders from among its own members{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 3, leader selection}}, needed sixty per cent to pass a decision to the Triarch and ninety to remove a leader{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 3, voting thresholds}}, and elected a Speaker to assign and track alliance tasks and report weekly{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 3, The Speaker}}. Leadership votes were held in public: "All votes for Leaders will be done on forum pages allowing everyone to vote for the leaders not just the alliance."{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 3, public votes}}

Beneath the council ran the two orders. Recruiters and community event planners sat under the Ordo Ministorum, the recruiters empowered to conclude non-aggression pacts with guilds outside the alliance.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Ordo Ministorum}} Captains and Land Consolidators sat under the Ordo Malleus, the consolidators assigning territories to guilds that needed them and designating land as free-for-all, off-limits or reserved for events.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Ordo Malleus and Land Consolidators}} Honorary Members, who held no office but sat in on decisions, could be appointed only by the Shadow Advisor, and asking for the rank disqualified the asker.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Tier 5}}

Six goals were listed. The first was "To be the Greatest Alliance Wynn has ever seen since Ordo Malleus, and bypass every other within the community in Community Culture and Territories"{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Our Goals, 1}}; the second, "To Exterminate Guild Hate within the community and condemn it wherever it is found, and peacefully get rid of it"{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Our Goals, 2}}; the last, to unite every guild and alliance under one banner{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Our Goals, 6}}. A Buddy System let member guilds take newer guilds as sub-guilds and lend them territory until they were fit to join, with UltimateXeons given as the example of what it could do.{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Buddy System}}

Donations were mandatory{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Rules}} and members and guilds alike ran on three warnings that reset every three months{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Rules, warnings}}. A guild that left after swearing the Emperator's oath was to be branded "an Excommunicate Traitoris and word of their treachery will be spread until all shall know of their heresy".{{cite:gdoc-1u97hsmpzu2lapij|"The Emperial Truth", Brother Alliances}}

The Emperator was "the main figure head and the leader of the Emperium of Wynn... Their word is law within the alliance". Beneath the Emperator sat a Shadow Advisor — "the co-leader of the alliance", bound by an "Oath of the Shadow Advisor" — a War Leader (territory allocation, guild banks, war games), a Community Leader chosen by community poll, and an Economy Leader. A High Council of one to three representatives per guild voted on rule changes, leadership changes and admissions; Judges ruled on rule-breaking, and their word could not be over-ruled. A Buddy System let member guilds sponsor sub-guilds and lend them territory, and the constitution capped any single alliance at 10–15 guilds, requiring an overflow of five or more to be spun off as a "Brother Alliance" under its own Emperator.{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}}{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

The public-vote rule was kept. Three leadership elections ran on the alliance's own forum threads: a contest for the first Community Leader in May 2017, in which ElegantDeath campaigned openly and listed his backers{{cite:thread-188024-p02|p2 #26, ElegantDeath, 10 May 2017}}; a poll for the second, between Rani, uriahsanabria and Szlili{{cite:thread-188024-p07|thread poll}}; and a third in September 2017 between ElegantDeath, RetiFile and IceResistance, canvassed on the second thread by [[drew1011|Drew1011]], [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] and others.{{cite:thread-202724-p03|thread poll and p3 #41–49, 24–26 Sep 2017}}

Applications were processed in the thread itself. Silent Heroes was accepted on 6 August 2017, and [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] applied the following day on the constitution's form — guild name and tag, leader, activity, war or community, willingness to take leadership roles, and how the guild would help the alliance grow — and was accepted within the hour.{{cite:thread-188024-p07|p7 #123, #126 and #127, 6–7 Aug 2017}} Tranquility [PaT], led by DemoGhost and self-described as "War", applied on 12 September 2017 and was answered by Drew1011 as Shadow Advisor.{{cite:thread-202724-p02|p2 #26 and #27, 12 Sep 2017}}

The alliance also concluded at least one treaty. A non-aggression pact between the Emperium and Knights of War [KOW] was signed on 13 July 2017 by DestroyYouAll for Knights of War and SnarbyDragon for BuildCraftia on the Emperium's behalf, and officiated by Lestrade, one of the alliance's judges; its terms were set out in images that were not preserved. The pact reserved to the Emperium "the right to change any terms and conditions under any circumstances".{{cite:gdoc-1xnystdpu-spsjds|Emperium of Wynn non-aggression pact, 13 Jul 2017}}

Its expiry was set by the other guild's growth rather than by a date. Reported to the High Council on the day of signing, the pact was to lapse once Knights of War, then at level 18, reached level 45, and its leader was said to be open to bringing the guild into the alliance later.{{cite:emperium-of-wynn-membership-2017-discord-private|13 Jul 2017}}

An earlier instrument had been drafted at the top and handed downwards. On 17 May 2017 the founder put a non-aggression pact with the Aur alliance to the High Council, undertaking mutual non-hostility and offers of help in community matters and in wars, and providing that a breach by the Emperium's side would be answered both to the other alliance and to the Emperium's own Judges.{{cite:emperium-of-wynn-membership-2017-discord-private|17 May 2017, the draft}} Finishing and delivering it was given to the Community Leader and a Judge as a first task.{{cite:emperium-of-wynn-membership-2017-discord-private|17 May 2017, the delegation}} No counterpart text was ever kept.

