The founding settlement of 21 February and its draft are described at [[the-federation|the Federation]].{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|draft and announced maps compared, 20–21 Feb 2018}} Its list of ground open to anyone named fourteen territories and went out as an image, so which fourteen went unwritten.{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|free-for-all list, 21 Feb 2018}} From 10 March the open list was published in words, and it grew as the assigned map shrank.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018, 3/24/2018 and 4/22/2018 6:22 PM}}

Absence from an allocation was not departure from the alliance. The map of 10 May lists [[dogsamongus|DogsAmongUs]] at no territories rather than dropping it, and gives [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]], absent from 22 April, twenty-nine.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|5/10/2018}}

## The fortnight the map concentrated

Two of these maps were revised after they were published. The allocation of 24 March was edited on the 27th and the one of 22 April on the 27th of that month, and only the revised text came down.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|allocations of 24 Mar and 22 Apr 2018, both revised days later}} The counts below are therefore what those documents finally said rather than what they said on the morning they went up, and the gap between the maps of 10 and 24 March is a fortnight in their datelines and something less definite in what they record.

What the edit of 27 March did to the second map can be stated exactly. The copy the guild leaders ratified names nineteen free-for-all territories; the published text names twenty-one, adding Wybel Island and Herb Cave.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|the ratified draft against the published announcement, 24 Mar 2018}} At 15:28:25 UTC on 27 March the alliance's leader asked in the leadership channel for Wybel Island to be added because it was not on the published list, and twenty seconds later for Herb Cave as well; the announcement carries an edit stamp of 15:30:56.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|27 Mar 2018, the two requests and the edit stamp}} So the nineteen is what the leaders voted through and the twenty-one is the list from the morning of the 27th. A member guild passing the alliance's lists to its own members had twelve open territories on 10 March, nineteen on the 24th, and twenty-one when it next posted the list on 9 April.{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|3/10/2018, 3/24/2018 and 4/9/2018}}

The arithmetic agrees. The draft of 10 March divides 356 territories among twenty-one guilds, twelve open and thirteen held for the future; the version published that evening divides 362, twelve and seven; the draft of 24 March divides 362 among nineteen guilds, nineteen open and no future category. Each comes to 381.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|the three documents totalled}} The published text of 24 March comes to 383, and the two that break it are the two the edit added.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|the published total against the ratified one}}

Between 10 and 24 March the total assigned did not move: 362 territories on both maps.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, totals}} Forty-seven changed hands inside it, and the map concentrated.{{cite:federation-allocation-series-2018-discord-private|the March concentration}} [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] went from twenty-seven territories to thirty-one, [[imperial|Imperial]] from thirty to thirty-three, [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] from twenty-seven to thirty-two, [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] from sixteen to twenty-five, Angels of Eternal from thirteen to twenty-two.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, guilds that gained}} Kasai Shinrai fell from fifteen to five, [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] from twenty to thirteen, DogsAmongUs from twenty-one to thirteen, [[illustratus|Illustratus]] from ten to five, [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] from twenty-two to nineteen.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, guilds that lost}} Two guilds left the allocation entirely: [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]] at four territories and TheEnchanted at eight.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, guilds dropped}}

{{map:2018-03-24|The map on the day of the second March allocation}}

KingdomPhoenixes rose from fifteen to twenty-three, so this was not simply the large growing at the expense of the small; but the four largest holdings on 24 March had all grown, and the three smallest had all shrunk.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, ranked by count}}

## What changed between ratification and publication

The map the leaders approved on 10 March 2018 is not the map the alliance published two hours later, and the two texts are line for line the same but for three places. [[imperial|Imperial]] holds twenty-four territories in the approved draft and thirty in the published version, its region called South Light Forest in the one and Light Forest in the other.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|Imperial's holding in the draft and in the publication, 10 Mar 2018}} The list of ground held for the future falls from thirteen names to seven, losing Efelim Village, Efelim East Plains, Efelim South Plains, Efelim South East Plains, Light Forest West Upper and Light Forest North Entrance, and one guild's colour is renamed.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|the future-territory list and the colour change, 10 Mar 2018}} Six territories moved out of the future list and into Imperial between the vote and the announcement.

They were the price of a vote. Between 21:38 and 21:52 UTC, with the ratification still open and Imperial and [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] the last two guilds yet to vote, Imperial's representative told the leadership channel that the map gave the map-maker's own guild more ground and better ground than Imperial for a smaller war effort, and asked why the future territories had been left unassigned.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, Imperial's objection}} The map-maker answered that the list existed so that a guild which did unusually well could be rewarded without taking ground from anybody else.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, what the future list was for}} Imperial said it would take six of the Efelim territories and be content; the map-maker worked out aloud that this would put Imperial at thirty, and asked whether Imperial would then vote yes.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, the six Efelim territories}} The published map gives Imperial thirty, and nothing announced the change.

The future category did not outlive the second map. The allocation of 10 March carried a list of territories described as available later and open to anyone in the meantime, thirteen names as drafted and seven as published{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|the future list, 10 Mar 2018}}; the allocation of 24 March has no such list and no line at all between the per-guild assignments and the open ground.{{cite:federation-map-making-march-2018-discord-private|24 Mar 2018, no future category}} Every territory on the second map was either somebody's or everybody's. The ratification votes themselves are at [[federation-map-votes-2018|the Federation's map votes]].

## What territory was for

The alliance had two incompatible answers, argued in the open on 12 March 2018. The leader of Titans Valor said he had voted against the map although it treated his own guild well, because the smaller guilds that worked hardest had too little and ought to hold ten territories each.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the effort argument}} The Kingdom of Foxes' Viceroy answered that they had not earned more, and that twenty territories could not be given to a guild able to hold five.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the capacity argument}} Neither position was adopted.

The effort position was tested five days later. On 17 March Titans Valor announced that it had left its island territories unclaimed so younger guilds could grow into them.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|17 Mar 2018, the announcement}} Asked what had actually passed, the Viceroy answered that the only thing handed over was the least valuable island, to one small guild.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|17 Mar 2018, what was transferred}} Titans Valor's own allocation fell by seven in the same fortnight, from twenty territories to thirteen.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/10/2018 and 3/24/2018, Titans Valor}} Reading the map of 24 March as the answer to the argument of the 12th is this article's; nobody at the time set the two side by side.

On 22 March a member proposed that the alliance stop carrying guilds that could not fight, going through the enemies one by one to show none was still a threat: [[hackforums|HackForums]] had given up, [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]] could no longer war, Paladins United had joined, [[emorians|Emorians]] was nothing without allies.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|22 Mar 2018}} Three weeks after the largest war anyone in it could remember, the case being put inside the alliance was that it had no enemies left.

## 24 March

Two things happened on the day of the second March map. Four member guilds — Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United and [[the-hive|The Hive]] — began taking the territories of a fifth, [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]], and no vote for it was ever taken.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|24 Mar 2018, the attack}} The Fox Viceroy objected in the leadership channel that members could not attack allies, was told in the following minute that it was already under way and who was in it, and assented in a single word; another leader did not know what was happening and told them not to.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|24 Mar 2018, the leadership channel}} The attack began before the map went out; nothing shows the one drawn in answer to the other.

Three of the four attacking guilds hold more ground in the map published that afternoon than in the one a fortnight earlier, and BuildCraftia holds one territory less; Paladins United, the fourth, is reduced to Corkus alone.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018}}

A representative of Imperial told the leadership channel the same day that the guild had been ignored; that it had earned the contested Corkus region by fighting that front; that the ground it did get read as a consolation, handed over in bulk on the assumption it would not examine how little use it was; and that dormant guilds had received more than an active one.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|24 Mar 2018, Imperial's complaint}} The only answer was that placing every guild well was hard.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|24 Mar 2018, the reply}} Its allocation that afternoon was thirty-three territories, the largest on the map; the objection was to which ground, not how much.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018}}

## Who was drawing the map

On 27 March a leader charged that Kingdom Foxes behaved as though it ran the alliance and stood above its rules. The Fox Viceroy answered that no Fox member had ever claimed exemption, that no private group of former Coalition guilds existed, and that a two-thirds majority made it harder, not easier, for a small group to control a vote.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|27 Mar 2018, the answer}} The denial settles nothing about whether such a bloc operated. The figure he gave inside it does stand: ten guilds in the alliance had come through the whole of the [[coalition|Coalition]], fewer than half its membership — a number that weakened his own case the higher it went.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|27 Mar 2018, ten of the alliance's guilds}}

On 28 March two guild leaders asked for a process: that the published map be updated when one guild gave another territory, privately agreed changes included, and that there be a way to comment outside a vote.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|28 Mar 2018}} No adoption was ever announced, and the alliance never wrote its territory rules down.{{cite:alliance-governance-mechanics-discord-private|written rules, 2016–2019}}

By the end of the month the settlement was being repudiated in public. On 30 March a member told the war channel not to touch a set of territories, asserted them as his own, warned that he would attack anyone who interfered, and called the alliance toxic; six leaders and members answered with the same thinking-face reaction and the conversation moved on.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|30 Mar 2018}}

The capacity argument was settled in practice a few days later, on a member guild rather than in a rule. On 3 April the last warring member of DogsAmongUs said he could not get online and was the only one left; asked twice whether his guild still deserved its territory, he answered that if they could not take it they did not deserve it.{{cite:federation-map-disputes-march-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018}}

## April

The map of 22 April lists seventeen guilds and 327 territories, thirty-five fewer than a month before.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|4/22/2018}} Imperial held thirty-nine and Sins of Seedia thirty-six; Hall of Fame, at twenty-five in March, held three, and Paladins United four.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018 and 4/22/2018}} Six guilds from the March map are absent — among them Angels of Eternal, DogsAmongUs, Illustratus, and BuildCraftia, expelled by vote on 30 March{{cite:buildcraftia-war-2018-discord-private|expulsion vote, 30 Mar 2018}}{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|30 March 2018 entry}} — and four appear that had not been on it before, Emorians among them, ten weeks after the fighting that emptied its treasury.{{cite:emorians-guild-profile-discord-private|19 Feb and 12 Apr 2018}}

One of the six has a vote behind it. On 4 April 2018 the alliance asked its leaders whether to expel the guilds that had not claimed or attempted to claim the territory assigned to them, or that had been assigned none because they had shown they could neither claim nor defend it, and named four: [[illustratus|Illustratus]], DeathReapers, Immortalish and [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]].{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4 Apr 2018, the motion}} None of the four is on the map of the 22nd, and only Illustratus had been on the map of 24 March.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018 and 4/22/2018}} The vote is described at [[the-federation-april-2018|the Federation in April 2018]].

The reasons a guild left a map are not on the map, and several of the six have their own. What the four documents establish between them is an alliance that assigned its ground by negotiation and vote, published the result four times in ten weeks, and never set down what the ground was for.

## May and June

The two allocations that followed name nineteen member guilds each, against seventeen on 22 April: the April roll loses Angelic and gains [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]], [[lunatic|Lunatic]], [[dogsamongus|DogsAmongUs]] and [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]].{{cite:federation-allocation-counts-recounted-2018-discord-private|the rolls of 22 Apr, 10 May and 4 Jun 2018}} Nineteen is what members put the alliance at twice within eight days. On 11 May somebody in the war channel, reassuring a member guild under attack, told it that it was in an alliance of nineteen guilds that could lend it money and people.{{cite:federation-allocation-counts-recounted-2018-discord-private|11 May 2018, the war channel}} On 18 May a [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] officer posted to the advisory council a roster he said he kept on his own server — nineteen Federation guilds, ten in the opposing alliance he named The Round Table, two neutral — and his Federation column is the nineteen of the 10 May map exactly.{{cite:federation-allocation-counts-recounted-2018-discord-private|18 May 2018, the roster}}

Guilds carried on the map with nothing on them multiplied. One appears on 10 May with a zero and a blank where its region should be, and five on 4 June: DogsAmongUs, Constellations, [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]], [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] and [[paladins-united|Paladins United]].{{cite:federation-carried-its-dead-2018-discord-private|the zero entries, 10 May and 4 Jun 2018}} Whether a zero meant a guild assigned nothing or a guild whose assignment had lapsed was never said. Two of the five left three weeks after that map went up, in a single line of an announcement that gave no reason and cited no vote.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 6/25/2018}} The alliance had removed four member guilds in the first week of April for never having claimed the ground it gave them, and told another at the end of that month that an alliance built for war had no use for a member which had stopped playing.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4 and 28 Apr 2018}} Setting the doctrine against the two maps that followed it is this article's.

The June document is a third revision, alongside those of 24 March and 22 April. The announced copy of 4 June carries an edit stamp of 19:05 on the export's clock, four hours and twenty-seven minutes after it went up at 14:38, so its contents are evidence of what it said that evening and of what it said at 14:38 only by inference; the copy put to the vote that morning was edited three minutes after posting.{{cite:federation-map-by-image-june-2018-discord-private|the edit stamps on the two copies of 4 Jun 2018}} What the open list did across the three is at [[federation-free-for-all-territories|the free-for-all territories]]; the four maps of June, which were pictures rather than lists, are at [[federation-map-votes-2018|the Federation's map votes]].

## The census of 10 September

On 30 August 2018 the alliance published a Light Realm map, a Gavel map, an Ocean map, a Wynn map and a territory table, having told its members that morning to disregard a map they might already have seen.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|8/30/2018 6:32 AM and 10:28 AM}} On 10 September it published four images again — a combined Gavel and Light Realm map, an Ocean map, a Wynn map and a territory table — with a ping to the guild leaders and the war role.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/10/2018 2:54 PM}} Both tables carry a count for every guild.{{cite:federation-allocation-september-2018-discord-private|the tables of 30 Aug and 10 Sep 2018}}

