Halcyon belongs to a cluster of non-war alliances that appeared in the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]] alongside [[seraphim|Seraphim]] and [[aurelion|Aurelion]], at a point when a single guild — [[hackforums|HackForums]] — held close to half the territory map and open warring had become unrewarding for most guilds.

## History

Yamipanda, leader of ToastedPandas, posted the announcement thread on 8 June 2016: "On June 5th, 2016, the Halcyon Alliance was born. The Halcyon Alliance was founded upon the vision to create solutions of preparing for success, improving community ideals and player relations."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}} The terms were mutual aid and joint deliberation rather than a war compact: "This is an agreement for whenever help is needed, each member shall aid each other in whatever task it may be. Each guild shall work together to discuss any issues that may arise and compromise to reach agreement."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}

Its governance mirrored the pattern [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] used in the same period, splitting internal from external affairs: "Internal affairs are to be handled by individual guild leaders, while matters concerning foreign entities as well as within the whole alliance are to be dealt with by every guild leader and any other representatives."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}} The stated aim was social — "to provide an environment where members can feel comfortable socializing and gaming" — with events and challenges promised.{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]], owner of Holders of LE, signed on in the thread the same evening: "Glad to create an alliance with a guild as amazing as TnP. Long live Halcyon / To clarify, it's pronounce Hal-see-on."{{cite:thread-130444|post #4, 8 Jun 2016}} [[killerfish|Killerfish]] was credited by Yamipanda with "helping with most of the diction" and replied as an insider — "Now, let us all within the alliance see an age of Halcyon"{{cite:thread-130444|post #2, 8 Jun 2016}} — placing him inside the Halcyon circle a month before he became a founding council member of House of Sentinels, and eighteen months before he founded a [[coalition|Coalition]] guild.{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as last revised 29 Apr 2017}}

## Membership

Halcyon was founded between exactly two guilds, ToastedPandas and Holders of LE, and no third guild is recorded as joining, though a reader in the thread wished aloud that "this alliance includes increased amounts of guilds".{{cite:thread-130444|post #12, 10 Jun 2016}} Both members had appeared in the [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] roster of February 2016;{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016}} Holders of LE went on to join [[seraphim|Seraphim]] that August and [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] that October.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No dissolution was recorded, and Halcyon was never mentioned again after June 2016; a reply in the founding thread asking "how long will this last?" went unanswered.{{cite:thread-130444|post #14, 11 Jun 2016}} A social layer persisted underneath the territorial situation: the two guilds' leaderships stayed closely tied, and Drew1011 went on to lead [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] from October 2016 and to found [[the-federation|the Federation]] in 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## The record

Three things a reader would want are missing, and their absence is a fact about the record rather than about the guild. No formal disbandment was ever recorded and no date given on which the guild ceased to exist; nothing records who held it after its last leader walked away in July 2018; and its co-founder is named by the founder and by nobody else.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|the silence in the record}} Its second leader is [[whimsicality|Whimsicality]], the Kingdom Foxes Prime Minister and [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] co-founder. Her account was deleted before the guild channels were exported, so the identification rests on the people around her rather than on any account of her own: the [[coalition|Coalition]]'s leader names her as a co-founder of KingdomPhoenixes in January and again in April 2018, that guild's own Queen addresses her directly in its parliament channel, and by May members were pairing the two women by guild.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|convergent accounts, 2017–2018}}

## History

### Founding and the Coalition (2017)
The guild was founded on 1 November 2017 by the player dwIcy, who had left [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]] to start it and had previously left another guild whose leader would not let it grow; a second player, referred to as Lot, came in as co-leader.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|founding, 1 Nov 2017}} The founder gave the date twice, eight weeks apart in the summer of 2018, correcting himself onto it on the first occasion after starting to place the founding in December.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|founder's account, July–August 2018}}

By his account the guild entered the [[coalition|Coalition]] on the day it was founded, the alliance being short of members at the time; he named the alliance's leader, who was in the channel, as able to confirm it, and was neither contradicted nor confirmed in so many words.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|founder's account, 2018}} It appears in the Coalition's roster at the declaration of war on 21 December 2017, one of fourteen guilds.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|roster at the declaration of war, part 14, composed 22 Mar 2018}} Its tag was HoF throughout, ordinarily expanded as Hall of Fame; through January and February 2018 the same three letters also circulated in Coalition channels under a joking alternative expansion.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|Coalition channels, January–February 2018}} Under its founder it held Ragni, and it appears to have been the first guild to take the Rodoroc territory.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|territory, 2017–2018}}

Members divided their own history into numbered eras — an original guild under its founder, a second under the leader who followed him, and later guilds formed from its membership counted as further continuations under other names.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|members' periodisation}}

### The campaign against it (January–February 2018)
Through January and early February 2018 the guild was the standing target of [[alovilatious-treaty|the multi-guild targeting arrangement organised by Titans Valor's leader]]: members described being attacked daily for about a month, kept off the territory map entirely for a comparable period, and set upon by roughly five guilds every time they took a territory.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|January–February 2018}} It lost the overwhelming majority of its territory in a coordinated attack over roughly a day on 19 January 2018.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|19 Jan 2018}} A vote to admit a guild its members described as effectively a sub-guild failed on 27 January, five in favour to seven against with one abstention.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|27 Jan 2018}}

It won. On 7 February 2018 the guild declared the campaign against it decisively beaten{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Feb 2018}}, and by 20 February it held around sixty territories — its recorded high point — with a [[the-federation|Federation]] leader publicly crediting it with starting the alliance's re-invasion of the guilds that had walked out of the Coalition.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|20 Feb 2018}} Its chief [[snowythewolf|Snowythewolf]] had opened that war on 17 February by attacking [[emorians|Emorians]]' Llevigar territories, and two days later called the attack that wiped [[hackforums|HackForums]] off the map.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}

### Corkus (February–March 2018)
The guild was assigned Corkus and the West Ocean in the Federation's territory settlement of 21 February 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018}} Corkus was twelve territories rather than one — a city, a castle, a mine, forests north and south, a mountain, countryside, outskirts, an abandoned tower, docks and a sea port — which is why the region could be held in part, shared, and fought over piece by piece.{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|the twelve Corkus territories}} It negotiated for more, on the grounds that its active members were unsatisfied with a Corkus-only allocation, and was then attacked over the region continuously by House of Sentinels and [[paladins-united|Paladins United]], one of which members described as treating Corkus almost as an article of faith.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|February 2018}}

Defending it destroyed the guild's treasury. The bank fell from roughly 1.5 million emeralds to under 100,000 across late February 2018, and on 28 February an officer reported a further fall from about 600,000 to about 95,000, attributing it to the war effort and to low member activity.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|28 Feb 2018}} In the first week of March the guild came close to dissolving: its founder began warring as a recruit for other guilds rather than under its own tag, members openly called the guild dead, and its leadership acknowledged it had already begun letting its active players fight under other Federation guilds.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|March 2018}} Looking back five months later, members were precise about the cause — the original guild died because two guilds pursued it relentlessly while it held Corkus.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|members' account, mid-2018}} On 5 March, with the day's fighting still running, its leader asked the alliance's leadership channel whether anybody was free to join the guild for a while, said it was basically useless as things stood, and gave the reason: he could not get any help with warring.{{cite:federation-corkus-campaign-march-2018-discord-private|5 Mar 2018}} The same channel spent that day voting on terms under which [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] would keep the Corkus region provided it expanded no further, and voted them down.{{cite:federation-corkus-campaign-march-2018-discord-private|5 Mar 2018, the vote}} The alliance refused to freeze the province on the day the guild holding it said it could not hold it. The two exchanges ran in one channel on one afternoon and nobody in it put them together.

It had survived the campaign built to destroy it and lost the peace that followed.

### Leadership and the split (April–July 2018)
The co-leadership had already turned over in March, and it took forty-two seconds. On 3 March 2018 the guild's leader told the Federation's members' channel that his co-leader no longer held the office, giving a personal reason.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|3 Mar 2018, the office vacated}} A member told him at once that he could simply have said the office had changed hands.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|3 Mar 2018, the rebuke}} Eight minutes later he offered the channel a choice between two candidates, and members began proposing a third person instead.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|3 Mar 2018, the poll}} He told one of the two candidates that their vote did not count.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|3 Mar 2018, the vote disallowed}} Forty-two seconds after the poll opened he declared the third person his co-leader and apologised to the loser; the man chosen had voted for himself in the same exchange under a second handle on the same account.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|3 Mar 2018, the result}}

Nine days later a member of that man's guild asked the leader of [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] in the same channel whether he could join, and said he was finished with his guild leader.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the request}} The leader answered in the channel that his member had betrayed him and would not get the rank he wanted.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the rank refused}} The Fox leader asked whether it was true, was told the rank had been withheld, and admitted him a hundred seconds after his first message.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the admission}}

Two days after that the guilds exchanged officers and called it settled. Asked in the Federation's leadership channel on 14 March why there had been so many changes in Hall of Fame and what had become of its co-leader, its leader said that person had left and that a second officer had gone too.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|14 Mar 2018, the departures}} The leader of Kingdom of Foxes said both were now in her guild, and that one of Kingdom of Foxes' former Prime Ministers was now in Hall of Fame.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|14 Mar 2018, the exchange}} Hall of Fame's leader confirmed it and called the exchange a fair deal.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|14 Mar 2018, the fair deal}} Identifying that Prime Minister with the member who owned the guild the following month is this article's reading of the two records; nothing in the exchange names her.

Ownership passed from the founder to Whimsicality in April 2018, and by the 24th she had stepped back from day-to-day running and named another member as primary leader for the time being, citing a loss of confidence and the demands the guild made on her time.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|April 2018}} She had taken the guild in the same month she returned to [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], the guild she co-founded and had been banned from in November 2017, as one of its co-leaders{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|4/13/2018}} — and by early May members of other guilds were describing her and AurumKitsune as running one guild each.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|May 2018}} An alliance advisor characterised the guild in May as having cycled through roughly three co-leaders in two months.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|May 2018}}

Its founder left in June 2018, taking several war captains with him in what alliance leaders called a mini-uprising, and formed the guild Ex Nihilo; he said afterwards that he had gone because he would not serve under the guild's new leader, and Ex Nihilo was admitted to the Federation later that month despite lingering resentment over the split.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|June 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Viaire, 6/30/2018}} In late June its leader said publicly that she was considering disbanding the guild, following the split and harassment directed at her and at her members.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|June 2018}}

Three things happened on 1 July 2018. The guild was accused of holding a secret non-attack pact with an enemy guild, on screenshots posted by the guild its founder had formed; the Federation voted the same day to prohibit member guilds from holding war pacts or alliances with guilds outside the alliance; and the guild's leader announced she was stepping down, citing exhaustion and harassment.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|1 Jul 2018}}{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Federation guild-leader vote, 1–3 Jul 2018}} The rule that episode left behind is described at [[alliance-governance|alliance governance]]. By then the guild's own Discord had banned a number of Federation members who had clashed with or criticised its leadership, and alliance members were debating a public commitment to ban anyone found to have taken part in a harassment incident connected to the guild.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|summer 2018}}

### Departure and after (July 2018 onward)
Hall of Fame left the Federation on 25 July 2018 together with Verinian Trials, the two announcing the departure jointly and citing an anti-harassment policy the alliance had not enforced, and mistreatment by other members; they had planned a coordinated exit and simultaneous attack a month earlier.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|25 Jul 2018}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Two other accounts of that departure stand beside the guild's own. The leader of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] said in 2021 and again in 2024 that he had personally arranged the double departure and the two guilds' move to the rival Confederation, and had timed the announcement to land during a Federation social event.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|later accounts, 2021 and 2024}} He had said the substance of it on the morning itself, in the Federation's general channel: his guild had left, [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] with it, and they had then talked to Verinian Trials and Hall of Fame, which followed.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, the account in the general channel}} A member in the same channel answered that Hall of Fame following Titans Valor sounded unlikely.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, the doubt}} A Federation leader recorded a rumour at the time, flagging it as unverified, that the guild had left not over harassment but because it believed the two guilds together could beat the alliance.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|July 2018}} Nothing settles between the three.

Two further explanations went round the alliance the same morning. A member told the general channel that Verinian Trials had attacked them first and that Hall of Fame was full of fragile people{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, the first explanation}}; the founder, asked why Verinian Trials had left, said its leader wished to end up on the winning side.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, the founder's explanation}}

The alliance began taking the guild's ground before the departure was reported in the room taking it. The general channel had the news at 11:26; at 11:31 a member told the war channel to take Hall of Fame's territories, and at 11:36 another reported there that the guild was declaring its departure.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, 11:26 to 11:36}} The ordering shows the war channel moving before the news reached it, not the alliance moving before the guilds left. A minute later a member asked the leadership channel whether the two guilds' territories were free to attack; the founder answered in one word, which was the whole of the authorisation.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|25 Jul 2018, 11:37, the authorisation}}

It had lost a member two days before it lost the alliance. At 16:32 on 23 July a member reported in the war channel that a newly made guild was attacking [[dogsamongus|DogsAmongUs]] in the savannah; ninety minutes later members of Hall of Fame said somebody had left them the previous night and presumably made it, over something about trust, having told them he had broken theirs.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|23 Jul 2018, 16:32 and after}} They said they would chase him, and one agreed to try to bring him back.{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|23 Jul 2018, the pursuit}} A single player warring under the new guild's name took twenty-three territories in two and a half hours that night, twelve from Verinian Trials and eleven from DogsAmongUs, and lost three back to Hall of Fame.{{cite:territory-exchanges|exchanges involving FurryUnited, 23 Jul 22:28 – 24 Jul 00:56 UTC: 23 captures over 19 territories, 23 lost, none on the free-for-all list of 4 Jun 2018}}

By the end of the month the leadership of both departed guilds was applying to the alliance's largest guild. On the evening of 30 July the founder told the leadership channel that the two former leaders had both applied to [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], and that accepting both would leave his own guild holding the former leaders of each; a member answered at once that one of them had applied to [[lunatic|Lunatic]].{{cite:federation-hof-vit-exit-july-2018-discord-private|30 Jul 2018, 20:36, the applications}}

The alliance told its own membership the same morning that the pair "are leaving and have partnered with CGoW, get ready to War".{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/25/2018}}

Its territory collapsed within days under a coordinated multi-guild assault, and Federation leaders reported that the guild's entire leadership had either left or was leaving.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|late July 2018}} The captures were logged as they happened: the guild held fifty territories on 23 July 2018, thirty-one on the 24th, eight on the 25th — the day of the announcement — and three by 2 August.{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|running totals from the capture record, 23 Jul – 2 Aug 2018: 50, 31, 8, 3}} On 26 July it announced it would stop warring and leave all alliances to become a community guild, following what it described as severe harassment directed at its leadership; the following day its leader left the guild for good, saying this time it was permanent, without formally passing it to anyone in game.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|26–27 Jul 2018}}

It did not stop existing so much as stop functioning. In August 2018 it was one of four guilds found to be capturing territories and handing them undefended to [[hackforums|HackForums]]{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|August 2018}}{{cite:federation-at-its-height-2018-discord-private|August 2018}}; in early September it was reported to be about to leave the Confederation; and by October members described it as a remnant holding its former officers, its leader keeping the guild while saying she wanted nothing to do with it.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|September–October 2018}} After 2018 the guild appears only in the past tense, or as the punchline of jokes about guilds already dead, and it was never again recorded as active.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|2019 mentions}}

## Territory

It was the second largest taker of Corkus ground in the province's contested winter, behind only [[paladins-united|Paladins United]]: 498 captures on Corkus territories against Paladins United's 717 between the log's first row on 3 January 2018 and 29 March, out of 2,478 by all guilds.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures on territories named Corkus*, by attacker, 3 Jan – 29 Mar 2018 UTC, raw: 2,478 total, Paladins United 717, Hall of Fame 498}} No free-for-all list held in this repo names a Corkus territory, and the list in force before 10 March 2018 is not recoverable, so the figures are raw. Its own Corkus fighting stopped in March; the summary counts that run from 30 March 2018 begin after it and place the guild nowhere near the top.{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|capture record from 30 Mar 2018}}

Beyond Corkus and Ragni its recorded holdings run to the West Ocean, Llevigar, Cinfras, Nemract and Tree Island, the last still being defended against it by House of Sentinels in July 2018.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|territory anchors}} It was allotted 26 territories in the Coalition's working map of February 2018 and 38 in the alliance's final allocation{{cite:drew1011-storytime|working map and allocation list, part 17}}, and held the swamp, Olux and the Llevigar plains and farms in the Federation's map of 24 March 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|territory map of 3/24/2018}} One member's account has [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] formed for the express purpose of destroying the guild.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|members' account}}

