## Legacy
Horologium closed the chain of ever-smaller successor blocs descending from Terra. Within the year its survivors resurfaced in the community alliances of 2020: Titans Valor (with Lux Nova) in [[Hestia]], and The Simple Ones in the [[Empire of Nemract]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

**House of Sentinels** [Snt] was founded on 2 July 2016 by Pyrias{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jul 2016 entry}} as a community guild, "in hopes of being a place of respite for those who need it"{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as last revised 29 Apr 2017}}{{cite:thread-187152|post #1, Pretzule}}.

## Foundation

The guild was created the same day [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] disbanded the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]]{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2 Jul 2016 entry}}. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] wrote: "After Fox was disbanded, the House of Sentinels [Snt] was created to house the now guildless Fox members. Misty and Pretzule, two ex Fox members, were its leader and Co-Leader."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L550–551, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} He treats "Misty" and "Pyrias" as one person — an identification no other source states outright, though the guild's thread is opened by a forum account named Misty and lists Pyrias first on its council{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as last revised 29 Apr 2017}}.

## Valkyrie and Aurelion

The new guild took the Kingdom of Foxes' place in [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L552, composed 23 Jan 2018}}. House of Sentinels was one of the four guilds of Valkyrie's August 2016 relaunch{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, thread opened 29 Aug 2016}}, and Yuno F Gasai answered a rival with "pretzule leads a Valkyrie guild tho"{{cite:thread-147790|post #8, 29 Aug 2016}}. The guild left Valkyrie about 12 February 2017 — "a mere five days after the leadership change", Drew1011 wrote{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L670–671, composed 16 Feb 2018}}.

In February 2017 the guild anchored [[aurelion|Aurelion]], a small community alliance, joining it on 14 February 2017. Its council that spring was Pyrias, Pretzule, wrxryuu, [[killerfish|Killerfish]], ChaChaChaChino and 01100110111{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as last revised 29 Apr 2017}}.

## The Coalition

In its later thread the guild announced a change of purpose: "Due to a few reasons our guild will also be focusing on warring with other guilds and maintaining territory."{{cite:thread-187152|post #1, Pretzule}} It was the fourth guild to enter the [[coalition|Coalition]] in October 2017, after [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], KingdomPhoenixes and Gilded Sparrows{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L869}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Oct 2017 entry}}, and it was on the alliance's roster at the declaration of war on 21 December 2017{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L927–941}}.

The Coalition's own channels record the walkout of 16 February 2018 as six departures rather than five, House of Sentinels leaving within minutes of HackForums alongside Paladins United, and the rest following over a few hours.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

## Alliance Alliance and after

On 16 February 2018 the Coalition announced a division of the Wynn province that allotted House of Sentinels "Swamp, Dark Forest, and Rymek"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|screenshot of the announcement of 16 Feb 2018}} — 36 territories{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}}. Within the hour the guild left with [[hackforums|HackForums]], [[paladins-united|Paladins United]], Kangronomicon and [[emorians|Emorians]] and formed [[alliance-alliance|Alliance Alliance]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1057–1059}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|17 Feb 2018 entry}}. Drew1011 wrote that House of Sentinels made no attempt to raise the dispute with him beforehand and simply voted no{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1062–1069}}; the guild's own account of that period is not recorded. The guild left Alliance Alliance on 12 March 2018 and returned to neutrality{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1102–1104}}.
A participant's narrative written that August adds a step between the two: having left the alliance formally, the guild briefly considered joining [[the-federation|the Federation]] before changing its mind and going neutral instead.{{cite:federation-march-2018-discord-private|participant's narrative, August 2018}} That sequel comes from a memory set down months afterwards, and it is wrong in its one substantive particular. The guild did ask, on 12 March 2018, and the Federation refused it in eight minutes.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the request and the refusal}} It was not listed among the [[the-federation|Federation]]'s members in November 2018.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

## Eleven days in March 2018

On 1 March 2018 the guild stood on the list of nine given in the Federation's general channel as the guilds attacking it, and that morning the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]]' war coordinator reported that it had left another front to strike [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]]; Hall of Fame's leader said the guild had a great many people in the war servers.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|1 Mar 2018, the enemy list and the attack}} The alliance did not think it could be made to stop. On 4 March a member told the same channel that after the alliance it had fought alongside was beaten this was the guild that went on warring, and that leaving it alone would only prove to it that carrying on was worth doing.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|4 Mar 2018, why it could not be beaten into stopping}}

Eight days later it applied to join. The motion went to the Federation's voting channel at 11:30 on 12 March 2018 under a joking name for the guild, which the alliance's founder clarified an hour and nineteen minutes afterwards; at 11:38 a member told the leadership channel that the vote was over and that a third of the guilds had voted against, which under a two-thirds threshold made the outcome certain.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the motion and the declaration}} Two members gave the count in the same minute, first as eight against to one in favour and then as seven against to none, one of them complaining about the voting system.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the two counts}} The motion carries no marks at all as exported, so the only count of it is the one the alliance's own members wrote down eight minutes in, disagreeing with each other.{{cite:federation-ballot-seeding-march-2018-discord-private|the House of Sentinels motion as exported}} How that ballot was built is at [[federation-ballots-march-2018|the Federation's ballots in March 2018]].

Its fighters left the same evening, for the guild the Federation had admitted five days earlier. The founder reported to the leadership channel on 12 March that a member had left House of Sentinels; another asked who owned the guild now and observed that a second had gone; and the leader of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] said that member had left the day before and joined his guild about half an hour later.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the departures reported}} Ninety minutes on, the founder named three moves into Paladins United in all, said a member with no interest in wars was now in charge of the guild, and said he did not think it would even attempt to rebuild its warring strength.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|12 Mar 2018, the succession and the assessment}}

There was no defeat and no disbandment; the guild stopped being a war guild inside a day. Writing five months later, the Federation's founder placed the end of the war at about this point, recording that House of Sentinels had left the opposing alliance on 12 March, that another enemy guild had slowed almost to a stop, and that from there the opposing bloc ceased to be a genuine danger.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|30 Aug 2018, the founder's retrospective}}

Its own side of why the fighting had happened came four days after the refusal. Taunted in the general channel on 16 March 2018 that he had bankrupted his guild by boasting about holding Corkus, the leader of Hall of Fame answered that the leader of Paladins United had told him they meant to go for Corkus regardless, that the boasting had made it more intense but was not the main factor, which was where the territory sat — and that he was fairly sure House of Sentinels had targeted him because of how openly he had said what he thought of them.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|16 Mar 2018, why the two guilds fought}}

A week later a complaint from one of the guild's members was carried into the Federation's own channel and endorsed there. On 23 March 2018 the leader of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] relayed a statement he attributed to a House of Sentinels member: that people were no longer friends because they were in different alliances, that guilds were hated for having different strategies, and that now warring had been fixed many war guilds were not interested in warring.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|23 Mar 2018, the statement relayed}} He said he agreed and that they should listen; he was answered that this was not new, and by another member that no hostility was apparent, and replied that he had not signed up for it when he made a guild and that everyone needed to change.{{cite:house-of-sentinels-march-2018-discord-private|23 Mar 2018, the answers}}

## Disbanded, and dealing with the Federation nine weeks later

At 18:25 on 2 May 2018 a member told the Federation's general channel that House of Sentinels had disbanded, and the answer in the channel was a shrug and a cheer.{{cite:federation-carried-its-dead-2018-discord-private|2 May 2018}} Early the next morning a member said he had partly killed it in order to see other guilds, the alliance's founder marked its passing, and a member described Angelic — a guild the Federation had voted in three weeks earlier — as essentially what was left of its people who had not gone inactive.{{cite:federation-carried-its-dead-2018-discord-private|3 May 2018}}{{cite:federation-ballot-record-april-june-2018-discord-private|the Angelic admission, 12 Apr 2018}}

It took and lost no territory at all between 1 April and 30 June 2018, and no day of that quarter is missing from the capture log.{{cite:territory-exchanges|House of Sentinels as attacker or defender, 1 Apr – 30 Jun 2018 UTC: no exchanges; no absent days in that span}} It reappeared at 01:42 UTC on 6 July, taking Tree Island from [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], and took five territories from [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] between then and the 8th.{{cite:territory-exchanges|House of Sentinels exchanges, 6–8 Jul 2018 UTC}}

On 7 July 2018 the Federation's founder put a motion to the voting channel reporting that House of Sentinels had asked for Tree Island and that a member had said the guild would help attack BuildCraftia if it were granted; the alliance announced the arrangement later the same day.{{cite:federation-carried-its-dead-2018-discord-private|7 Jul 2018, the motion and the announcement}} The guild was already holding Tree Island and already fighting BuildCraftia when the motion went up: its first capture off that guild fell at 23:58 UTC on 6 July, earlier than any hour of 7 July on the alliance's clock, which ran seven hours behind the log that summer.{{cite:territory-exchanges|House of Sentinels from BuildCraftia, 6 Jul 2018 23:58:33 UTC}} Setting the motion beside the log is this article's. Whether the guild had reformed in the meantime, or the report of 2 May was simply wrong, was never established.

## Back on the map, 2019–20

The guild went on fighting long after it left the alliances. It took 34 territories in July 2018 and 38 in August, then one in December 2018 and one in June 2019; in October 2019 it took 152 and in November 87, and its last capture fell on 26 December 2020.{{cite:territory-exchanges|House of Sentinels captures by month, Jan 2018 – Dec 2020, UTC; the eighteen free-for-all territories declared 14 Sep 2019 are not netted out}} It held no territory at the end of either autumn month, so the fighting of 2019 shows as churn rather than as an attempt to hold ground.{{cite:territory-exchanges|holdings reconstructed from the last exchange on each territory, 31 Oct and 30 Nov 2019, UTC}} Whether the guild of 2019 was under the same leadership as the guild of 2018 went unrecorded. When [[terra|Terra]]'s war channel discussed the guild that September it was as a name out of the past, cited to place another old tag in [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]'s membership ([[the-map-refilled|The map refilled]]).{{cite:the-map-refilled-2019-discord-private|war channel, 21 Sep 2019}}

HungHung filed [[avicia|Avicia]]'s updates to [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] during 2021, including routine guild-level corrections in May of that year{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #130, 3 May 2021}}. On 7 July 2021 he posted the request that became the only public record of an entire alliance: "Can you also add Avicia [AVO], Blue Nations United [IBT], [[shadowfall|ShadowFall]] [Shy], and TheNoLifes [TNL] in the Niflheim community alliance? Don't replace valhalla, just add it as a second alliance please :)"{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}}

The post is doubly valuable. It names [[niflheim|Niflheim]]'s four member guilds, and its second sentence records that those same guilds simultaneously belonged to the war alliance [[valhalla|Valhalla]] — direct evidence that community and war alliances ran in parallel over the same membership rather than replacing one another{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}}. Sg_Voltage answered within the hour: "Should be set, let me know if you want anyone else added to the community!"{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #147, 7 Jul 2021}}

No other source lists Niflheim's membership, and HungHung's rank within Avicia is not stated anywhere in the record.

IceResistance founded [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] [ANO] on 2 July 2017 and opened its recruitment thread on 15 October 2017, where the guild's first hierarchy read "IceResistance | Leader of Titans Valor"{{cite:thread-206094|post #1 (OP), thread opened 15 Oct 2017; "Est. July 2nd, 2017"}}. Two weeks after founding he applied on the guild's behalf to the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]], describing a ten-member guild that was "Mostly community guild for the most part currently. Since we are still growing, we are not a War guild yet, although Titans Valor will always be partly community"{{cite:thread-188024-p06|p6 #102, 15 Jul 2017}}{{cite:thread-278112|post #11, 2 Dec 2020 (the same framing restated: "umm ANO community guild FIRST / war second")}}; the alliance's roster records "Titans Valor (ANO) - Owner: IceResistance"{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster, 7 May 2017}}.

Against [[sheepn|Sheepn]]'s moderation pamphlet of December 2020 he defended the staff: "Moderators will not ban players without reason. Mods should also be able to participate in guilds just like any other player without being accused of bias and other slander."{{cite:thread-279337|post #17, 19 Dec 2020}}

[[titan-times|Titan Times]] vol. 6 marked "the long term hiatus of ANO's founder, IceResistance"{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}; by vol. 9 he is "ANO founder and previous owner"{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}. The guild's later roster lists Calluum as Owner and IceResistance as Chief and Founder{{cite:thread-206094|post #1 (OP), as later revised}}. Interviewed in vol. 20, Calluum said he took the role because "No one else wanted it when pally was stepping down"{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol20|vol. 20, 23 Nov 2025}} — the only public statement touching the handover, and it identifies no one further.

Returning to the forums on 2 October 2025, IceResistance argued that public channels had displaced real diplomacy: "Once upon a time, guilds had their own channels, their own Discords, their own backrooms where actual conversations happened. Alliances were formed, enemies were negotiated with, all behind closed doors. And it worked."{{cite:thread-322643|post #1, 2 Oct 2025}}

In March 2019 IceResistance posted an essay on the guild community's condition, arguing that war and community relations had fused and that the fusion was the problem: "Wars are suppose to be fun, a friendly competition over the map. Too often though do we end up taking that tension outside of war, and into the community itself, overall losing that separation." He asked guilds to look at themselves rather than blame each other, and declined to prescribe a remedy.{{cite:thread-245207|post #1, opening post as last edited 7 Mar 2019}} The replies from warring guilds were unsympathetic. Robturne of [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] answered "do you know how boring the community would be if there was no conflict?"; [[goden|Goden]] rated it "solid 8/10 on the poetic elements here" and said the community was fine as it was. IceResistance restated the point: nobody should end a friendship over being on opposite sides of a war.{{cite:thread-245207|p1 #4–6, 2 Mar 2019}}

The year before, he had assembled [[alovilatious-treaty|the multi-guild targeting arrangements of early 2018]]. The first was announced in the [[coalition|Coalition]]'s own general channel on 22 January 2018, its stated object to keep Hall of Fame off the territory map; he gave it the name Alovilatious Treaty, and the Coalition replaced that within the hour with a nickname derived from a pasta shape.{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition general and war channels, 22 Jan 2018}} A second campaign opened against the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] on 10 February.{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition leadership channel, 10 Feb 2018}} Five weeks after the first announcement he denied in [[the-federation|Federation]] channels that any such arrangement had existed, and rejected [[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s written record of the February action as fabricated.{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Federation war and leadership channels, 21 and 28 Feb 2018}} He posted as Ice through this period, the handle the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] matched to his in-game name when it announced his election as Community Leader in September 2017.{{cite:emperium-announcements|9/1/2017}}

Icey_Diamond co-led [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] [DDT] with [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]]. The [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]]'s thread names the pair as the guild's two representatives — the fullest leadership roster recorded for any 2018 sub-alliance.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} DiamondDeities was accepted into the pact on 18 July 2018.{{cite:thread-227373-p02|p2 #24, 18 Jul 2018}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s Federation tribute counts Nitrogen2Oxygen and Icey_Diamond among its most trusted friends.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

DiamondDeities went on through [[sol|SOL]], [[terra|Terra]], the [[council-of-canyon-kingdoms|Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] and [[horologium|Horologium]] before Nitrogen2Oxygen disbanded it on 8 January 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Idiot Co [ICo] is a Wynncraft guild created on 26 Nov 2017.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-idiot-20co|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## History

### The quiet years (2017-2022)

Little of Idiot Co's first five years was recorded. In February 2021 it was among the guilds actively warring in the desert during the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]]; which side it fought on is not known.{{cite:thread-286375|post #4, 20 Feb 2021}}

### smtn elf (2023)

Idiot Co joined [[smtn elf]], the great super-alliance descended from [[Cucumber Company]], by late March 2023, when it held alliance territory.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}} It remained until the alliance quietly dissolved in mid-2023 after [[The Aquarium]] and [[Avicia]] walked out.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Aquarium war (2024-2025)

On 29 Apr 2024 Idiot Co ignited [[idiot-co-aquarium-war|the biggest war since 2021]] against The Aquarium, raging through mid-July with a peak of 5,045 territory exchanges in a single week, and returning for a second round from November 2024 into January 2025.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war spanned the Rekindled World map rework of 10 Aug 2024. As in all wars of [[private-diplomacy-era|the private-diplomacy era]], any wider coalitions involved went unrecorded; only the two principal guilds are known.

### The guild in public

Idiot Co's owner through this period, TheNelston, was also the era's principal guild-war content creator. He introduced himself in December 2023 as "the current owner of Idiot Co, which is one of the larger guilds on the server" and published a critique of the guild system{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-m2g6zqx2dko|video description, 9 Dec 2023}}, then a two-part public guide to warring and war economics in 2024 written, he said, "to do my part as the owner of a large guild in making the guild scene more active".{{cite:youtube-com-feeds-videos-xml-channel-id-ucjooggtimerj6rxphwebgxg|channel feed: "Wynncraft: The ULTIMATE Guild War Guide!", 18 Feb 2024}}

## Alliances

- [[smtn elf]] — by 25 Mar 2023 – Jun 2023 (the alliance's quiet end){{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}

No other alliance membership was ever recorded.

## From alliance to guild

The name belonged first to a server rather than a guild. When [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] was destroyed in the Gavel Invasion of December 2017, its remnant Discord was renamed rather than abandoned, becoming Illustratus, and the guilds fighting on from it used the name for themselves before any alliance existed to carry it.{{cite:guild-lineage-and-succession-discord-private|Illustratus}} [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s own history puts it plainly: through January 2018 it fought the [[coalition|Coalition]] alongside the other War Syndicate remnants under the name Illustratus, without that being an official alliance.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Jan 2018}} Its leader suggested the name for that server, and afterwards ran a side-alliance under it — an alliance of equals, by his account, that targeted Hall of Fame and Kingdom of Foxes before going inactive.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|Illustratus as a side-alliance}} Reconstructing it in September 2018 with the man who had rebuilt the server, he said the name had been his instruction and his condition: the word standing for the alliance War Syndicate ought to have become, applied once War Syndicate had already ceased to function.{{cite:illustratus-naming-discord-private|September 2018}}

The order matters, because the public record leaves it looking contradictory. The name attached to the server first, then to the grouping fighting on from it, and only afterwards to a guild — which is why a February 2018 founding and a January 2018 usage are both accurate.{{cite:illustratus-naming-discord-private|September 2018}}

On 16 February 2018, the day the Coalition split, Titans Valor established Illustratus as a subguild carrying the tag Ius.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Feb 2018}} It was in that form that the War Syndicate remnant merged with the Coalition's surviving half to make [[the-federation|the Federation]].{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

### A second account of where it came from

[[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s leader described a different lineage in passing on 13 July 2018: that two alliances had been forged from the War Syndicate's remains, that few people knew it, that Aphelion — the one he had put together himself — merged with the other after the [[coalition|Coalition]] attacked it at night, leaving the old bloc almost whole again, and that Illustratus came out of that merger.{{cite:war-syndicate-successors-discord-private|13 Jul 2018}}

He said it once, and nobody else said it at all.{{cite:war-syndicate-successors-discord-private|2018}} Everywhere else the guild's origin appears only in the general form, as having come from the War Syndicate's remains.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, DerpyEmerald24's guild-history timeline image}}

## The admission

The guild was inside the alliance before anyone voted on it. Illustratus holds Nemract in the Federation's first published territory assignment, on 21 February 2018{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018}}, and on 24 February the alliance's leader discovered that it held alliance territories and Discord roles despite never having been admitted.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|24 Feb 2018}} A vote on admitting it failed the next day, three in favour to seven against.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|25 Feb 2018}}{{cite:federation-first-month-2018-discord-private|admission votes, late February 2018}}

Within days its parent guild announced that Illustratus was breaking away to become an independent guild, and a second vote was run in early March.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|early March 2018}} That motion went to the Federation's voting channel on 7 March 2018 and it failed too, though its mover thought otherwise: on the 9th the leader of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] told the leadership channel that the vote stood at ten to two and that this was a four-fifths majority, and the alliance's founder told him that was not how it worked and set the rule out.{{cite:federation-ballot-seeding-march-2018-discord-private|9 Mar 2018, the four-fifths claim}} The motion carries eleven in favour, four against and two abstaining, with nothing to take off it, against a threshold of fourteen on the founder's stated rule and his count of twenty-two member guilds.{{cite:federation-voting-machinery-march-2018-discord-private|multi-option reactions across the fourteen March motions}}{{cite:federation-ballot-seeding-march-2018-discord-private|the Illustratus motion's tally, 7 Mar 2018}} The threshold figure is this article's arithmetic from the rule and the electorate as the founder gave them, and nobody in the channel produced it. The rule that decided it had been proposed three days earlier. On 7 March the alliance's leader put it to the leaders channel that guilds which did not vote within twenty-four hours should count as abstaining, his stated reason being general: silent guilds were making a two-thirds majority unreachable.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Mar 2018}} On 10 March he announced that the vote had ended, that he supposed they were in the alliance, and that non-votes would from then on be counted as abstentions — the rule and the result together; another guild leader asked where the vote had been held.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|10 Mar 2018}} Members were still asking on 14 March how a guild whose admission had failed came to be admitted as its own guild, and on 17 March a guild leader left the alliance's leaders channel over the way abstentions had been counted.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|14–17 Mar 2018}}

Two things happened between the failed vote and the successful one: the guild changed what it was, from a subguild to an independent guild, and the rule for counting the vote was announced at the moment of its result. Whether the second decided the first is not stated anywhere.

## Attacked for the status it could not change

Being a subguild was understood on all sides as the reason the guild was being hit, and the person running it said so first. On the afternoon of 1 March 2018 Illustratus's representative told the Federation's war channel that he was being targeted again and thought Prius Power was going after Illustratus territories deliberately.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|1 Mar 2018, the complaint}} A member answered that this was because Illustratus was a subguild.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|1 Mar 2018, the reason given}} The representative said he wished he was not one, and that he had already asked the leader of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] about ceasing to be one.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|1 Mar 2018, the release already sought}} The status that made the guild useful to its parent was the status that made it a target.

The alliance could not say whether the guild belonged to it. On 7 March the Titans Valor leader told the leadership channel that his own war record looked thin because he had sent every active captain he had to Illustratus and had been warring alone since, and asked the alliance's founder to say where Illustratus stood.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the question put to the founder}} The founder said it was not in the alliance, that it was Titans Valor's subguild, and that the alliance had voted against letting it in; the Titans Valor leader said twice that it was in.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the two positions}} In the same minute a third member said he was attacking Illustratus.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the attack announced}}

It ended administratively rather than by decision. Later that afternoon the Titans Valor leader said Illustratus had been created to serve his guild by helping the alliance.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, what the guild was for}} The founder said he had taken the Illustratus representative's roles away and that the representative had left.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the roles removed}} Eight minutes after that the Titans Valor leader asked whether he might open a vote for Illustratus, and was told he was allowed to.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the permission to open a ballot}}

## A guild forbidden to defend itself

Two days later the parent guild set out the terms it had been given. On the afternoon of 9 March 2018 the Titans Valor leader told the leadership channel that [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] had recently said it would wipe Illustratus out, and that if Illustratus defended itself Titans Valor would be punished for it.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|9 Mar 2018, the threat and the liability}} He restated it as Illustratus having had the right to defend its own land taken away, though it was no longer a branch of his guild.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|9 Mar 2018, the right withdrawn}}

His last argument was a comparison, and the capture log does not support it. He said Illustratus had done more warring for the alliance than Titans Valor had.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|9 Mar 2018, the comparison}} From 1 to 9 March the two are level — seventy captures against seventy-one — and across February and the first nine days of March Titans Valor took nearly twice as many, 361 against 193.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures by Illustratus and by Titans Valor, 1 Feb – 9 Mar 2018 UTC, raw: no enumerated free-for-all list covers the window, so neither figure can be corrected for open ground}} The two counts are not independent of each other in any case, since by his own account the players taking Illustratus's territories were his.{{cite:illustratus-and-the-subguild-rule-march-2018-discord-private|7 Mar 2018, the captains sent}}

## It stopped fighting in March

Illustratus fought in its first weeks in the alliance and then stopped. It took 123 territories in February 2018 and seventy-two in March, the last of them on the 11th, and took and lost nothing for the five and a half months that followed.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Illustratus captures by month, 2018; no exchanges 12 Mar – 28 Aug 2018 UTC}} It came back for three short bouts, on 29 and 31 August, on 1 and 10 September, and on 20–21 November 2018, amounting to twenty-four captures in all.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Illustratus exchanges, Aug–Nov 2018 UTC}} It held Nemract in February and had shrunk to five territories, in the Detlas suburbs, by the map of 24 March 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|territory maps of 2/21/2018 and 3/24/2018}}

## The expulsion vote

The silence fell in the middle of the alliance's first argument about its dead members. On 4 April 2018 the Federation put to its guild leaders whether to expel the members that had not claimed or attempted to claim the territory assigned to them, and named four; Illustratus was one of them.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4 Apr 2018, the motion}} On the 6th the alliance's founder had all four taken off its ally list.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|6 Apr 2018, the removals}} Illustratus is not on the allocation of 22 April 2018, which lists seventeen guilds and 327 territories.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|4/22/2018 2:34 PM}} The vote and its aftermath are described at [[the-federation-april-2018|the Federation in April 2018]].

No readmission was ever announced, and its Federation membership runs in the alliance record to the dissolution of 10 November 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The practice that produced it — a guild raising a second guild to hold or feed it territory — is described at [[territory-warfare|territory warfare]].

Imperial [Imp] is one of the oldest guilds in the warring record, created on 14 Jan 2015.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## History

### Valkyrie and the Federation (2015-2018)

On 2 Jun 2015 Imperial co-founded [[Valkyrie]] with Kingdom of Foxes (today [[Kingdom Foxes]]).{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} It did not stay: Imperial was still among the member-guilds of the alliance's second relaunch thread of August 2016,{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, relaunch of 29 Aug 2016}} but by the third relaunch thread of 15 October 2016 it had gone — "tmw the alliance originally made by Imp and Fox has neither Imp nor Fox in it", one poster wrote,{{cite:thread-159734|post #2, 15 Oct 2016}} to which Ascended Kitten of Imperial replied, "Hey, we are pretty alive :3 Just not in the alliance anymore".{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, 15 Oct 2016}} Imperial's membership is next recorded in September 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The gap matters, because later accounts describe Valkyrie as a continuous four-guild bloc including Imperial.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}}

The guild ran a private council of its own, referred to as the Duma, whose membership and discussions were kept distinct from the guild at large.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|guild governance}} In December 2016 it proposed a formal dual-citizenship arrangement to the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]], under which a player could belong to both guilds at once; that guild's council declined the citizenship element and adopted a standing policy of neutrality days afterwards.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|December 2016}}{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} Leadership passed through at least four holders across the period, and a rival guild's council observed in December 2016 that Imperial was not genuinely independent, still deferring to a leader who had stepped down.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|December 2016}} The guild appears to have gone dormant before 2018 and to have been revived through the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]]' intervention, after which it returned to alliance politics.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|January 2018}}

The attempt to remove its leader is recorded from both sides. A group of alliance leaders moved to strip him of the leadership of the guild and of the alliance he also headed; he refused to step down, called their bluff, and announced that Imperial would leave the alliance altogether.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|leadership dispute}} [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]'s own account of October 2016 describes the same sequence from the other end — an ultimatum drafted by the other guild leaders, a refusal, and Imperial's withdrawal.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L567–578, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

Imperial was a member of [[the-federation|the Federation]] from its founding in February 2018 through [[federation-era|the Federation era]];{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} during the November 2018 collapse its exit 'for independence... snowballed into a major attack on Fed together with the enemy alliance [Ent]', Ascended Kitten of Imperial wrote the following morning - part of the cascade that killed the alliance on 10 Nov 2018.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}}

### The unremovable member

By 2019 Imperial held permanent, unremovable membership of [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] under that alliance's own rules: it could not be disciplined or expelled whatever it did.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|Valkyrie rules, 2019}} The consequence arrived when a different member guild left an allied alliance without the consultation Valkyrie's rules required. There was no mechanism to answer it, and the guilds that noticed did not try to reform the rule — they left and founded [[terra|Terra]] against it.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|August 2019}}{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|August 2019}}

It had already survived one campaign built around it. In March 2019 [[the-consortium|the Consortium]] named Imperial its principal enemy, put it on a published roster and called every allied guild to war on it at once; at the end of the month its leader concluded that the guild could not be beaten by those means, citing its treasury and its active fighting force.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|March 2019}} The coalition that formed later that year counted at least three earlier failed attempts on it, and recalled that during one three-day wipe Imperial's members had begun leaving and its leader had been desperate.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}}

Its opponents' definition of victory was not territorial. The war would be won, one of them said, when Imperial asked to negotiate.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}} They planned the attack as a scheduled event — midday on 7 September, expected to run for days — and overruled a vote to postpone it when the lead organiser became unavailable.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}}

Imperial was that coalition's principal target. Its opening operation, the coordinated raid of 7 September 2019, wiped Imperial and much of its alliance's territory within roughly twelve to sixteen hours, and by the following day the alliance's core guilds held no territory at all.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Sep 2019}}{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|the raid of 7 Sep 2019}} It recovered inside two months: by November 2019 it was a founder of [[artemis|Artemis]], the alliance that absorbed its defeated predecessor.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|November 2019}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Its disputes over the Corkus region recur across the whole period, involving at least three other guilds at different times, and it was still gaining and ceding ground there in late 2018.{{cite:imperial-guild-profile-discord-private|Corkus disputes, 2018}} Corkus was twelve territories rather than one, and Imperial was the largest single taker of them in the seven months from 30 March 2018, with 1,575 captures against [[paladins-united|Paladins United]]'s 1,534 out of 5,927 in all; 719 of Imperial's came directly from that guild, against 946 the other way.{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|the twelve Corkus territories}}{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|Corkus captures by guild, 30 Mar – 8 Oct 2018: 5,927 total, Imperial 1,575, PUN 1,534, Kingdom of Foxes 504}}

### Luna and the wars of 2019

Imperial founded [[Luna]] on 14 Feb 2019 to counter [[SOL]],{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} and led its war on Kingdom Foxes, attacking Fox 660 times over five months.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with Imperial as attacker and Kingdom Foxes as defender, 16 Feb – 8 Jul 2019 UTC: 660. Raw — no free-for-all list was published within ninety days of the window, so none can be subtracted}} In March 2019 Imperial was the map's largest holder, at 85 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 3 Mar 2019}} On 29 Aug 2019 [[Emorians]] and [[Avicia]] left Luna and declared war on Imperial specifically;{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Luna collapsed that September in the Luna–[[Terra]] war, in which, [[arkada|Arkada]] wrote, Terra's guilds "focused on toppling one guild in particular, Imperial".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}}

Imperial went first, and the alliance did not outlast the morning. Enemy-held territory stood at 108 at 00:48 on 10 November 2018, with members already reacting to the guild's departure; its official withdrawal statement came at 02:55, Arisen's at 03:36, and the Aesir bloc announced its joint departure at 08:00 — seven hours and twelve minutes from first to last.{{cite:federation-collapse-2018-discord-private|Federation and Aesir channels, 00:48–08:00 on 10 Nov 2018}} Imperial's own statement said the split was amicable, and that it expected fighting against the Federation to be more enjoyable than fighting alongside it.{{cite:federation-collapse-2018-discord-private|withdrawal statement, 10 Nov 2018}}

### The Valkyrie join-date problem

Whether September 2019 marks a return to Valkyrie or only a first mention is unclear. Writing on 14 Sep 2019, [[arkada|Arkada]] of Titans Valor opened his account of the war with: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians, have existed for longer than I've played Wynncraft."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} He was a hostile observer describing an established bloc — yet Imperial and [[Paladins United]] are recorded entering Valkyrie only that September, weeks after Emorians had left it in the revolt of late August, so that on those dates his four guilds were never simultaneously members.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The September dates are probably first mentions rather than joins; when Imperial actually rejoined is not known.

### Artemis, Goose, and the quiet years (2019-2022)

Imperial co-founded [[Artemis]] on 30 Oct 2019 with Paladins United and Caeruleum Order.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} In March 2020 GoulartJJ, an Imperial player who by then led the guild ShadowFall, introduced himself on the forums as "the Shadow Fall leader and one of Artemis leaders" — see [[goulartjj|GoulartJJ]].{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} By December 2020 Imperial had drifted to the opposing coalition, appearing in the 18 Dec 2020 list of anti-Artemis guilds that became [[Goose]]{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}, and remained there until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} No war-bloc membership was recorded after 2021; Valkyrie, with Imperial a member, was last mentioned on 19 Sep 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The guild itself continued. Its dynastic styling was in use by March 2019, when a parody roster gave Ascended Kitten as Empress over a court of the House of Vonamor{{cite:thread-245468|post #1, HerbCookie, 9 Mar 2019}}, and a recruitment thread headed "10 years going strong!" still carried it in July 2025, with an Empress, four royals, seven margraves and margravines, and admission handled through a Discord application channel.{{cite:thread-196016|post #1, opening post as last edited 13 Jul 2025}}

