**Kangronomicon** [Fuq] was created on 23 December 2014, one day after guilds were released; its creator was never recorded{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2014}}.

## History

### 2015: Spham and the subguild system

In early March 2015 Kangronomicon was one of four guilds that founded the alliance Legio Praetoria, with KnightOfValor, [[imperial|Imperial]] and [[nethers-ascent|Nether's Ascent]]; Imperial and KnightOfValor left on 5 June 2015 and the alliance collapsed about a month later{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2015}}. Through mid-2015 the guild was led by [[spham|Spham]] — "Being leader of Fuq, we're pretty sure you can get @SSEEBBYZ to do that", one contemporary wrote to her{{cite:drew1011-storytime|forum post by Kuroi reproduced as a screenshot at L25, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] later wrote that "Kangronomicon [Fuq] and Nether's Ascent [TNA] were essentially the Hax of mid 2015"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L32, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. A contemporary made the same comparison in the other direction in June 2016, describing [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[libertas|Libertas]] as a "rule of two" that "many distinguished scholars compare … to the ancient guilds of 'The Nether's Ascent' and 'Kangronomicon'"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}.

The guild ran a system of subguilds. [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] became one on 14 August 2015 and was promoted to full ally about five weeks later, receiving nine territories around Nemract{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L96–100, L111–114, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. During August 2015 a glitch prevented Kangronomicon from starting wars at all, and its subguilds were tasked with recapturing anything taken from it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L34–35, composed 19 Jan 2018}}.

Kangronomicon passed Nether's Ascent in experience to take first place shortly before September 2015. Spham then quit guilds and passed the guild to her senior chief Dar_Krusos, known as Kru, within hours of the change of ownership at Holders of LE on 22 September 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L104–107, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. That autumn the guild came under sustained attack from the [[concordia|Concordia]] alliance; by late September or early October 2015 it held no territory in the province at all{{cite:drew1011-storytime|territory map reproduced as a screenshot at L145}}.

### Ordo Malleus

Kangronomicon was one of the seven founding guilds of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] on 6 November 2015, listed under Kru{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178}}, and appears in the alliance's only recorded roster, of February 2016, as "Fuq, Kangronomicon"{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}. Its chief Paladin A'renos organised the alliance's recruitment and created its leader chat, and Drew1011 described Kru as its senior authority{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L155–190}}. After the alliance collapsed on 9 March 2016 Drew1011 wrote that Kru left Wynncraft and "to this day he has never returned, except to pass down leadership of Kangronomicon"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L462–463, composed 23 Jan 2018}}.

### 2018

The guild was still active three years after its founding: a new recruitment thread was opened by Chawwh on 27 February 2018 with the guild at level 56{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-54-order-post-date-direction-asc|guild thread index row, Chawwh, 27 Feb 2018}}. The [[coalition|Coalition]] admitted it at 12:20 on 16 January 2018, forty-six minutes before publishing a territory list it was not on; the list was rewritten on the night of the 20th to give it Llevigar, and the guild that had held Llevigar was moved to the south ocean.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018 12:20 PM and 1:06 PM, revised 20 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 16 January allocation before and after the edit}} The admission had carried by eleven votes to none, with six abstentions.{{cite:coalition-voting-record-january-2018-discord-private|15–23 Jan 2018, the admission}} It was allotted 25 territories in the Coalition's February 2018 division of the map{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}}, and left the alliance with four other guilds to form [[alliance-alliance|Alliance Alliance]] — on 16 February 2018 by Drew1011's account{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1057–1059}}, on the 17th by the community timeline{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Feb 2018}}. Kangronomicon stopped warring around 12 March 2018, one of the markers of the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]'s end{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1102–1104}}.

The Coalition's own channels place Kangronomicon fifth in the sequence of six guilds that withdrew on the evening of 16 February 2018.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition general channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

Three days later the guild was one of three that [[the-federation|the Federation]] counted as broken in the war of its founding week, its collapse put at total across the canyon and Gavel.{{cite:federation-founding-week-2018-discord-private|19 Feb 2018}}

The capture log dates the break to the two days after. Counting only captures outside the fourteen territories the Federation declared free-for-all that week, Kangronomicon took 89 on 17 February and 73 on the 18th, then 59 on the 19th, 16 on the 20th and none at all on the 21st, and it never returned to that tempo before it stopped warring in March.{{cite:territory-exchanges|daily captures outside declared free-for-all territories, Kangronomicon, 17–21 Feb 2018}}{{cite:federation-first-map-2018-discord-private|free-for-all list, 21 Feb 2018}} On the morning of the 21st [[dogsamongus|DogsAmongUs]], admitted to the Federation during the fighting, took Ragni, Ragni East Suburbs, Katoa Ranch and Emerald Trail from it inside twenty-one minutes.{{cite:territory-exchanges|DogsAmongUs captures from Kangronomicon, 21 Feb 2018, 00:12–00:33}}

