## Legacy
Khaos was the last opponent of the Valhalla line, and its fade set up the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]]: within months its guilds and their former enemies were trading territory as allies inside Cucumber Company.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

Kingdom Foxes [Fox] carries one of the longest continuous histories in Wynncraft guild warfare, spanning [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]] to the 2020s.

## History

### Foundation (2014)

The guild came out of two competing proposals of April 2014: Fibunny's United Federation of Animals and, in response, [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]]'s Animal Kingdom.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2014}} LoveLusting established the Kingdom of Foxes on 2 June 2014.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2014}}{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section IX: The Alliance}} A design of separate branches was abandoned in July for a linear hierarchy, and in August the United Federation of Animals was absorbed whole, its founder becoming the first Viceroy of the Foxes.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jul 2014 and Aug 2014}} The first Foxen Inquisition, a review of the membership, ran from 24 to 28 September 2014 in anticipation of the release of guilds.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2014}}

Guilds themselves arrived that winter. The Nether's Ascension merged into the Kingdom of Foxes in December 2014 as Her Majesty's Army and left after about fifteen days; the guild was incorporated in-game as Kingdom Foxes [Fox] on 22 December 2014, the day [[the-guild-update|the Wynnter Update]] implemented guilds, and CptShroom raised the Foxen Royal Navy [RFN] as a subordinate guild.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2014}} The Foxen Royal Navy was disowned on 24 April 2015.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2015}}

### Kingdom of Foxes and Valkyrie (2015-2016)

'Kingdom of Foxes' co-founded [[Valkyrie]] with [[Imperial]] on 2 June 2015 — an alliance 'not established for the purpose of war', governed by an Electorate of guild masters, that became the longest-lived in Wynncraft history.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} The alliance was relaunched twice, in August and October 2016.{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, relaunch of 29 Aug 2016}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, relaunch of 15 Oct 2016}} [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]], styled Queen of the Foxes, founded the guild{{cite:thread-89227|post #1, LoveLusting}} and the alliance.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} The founding date was chosen for the guild's first anniversary.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.1) Our History}}

The year before it had passed through two confrontations. The Wynnter War of January 2015 was a month of tension between the Tetra Alliance and the Grand Entente, and comparable tensions with [[legio|Legio Praetoria]] followed in March.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2015 and Mar 2015}} [[spham|Spham]] was brought over from [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]] in April 2015 to help revive the guild and was voted out by its members shortly afterwards.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2015}} The merger that produced Valkyrie counted the Kingdom of Foxes as part of Legio Praetoria on a formality, and it left with [[imperial|Imperial]] and the Knights of Valor a few days later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2015}}

The guild then refused every offer made to it. Kangronomicon approached the Foxes and Imperial for an alliance in September 2015 under Dar_Krusos and was declined on isolationist grounds; [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] invited both guilds that November and was refused too.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2015 and Nov 2015}} On 20 November 2015 the Kingdom of Foxes introduced guild awards in the form of orders, medals and decorations — the first guild to do so, by its own history — and held the first Foxen Award Ceremony in Troms eight days later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2015}} Ceremonies became the guild's fixed institution, held two to four times a year in Nesaak, Ragni, Cinfras, Troms and elsewhere for the next five years.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2015 – Apr 2021}}

Valkyrie ran a joint operation, Operation Old Glory, from 1 January 2016, and the Foxes and Imperial began a joint re-branding on Imperial's first anniversary a fortnight later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2016}} Snowing was crowned Queen Consort at the Spring Ceremony in Cinfras on 5 March 2016. The Ordo Exodus — the departure of Holders of LE, [[libertas|Libertas]], Death Reapers and others from Ordo Malleus — ran from 22 February to 9 March 2016, and Ha Ha United and Holders of LE were announced into Valkyrie at Imperial's second award ceremony on 18 March.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb 2016 and Mar 2016}} LoveLusting handed the crown to Kurumi on 5 April 2016 and reclaimed it on the 26th, redistributing the guild's titles and offices on her return.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2016}} The Queen's Cross, the guild's highest decoration, was awarded for the first time on 2 June 2016, to Misty.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2016}}

### The disbandment, the re-registration and the revival (2016)

LoveLusting disbanded the Kingdom of Foxes on 2 July 2016 after a dispute. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] declined to relay the quarrel — "I was not part of it and have not heard the story from anyone without massive bias" — writing only that "it ended with Ari disbanding her guild".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 8, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The cause of the disbandment was never recorded. He wrote that "after Ari disbanded Fox, a few rogue Hax members recreated it with the same name and tag"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 9, composed 26 Feb 2018}}: the guild listed in the API today, created on 3 July 2016, one day after the disbandment — a hostile re-registration by outsiders, not a rename by the guild itself.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

LoveLusting proposed a revival on 21 November 2016, and the new guild was created on 24 November 2016: "So, on November 24th, we created Foxton Legacy [Eon]. Foxton Legacy because Ari's name in the guild lore was Arianna Foxton, and Eon to represent that her legacy would last an Eon."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 9, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The guild carried that name for roughly its first two and a half months, because the Fox name and tag were unavailable. Drew1011's forum profile records him as "King of the Foxes" from 1 December 2016{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011 forum profile custom-title chain}} and the community guild timeline dates the revival to 3 December 2016{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} — both a week or so later than the creation date his narrative gives. The guild's own handbook accounts for all three dates: the new guild was created on 24 November 2016 and declared as [Eon] on the 25th, its thread was posted on 1 December, and on 3 December a deal returned the original Kingdom Foxes name and tag and the first State Council was formed.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section X: Historical Timeline, Nov–Dec 2016}} The Guild History instead dates the establishment of Foxton Legacy to 25 November 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2016}} LoveLusting left the guild again on 10 December 2016, giving up the office of Council Designer.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section X: Historical Timeline, Dec 2016}}

The recovery of the name was a transaction. The player holding it on an alt account was approached through a third party who handled the negotiation, and the money came from inside the reviving guild.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|revival, November–December 2016}} Only after that did the guild that had been the Kingdom of Foxes get to carry the name again. Its motto changed three times over its history, which one of its leaders used to mark off the guild's eras.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|guild history}}

![Four Discord messages of 21 November 2016 in which Ari (LoveLusting) tells Drew1011 to "take my crown" and "reestablish the kingdom". Drew1011's account presents this exchange as the start of the Kingdom of Foxes revival; the screenshot comes from that account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/24-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|screenshot dated 11/21/2016, part 9}}

The guildless members of the disbanded guild were absorbed by a guild founded the same day: House of Sentinels [Snt], created on 2 July 2016 by Pyrias.{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}} The House of Sentinels, Drew1011 wrote, "was created to house the now guildless Fox members. Misty and Pretzule, two ex Fox members, were its leader and Co-Leader", and "Snt had taken Fox's place in Valkyrie"; the Misty of his narrative is Pyrias.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 8, composed 26 Feb 2018}} He names the same person as Queen of the revived guild from 24 November 2016 until she stepped down on 28 January 2017, LoveLusting being restored on 7 February 2017.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 10, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

### Government

The revived guild was governed by a State Council of seven portfolios — Secretary, Justiciar, Chancellor, Designer, War Commander, Treasurer and Advisor — whose holders alone carried the in-game rank of Chief, above Captain, Recruiter and Recruit.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Sections III and IV}} Councils were numbered afresh at every reshuffle, and nine of them sat between 3 December 2016 and 12 February 2017. The first was [[drew1011|Drew1011]] as Chancellor, Teumessi as Secretary, [[killerfish|Killerfish]] as Justiciar, 01100110111 as Advisor and LoveLusting as Designer.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section XI: State Council Timeline}}

Titles ran alongside the ranks and carried no power of their own: royalty, viceroyalty, five grades of nobility from duke to baron, and a minor nobility of lords, ladies, dames and knights, each with its own form of address.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section V: Titles and Addresses}} A Table of Honour set out fourteen awards in four classes, the highest being the Queen's Cross, for "Extreme loyalty and dedication to the State Council, or an act of never-ending valour and gallantry"; wearing a medal in a forum signature that had not been awarded meant immediate demotion.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Sections VI and VII}} An elected Prime Minister was added to represent the gentry in Parliament from 16 April 2017, when Whimsicality won the first election; the office ran through regular elections until at least April 2021.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017 – Apr 2021}}

The council also priced its own ranks, fixing a published exchange rate between experience earned and emeralds donated and admitting members to each grade at it.{{cite:guild-finance-and-war-discord-private|Kingdom of Foxes council, 2017}} A recruiter's grade could be had at eight hundred thousand experience with five liquid emeralds donated, or at four hundred thousand with ten, which set four hundred thousand experience against five emeralds; the scale was then applied to the members the guild already had.{{cite:guild-finance-and-war-discord-private|Kingdom of Foxes council, January 2017}}

The handbook named six priority territories — Temple of Legends, Ahmsord, Animal Bridge, Jungle Lake, Crater Descent and Desert East Lower — capped spending at 3,000 emeralds per territory, told warriors to move on after two failed attempts at the same target, and made attacking an allied territory a demotable offence.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section VIII: Territory Priorities & War Policies}}

The council's own proceedings over the winter of 2016–17 fill in how the structure worked in practice. A King and Queen sat as co-monarchs, each also holding a portfolio — foreign relations and applications respectively — alongside a Justiciar and an Advisor to the Crown.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} A new council was reckoned to begin whenever its composition changed: the second dated from a monarch's departure, the third from a new member's confirmation, and the fifth from the appointment of the guild's first War Commander in January 2017.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council numbering, December 2016 – January 2017}} The council held that none of this was invented, an earlier era of the guild having run a Parliament rather than a State Council.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} It also maintained a royal house name for its monarchs, and in December 2016 debated and formally changed it, replacing the name used by the previous dynasty.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}}

Senior appointments ran as timed trials. Two candidates for War Commander were assessed over a week in December 2016 and rejected, the council recording that broken in-game war mechanics had made it impossible to evaluate them fairly; a third was appointed on a one-week trial in January 2017 and confirmed by vote.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|War Commander trials, December 2016 – January 2017}} Membership requirements were legislated in writing — an inactivity policy giving a warning after ten days offline without notice and removal thereafter, and a rank system with explicit experience and donation thresholds for each grade — and then enforced: on adopting the rank system the council reviewed the whole membership list, promoted and demoted members to match the new thresholds, and removed two who did not respond.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|membership legislation and review, December 2016 – January 2017}} In January 2017 an advisor proposed restructuring the guild from a monarchy into a tiered system in which each council member headed a division — an oligarchy in the proposal's own framing — and it was not adopted.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|restructuring proposal, January 2017}}

### Parliament restored (2017–2018)

The State Council lasted fourteen months. Narrating the period a year afterwards, the former King dated his own abdication and the restoration of the previous line to 7 February 2017; the Parliament the guild had run in its first era was restored after that return rather than with it.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|former King's account, 15 Feb 2018}} The restored Parliament continued its old numbering rather than starting afresh, so that in the guild's own reckoning the State Council was an interruption rather than a government.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|February 2017}} On 6 February 2017 the sitting King told the leaders' room that the former monarch would return the next day and that he would step down, and on the morning of the 7th he announced it in the guild's announcements channel.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|6–7 Feb 2017}} She put the count at her seventeenth Parliament on the 13th, sixteen having sat before she left, which is the number his own later account gives.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|13 Feb 2017}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L679, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} She spent the night of 12 to 13 February recasting the guild as a military command with its noble titles laid over the ranks, while the deputy was still numbering the sessions of the government it replaced.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|12–13 Feb 2017}} A separate account has it sitting two weeks later and creating NA, EU and OCE Regional Managers.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|21 Feb 2017}} 

Parliament had a room before it had members: its channel opened on 22 February 2017 and stood empty for two days, and on the 24th the deputy welcomed its members into it and the monarch told them they were the guild's new officers.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|22–24 Feb 2017}} The three regions were not filled together. On 21 February the monarch named candidates for the North American and European posts and left the Oceanic one open; on the 24th the deputy proposed a second North American name and advised leaving the Oceanic post empty for the time being, and the appointments went out that afternoon with a round of promotions.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|21 and 24 Feb 2017}} The scheme therefore began with two North American managers, two European ones and no Oceanic manager at all, there being too few Oceanic members to warrant one.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L682, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} Three of those four had belonged to the pre-disbandment guild and rejoined at the revival; the fourth had not.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L683, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} The Oceanic post was filled on 3 March 2017, when the announcements channel named its holder, another member of the original guild.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|3 Mar 2017}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L684, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} A member poached from [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]] became the third North American manager shortly afterwards, at the bottom of the Parliament.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L685, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}

The guild's own council timeline runs the ninth and last State Council to 12 February 2017, five days after the throne changed hands.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section XI: State Council Timeline}} The two records describe different acts rather than the same one twice: a monarch resumed the throne on the 7th, and the council he displaced was wound up on the 12th.

Parliament then ran contested elections. The first, in April 2017, was won fifteen votes to three, and the seat was named Prime Minister after the vote rather than before it — the office was defined by the election that filled it.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|April 2017}}{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017}} Four members were demoted from Parliament in a single night that September, two for insubordination and two for inactivity, and the guild rejoined the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] the next day, on 23 September 2017, to the displeasure of a good number of its members.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-in-the-emperium-2017-discord-private|the demotions and the rejoining}}{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2017}} The demotions came out of a quarrel between the guild's foreign-affairs officer and members of Parliament over what he took as disrespect, including a refusal of an application that was itself disputed; he is the officer who had been King before the restoration, so the account of the quarrel is the account of a party to it.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|the officer's account}} He gives the demotions and the rejoining as one sequence and does not say that either caused the other. The second Prime Ministerial election ran from 27 to 29 January 2018 with three candidates, and was won by the member who went on to run the guild's wars for the whole of the Federation period.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-parliament-discord-private|27–29 Jan 2018}}

The elected seat outlasted the constitution that created it. Parliament was restored to replace a State Council, the Prime Ministership was invented to fill a gap inside it, and elections to that office were still being held in April 2021 — four years and several governments later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017 – Apr 2021}}

### Foreign policy and the fall of the winter council

The council conducted something recognisable as foreign policy. In December 2016 [[imperial|Imperial]] proposed a formal dual-citizenship arrangement under which members could belong to both guilds at once; the council declined the citizenship element, and days later adopted a standing policy of neutrality, agreeing to avoid permanent foreign alliances in future and citing its own prior permanent alliance as the reason.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} It decided against becoming a war guild at all, settling for occasional territory raids, and refused to extend Discord administrative permissions beyond its four founding council members after an informal vote.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} In the same month a newly appointed advisor told the council, unprompted, that after joining she had continued to have access to a rival guild's private council channel and had been relaying what she saw there.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}}{{cite:espionage-and-infiltration-discord-private|December 2016}}

The structure did not survive the winter. An officer resigned from the council in late January 2017; at the beginning of February the King stepped down and the guild's earlier monarch returned as sole ruler, a change the council described as restoring the original line.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|State Council, late January – February 2017}} Several former council members left for a rival guild at the same time, which the departing King recorded as a betrayal.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-government-2016-discord-private|February 2017}}

On 16 February 2017 a member asked in the leaders' room what the guild gained by staying in [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]. The deputy answered that they meant to revive the alliance and were settling the guild's own affairs first; the monarch said it practically did not exist and was a non-issue for them.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|16 Feb 2017}} Writing a year afterwards the deputy put the same weeks differently, saying that with the alliance's other guilds dead there had seemed no point in reviving it at all.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L670–671, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} On 8 March 2017 the monarch announced that she was remaking the guild's Discord; the new server went up on the 9th, members were invited across on the 9th and 10th, and those still in the old one were cleared out on 21 March.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-state-council-2016-2017-discord-private|8–21 Mar 2017}}

### The Emperium of Wynn (2017)

Kingdom Foxes was a member of the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]. By 17 October 2017 it was one of the alliance's four remaining member guilds, listed as "Kingdom Foxes [ Fox ] - Owner LoveLusting/Drew1011".{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

Drew1011's account describes two separate memberships. The first began in about May 2017 on a 14–4 guild vote, with Fox holding three of the alliance's six judge seats, and ended thirteen days later after an argument between alliance officers and Fox members in the alliance Discord.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 11, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The second began in about September 2017, a decision he says he and LoveLusting took the day after he demoted four members of the guild's Parliament; he wrote that it "caused a significant amount of members to join and form their own guild, KingdomPhoenixes [Phx]".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The guild's own history dates that first membership to 22 April – 5 May 2017, a span of thirteen days, and gives its end as a dispute between the Foxes and many of the alliance's members; it dates the second to 23 September 2017, three weeks after Drew1011 was elected Shadow Advisor of the Emperium, an office open to candidates from outside the alliance.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017, May 2017 and Sep 2017}} KingdomPhoenixes split from Kingdom Foxes in September 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} and was established on 23 September 2017{{cite:thread-204381|post #1, 24 Sep 2017}}; the motive appears only in his account. He also attributed the guild's later turn to warring to the rivalry that followed, calling it "the single most important cause of Fox's transformation from a purely community guild to one of the top War guilds in the community".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

Challenged a week later by the Emperium leader who had invited the guild back, he allowed that KingdomPhoenixes would probably have been founded in any case, its founder having already said she meant to leave.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-in-the-emperium-2017-discord-private|4 Mar 2018}}

Drew1011 held the title "Viceroy of the Foxes" from 7 February 2017 to 7 February 2019, the title he was still carrying when he wrote the Federation Tribute.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} Other officers of the era included Goden, who rose from recruit to guild leader and was named among the Federation's foremost war leaders,{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} and Robturne.

### The Coalition (2017-2018)

In October 2017 Kingdom Foxes co-founded the [[Coalition]] with KingdomPhoenixes, Gilded Sparrows and House of Sentinels; the Coalition took the Wynn Province on 23 Nov 2017, wiped [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] on Christmas Day, and gained full map dominance.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Drew1011 places Fox and KingdomPhoenixes as the two co-founders, with Gilded Sparrows third and House of Sentinels fourth, and describes the alliance as built "with the sole purpose of bringing down War Syndicate".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}}

### The Federation era (2018)

When five guilds split off in February 2018, starting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]], Kingdom Foxes went with the Coalition remnant into the Federation and remained until [[the-federation-dies|its collapse on 10 Nov 2018]].{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} The territory allocation announced inside the Coalition on 16 Feb 2018 assigned Fox 36 territories, in North Canyon and Nesaak.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|allocation announcement of 16 Feb 2018, part 17}} In April 2018 Fox was the map's largest holder, at 82 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 16 Apr 2018}} In the winter interregnum that followed, the community timeline records 'valk owning most of Gavel'.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

### The most fighting in the game

At 26 July 2018 the guild held 64 territories, level with [[emorians|Emorians]] and just ahead of [[imperial|Imperial]] on 60 — three guilds of one alliance holding 188 of the 383 territories then in known hands.{{cite:federation-governance-2018-discord-private|running totals at 26 Jul 2018: Emorians 64, Kingdom Foxes 64, Imperial 60 of 383 held}}

The guild measured its own share of the alliance's war and then withdrew it. On 17 July 2018 its Viceroy put Kingdom Foxes at twenty-five per cent of every war the alliance had ever fought, said the balance was bad and that he did not mean it against any other guild, and the same day told the leadership channel that the guild would stop helping allies until further notice and fight only for its own assigned territory and for free-for-all ground.{{cite:federation-july-2018-discord-private|17 Jul 2018}} The other leaders had been asked to carry more and had mostly not done so or been unable to, he said, and the quarter of the fighting his guild was doing rested on three or four people.{{cite:federation-july-2018-discord-private|17 Jul 2018}} A fortnight later it was besieged through a night and a day — see [[the-federation-july-2018|the Federation in July 2018]].

Between 30 March and 8 October 2018 the guild made 19,062 territory captures — about one in eight of every capture logged in the game, and some seventy per cent more than any other guild — peaking at 145 territories held.{{cite:who-fought-2018-discord-private|Kingdom Foxes: 19,062 of 155,498 captures (12.3%), peak 145}} It also lost 19,042 in the same period, a net gain of twenty: it did more of the fighting than anyone and finished where it started, which was true of every large guild of the period.{{cite:who-fought-2018-discord-private|net change by guild, 30 Mar – 8 Oct 2018}} Not every capture was a fight — territories could be handed over undefended by arrangement — so the total is a ceiling on the fighting behind it rather than a measure of it.{{cite:federation-august-2018-discord-private|August 2018}}

The volatility behind those numbers was extreme enough that nobody could say what the guild held. On 16 August 2018 a stats bot put it at a hundred territories and first on the server while a member counting by eye made it barely a third of that; its holdings moved between forty-eight and a hundred and twelve that day across 1,701 transfers.{{cite:federation-august-2018-discord-private|16 Aug 2018: holdings range 48–112 across 1,701 transfers}} What that record measures, and what it does not, is set out at [[territory-warfare|territory warfare]].

### From neutrality to the front line

In December 2016 the council had resolved to avoid permanent foreign alliances and decided against becoming a war guild at all, settling for occasional raids.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|State Council, December 2016}} Fourteen months later the guild was the principal fighting guild of the largest alliance on the server: attacked by four guilds simultaneously across several fronts in March 2018, and at points holding the highest territory count in the game.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|2018}} The reversal was never remarked on at the time. The leadership had turned over twice in the interval, and the guild that adopted the neutrality policy and the guild that abandoned it had few members in common.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|leadership turnover, 2016–2018}}

It was also a target. From 10 February 2018 it was the object of the second of [[alovilatious-treaty|the multi-guild targeting arrangements of that winter]], losing roughly half its territories at the campaign's peak before allied guilds reclaimed most of the ground the following day.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|February 2018}}{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition leadership channel, 10 Feb 2018}} Its most persistent rivalry of the period was with a guild founded by its own former members, which members said had copied its structure; the two fought openly, reconciled, and afterwards co-founded an alliance together.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|2018}}

### Institutions and the Eternal War (2018)

Kingdom Foxes built standing military and civil institutions through 2018: the Royal Dragoons on 14 February, the Royal Academy on 2 May, the 1st Royal Fusiliers on 7 July and the 2nd on 4 August, the three warring regiments merging again that August and September.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb–Sep 2018}} A second Foxen Inquisition was held from 17 to 20 May 2018 after an information leak was discovered.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|May 2018}} The Royal Engineers were publicly acknowledged as a guild institution on 18 April 2020, when [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] was appointed their first representative to Parliament.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2020}}

BuildCraftia [BCr] attacked territories assigned to Kingdom Foxes on 24 March 2018 while both guilds were inside [[the-federation|the Federation]], and was voted out of the alliance on the 30th; the fighting that followed was called the Eternal War and ended on 19 September 2018 when BuildCraftia's leader was banned.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Mar 2018 and Sep 2018}} Within Valkyrie, the alliance split the Durum Isles between its members on 16 April 2018 and invited [[emorians|Emorians]] to join on 5 May.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2018 and May 2018}} Two long defensive actions of that summer were recorded by name: the seven-hour Battle of Nether's Gate on 17 June 2018, in which The Hive was the focus, and the sixteen-hour Siege of Ranol's Farm of 29–30 July, in which Kingdom Foxes was.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2018 and Jul 2018}}

### The wars of 2019

Money ran through the year's fighting, and the guild's own reserves are at the centre of the most striking account of it. A leader in the coalition that formed against [[imperial|Imperial]] said in September 2019 that six million emeralds had come out of Kingdom Foxes' reserves during the summer offensive to pull an attacking guild off Imperial, after which Imperial was allowed back onto the map; another leader in the same conversation was audibly surprised by the figure, and a third said Foxes had to rescue Imperial repeatedly.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}} The episode falls in a period the surviving channels do not cover, and it is one participant's recollection two months after the fact rather than a contemporaneous record.

What is not in doubt is what the coalition did next. In the same conversation its organiser instructed members not to accept emerald deals, to report anyone who approached them with one, and stated that the coalition would not take money.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}} A group preparing to attack the wealthiest guilds on the server found it necessary to begin by forbidding its own members from being bought.

During the coordinated raid of 7 September 2019 that broke [[luna|Luna]]'s hold on the map, Kingdom Foxes negotiated separately from its alliance, agreeing a non-aggression deal with the attacking coalition under which it gave up specific territory claims in exchange for being left alone.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Sep 2019}}{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|the raid of 7 Sep 2019}} It was the only guild on its side to come through: an hour before the assault it held 71 territories, and by nine the next morning it held 68, while [[imperial|Imperial]] was down to one and three other Luna guilds to seven apiece.{{cite:territory-exchanges|holdings from the last exchange on each territory before 7 Sep 15:00 and 8 Sep 09:00 2019, UTC}}

Its war team had already decided the raid by refusing to fight in it. Three days afterwards [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s leader told [[terra|Terra]]'s leadership channel that Kingdom Foxes had honourably stopped aiding Imperial and that this was part of why the coalition had got such quick results; another Terra leader corrected him, saying the guild had stopped because its entire war team had gone on strike, its leader having said that anybody in the guild who helped Imperial would be doing it alone.{{cite:terra-institutions-2019-discord-private|10 Sep 2019}} That is the account of the coalition attacking it, of a decision taken inside the guild. It was the second time in fourteen months Kingdom Foxes withheld its fighting from allies, and the first time the decision came from below the leadership: in July 2018 its leaders had suspended help to their Federation allies themselves.{{cite:federation-july-2018-discord-private|July 2018}}

The peace that followed was written down. Terms agreed with Terra on 17 September gave complete and enduring neutrality in both directions and released about twenty-five territories, effective immediately, and bound each side not to send its members into subguilds or foreign guilds in order to attack the other's claims.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|17 Sep 2019}}

Kingdom Foxes left the Federation on 10 November 2018 and declared war on [[hackforums|HackForums]] on 13–14 November to check its expansion in Wynn. Further declarations followed: on 12 December 2018 against Achte Shadow, Wrath of Poseidon, Beyond the Scene, Spectral Cabbage and TheNoLifes, in defence of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] and Emorians territory, and on 26 December against [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] and HackForums.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2018 and Dec 2018}}

[[Luna]] fought Kingdom Foxes across 300+ territories from 15 Feb 2019 — Imperial alone attacked Fox 660 times.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with Imperial as attacker and Kingdom Foxes as defender, 16 Feb – 8 Jul 2019 UTC: 660; distinct territories with Kingdom Foxes on either side over the same window: 381. Raw — no free-for-all list was published within ninety days of the window, so none can be subtracted}} Peace came stepwise, and each settlement divided ground rather than awarding it. The DiamondDeities war ended on 10 January 2019 with Lava Lake declared free-for-all, the HackForums war on 8 February with Sky Islands split, and a second DiamondDeities war, declared on 17 February, on the 24th with Molten Heights split and Molten Reach declared free-for-all.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2019 and Feb 2019}} The Treaty of Rodoroc with [[DiamondDeities]] took effect 2 Mar 2019, and the Treaty of Ternaves (6 Jul 2019) split the dissolved Celestial Tigers' land; Fox joined Luna on 8 Jul 2019. Kingdom Foxes declared war on [[fantasy|Fantasy]] on 7 June 2019 in what it called the Second Canyon War and claimed the Air Temple region on the 19th, and on 6 July it was attacked by more than fifteen guilds at once, including HackForums, DiamondDeities and BuildCraftia, in a day it called the Sunday War; two days later DiamondDeities and HackForums were wiped and Fox entered Luna.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2019 and Jul 2019}} Its departure on 18 Sep 2019 collapsed Luna. Three days earlier it had co-founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]], which it left on 2 Nov 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} [[Terra]] wiped Imperial, Paladins United and the rest of Luna from the map on 7 September 2019, and Kingdom Foxes, the last Luna guild still holding ground, declared a ceasefire the next day; it left the Council to take part in Imperial's Reconquista, which recovered the Imperial and Paladins United homelands on 3 November.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2019 and Nov 2019}} On 21 December 2019 it became the first guild to hold every Silent Expanse territory at once, and the following day it passed 50,000 recorded wars.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2019}}

### Artemis and after (2020-2022)

By March 2020 Kingdom Foxes was a member of [[Artemis]],{{cite:thread-263975|9 Mar 2020}} remaining through [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021. Three guilds left the alliance and attacked it on 18–19 December 2020, and on 16 January 2021 an attack by [[goose|Goose]] took Kingdom Foxes to zero territories for the first time since February 2018.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2020 and Jan 2021}} On 5 February 2021 the guild dropped all its territorial claims and announced a turn away from warring, after reassessing its direction in the wake of an overhaul of the guild system; it returned to warring on 3 April 2021.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb 2021 and Apr 2021}} It joined [[Cucumber Company]] in spring 2022, one of the alliance's fourteen guilds that June;{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} it appears to have left in early July 2022, after which it fought its former bloc.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Fox was still a Valkyrie member as late as 19 September 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The guild in 2026

Kingdom Foxes runs its own site, which gives the guild's founding as 2014 and shows a roster of 101 members across three regional divisions — 48 in the Americas, 30 in Europe and 23 in Oceania.{{cite:kingdomfoxes-com-members|roster page as rendered 4 Sep 2026}} The rank ladder is still the one the 2017 handbook describes, in a later form: House Everton at the head, then High Nobility, Nobility, the Prime Minister, the Landed Gentry and the Gentry, each mapped onto an in-game rank. SpaseCow held the crown as King and guild owner, with Robturne as Prince, SaltyKing as Viceroy and photor320 as Archduke; three former Prime Ministers of the 2019–2021 elections were still on the roster.{{cite:kingdomfoxes-com-members|roster page as rendered 4 Sep 2026}}

