## Origins

The thread's opening line, as last edited in October 2018, reads "Started by few descendants of another kingdom"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1, as last edited 9 Oct 2018}}. Drew1011 quoted the same sentence in a different form — "Started from a few descendants of crumbling Kingdom..." — and wrote that the word "crumbling" was what began the feud between the two guilds{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L826–830}}. The opening post was edited more than a year after it was written; which wording stood in September 2017 is not known.

Drew1011, then Fox's Viceroy, identified the "kingdom" as [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and attributed the split to Fox's decision to rejoin the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] — "It caused a significant amount of members to join and form their own guild, KingdomPhoenixes [Phx]"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L810–813}}

Its founder gave a different cause herself two months later. On 14 April 2018 she told [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s war channel that KingdomPhoenixes had been created after she was demoted in Kingdom Foxes for what she considered poor reasons, and that it still existed because she enjoyed leading it and Kingdom Foxes would not restore her rank.{{cite:federation-carried-its-dead-2018-discord-private|14 Apr 2018}}

The guild's fighting stopped before its allocation did. It appears in the capture log as an attacker 83 times in April 2018, four times in May and twenty-eight times in June, and not at all in July or August; no day of that spring is absent from the log.{{cite:territory-exchanges|KingdomPhoenixes as attacker by month, Apr – Aug 2018 UTC; a name-appearance count, so no free-for-all subtraction applies}} — and wrote that the new guild copied Fox's structure{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L824–825}}.

The guild reached level 31, and its first star, four days after it was created, and level 41 on 5 November 2017.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entries of 9-27-17 and 11-5-17}} Iron was its first Viceroy; Alhecks was promoted in his absence on 9 October 2017, and on 15 October ElegantDeath briefly held the title of King while AurumKitsune spent half a day in Kingdom Foxes.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Oct 2017}}

An internal challenge came "after about a month": "the government officials decided that they wanted to try to take over the monarch... those that tried to start the coup got demoted"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1}}. Drew1011 described a different-looking episode in early October 2017, in which AurumKitsune handed the guild to ElegantDeath and briefly rejoined Kingdom Foxes before taking it back{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L853–863}}; the guild's own history dates that episode to 15 October.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Oct 2017}} Whether the two were the same event is not known.

### The November Exodus

At AurumKitsune's request, Drew1011 joined the guild on an alternate account on 2 November 2017 and became Viceroy in place of Alhecks.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}}{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-2-17}} The appointment split the guild, and the two Phoenix accounts of what followed differ. One dates the break to 3 November and has members leaving of their own accord after failing to force AurumKitsune's resignation, then banding together to create the Serpentem Empire [SNK].{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}} The other dates it to 4 November, names [[elegantdeath|ElegantDeath]], Whimsicality and Alhecks, and records them as removed for high treason and "forever forbidden from coming back" after trying to have the queen hand the guild over to them.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-4-17}} [[thundderr|Thundderr]], then one of the guild’s two chiefs and its king three weeks later, recalls the two as one sequence: Whimsicality and AurumKitsune fell out badly, AurumKitsune removed her, and Whimsicality and others then founded the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]].{{cite:thundderr-oral-history|on the November 2017 split}}

The guild's own channels bear that out, and go further. Asked in the general channel on 3 November what had happened, AurumKitsune said that someone had challenged her position, that she had demoted and removed them, and that they had taken most of their friends with them, confirming when asked directly that it was Whimsicality; another member the same evening recorded that Whimsicality had been demoted and that everyone had been removed from the guild's original Discord, which is why a replacement server had to be built.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-november-2017-discord-private|general channel, 3 Nov 2017}} The two documents are both right about different people: one officer was removed, and her allies left with her — and the departing group kept the old server, which is what the guild's own remark about being locked out of its Discord refers to.

Two reasons were given the same day, seven hours apart. In the early afternoon AurumKitsune announced the ban and described Whimsicality's motive as a belief that [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]]' leader would ruin the guild; late that evening she gave her own justification, that her position had been challenged.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-november-2017-discord-private|general channel, 3 Nov 2017}} The event log's ground — that the officers pressed her to hand the guild over — is the evening statement from her side, not a competing charge.

The documents' one-day disagreement has an ordinary possible cause: the channel stamps its times seven hours behind the international standard in early November — daylight saving did not end until the 5th that year — so that evening falls on 3 November as recorded and on the 4th once the offset is applied.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-november-2017-discord-private|timestamps, 3 Nov 2017}} How either document was compiled is not recorded, so that is an explanation rather than a reconciliation.

The founding is attested outside the guild: SNK stood in the Coalition’s roster at the declaration of war seven weeks later{{cite:drew1011-storytime|the rosters at the declaration of war, 21 Dec 2017}}, and the War Syndicate charter names ElegantDeath, one of the three the log says were removed, as its leader.{{cite:gdoc-1kdasl6eq7y_zssy|War Syndicate charter, list of allies}}

AurumKitsune passed the crown to [[thundderr|Thundderr]] on 22 November 2017 and resumed it in January 2018 on her return.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017 and Jan 2018}}{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-22-17}}

The guild's channels neither support nor contradict that date. Its leadership and voting channels were effectively closed for the fortnight, so no formal record exists either way; its general channel carried its heaviest traffic of the period on 22 November and mentions no handover; and two days later a member asked Thundderr whether he was king and joked about his progress towards it, with the monarch and another member using deliberately junior titles for him on the 26th.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-november-2017-discord-private|general channel, 22–26 Nov 2017}} The banter proves nothing on its own in a guild whose members joked about ranks constantly, but a guild's minutes and a guild's chat are not two witnesses to the same thing: one records what was decided, the other what people happened to say, and a handover can be minuted and never mentioned.

Her own announcement that evening put it differently, naming no king: "I am the leader and one of the creators of the guild and have been leading for 2 months now, but due to some complications I will be stepping down and leaving @Page Paige in charge."{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-public-announcements|11/22/2017}} Page Paige wrote almost every guild announcement for the two months that followed.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|23 Nov 2017 to 12 Jan 2018}}

### The channel, 2017–18

The guild ran the Prime Minister it had brought from [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] as a standing institution, elected every two months over a week — three days to register, three to campaign, one to vote — open to any member of the gentry.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|11/23/2017}} Elections were called in November and again in December.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|11/23/2017 and 12/11/2017}}

On 20 December 2017 Page Paige made captains of anyone who wanted to war, "[s]ince we are warring often nowadays", and the next day posted "Coalition is now attacking gavel, if any of you would like to help out. This is war!"{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|12/20/2017 and 12/21/2017}} Over Christmas the guild ran a weekly Saturday grinding event jointly with Kingdom Foxes, its start time settled by a poll of the members.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|12/22/2017 and 12/24/2017}}

On 11 January 2018 Drew1011 told the guild that "[a] disgruntled ex chief has kicked a few people from the guild", and Page Paige spent the day inviting them back.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|1/11/2018}} Ten days later AurumKitsune closed the subject: "Please refrain from talking about the incident that happened about a week ago... Talking about this may result in consequences."{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|1/21/2018}}

About fifteen members had been removed that day, and the [[coalition|Coalition]]'s own Discord server went the same evening, deleted by the guild's former monarch and rebuilt within the minute.{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|11–12 Jan 2018}} The removals were reversed fifty-six minutes after the deletion; the affair is set out at [[the-coalition-discord-deletion|the Coalition Discord deletion]].{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|12 Jan 2018, 05:16 UTC}}

She tried twice more to hand the guild on. On 1 February she offered it outright — "I am giving away the guild to someone, if you would be interested tag or pm me" — and the next day revised the plan: the person chosen "will now become the Viceroy instead of King/Queen and I will stay as Queen as more of a figurehead", to be someone already in the guild "who I can trust".{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|2/1/2018 and 2/2/2018}} [[drew1011|Drew1011]] was crowned King Consort a week later.

The channel also fixes the guild’s alliance moves to the day. "[P]hx is gonna be leaving coa" on 1 February 2018; "also we rejoined coa" on the 8th; and in the [[the-federation|Federation]] by 30 March.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|2/1/2018, 2/8/2018 and 3/30/2018}}

## War Syndicate and the Coalition

KingdomPhoenixes joined [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] and left it over the leadership episode above{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L856–863}}. Weeks later, in mid-October 2017, the guild co-founded the [[coalition|Coalition]] with Kingdom Foxes; Gilded Sparrows joined third and House of Sentinels fourth{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L869}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Oct 2017 entry}}.

![Discord message from the KingdomPhoenixes parliament channel, author "King ElegantDeath": "Now I know you all hate Fox, but they are the enemy of our somewhat enemy, Tnt / I'm somewhat thinking about a temporary alliance with them purely for the sake of elimination of BCr".](/images/chronicles/storytime/41-image.webp)

The guild held mainland territory when the Coalition took the whole Wynn province on 23 November 2017, and was on the alliance's roster at the declaration of war on 21 December 2017{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L927–941}}. It left the alliance on 1 February 2018 and rejoined on the 8th, and Drew1011 was crowned King Consort on the 9th{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Feb 2018}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1033, composed 11 Jul 2018}}, and the division of Wynn announced on 16 February 2018 assigned it "Mid canyon"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|screenshot of the announcement of 16 Feb 2018}}, 24 territories{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}}.

One week of March 2018 shows what a single representative cost the guild inside [[the-federation|the Federation]]. It had one active member in the alliance's leadership channel and no co-leader, and that member left the alliance's Discord in the first week of March.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|early Mar 2018, the departure}} On the 10th other leaders noticed the absence and could not say why.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, the absence noticed}} During the map ratification the same day the guild was refused canyon territory, the alliance's founder saying that its only active member did not have time to war and another leader answering that in that case it got none.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, the canyon refused}} On the 11th a member proposed adding it to a motion expelling two landless guilds, noting that removing it would free fifteen territories.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|11 Mar 2018, the proposal}} Another said its leader should be given one last chance, and the motion posted the next day did not name it.{{cite:federation-offices-and-roles-march-2018-discord-private|11–12 Mar 2018, the last chance}} On the 13th the member returned and explained the last piece: it was better that the alliance's founder set the ballots up, because if she did it her guild would not get a vote at all.{{cite:federation-ballot-seeding-march-2018-discord-private|13 Mar 2018, the KingdomPhoenixes answer}} One account could build a ballot or vote in one and not both, so within four days the guild could not vote, could not hold canyon ground and had been one line in somebody else's motion away from expulsion; reading the episodes together is this article's. How the ballots were built is at [[federation-ballots-march-2018|the Federation's ballots in March 2018]].

Its [[the-federation|Federation]] allocation fell through the spring: the South Canyon in the alliance's first assignment of 21 February 2018, then 15 territories on 10 March, 23 on 24 March, 13 on 22 April, 11 on 10 May, and none at all on 4 June.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|2/21, 3/10, 3/24, 4/22, 5/10 and 6/4/2018}} On 25 June 2018 the alliance announced that the guild had left it, alongside [[paladins-united|Paladins United]].{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 6/25/2018}} No readmission was ever announced, and by the middle of September its own members could not say whether they were in the alliance or not.{{cite:kingdom-phoenixes-september-2018-discord-private|14 Sep 2018}} There was no notice for them to be out of date about: the guild's welcome channel held a rules card and a card of links, posted eleven seconds apart on 13 January 2018 and both revised the following June, and neither named an alliance.{{cite:standing-documents-as-retrospection-discord-private|Kingdom of Phoenixes welcome channel, 13 Jan and 18 Jun 2018}}

Writing after the collapse of November 2018, Drew1011 credited AurumKitsune with "setting up the discord and coming up with things such as the 2/3 majority voting rule"{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}.

## The February 2018 walkout

[[whimsicality|Whimsicality]], one of the guild's two co-founders, returned to it as a co-leader on 13 April 2018 after her removal in November 2017 — the same month she took ownership of [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], so that by early May members were describing her and [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] as running one guild each.{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|4/13/2018}}{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|April–May 2018}}

KingdomPhoenixes left the [[coalition|Coalition]] on the evening of 16 February 2018, its leader confirming the departure as official in the alliance's guild-leaders channel; members counting the withdrawals that night and the following morning list it among them.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition guild-leaders channel, 16 Feb 2018}}

Its reason was not the one that took the other guilds out. Minutes before confirming the departure, its leader said in the same channel that the Coalition was finished, that its collapse let her do what she had been intending to do anyway, that she could not revive KingdomPhoenixes at that point, and that the guild's war force amounted to little more than herself.{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Coalition guild-leaders channel, 16 Feb 2018}} The redistribution that the other departures turned on does not appear in her account.

It was back inside the successor alliance within a day. Its leader was posting in [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s guild-leaders channel on 17 February, arguing two days later about which guilds should be kept; the guild appears on the remnant's list of new allies on the 17th{{cite:coalition-announcements|2/17/2018}} and held the South Canyon in the Federation's first territory assignment on the 21st, recorded as satisfied with the allocation.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 2/21/2018}}{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|Federation channels, 17–21 Feb 2018}} No readmission vote was ever recorded.

## Structure

The guild's ranks were a copy of the Kingdom of Foxes' arrangement of titles over in-game ranks. Its leaders were a King or Queen holding the owner rank and the power to override any decision, a Prince or Princess as heir, a Viceroy or Vicereine as second-in-command, and an elected Prime Minister who carried the gentry's concerns to parliament. Beneath them ran a nobility of dukes, marquises, earls, viscounts and barons — the last three serving as head, senior and junior regional managers — and a gentry of baronets, knights, squires and pages.{{cite:gdoc-1q2iebjuyn91dxov|Structure of Phx}}

Lego_DW answered [[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s tribute on 13 November 2018 asking recognition for "the absolute gods of war this alliance created" — himself, 21(n), [[goden|Goden]], _Antho74_, InnerJoker, 0x7cf and snowy — who "along with too many others to credit, were the ones that really held the alliance together in terms of war power".{{cite:thread-237070|post #18, Lego_DW, 13 Nov 2018}} It is the only list of [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s war leaders anywhere in the record.

In April 2020 he gave the alliance's genealogy differently from the accounts around it: "Coa never technically 'beat' WS rather when AA split from coa, Coa and WS merged to wipe a common enemy, this was a creation of fed."{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}} His conclusion — that the Federation was a [[coalition|Coalition]]–[[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] merger — matches the rest of the record; his premise that no wipe of War Syndicate occurred does not.

His forum profile records guild offices between October 2017 and July 2020: chief of The Mage Legacy and of Sins of Seedia, and owner of ZephraShredders.{{cite:wynncraft-forum-profiles|Lego_DW, member 88629}}

lotuss led Sins of Seedia, one of the three guilds that created the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] inside [[the-federation|the Federation]] on 25 March 2018.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

He posted the pact's public thread on 5 June 2018, describing Aesir as "an alliance, or if you will sister-ship pact, between 4 warring and growing community guilds".{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} The thread gives the pact's own origin story — [[fantasy|Fantasy]] and Sins of Seedia became friends during the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] era, were separated when Fantasy entered the [[coalition|Coalition]] and Sins of Seedia warred against it, and were reunited inside the Federation — and names two leaders for each member guild.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

His guild's co-leader [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]] is credited by [[drew1011|Drew1011]] as the first to accept the merger proposal that created the Federation.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

## History

### Formation
Luna was formed on 14 Feb 2019 by [[Imperial]], [[Emorians]], Blacklisted, BuildCraftia and others, explicitly to counter [[SOL]], the bloc left standing after [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s fall.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The community timeline lists [[Kingdom Foxes]] among the founders, but Luna's founding guilds were taking ground from Fox three weeks before the alliance existed and went on taking it through its first fortnight.{{cite:territory-exchanges|exchanges with Kingdom Foxes on one side and Imperial, Emorians, Blacklisted or BuildCraftia on the other, 25 Jan – 20 Feb 2019 UTC: first on 27 Jan 2019, then on every day from 13 to 19 February. Raw — no free-for-all list was published within ninety days of the window, so none can be subtracted}}

### The war on Kingdom Foxes
From 15 Feb 2019 Luna fought Kingdom Foxes across more than 300 territories; Imperial alone attacked Fox 660 times.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with Imperial as attacker and Kingdom Foxes as defender, 16 Feb – 8 Jul 2019 UTC: 660; distinct territories with Kingdom Foxes on either side over the same window: 381. Raw — no free-for-all list was published within ninety days of the window, so none can be subtracted}} The war ended when Fox joined Luna on 8 Jul 2019 — the day after the Treaty of Ternaves, in which Fox, [[The Simple Ones]] and ThisIsMurica divided the territory of the dissolved Celestial Tigers.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

### Full map control
After fending off an attack on Kingdom Foxes in July 2019, Luna wiped every guild on the map except [[Avicia]]; Avicia joined on 17 Jul 2019, and Luna held the entire map.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

{{map:2019-07-17|Luna at full map control}}

### Luna as the Valkyrie bloc
[[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]], writing on the opposing side in September 2019, described not a new alliance but a renaming: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians" broke a summer raid on Kingdom Foxes, took the map in under two days, and thereafter appears in his account as "the Valkyrie alliance, now calling themselves the Luna alliance".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” to “ASSAULTS ON BCR”, 14 Sep 2019}} He blames the raid's failure on Valkyrie's "controversial use of sub guilds", by which main-guild members "could defend land more quickly by branching into sub guilds", and names Blacklisted and BuildCraftia as the first defectors, followed by Avicia and The Simple Ones.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” and “THE FORMATION OF LUNA”, 14 Sep 2019}}

The renaming account matches Luna's role as the public war-fighting face of the [[Valkyrie]] network{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, but not the recorded dates: Luna formed in February 2019 against SOL, while Arkada places the bloc's emergence after the midsummer raid and counts Imperial and [[Paladins United]] as long-standing Valkyrie members, though their Valkyrie membership is first recorded in September 2019.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} The discrepancy is set out on the [[imperial|Imperial]] and Paladins United pages.

### Revolt and collapse
On 29 Aug 2019, after a leadership dispute, Emorians and Avicia left Luna and declared war on Imperial, spiralling into a large war over Gavel; ThisIsMurica was kicked the next day for sending fighters, and [[Terra]] formed in the chaos on 30 Aug.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Arkada adds a cause for the Emorians' turn from neutral exile to belligerent: Luna "seized all of its lands" after the departure, which he judged "a large mistake", since it made the Emorians sympathetic to the resistance.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“A RAY OF HOPE”, 14 Sep 2019}} In the Luna–Terra war of 7–19 Sep 2019, The Simple Ones defected to Terra on 8 Sep and Terra took map control the same day{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} — over 2,000 exchanges swept across 322 territories in ten days.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} A week of Luna counter-raids failed, and on 14 Sep 2019 Luna mounted an organised counter-raid that Terra had been warned of by a spy. Arkada wrote the same day: "In the morning, Luna struck, but we struck harder. In the late afternoon, Luna struck again, but we struck even harder."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“LUNA'S RETALIATION”, 14 Sep 2019}} Kingdom Foxes left on the 18th, and Luna collapsed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

The operation that ended Luna's map control was a single coordinated multi-guild raid on 7 September 2019, which wiped its principal target and much of the alliance within roughly twelve to sixteen hours; by the following day Luna's core guilds had been pushed entirely off the territory map.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|the raid of 7 Sep 2019}} Two things surfaced during the raid: [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] negotiated a separate non-aggression deal in the middle of it, giving up specific territory claims in exchange for being left alone, and another revealed that it had been informing for the attacking coalition since that coalition's founding.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|the raid of 7 Sep 2019}}

The alliance reconstituted itself that autumn. Its guilds regrouped as [[artemis|Artemis]], founded on 30 October 2019 by Imperial, Paladins United and Caeruleum Order — all three Luna members weeks earlier — and expanded with three further guilds over the following week.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|2 Nov 2019}} [[terra|Terra]]'s members treated the new alliance as Luna under another name, and Artemis raided Terra on 2 November.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|2 Nov 2019}}

## Membership
At its July–August 2019 peak Luna had ten member guilds at once.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

{{alliance:Luna}}

## Legacy
Luna's fall handed the map to Terra, whose core went on to found the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]]. Luna itself was the war-fighting face of the much older [[Valkyrie]] community network.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Background

[[Luna]] had [[luna-gains-full-map-control|held the entire map]] since 17 Jul 2019, but the [[emorians-and-avicia-revolt|revolt of Emorians and Avicia]] on 29 Aug cracked it open, and on 30 Aug [[Terra]] formed in opposition{{cite:community-guild-timeline|17 Jul, 29 and 30 Aug 2019 entries}} — a bloc of roughly a dozen guilds including TheNoLifes, [[Titans Valor]], [[DiamondDeities]], [[Fantasy]] and Paladins United. Terra's roster was never published{{cite:territory-exchanges|Terra's roster reconstructed from guild activity windows}}.

## The nine days before

The coalition's opening strategy was disputed the day after it formed. On 30 August 2019 a leader of [[emorians|Emorians]] told Terra's advisors that two attempts to drive [[imperial|Imperial]] off the map had already shown the coalition could neither do it nor hold the result, and proposed taking a weaker Luna guild instead and holding its ground as though it had already been allocated — control of territory rather than destruction of a guild.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|advisors' channel, 30 Aug 2019}} Terra's ambassador answered that the first attempt was a day old, that it had fallen on an awkward day of the week, that not every guild had heard yet, and that the same thing had been done before with fewer guilds — the reason for failure being inconsistency rather than impossibility.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|advisors' channel, 30 Aug 2019}} The Emorians leader's reply was that opening on a guild whose allies ranked high would fail over and over.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|advisors' channel, 30 Aug 2019}}

The map recorded both halves of the argument. Territory taken from Imperial ran to 253 captures on 29 August and 243 on the 30th, then fell away through the first week of September.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with Imperial as defender, daily, 29 Aug – 6 Sep 2019, UTC; no free-for-all list was published for the window, so nothing is netted out}} It reached three on the 6th, taken by two guilds; on the 7th it was 448, taken by twenty-eight.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with Imperial as defender, 6 and 7 Sep 2019, UTC; same window, nothing netted out}} Reading the figures against the argument is this article's.

The operation was run through spearhead guilds, each leading a set of others, with a written planning post as the authoritative version and an hour's notice to the alliance before it opened.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 6 Sep 2019}} It survived a substitution the day before. The leader of [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]], who was directing it, told the leadership channel that he would be away for part of it; MasterWynnLords' leader pointed out that DiamondDeities was the spearhead his guild and FinalFront were going in with, and asked who would lead them.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 6 Sep 2019}} The role was reassigned to another guild, DiamondDeities dropping back to supporting Emorians, and the change was to be edited into the planning post rather than announced.{{cite:terra-before-the-raid-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 6 Sep 2019}}

## Course of the war

The decisive fighting ran 7–19 Sep 2019{{cite:community-guild-timeline|7 Sep 2019 entry}}, and 12,516 territory exchanges across 364 territories fell in the ten days from the 6th{{cite:territory-exchanges|6–16 Sep 2019, UTC}}. The fighting was spread across the map rather than concentrated on the ground that churned anyway: the forty busiest territories took 37% of those exchanges, against 67% in the last ten days of July, when Luna held everything.{{cite:territory-exchanges|top-40 territory share, 6–16 Sep against 20–30 Jul 2019, UTC}} No list of territories open to all was published for either window, the last enumerated one having appeared in October 2018; [[terra|Terra]] declared eighteen on 14 September 2019, a week after the raid, and maintained the list into December.{{cite:federation-public-announcements|Drew1011, 10/12/2018}}{{cite:terra-alliance-announcements-discord-private|14 Sep – 11 Dec 2019}} Neither figure here is netted against a declaration.

### The raid of 7 September

The attack was planned as a scheduled event. It was fixed for midday, expected to run for several days, and when the lead organiser became unavailable a vote to postpone it was started and overruled by the rest of the leadership.{{cite:foxes-imperial-2019-discord-private|September 2019}} Which noon was meant went unrecorded.

The map turned over at four in the afternoon UTC. Exchanges had run at about sixty an hour through the day; they reached 174 in that hour, peaked at 361 and 364 between six and nine in the evening, and stayed above a hundred until eight the next morning — 3,482 exchanges across 325 territories in sixteen hours.{{cite:territory-exchanges|hourly counts, 7 Sep 16:00 – 8 Sep 08:00 UTC}}

An hour before it began, [[imperial|Imperial]] held 76 territories, [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] 71, [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] 67, Blacklisted 47 and [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] 39; by nine the next morning Imperial held one and the other three held seven apiece, and by midday on the 9th those three held none at all.{{cite:territory-exchanges|holdings from the last exchange on each territory before 7 Sep 15:00, 8 Sep 09:00 and 9 Sep 12:00 UTC}} Kingdom Foxes came out of it with sixty-eight, having agreed a separate non-aggression deal while the operation was still running.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Sep 2019}}

Arkada's account, written a week afterwards, has the raid ending in nearly six hours in "the complete wipe of all Luna guilds except Kingdom Foxes".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}

The turning point came within a day: on 8 Sep [[The Simple Ones]] defected from Luna to Terra, and Terra took control of the map that same day{{cite:community-guild-timeline|8 Sep 2019 entry}}.

{{map:2019-09-08|The map as Terra took control}}

Luna fought on for another ten days until [[Kingdom Foxes]] left on 18 Sep, and the alliance collapsed{{cite:community-guild-timeline|18 Sep 2019 entry}}.

## Aftermath

Victory dissolved the victor almost as fast as the vanquished. On 15 Sep, mid-war, Terra's core founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]]{{cite:community-guild-timeline|15 Sep 2019 entry}}; Terra itself [[terra-falls|fell]] on 2 Nov 2019{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image}}, seven weeks after taking the map.

Terra spent the fortnight after the raid settling rather than fighting, and by 21 September its ambassador reckoned that about forty territories had passed out of the alliance's hands through departures, with six more taken and another twenty expected to follow.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|21 Sep 2019}} How the war was wound up is treated in [[the-terra-settlement|the Terra settlement]].

## The victors' account

The alliance corrected itself faster than it congratulated itself. At 22:11 on the night of the raid a member told the war channel that [[luna|Luna]] was practically wiped{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 22:11 on 7 Sep 2019, the claim of a wipe}}; the ambassador answered a minute later that it was on its way and that [[imperial|Imperial]] had to be warred consistently.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 22:12 on 7 Sep 2019, the correction}} Half an hour earlier a member had reported [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] and [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] attacking Terra ground at Ragni and asked for help.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 7 Sep 2019, the attack at Ragni}} Earlier that evening the ambassador had told the channel that Raiju's, SbN's and Corsairs' claims were wrecked{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 18:05 on 7 Sep 2019, the wrecked claims}}, and that BuildCraftia was refusing to help because Imperial had attacked BuildCraftia's own claims without asking or warning, as part of an anti-wipe strategy.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 18:05 on 7 Sep 2019, BuildCraftia's refusal}} That last is Terra's account of a quarrel inside the alliance it was destroying.

Who had planned the operation was disputed in public four days later. On 11 September ThisIsMurica's leader told the general channel that the war planner's plan had been to attack Imperial and nothing more, and that he and two other leaders had turned it into a full wipe{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|alliance-general channel, 17:53 on 11 Sep 2019}}, listing the attack on [[paladins-united|Paladins United]], the wiping of Corsairs and SbN, and the wiping of Paladins United with [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]].{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|alliance-general channel, 11 Sep 2019, the list of operations}} The war planner answered that his plan had extended, that those actions had been under his command, and that the attack on Imperial had been organised by him alone though he gave the credit to everybody.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|alliance-general channel, 11 Sep 2019, the planner's answer}} A third leader told him to share the credit; a fourth said the plan had amounted to attacking Imperial and negotiating a deal.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|alliance-general channel, 11 Sep 2019, the other two leaders}} How wide the plan had been was never agreed by the people who fought it.

Peace with the enemy's second guild collapsed over one territory. On the evening of 10 September the ambassador told the war channel that Paladins United had chosen the violent option against generous terms, and that the negotiator it sent had wanted to compromise and tried hard{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 10 Sep 2019}}; its other chiefs, he said, were too proud to make peace without extracting a consequence.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 10 Sep 2019, the account of the guild's chiefs}} Their final counteroffer was to make Avos Temple a free-for-all and keep the rest.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 10 Sep 2019, the counteroffer}}

An enemy count moved by tens within the hour. At three in the afternoon of 27 September, on the export's clock of UTC-07:00, the discord-management lead told the war channel that the enemy alliance stood at forty territories, naming Paladins United in Corkus, Imperial in Aldorei and BuildCraftia in Wynn{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 15:00 on 27 Sep 2019}}; forty seconds later the ambassador corrected him to thirty-two or thirty-three.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 15:01 on 27 Sep 2019, the correction}} At 22:00 UTC that day those three guilds held twenty-four territories between them, two by midnight and thirty by the middle of the following morning.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Imperial, Paladins United and BuildCraftia holdings from the last exchange on each territory at 22:00 on 27 Sep and 00:00 and 11:38 on 28 Sep 2019, UTC; holdings include the free-for-all ground declared 14 Sep 2019 as amended, whose names are held outside this repository}} Neither figure given in the channel matches the log, and which guilds the count covered was never written down.

The alliance dated its enemy's break-up from Discord roles rather than from territory. On 25 September a member told the leadership channel that Blacklisted had left Luna{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 07:03 on 25 Sep 2019}}; asked how he knew, the discord-management lead answered that none of the guild's members held roles in the enemy's server any more, as had happened with [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and others.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 25 Sep 2019, the method}} Blacklisted and Lunatic Mox had both gone overnight and Mox was already neutral{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 25 Sep 2019, the two departures}}, and another leader cautioned that Paladins United still held about half of Corkus.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 25 Sep 2019, the caution about Corkus}}

What the war had been for was answered twice, and not the same way. On 15 September ThisIsMurica's leader posted a farewell to the leadership channel saying his objective was complete, and that the reason he had come to warring was that [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] held power and it no longer did.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 18:58 on 15 Sep 2019}} His guild could function without him, he added, and he had been considering leaving for three months.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 15 Sep 2019, the succession}} Six weeks later, asked in the war channel why [[emorians|Emorians]] was not with Luna, one of its leaders said the guild had left Luna without telling them first and had been kicked from Valkyrie for it{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 16:55 on 28 Oct 2019}}, and that [[the-simple-ones|The Simple Ones]], ThisIsMurica and [[avicia|Avicia]] came with it and Terra was formed.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 28 Oct 2019, the three guilds}} He said in the same conversation that Terra had offered the enemy the whole of Corkus at the wipe and been refused.{{cite:terra-accounting-for-the-war-2019-discord-private|war channel, 28 Oct 2019, the Corkus offer}}

## The record

The guild's name and its tag did not match: it was called Lunatic and carried the tag Mox, and it appears in rosters and in the alliances of 2019 as Lunatic [Mox].{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|naming, 2018–2019}} Its leader introduced himself in alliance channels as the leader of Lunatic, also known as Mox, and its members were written variously as Lunatic, Lunatics and Lunotic. The mismatch was noticed at the time — a member asked outright in August 2018 why Lunatic's tag was Mox, and got no serious answer.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|August 2018}}

Four things a page would want are missing. The founding is given as a month and never a day; no disbandment was ever recorded; no founding roster survives; and the guild is never recorded holding territory under its own name for any length of time before its Federation assignment.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|the silence in the record}}

## History

### Founding (April 2018)
The guild was founded in April 2018, a date two members placed there independently — one saying in May that it had been made about a month earlier, another recalling in August that it was made in April.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|founding, April 2018}} The captures logged at the time agree: its players first warred under the guild's name on 28 April 2018, and it took its first recorded territories on 8 May.{{cite:corkus-contested-2018-discord-private|first wars 28 Apr 2018, first territories 8 May 2018}} It came out of [[imperial|Imperial]]: its leader said the founders had started a riot inside that guild and then created their own, and a second leader said the guild had been born from Imperial before the general exodus that emptied it out.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|guild origins}} A member of the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] separately claimed the guild as one of Fox's children, and was corrected in the same exchange by one of its leaders.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|guild origins}}

Who founded it is not settled. The leader known as yule said repeatedly that he had created it and that his alt account owned the guild; a leader in another alliance said in October 2019 that [[sheepn|Sheepn]] had made it, and that yule and lego had led it with him.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|founding accounts, 2018–2019}} Sheepn's connection to the guild does not rest on that account: the alliance's war-tracking bot logged a series of war transitions for him under the guild's name on 3 May 2018, generated from game state rather than from anyone's recollection.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|war-tracking bot, 3 May 2018}} The three are consistently described together as its founding leadership, and nothing in the record orders them.

### The Federation (May–August 2018)
[[the-federation|The Federation]] admitted the guild on 9 May 2018, and the admission went badly: an initial vote went against it, and a revote followed after new information and confusion over whether the two-thirds threshold had been met.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|admission, 9 May 2018}}

Almost everything recorded afterwards is a complaint. A member guild filed a formal accusation of poaching in the alliance's general channel in late May 2018, naming the guild as the chief offender in recruiting members away from allies; a separate approach from another guild raised a Mox-affiliated player harassing its officers; and by June its most prominent recruiter had been banned from the Federation's Discord server.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|May–June 2018}} A Federation-wide vote on expelling the guild was held on 12 June 2018 and failed; it had been prompted by a member the guild had already removed for disrespectful behaviour, and the guild leader who initiated it left the alliance afterwards.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|12 Jun 2018}} In the same week a figure associated with a third member guild was found to have paid the leader of an enemy guild to target Mox, and left his own guild once it was discovered.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|June 2018}} Four separate quarrels inside one alliance in six weeks turned on the same guild, and the alliance kept it.

Its own leadership was thinly held. Its leader stepped back for about a month from mid-June 2018, for reasons outside the game, appointing lego as interim leader; by late July members were openly unsure who led it, one member holding the title without evidently exercising it, and a founding member left abruptly at the end of the month.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|June–July 2018}} Its territory grievance was Nesaak: the leader complained formally in the alliance's leaders channel in July 2018 that the assignments were unfair and had pushed the guild into contested Nesaak land, and it swapped assigned territory with [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] in the alliance's full remap that August.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|July–August 2018}}

As members described the arrangement in August 2018, the guild sat inside a network of subguilds: The Divine Swords had been a Mox subguild and was independent of it by then, LE Flowers and Aphelion were named as subguilds beneath the DiamondDeities and Mox structure, and a Mox splinter guild was blamed that month for wiping another Federation guild's assigned territories overnight while none of its members were online.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|August 2018}}

The alliance's founder went over the campaign against the guild in October 2018 and set a limit on it. On the 14th a member of the war channel said the guild's leader had faced an attempt to hire [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] against his guild, a motion to put it out of the alliance, and sustained criticism.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|14 Oct 2018, the three things listed}} The founder confirmed the attempted inducement and the motion, and made a point of the limit: one leader had acted alone rather than the leadership acting together, though several leaders had been openly critical of the guild and its leader.{{cite:changing-sides-as-remembered-2018-discord-private|14 Oct 2018, the founder's qualification}} He did not name the man. In the account given at the time the payment had been made rather than attempted, and the person who made it was not described as a guild leader.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|June 2018}}

### Odysseia, and the shell (August 2018)
The guild was emptied rather than destroyed. On 24 August 2018 its leadership and active members left it, together with those of Ex Nihilo, to found a combined guild called Odysseia; a participant described the mechanics plainly — nearly every active member was moved across the moment the new guild existed, and the outgoing leader was left behind with what remained. Members of the new guild called it a second Mox.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|24 Aug 2018}}

What happened to the shell is contested, and the guild's own leader argues both sides. At the end of August 2018 members in the alliance channel said Mox had left, and its territories were put on hold rather than reassigned.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|late August 2018}} Six months later, asked directly in another alliance's channel whether the guild had been expelled for low activity, the same leader said the real reason was that he had kept Mox inside the Federation after Odysseia had joined it — the near-empty guild still in the room — and acknowledged that this could fairly be called spying and that he had been doing something he should not have. A second leader of the guild answered that another guild had done the same without anyone minding.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|March 2019}}

### The departure recorded in a strike-through (31 August 2018)

The guild stopped fighting before it stopped existing. Its last day of territory exchanges in August was the 25th, when it took forty-seven territories and lost forty-seven; from then until the small hours of 1 September it made no capture and lost none.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Lunatic captures made and suffered by day, 20 Aug – 30 Sep 2018 UTC, raw — the declaration in force from 30 August was published as a map and its territories cannot be named}} The log ran through those days unbroken, so the silence was the guild's.{{cite:territory-exchanges|runs of days carrying no rows since 2018: none between 25 Aug and 1 Sep 2018}}

The alliance recorded the departure inside a document about something else. At 18:48 on 31 August 2018 a member put a motion to the voting channel setting out that the leader they had believed was taking Lunatic over would not be handling it, that all its active fighters had gone to the new guild, that another member guild's alternate account owned it, and that it could not reclaim its territories.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the motion as posted}} He called this a good opportunity to let go of guilds that could not hold their own.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the argument}} The motion proposed expelling two guilds, and was revised eight seconds after it went up, the half naming Lunatic struck through and replaced by a note that the guild had left of its own accord.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the edit and what it struck}} That strike-through was the alliance's only contemporaneous statement of the fact, and it sits inside a document about something else. The surviving half, on Kasai Shinrai, carried; its tally is at [[federation-ballots-august-2018|the Federation's ballots in August 2018]].{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the surviving half}}

The membership had not been told and found out by asking. At 19:42 a member asked the war channel whether Lunatic was still in the Federation and was told it was not.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the question}} Another asked why nothing had been announced, and a third said there had better be an announcement, because the guild was at that moment attacking them in Llevigar.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the complaint}} A fourth asked why the guild's role was still standing in the alliance's own Discord.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the role}} The announcements channel carried a single sentence at 19:50 clarifying that the guild had left, eight minutes after the complaint.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the clarification}}

The complaint can be timed against the map. The alliance's messages are stamped seven hours behind the capture log, so 19:42 on the 31st is 02:42 on 1 September there, and in the twenty minutes either side of it Lunatic took Llevigar Entrance, Llevigar and Llevigar Gate East from [[emorians|Emorians]].{{cite:territory-exchanges|Lunatic captures from Emorians at Llevigar, 1 Sep 2018 02:23, 02:34 and 02:44 UTC}} Eighteen exchanges were the whole of the guild's activity between 25 August and the end of September: two at Hive against [[thenolifes|TheNoLifes]], twelve at the four Llevigar territories against Emorians, and four in which [[odysseia|Odysseia]] — the guild its own fighters had walked into a week earlier — took all four off it between 04:12 and 04:19.{{cite:territory-exchanges|complete Lunatic record, 26 Aug – 30 Sep 2018 UTC: 18 exchanges, all on 1 Sep}} How much of that night was fought on open ground cannot be established: the declaration in force was published as a map with the free-for-all ground shown rather than listed, and no Llevigar territory appears on any list the alliance wrote out in text during 2018.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|the free-for-all declaration of 8/30/2018, published as a map}}

The same evening the leadership channel argued about whether guilds in that condition should be removed at all. A guild leader set out the case against: an expelled guild is one more potential enemy, and both [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] and [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] had been thought finished and had campaigned as soon as they were outside.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the case for keeping}} The leader of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] answered that his own guild had withdrawn voluntarily when it went inactive rather than sit in the alliance as dead guilds did.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the answer}} The alliance's map-maker said the real difficulty with dead guilds was voting.{{cite:federation-lunatic-mox-departure-august-2018-discord-private|31 Aug 2018, the voting difficulty}} It was an argument advanced that evening and not the alliance's position.

### 2019
By September 2018 its remaining leader said the guild existed only nominally, and members of other guilds had been calling it dead for a fortnight.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|August–September 2018}} It did not stay written off. It was proposed as a member of [[the-consortium|the Consortium]] in March 2019, and by September 2019 it was fighting as part of [[luna|Luna]], raiding [[terra|Terra]] territory across Corkus, Ragni, Nesaak and Cinfras over several days.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|March–September 2019}}

On 21 September 2019 it declared neutrality and left Luna, without putting the decision to a vote of the alliance's guild leaders, which at least one of them criticised.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|21 Sep 2019}} In the weeks that followed Terra's leadership transferred contested territory to it as part of a neutrality arrangement, without telling the allied guild whose income that land had been supporting, and a member of a third guild announced he intended to attack it regardless, through a separate guild he controlled, on the argument that the neutrality did not bind him.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|autumn 2019}}

In October 2019 one of its founding leaders left the game abruptly, leaving yule and lego as its leadership; the leaders of the opposing alliance treated the loss as a serious blow to the guild.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|October 2019}} On 2 November 2019 [[artemis|Artemis]] took it in, when Luna rebranded and expanded alongside its original members.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|2 Nov 2019}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It was not recorded active after that month, and what became of it is not known.{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|November 2019}}

## Alliances

- [[the-federation|Federation]] — 9 May to late August 2018{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|admission, 9 May 2018}}{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|late August 2018}}
- [[the-consortium|The Consortium]] — proposed as a member, March 2019{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|March 2019}}
- [[luna|Luna]] — by September 2019, to 21 September 2019{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|September 2019}}
- [[artemis|Artemis]] — from 2 November 2019{{cite:lunatic-mox-guild-profile-discord-private|2 Nov 2019}}

Lux Imperius was announced in the guild subforum on 16 September 2016 by valvoid, posting under the name xMC_Master11x{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Lux Imperius! Community Alliance!, valvoid, 16 Sep 2016}}, as an alliance "founded by @xMC_Master11x, @motoki1, @BlackbirdMC, @Loxotus, and @Arkam initially for war and community purposes. Lux Imperius is now a community alliance that values honor, prestige, and respect."{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} It sits among the cluster of non-war alliances that formed in [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]] alongside [[halcyon|Halcyon]], [[seraphim|Seraphim]] and [[aurelion|Aurelion]], while [[hackforums|HackForums]] and its partners held most of the territory map.

## History

The member guilds, with their leaders and founding dates, were: Dragon's Arise [DsA], "founded in July of 2016 by @xMC_Master11x"; UltimateXeons [UXs] under motoki1, "a Community Guild (Also Semi-War)"; Eternal Legacy [ETL], led by Commer after nicedoge509 and dated to 27 February 2015; WarLords [War] under Arkam; GrimNation [GrN] under MagicGum; and Beasts [BST] under Beastovrlrd.{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} Beasts was announced as a new member on 12 October 2016.{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #29, 12 Oct 2016}}

Membership was closed and deliberately kept small. "As lux imperius prefers to invite guilds without them asking we will look in about Forum Ninjas", Loxotus told one applicant{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #31, 12 Oct 2016}}; valvoid told another that "generally we don't let many guilds in as it is much harder to do events, it is less prestigious, etc."{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #37, 13 Oct 2016}} Both requests were refused on 15 October, because "the alliance would become too large".{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #48, 15 Oct 2016}} Asked why an alliance that admitted nobody kept a public thread at all, Yuno F Gasai answered for it: "So they could posts announcements and so that everybody will know they exist."{{cite:thread-153722-p03|posts #54 and #55, 16–17 Oct 2016}}

The thread nonetheless drew a response from the bloc that held the map. TheHipster posted a mock-declaration signed "BLACKLISTED" — "I see, so you plan to build an army of weaker powers to gain a foot against us... when you hear the drums of war, the only light to pass under the shadows of our steeds will be the fires of our guns"{{cite:thread-153722|post #16, 17 Sep 2016}} — which Yuno F Gasai read as confirmation of who felt threatened: "That short paragraph you wrote is what members of a powerhouse write when an alliance is made against them. The only current powerhouse is hax."{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #21, 18 Sep 2016}} A month later TheHipster disclaimed it as a joke{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #50, 16 Oct 2016}}, and the argument that followed set out [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]]'s place in that bloc.{{cite:thread-153722-p03|posts #49 and #52, 16 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p04|post #62, 20 Oct 2016}}

## Membership

As of 25 October 2016 the roster named six guilds: Dragon's Arise [DsA], UltimateXeons [UXs], Eternal Legacy [ETL], WarLords [War], GrimNation [GrN] and Beasts [BST].{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} Earlier that month it also included a seventh, Aquafinity [Aqu], "created by @Loxotus and @Wynncraftian on 9/2/16"; Loxotus described it as "allied since creation".{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #30, quoting the opening post, 12 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #38, 13 Oct 2016}} No departure was announced, and UltimateXeons' own recruitment thread still listed Aquafinity a year later, so whether the omission was a removal or an editing slip is unrecorded.{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, "Old alliances" list, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} The alliance predates machine-recorded alliance data, which begins in January 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Membership of one alliance did not preclude membership of another in this period. Dragon's Arise appears earlier in the year among the guilds of the Astrafteri Affinity, a bloc formed around January 2016 that [[hackforums|HackForums]] also joined.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L352–358, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} Lux Imperius itself appears to have taken no part in the territory war.

## The Ordo Malleus misattribution

UltimateXeons' recruitment thread carries an "Old alliances" section headed "(Lux Imperius)" and listing six tags — DsA, ETL, War, Aqu, GrN, BST.{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, "Old alliances" list, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} The list has been misread as the membership of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], because motoki1 announced joining Ordo Malleus in the same thread in February 2016.{{cite:thread-109350|post #7, motoki1, 20 Feb 2016}} The two rosters are unrelated: Ordo Malleus' only recorded roster is the twelve-guild list in the same thread's opening post, headed by the rule "Don't attack the territories that ally guilds own".{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} The six tags belong to Lux Imperius, not [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]].

## Legacy

No dissolution was ever recorded; the alliance's last recorded business, on 19 October 2016, is an Aquafinity event planned for December 2016, to which "All leaders of a guild in Lux Inperius is invited and is allowed to bring 1 friend."{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #60, 19 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p04|post #61, 19 Oct 2016}} By 30 November 2017 [[ultimatexeons|UltimateXeons]] had moved it to an "Old alliances" list and its own live alliance section read "None at the moment!"{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} Two members reappear later: Dragons Arise in [[aurelion|Aurelion]]{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}}, and Beasts under Beastovrlrd in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] of 2017.{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster}}

**Mr_Robin_Hood** opened the thread that created [[the-banhammer|The Banhammer]] on 8 June 2016, the first of two anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] alliances posted that month.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: The Banhammer (anti-hax), Mr_Robin_Hood, 8 Jun 2016}} His opening post gives the earliest hard territory count on record for [[hackforums|HackForums]] — "its that Hax currently owns 94 territories" — and the proposal it justified: "the only way for us to be able to beat them / is if all of the guilds unite!... we create one big alliance / where none of the guilds in the alliance attack eachother so that / even weaker guilds can hold territories."{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}}

He ran the alliance from a forum conversation, asking guild owners to message him directly{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}}, renamed the thread on the evening it was posted{{cite:thread-130386|post #16, 8 Jun 2016}}, and spent most of his subsequent posts defending it against the charge that it was a hate thread. "It was never intended to hate on HAX i know they are a hard working and honourfull guild," he wrote on 9 June. "its just that i think the smaller guilds could really benifit from an alliance because of how strong hax is right now."{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #26, 9 Jun 2016}} Asked why he singled out one guild, he answered with a comparison of holdings: "a bunch of guilds that have a lot of territories...... like who? TTZ with about 12% of what hax has? or WTh with a nice 3%?"{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #29, 9 Jun 2016}} His last recorded post, thanking a poster who had spoken up for the alliance, reads: "I was about to give up on this whole thing and you really saved my day."{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #40, 9 Jun 2016}}

His guild membership was never recorded, and nothing else about him is known.

**Naraka00** led [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] [BLA] with [[neonrider|NeonRider]] from the guild's creation on 19 January 2016, and kept its recruitment thread through 2016 and 2017.{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} Under the heading "ALLIANCES AND ALLIES", the thread stated from the inside the arrangement of the bloc that held the 2016 territory map: "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} No other member guild of the bloc wrote the alliance down.

The guild styled itself as pirates — "Yo-ho-ho. We are Blacklisted, a guild of friends who aim to claim ultimate victory!" — with its capital at Selchar, territory "composed by the great ocean islands", and Treasure Thursday, a weekly war night whose prize was five unidentified legendaries "for the person who gets more territories".{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} He handled the guild's applications himself through 2016.{{cite:thread-131893|posts #7 and #9, 22 Jun 2016}}

He was again among Blacklisted's leaders in 2018{{cite:thread-219617|post #1, as last revised 29 Aug 2019}}, and he remained active on the Wynncraft forums long after: in August 2022 he replied to a guild recruitment thread with a moderation notice, "Hi, avoid bumping your thread so much, you can only bump it twice per day."{{cite:thread-301804|post #10, 3 Aug 2022}} As of September 2026 his forum account carries the Staff Member, Mod Manager and Moderator banners and gives his guild as Blacklisted.{{cite:thread-131893|forum profile banners and guild field in the page markup, captured 3 Sep 2026}}

**NeonRider** led [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] [BLA] from its creation on 19 January 2016, jointly with [[naraka00|Naraka00]]: "Our guild was founded on 19/01/16 and the leaders are @NeonRider and @Naraka00."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} In the guild's successor thread of 2018, milo890 wrote "the leaders are @NeonRider, @Naraka00, and I".{{cite:thread-219617|post #1, as last revised 29 Aug 2019}}

He entered the era's public argument over territory once. On 2 March 2017, in a thread demanding that [[hackforums|HackForums]] be capped and in which Blacklisted had just been named among the bloc's holders, he answered the premise directly: "It's cute that you guys think that my guild is super op but in reality it's only me doing wars and we're down to 1.7mil emeralds."{{cite:thread-179383|post #18, 2 Mar 2017}}{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}} No other statement by a Blacklisted leader about the guild's warring capacity survives from the period.

He was still posting in the guild's second recruitment thread in September 2018{{cite:thread-219617|posts #15 and #16, 20 and 25 Sep 2018}}, and his forum profile still gave his guild as Blacklisted as of September 2026.{{cite:thread-179383|forum profile guild field in the page markup, captured 3 Sep 2026}} Nothing else about him is recorded: no founding account, no war record, and no departure.

## History

Nether's Ascent was created on 21 December 2014 by Francis12qwasyx, the same day as [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] and one day before guild warfare was released{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2014}}.

In early March 2015 it was one of the four founding guilds of the alliance Legio Praetoria, with KnightOfValor, [[imperial|Imperial]] and [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]]; two of the four left on 5 June 2015 and the alliance collapsed roughly a month later{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2015}}. Through the summer of 2015 Nether's Ascent and Kangronomicon between them held the map. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] described the pair as "essentially the Hax of mid 2015"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L32, composed 19 Jan 2018}}, and a June 2016 forum post reached for the same comparison, calling [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[libertas|Libertas]] a "rule of two" that "many distinguished scholars compare … to the ancient guilds of 'The Nether's Ascent' and 'Kangronomicon'"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}.

The guild was a standing target for smaller guilds trying to make a name. Drew1011 wrote that Holders of LE ran deliberate skirmishes against it in mid-2015, "frequently … able to take and hold about 6-7 territories before they pushed us back", specifically in order to be noticed by Kangronomicon{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L31–33, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. Kangronomicon passed Nether's Ascent in experience to take first place shortly before September 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L105, composed 19 Jan 2018}}.

### The allegation of diverted attacks

Drew1011 recorded a suspicion that Nether's Ascent redirected hostile guilds onto its own ally: "Myself and many others suspect this is because of the terribly kept secret that TNA would often make deals with other guilds where they managed to persuade other guilds to instead attack their Fuq, their ally"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L147, composed 19 Jan 2018}}. He offered no evidence for it, and the question was never settled. The map he reproduces beside the passage shows [[validus|Validus]] and its allies holding most of the province with Kangronomicon absent from it entirely while Nether's Ascent retains its whole eastern block{{cite:drew1011-storytime|territory map reproduced as a screenshot at L145}}; the image is consistent with the claim but was selected by the person making it.

### Later record

Unlike most guilds of its cohort, Nether's Ascent outlived the period. It was still recruiting members away from other guilds in 2016 — an applicant to Libertas in September 2016 wrote "i was in [[validus|Validus]] and now i'am in nether ascent but I'm not satisfied of the guild anymore"{{cite:thread-119596-p15|post #286, Synchr0, 30 Sep 2016}} — and it was a member guild of [[the-federation|the Federation]], listed as "Nethers Ascent [TNA]" in the November 2018 roster{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}. 

Its Federation membership can be dated exactly. On 3 September 2018 a member asked the alliance's leadership channel how many votes Nether's Ascent needed to pass; the founder answered that there were sixteen guilds, so eleven yes votes were required, and within a minute another member said the guild was in.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|3 Sep 2018}} The alliance announced the admission the same day and, half an hour later, that it had assigned the guild the six Rymek territories taken from a member expelled the day before for spying.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/3/2018}}

It did not keep them long. On 11 October a Federation leader argued in the leadership channel that the guild's holdings should be reduced, because it plainly could not manage its boundary and its rate of reclaiming had become very low, which made it a hindrance on the map with enemies about; he said he had spoken to the captain warring for the guild, who told him he did not play often and who declined an offer of help from another guild's captains, and two other leaders agreed.{{cite:federation-october-2018-discord-private|11 Oct 2018}} That is the alliance's assessment of a member guild, made in the alliance's own channel, and Nether's Ascent left no answer to it. The capture log shows the decline it describes: 404 captures in August 2018, 361 in September, 147 in October and 22 in November.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Nethers Ascent captures by month, Jun 2018 – Jan 2019 UTC}}

The guild left the alliance on 29 October 2018, in a run of six membership changes announced across sixteen hours.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Goden, 10/29/2018}} No reason was given for the departure. The founder's tribute of 13 November still lists it, that roster being a record of every guild that had been a member rather than of the membership at the end.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} When the guild ended was never recorded.

### The return of 2019

Its fighting did not end with its alliance. The guild took two territories in January 2019 and none at all between February and September, then 816 in October, 1,646 in November and 1,016 in December — 2,462 of them spread across 266 different territories in October and November alone, and none of them held at the end of either month.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Nethers Ascent captures by month, and distinct territories and month-end holdings Oct–Nov 2019, UTC; the eighteen free-for-all territories declared 14 Sep 2019 are not netted out}} Its last capture fell on 9 October 2021.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Nethers Ascent captures, Jun 2018 – Oct 2021, UTC}}

That autumn it broke a guild. [[the-simple-ones|The Simple Ones]] left [[terra|Terra]] for neutrality on 21 September 2019{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}, and in October Nether's Ascent took 341 territories from it and [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] 149, the two largest shares taken from it by anybody that month.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures with The Simple Ones as defender, by attacker, Oct 2019, UTC; the eighteen free-for-all territories declared 14 Sep 2019 are not netted out}} On 16 October Terra's ambassador told the leadership channel that The Simple Ones had been broken by a new grouping of three guilds, of which Nether's Ascent was one, and three weeks later the same grouping was reported as fighting on Terra's side ([[the-map-refilled|The map refilled]]).{{cite:the-map-refilled-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 16 Oct 2019}}{{cite:terra-november-collapse-2019-discord-private|war advisory, 2 Nov 2019}}

