## History

The thread opened on 8 August 2016 with an unusually candid statement of purpose. "Do you like guild wars? Do you like dominating the territory map and controlling the entire province of Wynn...? Well get the fuck out then," the opening post began, before setting out the terms: "The Seraphim alliance is a 100% community based alliance... There's no intention of actively providing support for guild wars."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}} What it offered instead was a way around the guild-slot cap of the period — "an opportunity to grown their communities beyond the bugged-out, limited guild slots" — plus shared art and thread graphics, and the founder was frank about his motive: "80% of the reason I set this up is because I want an excuse to make new graphics." Membership was deliberately non-exclusive: "any guild can join the alliance, regardless of if they are already in another alliance."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Within a day the thread was taken over by an argument between veterans about whether [[hackforums|HackForums]]' position resembled [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]]' earlier control of the map. That exchange — Glitchedslayer against [[drew1011|Drew1011]], LeoDiesAlot and Yuno F Gasai — preserved much of what is known about Ordo Malleus, Hax's ejection from it, and the composition of the bloc holding territory in 2016{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}. LeoDiesAlot, a chief of [[libertas|Libertas]] and so describing his own guild's arrangement, said that Hax "work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories".{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, LeoDiesAlot, 9 Aug 2016}}{{cite:thread-119596-p09|post #171, yosteric5 naming LeoDiesAlot a chief, 11 Aug 2016}} The founder's own verdict on his thread: "Thanks for hijacking my thread gais. Appreciate it."{{cite:thread-143392|post #16, 9 Aug 2016}}

## Membership

Seraphim had four recorded member guilds: Saltiest, [[libertas|Libertas]], FOX and Holders Of LE.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening-post roster graphics}} In September 2016 Libertas held 60 territories, second only to HackForums' 146{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback Machine capture of the api.wynncraft.com guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016 (pre-2018 territory snapshots)}}, so a declared community alliance with no war function counted among its members the map's second-largest warring power. Holders Of LE was simultaneously a member of [[halcyon|Halcyon]]{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, opening post (Halcyon founded 5 Jun 2016 between ToastedPandas and Holders of LE)}} and joined [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] that October{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}}, which the alliance's own rules expressly permitted.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Seraphim predates the machine-recorded alliance logs, which begin in January 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No activity after the founding was ever recorded, and neither was the alliance's end. Its legacy is the argument it hosted: much of what is known about Ordo Malleus, and the clearest contemporaneous statement that HackForums was not acting alone, were written on the thread of an alliance set up as a joke about not warring.{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}

The Serpentem Empire was founded in the first week of November 2017 by members who had just left or been removed from [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], in the break that followed [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] making [[drew1011|Drew1011]] her viceroy.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}}{{cite:thundderr-oral-history|on the November 2017 split}}

The Phoenix event log names three officers struck off on 4 November: [[whimsicality|Whimsicality]], [[elegantdeath|ElegantDeath]] and Alhecks.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-4-17}} ElegantDeath appears as the guild’s leader in the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] charter’s list of allies, which is the only source naming anyone at its head.{{cite:gdoc-1kdasl6eq7y_zssy|War Syndicate charter, list of allies}}

## In the wars of 2017–18

Seven weeks after its founding the guild was on the [[coalition|Coalition]]’s side at the declaration of war on 21 December 2017, in a fourteen-guild roster that also held KingdomPhoenixes — the guild its founders had just left.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|the rosters at the declaration of war, 21 Dec 2017}}

It then spent about a week inside the alliance with no ground of its own. The territory list of 16 January 2018 gave it the south ocean, and the revision made to that document on the night of the 20th took it off the map altogether.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|16–20 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, revised 20 Jan 2018}} On the afternoon of the 23rd, nine minutes before the next list went up, the alliance's leaders were choosing a single territory on the edge of the map to give it, and a member reciting the alliance's guilds that evening left it out and had to be corrected.{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, the edge territory}}{{cite:coalition-membership-january-2018-discord-private|23 Jan 2018, 19:33}} The list published that evening gives it Kander — but that text is the version revised on 28 January, after the departure of Kasai Shinrai, to which the drafts circulated hours before publication had given Kander.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018, revised 28 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|the 23 January drafts}}

Its appearance in the War Syndicate charter is harder to place. That document lists it among the alliance the Coalition went to war with, and it is undated; since the guild did not exist before November 2017, the charter must have been written or revised after that, and the guild must have stood on both sides at different points. Nothing says when it changed.

It went on into [[the-federation|the Federation]], which assigned it four territories at Lusuco and Twain.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|territory assignment, Serpentem Empire}} It is named on the alliance's list of every guild that was ever a member, published at the dissolution in November 2018.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

Its fighting ended in March. Its last territory exchange either way falls on 14 March 2018, and it took and lost nothing afterwards.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Serpentem Empire, last exchange 14 Mar 2018 UTC; none thereafter}} On 4 April 2018 the Federation voted on expelling the member guilds that had not claimed or attempted to claim their assigned territory, and named it among four; two days later the alliance's founder had all four taken off the ally list, and none of them appears on the allocation of 22 April.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4–6 Apr 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|4/22/2018 2:34 PM}} Nothing later about the guild was recorded.

ShadowFall [Shy] was created on 21 Aug 2017.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Its first years went unrecorded; its warring history begins in 2020.

## History

### An Artemis leader (2020)

In March 2020 ShadowFall's GoulartJJ posted on the forums as a leader of [[Artemis]], the map-holding alliance of the day.{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} The guild joined the community alliance [[Niflheim]] on 27 Dec 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The side-switch (2021)

On 1 Feb 2021, mid-way through the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]], the [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] recorded that 'BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now' — a defection from the Artemis camp to [[Goose]].{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} ShadowFall fought with Goose until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, then became a founding member of [[Valhalla]] and followed it into [[Vanir]], while retaining its Niflheim membership{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} until that alliance dissolved on 18 Dec 2021, the day Vanir collapsed.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Into The Aquarium's orbit (2023)

By August 2023 ShadowFall was a subguild of [[The Aquarium]], part of the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact's shared infrastructure alongside Avoquarium [HQs] and Avicia's the Avos.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} How and when it passed into TAq's orbit is not known.

