On 18 December 2020 Sheepn, then of Diablo [DXI], opened thread 279337, "Guild Moderators" — the best-documented political flashpoint between the ignition of the war against [[artemis|Artemis]] and the naming of [[goose|Goose]] a month later. Its opening sentence supplies the era's clearest framing of the conflict: "there is currently an ongoing large-scale conflict between Artemis, the map-holder alliance, and a currently unnamed group of anti-Artemis guilds."{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}

The complaint was that "a moderator affiliated with a major Artemis guild" had banned two prominent members of the leading anti-Artemis guild for macro use, when the numpad spamming they described was "publicly known to be NOT bannable and allowed by moderation"{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}. The thread's thesis was structural rather than personal: "The root of the problem boils down to the moderation team failing to adapt to the modern way guilds operate even though many Moderators come from guilds, and a lack of set-in-stone rules for guilds related issues."{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} Sheepn closed with a request not to "name drop or harass the moderator involved"{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}.

The replies made the thread a record in itself. [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] answered that "Moderators will not ban players without reason"{{cite:thread-279337|post #17, 19 Dec 2020}}; Carrie of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] located the real fault in the team's "lack of communication, being on the same page"{{cite:thread-279337|post #18, 19 Dec 2020}}; Miles_ questioned a rule enforceable only when players incriminate themselves{{cite:thread-279337|post #20, 19 Dec 2020}}. Read together with the guild tags of its participants, the thread also preserves the membership of the then-unnamed coalition — Diablo, Eden, [[avicia|Avicia]], HICH, Bovemists, Lily Pad, Ultra Violet, [[emorians|Emorians]], The Dark Phoenix, Paladins United and [[imperial|Imperial]] — and places [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and Titans Valor in Artemis{{cite:thread-279337|posts #1–#20, 18–19 Dec 2020, read with the participants’ forum guild badges (badge markup, not post text)}}.

Sins of Seedia (SDU) was founded on 6 May 2017, per the official guild API.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} It spans nearly the whole recorded history of alliance warfare, from the Federation era to the present.

## History

### Founding and the early years

Its founders told the story themselves in an alliance channel in August 2018, without any of the grandeur that usually attaches to guild origins: three of them, about four liquid emeralds pooled between them, and a guild hall taken in Troms.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|founders' account, August 2018}} One of the three is consistently credited with creating the guild — she said so herself in March 2018 and was addressed as its maker again that October — and the identification rests on those statements rather than on any roster.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|founders' account, 2018}} An older alliance, Zenith, is the earliest bloc members place the guild in; they described it as having been broken apart by a campaign that took weeks to prepare.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|Zenith}}

A guild-bank collapse shadows the same period, and the record gives two views of it. The [[coalition|Coalition]] noted in January 2018 that it had granted the guild the Jungle territory to help it recover financially after a chief drained its treasury, and in July 2018 members repeated, half in jest, that the founder had been the one who drained it.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|January and July 2018}} Her own account, given in October 2018, is less dramatic: she had spent roughly a million emeralds on a single guild-hall defence without knowing what she was doing, buying high-level defenders one at a time when each cost around 250,000, and was not sanctioned for it because she was a friend and had made the guild.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|founder's account, October 2018}} Whether that defence is the drained bank of January is not stated anywhere; the two accounts sit side by side and fit each other.

### From enemy to core (January–March 2018)

For its first recorded period the guild was the Coalition's enemy rather than its member. That alliance's leader accused it in January 2018 of breaking a standing pact by resuming attacks, and later the same month of duping in-game currency and distributing it to fund unusually expensive territory defences; no adjudication of either charge was ever recorded.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|Coalition channels, January 2018}} It was separately accused of a pattern of overrunning smaller guilds rather than fighting stronger ones, and a figure associated with it approached Coalition members that month to persuade them to leave the alliance.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|January 2018}}

Three weeks later it changed sides. On 17 February 2018, with the Coalition reduced to a rump by the mass walkout of the day before, the remaining guilds recruited outside help and it came in as an active participant; within two days it was fighting alongside them, and within a week members were naming it among the alliance's core.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|17–24 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|16–18 Feb 2018}} Nobody in the record treats the reversal as remarkable.

Its arrival cost another guild its leadership. Federation leaders noted on 17 February 2018 — the same day — that Peace and Tranquility [PaT] had effectively collapsed after its senior members joined Sins of Seedia, and that it no longer counted in the alliance's politics.{{cite:angels-of-eternal-discord-private|17 Feb 2018}} Both guilds had appeared the previous month in the same grouping of guilds assembled from War Syndicate's remains.{{cite:angels-of-eternal-discord-private|January 2018}}

### Load-bearing (2018)

The guild mattered structurally beyond its own strength. In March 2018 the leader of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] told the Federation's war channel that his own senate had voted to join the alliance on the strength of Sins of Seedia's adherence to it, that his guild meant to stand wherever that guild stood, and that a departure by it would trigger a vote in his senate which he expected would follow it out — one member guild's membership held by another member rather than by the alliance.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|Federation war channel, March 2018}}

It also brought guilds in and absorbed them. It championed the vote that admitted Deimos in February 2018, which passed unanimously, and an allied guild was admitted eight to one the following day.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|February 2018}} [[fantasy|Fantasy]] had merged into it by October 2018 and the guild Aphelion merged in on 10 November 2018; members of The Divine Swords moved across in numbers through mid-2018, to the point that one of that guild's members claimed in July 2018 that his guild had effectively taken Sins of Seedia over, putting some eighty per cent of its active warring force at his own people.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|mid-to-late 2018}} Its own representation in the alliance's leadership channel was less stable: the same representative had his leader, captain and advisor roles revoked by the guild in June 2018 for inactivity and disruption, and was stripped of guild-leader access in the alliance channel again in July.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|June–July 2018}}

### Federation era

Sins of Seedia enters the record as a founding-era member of [[The Federation]] in February 2018.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} On 25 Mar 2018 it co-founded the [[Aesir Pact]] with [[Fantasy]] and IceBlue Team — a pact of sister guilds "especially dedicated to Gavel, and the birth place of Aesir, the canyon" — with its leader simplyinfinity_ named among the pact's creators.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018}} The Aesir guilds were the Federation's last defenders: as [[the-federation-dies|the alliance fell]] on 10–11 Nov 2018, they quit only after fourteen hours of constant warring.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}}

Members treated Aesir as a grouping distinct from the Federation rather than a faction within it, and noted that two of its guilds held a standing pact with a guild the Federation otherwise treated as hostile.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|Aesir, from September 2018}}

On 10 November 2018 Sins of Seedia joined its two fellow [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] guilds in a joint withdrawal from the Federation, and the pact continued as an independent alliance into March 2019, dividing the Canyon between its members within hours of leaving.{{cite:aesir-pact-2018-discord-private|10 Nov 2018 – Jan 2019}}{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|22–26 Feb 2019}} Blacklisted's terms for releasing [[the-canyon-concession|the Canyon]] on 31 December 2018 required Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team to help against [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]; neither did.{{cite:aesir-canyon-conceded-december-2018-discord-private|31 Dec 2018}} On 2 January 2019 a member writing for the guild rather than for the alliance said it was tired of being pulled towards Valkyrie and Olympus, would be neither's, and that the others could take a side if they wished.{{cite:aesir-council-after-the-concession-2019-discord-private|2 Jan 2019}} By 23 February members were describing the guild as absent and saying it would not be back unless its leader became active again.{{cite:aesir-oligarchy-membership-and-election-2019-discord-private|23 Feb 2019}}

### After the Federation (2018–2019)

It became a target in its own right immediately. Its truce with [[hackforums|HackForums]] broke in December 2018, and at the end of that month [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] and an allied guild took territory from it and IceBlue Team, with a reported thirty territories lost from one of the two.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|December 2018}} In January 2019 its leader said the guild was tired of being pressed by both major blocs to pick a side in the dispute then running.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|January 2019}} Its application to [[the-consortium|the Consortium]] was relayed into that alliance's voting channel on 27 March 2019, from a new leader of the guild writing under a revival tag and giving as its reason that the whole of the original Aesir membership was already inside.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|the application, 03:06 on 27 Mar 2019, export clock}} The same evening a Consortium member proposed celebrating the guild's return to [[aesir-pact|Aesir]], and the leader of IceBlue Team agreed.{{cite:aesir-into-the-consortium-march-2019-discord-private|27 Mar 2019}} By September 2019 the guild was named among the loose coalition of guilds fighting [[luna|Luna]] — though its position was disputed within days, members of the opposing alliance describing it as formerly anti-Luna but by then warring against two of their own guilds.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|March–September 2019}}

### Later blocs

The alliance record then goes quiet for over two years. Sins of Seedia reappears in [[Artemis]] from March 2021, staying until [[the-great-collapse|the alliance collapsed]] on 11 May 2021.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In the 2022 realignment it joined [[Cucumber Company]]; the alliance's full fourteen-guild roster — the last public alliance roster ever posted — was submitted to the forum megalist on 26 Jun 2022 by SDU's own TherapueticLiz.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} The guild carried through the rename into [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]] and stayed until the alliance's quiet end in June 2023.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

As of September 2026 the guild remains active — level 90, around 75 members, led by TherapueticLiz — holding no territories.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

