smtn elf fell apart in June 2023 when [[The Aquarium]] and [[Avicia]] walked out.

## History

### From Cucumber to elf
At the start of Season 8 “Cucumber was archived. The new alliance name is called Smtn else,” recorded the [[titan-times|Titan Times]], which also reported Gang of Fools having “left and betrayed the alliance” and welcomed [[Paladins United]], [[The Simple Ones]] and TerraLune.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-tfcs3b6emlq|"SMTN ELSE SLANDER", TherapueticLiz, uploaded 3 Oct 2022}} For Christmas 2022 “Smtn else” became “smtn elf” and was never renamed back{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}}; by 17 February 2023 a forum thread was calling it “unquestionably the greatest super-alliance of 2023” — a tongue-in-cheek thread, but the name and the bloc's scale were real.{{cite:thread-306790|Wynncraft forums thread 306790, 17 Feb 2023}} Season 8 brought a rename rather than a reformation, and the full Cucumber roster carried through it.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol8|vol. 8}}

### 2023
Mid-season, busted moments joined (a brief stint, over by the end of May), Nefarious Ravens left “on account of the guild disbanding” — its last territory exchange was 9 March 2023{{cite:territory-exchanges|last exchange with Nefarious Ravens on either side, 9 Mar 2023 20:32:53 UTC; a last-appearance check, so no free-for-all subtraction applies}} — and [[Idiot Co]], which joined that spring, held alliance territory.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}

### The end
In June 2023 The Aquarium and Avicia quit, rejecting pressure — led by busted moments — to shrink their territorial claims: [[the-avocado-split|the Avocado split]].{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}} The alliance was last mentioned in Avicia's Season 12 post of 10 June 2023 (“To our other allies in smtn elf... for the hqs”){{cite:thread-308780|Avicia Season 12 post, Wynncraft forums thread 308780, 10 Jun 2023}}; the Season 13 post of 19 August 2023 did not mention it at all.{{cite:thread-310286|Avicia Season 13 post, Wynncraft forums thread 310286, 19 Aug 2023}} No dissolution was ever announced, and no war among the guilds left behind was ever recorded — smtn elf did not break up so much as quietly cease to be. They went on exchanging territory in quantity: 34,152 exchanges among the thirteen between 16 June 2023 and 28 December 2024, but so evenly matched pair by pair that the traffic reads as allied trading rather than fighting.{{cite:territory-exchanges|exchanges with both attacker and defender among the thirteen guilds remaining after 15 Jun 2023, 15 Jun 2023 – 31 Dec 2024 UTC, raw: 34,152 across 518 territories, largest pairs within 5 per cent of even in both directions}}

## Membership
The roster carried over from [[Cucumber Company]] at the Season 8 rename; joins date to around the season boundary.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

