## The map on the morning after

An hour before the assault began, the [[luna|Luna]] guilds held the map between them: [[imperial|Imperial]] 76 territories, [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] 71, [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] 67, Blacklisted 47, [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] 39.{{cite:territory-exchanges|holdings from the last exchange on each territory before 7 Sep 2019 15:00 UTC}} Eighteen hours later Imperial held one and the other three held seven apiece{{cite:territory-exchanges|same reconstruction at 8 Sep 2019 09:00 UTC}}; by midday on the 9th those three held none.{{cite:territory-exchanges|same reconstruction at 9 Sep 2019 12:00 UTC}} No list of territories open to all was in force on the night of the raid: the last enumerated one had been published in October 2018, and Terra did not declare its own eighteen until 14 September.{{cite:federation-public-announcements|Drew1011, 10/12/2018}}{{cite:terra-alliance-announcements-discord-private|14 Sep 2019}} None of these figures is netted against a declaration.

The coalition's own count of the night, set out minutes after the fighting stopped, had three guilds wiped from the map, three more cut by over half and a seventh reduced by close to twenty territories{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 7 Sep 2019}}, with one enemy guild down to two or three at the high point.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 7 Sep 2019}} A member added that they had nearly wiped a guild they had not intended to touch.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 7 Sep 2019}}

Kingdom Foxes was the exception, going into the night with seventy-one territories and out of it with sixty-eight{{cite:territory-exchanges|Kingdom Foxes holdings, 7–9 Sep 2019, UTC}}, having negotiated a separate non-aggression deal while the operation was still running.{{cite:kingdom-of-foxes-guild-profile-discord-private|7 Sep 2019}}

## Ceasefire by instruction

A ceasefire here was an order to the people doing the fighting, with a boundary drawn across the map inside it. At about a quarter to five on the morning of 8 September a Terra leader told the war channel to leave Paladins United alone in Corkus, that its island holdings were open without restriction, and that terms were being discussed.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}} A fighter said he did not agree and asked why anybody would consent to it{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}}; the answer he got was that it was politics, and that having the guild on side would be useful.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}}

Later the same morning a beaten guild was to be held off the map altogether, having agreed to stay off it until told otherwise while its mistakes were discussed and a long list of conditions was prepared.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}}

The alliance did not always issue one order at a time. On the afternoon of the 8th one leader told the war channel that [[hackforums|HackForums]] was trying to claim the jungle and was fair game, ranking it second behind finishing the defeated alliance{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}}; within the same minute another told the channel not to attack it and that its claims would be discussed with it, and said so twice more as the argument ran on.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}} A member of a third guild said HackForums was a friend but the jungle was his guild's, and asked what it had done to deserve it.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|war channel, 8 Sep 2019}} Its claims were a live question because the alliance had voted against admitting it{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|12 Sep 2019}}, and would vote again on the 17th.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|voting channel, 17 Sep 2019}}

## Terms decided by asking each other

The alliance had won a war and had no procedure for ending one. Asked on the morning of 8 September whether they were voting on which of the beaten guilds could keep land, a member posted his own answer guild by guild — one to keep a province, one to keep part of the canyon but much less, one to get nothing — and others added regions and numbers underneath.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}} A leader's account in the same exchange had a disputed territory handed to an allied guild after the alliance threatened the guild holding it.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}

Such procedure as there was got argued over rather than followed. One leader instructed the channel that claims would be discussed once the talks with the two guilds still negotiating had finished, and that leaders could register what they wanted meanwhile without any guarantee{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}; another pressed that the coalition should negotiate rather than take whatever was offered, on the principle that the beaten should end with fewer territories than they had held{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}; a third proposed leaving the allocation to the alliance's designated managers.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}

Terms were discretionary and the spread was wide. On the same morning that one guild was being offered a province and another a reduced share of the canyon{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}, word came through that a third wanted to know whether it would be given anything at all; the channel laughed, and a leader said that if anything it was getting wiped.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}} No reason for the difference was ever given.

The beaten came one at a time. [[buildcraftia|BuildCraftia]] tried on 9 September to change sides, and another guild approached the alliance again about working together{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 9 Sep 2019}}; members observed that BuildCraftia had nowhere else to go, and said they were surprised it and one other had not yet given up on the alliance they were in.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 9 Sep 2019}} That the defeated negotiated separately rather than as a bloc is this article's reading of those approaches; no participant says it.

The most expensive claim came with a service attached. Arguing on 8 September to keep thirty-three claims, ILQ's representative told the coalition's leaders that his guild and four subguilds had been spying inside Luna on their behalf since a named guild left it, and that they had wiped two enemy guilds{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}; a leader answered that thirty-three was too much and that he liked the idea of their keeping some but not all.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}}

Paladins United gave up its ocean, its swamp and the Light Isles and kept the contested Corkus region.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}} [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]]'s leader objected that every alliance did this for that guild, that it felt entitled, and that this was why it was so highly levelled, tracing the pattern to the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] era.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 8 Sep 2019}} He had been present eighteen months earlier when [[the-federation|the Federation]] voted down a peace that would have let the same guild keep the same region, and then admitted it and granted the region anyway.{{cite:federation-march-2018-discord-private|March 2018}}

The fullest settlement offered to anybody never took effect. On 10 September Terra's ambassador said he felt bad about the outcome, because the beaten guild's designated negotiator had argued hard inside his own leadership that keeping a fair share of the contested province would pay for itself in peace, and had lost.{{cite:terra-terms-of-surrender-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 10 Sep 2019}} That is his account of another guild's internal politics, given from the winning side.

## The first post-war vote

Voting on its first post-war map on 13 September, a leader told the channel that the earlier phase had been for establishing what each guild wanted to claim{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|13 Sep 2019}}, and proposed rearranging the ballot so that each guild had one vote, because a guild holding two or more made it unfair.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|13 Sep 2019}} Kingdom Foxes' Viceroy answered that duplicate voters had to be removed by hand, that people never listened, and that co-leaders would always try to vote as well.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|13 Sep 2019}} The draft split of the conquered ground had been assembled by a few leaders rather than by the whole leadership, which caused a dispute of its own, alongside an argument over who had the authority to allocate the new ground at all.{{cite:terra-victory-september-2019-discord-private|September 2019}}

## Counting the votes

Terra settled questions by putting an emoji on a message. Two habits pushed the totals above the votes: whoever posted a motion normally reacted to every option, so each choice opened with one vote that was not one{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|the voting channel, September 2019}}, and a reaction could be taken off at any time afterwards.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|reactions removed after a close, September 2019}}

The alliance made the first of those subtractions itself. Defending the new territory map in the voting-discussion channel on the evening of 13 September, the ambassador gave the result as eighteen in favour and three against and said he had narrowed the count to guild masters by hand{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|voting-discussion channel, 13 Sep 2019}}; there would have been a fourth against, he added, had the leader who walked out of the Discord that afternoon been counted.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|voting-discussion channel, 13 Sep 2019}} The motion had gone up the previous evening and carried nineteen reactions in favour and four against at the export, the account that posted it on both options — eighteen and three with the seed removed.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|the map motion of 12 Sep 2019 and its exported reactions}} The same pair of numbers was reached four hours apart from opposite ends.

The placeholder had a name in the room. Twenty minutes after the motion to expel Azeron opened that evening, one leader reported it as thirteen in favour and three against and another corrected him on the spot to two, one of the opposing reactions being the war planner's marker rather than a vote.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|voting-discussion channel, 13 Sep 2019}} That motion was still running; it closed at nineteen to four, or eighteen to three net of its mover.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|the expulsion motion of 13 Sep 2019 and its tally}}

One vote per guild was practice before it was a rule. It was being applied by hand on the 13th; on the 15th a member of the guild-leaders' channel argued for it on the precedent of an earlier alliance that had tried two votes per guild and given it up, because not every guild had two people in its leaders' channel.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|guild-leaders' channel, 15 Sep 2019}} Two leaders including the ambassador endorsed him inside the half hour.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|guild-leaders' channel, 15 Sep 2019}} It first appears in the text of a Terra motion on the 17th.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|the motion of 17 Sep 2019}}

What the rule concealed was stated once. On 18 September, with the readmission of [[hackforums|HackForums]] open, MasterWynnLords' leader told the voting-discussion channel that opinion inside his guild ran about fifty-five to forty-five in favour, and that he and his chiefs had decided to vote against.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|voting-discussion channel, 18 Sep 2019}} An hour later the ambassador asked whether the guild had swapped its vote, immediately before announcing the result.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|voting-discussion channel, 18 Sep 2019}} Whether it had was never settled.

A vote stayed changeable while its motion ran: during the argument over the map revision on 29 September a leader told a member of the objecting guild to change his, the dispute behind it having been settled.{{cite:terra-vote-counts-checked-2019-discord-private|29 Sep 2019}}

## Three neutralities in six days

Having taken the map, Terra spent the following fortnight barely fighting. It settled instead, and settled three guilds three different ways.

**By treaty.** Terms agreed with Kingdom Foxes on 17 September gave complete and enduring neutrality in both directions, released about twenty-five territories, and took effect immediately.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|17 Sep 2019}} Its second clause is the one without parallel: neither side might send its members into subguilds or foreign guilds in order to attack the other's claims.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|treaty terms, 17 Sep 2019}} That was the standard way round a truce, and both sides gave it up in writing.

**By purchase, with ground that was not theirs to sell.** On 21 September contested territory was handed to [[lunatic|Lunatic]] as the price of its leaving the enemy alliance and going neutral{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} — ground [[the-mage-legacy|Mage Legacy]] depended on for its experience gain, which was not told, not compensated and not consulted.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} A member noted that the alliance's Discord managers had done the voting; a guild leader asked why the matter had not gone to the guild leaders at all, and got no answer.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}

**On sufferance.** ILQ's withdrawal was negotiated line by line on 19 September: its leader wanted only to exist, would return a named territory, would not make war, and would treat any move on its claims outside an agreement as war.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 19 Sep 2019}} A Terra leader answered that it might exist, but with a reduced land count, and that if it could not hold its lands Terra would take them.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 19 Sep 2019}}

It left on the evening of 21 September, a day earlier than the week's notice it had given{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 16 and 21 Sep 2019}}, and the parting was warm on both sides: the departing leader thanked them for the time the guilds had spent together, and a Terra leader said he hoped the defeated alliance would stop targeting it.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} Two minutes later another leader said it was time to eat ILQ.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}

The clause was ten days older than the treaty: the two-day truce announced on the night of the raid already barred either side from sending its members into subguilds or other guilds in order to attack the other's claims.{{cite:terra-written-plan-and-the-raid-2019-discord-private|7 Sep 2019, the announced terms of the truce}} It was tested inside the alliance four days after the treaty was signed. On 21 September a member of ThisIsMurica said he would war Lunatic under another guild's tag rather than his own{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}; leaders answered that it would put him at war with the Foxes, that Lunatic would find out, and that he was trying to get round the rule{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}, one telling him flatly that he would not be touching them unless they broke neutrality first.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} Reading the refusal against the treaty is this article's connection; nobody in the exchange makes it.

## Who belonged to what

On 27 September the alliance published to all members a relations list it described as properly updated and better formatted, sorting every guild it knew of into five categories: allies, the neutral canyon grouping, distant allies, plain neutrals, and enemies with their subguilds.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|27 Sep 2019}} No alliance in this record kept a more granular account of where it stood with everybody else; the Federation ran one list of enemies and the [[coalition|Coalition]] three classes of territory.

The columns are datable, and not to September. The list moved at least four times after it went up: the same office announced updates on 11 October and twice in November, and the export's edit field carries only the last of them, 1 December.{{cite:terra-relations-card-redated-2019-discord-private|the card's channel, 27 Sep – 7 Nov 2019, against the edit stamp}} The surviving text names among Terra's allies a guild whose application was not put to the alliance until 31 October.{{cite:terra-relations-card-redated-2019-discord-private|Merashold's first appearance and the motion of 31 Oct 2019}} It places among its enemies four guilds that were inside the alliance in September, two of them admitted by recorded ballot that month.{{cite:terra-relations-card-redated-2019-discord-private|the four guilds and the September ballots}} And it keeps in the enemies column a guild its own notice of 11 October had moved to the neutrals.{{cite:terra-relations-card-redated-2019-discord-private|the notice of 11 Oct 2019 against the surviving text}} What survives is the alliance's view of the map somewhere between 31 October and 1 December — the weeks it was losing guilds every few days — and it is evidence about September of nothing at all.

## What the peace cost

On 21 September the ambassador totalled the losses: with Titans Valor and [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] gone and Phantom Hearts in the neutral canyon grouping, about forty territories had passed out of the alliance's purview and six more had been taken{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}}, and ILQ's expected departure would remove roughly twenty more.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} What worried him was not the ground but that there was much less room left in which to place guilds.{{cite:terra-mid-september-2019-discord-private|leadership channel, 21 Sep 2019}} Three weeks after taking the map, more of it had left the alliance by negotiated exit than any enemy had taken back.

The season's last settlement was made with the guild attacking Terra hardest. On 10 October a leader opened a vote on a neutrality deal with Blacklisted under which each side would leave the other's claims alone{{cite:terra-october-2019-discord-private|voting channel, 10 Oct 2019}}, arguing that it removed one of the four or five enemies the alliance had left and that, whatever he thought of the guild, it was objectively the strongest enemy they faced.{{cite:terra-october-2019-discord-private|voting channel, 10 Oct 2019}} Blacklisted was making no demand for land at all: it wanted only to be left alone while it settled its own scores with the neutral canyon grouping and with independent guilds.{{cite:terra-october-2019-discord-private|10 Oct 2019}} The vote closed on the 11th and the guild came off the enemy list.{{cite:terra-october-2019-discord-private|11 Oct 2019}}

Few conflicts of the period were named at all. This one was named by the guilds that fought it, and named for its method rather than its ground.

## The record

Three kinds of record cover the week and none of them covers all of it. The [[coalition|Coalition]]'s information and announcement channels are contemporaneous and give the rosters and the territory maps.{{cite:coalition-information|1/11/2018}}{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/18/2018 and 1/23/2018}} Its leadership channel supplies the days themselves.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16–19 Jan 2018}} The cause, the name and the consequence come from two retrospectives written months afterwards, one in May 2018 and one in July.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1023–1030, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|recounted July 2018}} All of it is from the alliance's side.

## Background

On the evening of 11 January 2018 the Coalition's Discord server was deleted by the former monarch of [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], one of the two guilds that had founded the alliance, during a quarrel inside that guild; a replacement was created forty seconds later.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1022, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|11 Jan 2018}}{{cite:coalition-discord-deleted-january-2018-discord-private|12 Jan 2018, 04:19–04:20 UTC}} She gave her reason in her own guild's channel a minute afterwards and apologised within the hour — see [[the-coalition-discord-deletion|the Coalition Discord deletion]]. The first post on the new server was a card of fourteen member guilds and fourteen enemy guilds with Fantasy among the enemies, but it was last revised on 14 February 2018 and only the revised text was kept, so it places Fantasy outside the alliance a month after this week rather than at the start of it.{{cite:coalition-information|posted 1/11/2018 9:33 PM, last revised 14 Feb 2018}} On 16 January a member asked in the leadership channel whether Fantasy was still in the alliance, and three others confirmed it had left.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} The date its membership ended was never written down.

The Coalition's leader gave the cause as a misunderstanding about ground. Early in January Fantasy's leader [[viaire|Viaire]] asked for more territory than the two Air Temple territories he had first been given; he was told the request would be looked at when the next map was drawn, it was then forgotten, and Fantasy received nothing further. "Viaire believed this to be some sort of personal attack against him and that I purposefully did not give Fux any more territories."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1023–1024, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}

A second retrospective from the same side, given in July 2018, reads the episode the same way and treats it as the cause of everything that followed.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|recounted July 2018}}

## The fighting

The first exchange between the two guilds falls at 01:43 UTC on 16 January 2018, when Kingdom Foxes took Air Temple Lower from Fantasy; Air Temple Upper followed nine minutes later, and Fantasy took Cliffside Valley from Fox in between.{{cite:territory-exchanges|first Fantasy–Kingdom Foxes exchanges, 16 Jan 2018: 01:43, 01:49 and 01:52 UTC}} The member who reported the fighting on the 16th put it at about twenty hours old, which on the Discord export's winter clock of UTC-08:00 places its beginning on the evening of the 15th — the same hour as the first captures.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} The two records agree closely on when the war started and disagree about who moved first: the retrospective has Fantasy opening it against the Fox canyon.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1023, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}

The method gave the war its name. Fantasy attacked every territory the alliance had assigned and defended each with one mob, taking ground everywhere and holding none of it.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|January 2018}} Wars at the time took several attempts to start, so a single defending mob could cost a quarter of an hour to reach and kill.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1026, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}} The capture log reads the same way from the other end: 260 exchanges between the two guilds across thirty-one territories in six days, and ground Fantasy took from Fox changing hands again after a median of twenty-nine minutes.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Fantasy–Kingdom Foxes exchanges 16–21 Jan 2018: 260 across 31 territories, median 28.9 minutes to the next exchange, UTC}} Three territories in the canyon turned over more than twenty times each.{{cite:territory-exchanges|most-exchanged territories, Fantasy–Kingdom Foxes 16–21 Jan 2018, UTC: Burning Farm 33, Canyon Path North Mid 25, Canyon Valley South 25}}

The Coalition's replacement server carried no list of free-for-all territories before 16 January, and the one posted that day was a map rather than a list of names, so no open ground can be taken out of those counts.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018: "Free for all territories are in black."}}

The alliance built a register in the middle of the week and lost it. On 17 January it announced a listing sorting every territory it did not own into assigned, truced and free-for-all ground; the channel holding it had been deleted by the 20th, and the alliance's free-for-all position for January cannot be recovered.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/17/2018 6:04 PM}}{{cite:coalition-standing-documents-january-2018-discord-private|17–20 Jan 2018}} What the alliance published about its territory that month, and what it altered afterwards, is at [[coalition-standing-documents|its standing documents]].

In the same exchange of the 16th the alliance's leader said the guild had to be discouraged, and that the quickest way was to attack it with several guilds at once.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|16 Jan 2018}} Over 18 and 19 January seven guilds took territory from Fantasy: Kingdom Foxes, [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]], [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]], [[imperial|Imperial]], [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]].{{cite:territory-exchanges|guilds capturing from Fantasy, 18–19 Jan 2018, UTC; no free-for-all list in force for the window}}

## A settlement discussed and not reached

On the morning of 18 January the Kingdom of Foxes' leader asked the alliance whether his guild might be assigned two other regions instead, saying it was gaining no experience and losing money where it was, and making the request conditional on some other guild taking the canyon.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|18 Jan 2018}}

The alliance announced the move to its members the same morning: "In the wake up the attack on canyon, Fox will be moving our territories to Wynn."{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/18/2018 11:15 AM}}

That afternoon a member reported the opposing leader's terms — he would take nothing that left him fewer than about half of the twenty-four territories he was asking for — and another proposed offering ten, with more to follow if he kept to them.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|18 Jan 2018}} No agreement was recorded. On the morning of the 19th a member said the pact was over and that Fox could fight back if the canyon were attacked again, and remarked that Fantasy had been finished off the night before; that evening, asked whether the truce still held, he said it did not, that their own side had broken it, and that he was attacking at that moment.{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|19 Jan 2018}}

The claim that Fantasy had been finished does not survive the capture log. All fourteen of its captures from Kingdom Foxes on the 19th fell between 17:28 and 21:07 UTC that evening, a run of ground taken back in under four hours.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Fantasy captures from Kingdom Foxes, 19 Jan 2018 17:28–21:07 UTC}}

## The end, and what came out of it

The last exchange between the two guilds is on 21 January at 04:34 UTC. Across the 20th and 21st Kingdom Foxes took eight territories from Fantasy and Fantasy took none back.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Fantasy–Kingdom Foxes exchanges, 20–21 Jan 2018, UTC: Fox 8, Fantasy 0}} The alliance's account of why gives no defeat: after almost a week of constant warring Fantasy's leader grew tired of it and stopped.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1030, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}

The canyon question was settled on the map instead of in the terms. The alliance's territory list of 23 January left Kingdom Foxes holding North Canyon and added Cherry Blossom Forest and Temple Island to it — Wynn ground granted rather than the canyon given up.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/23/2018}} Fantasy appears on none of the alliance's territory lists of January or February 2018.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, 1/23/2018 and 2/1/2018}}

Two rules came out of the week. Alt accounts and alt guilds were used during the fighting to multiply Fantasy's strength, and the game's moderators ruled that warring on alts was unfair; the alliance adopted a ban of its own with a grace period.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1029, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}{{cite:coalition-founding-2017-discord-private|rule changes, January 2018}} On 31 January the alliance told its captains to wait ten minutes before attacking a Wynn territory, so that the guild which had just lost it had a chance to take it back.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/31/2018}}

The consequence the alliance thought mattered most fell on the guild that had been attacked. Because every captured territory was held by a single mob, anybody could take it straight back, including members too low-levelled to fight a real defence — and doing that over and over is what first drew two of the Kingdom of Foxes' fighters into warring at the volume they sustained for the next year.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1027–1028, part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}{{cite:the-trench-war-january-2018-discord-private|recounted July 2018}}

TherapueticLiz — the in-game name carries the transposed spelling "Therapuetic" — appears in the record with [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] from 2018, posting in the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] thread that June{{cite:thread-227373|posts #9, #12 and #17, 5 Jun 2018}} and writing in the Federation Tribute of 13 November 2018: "Glad I was apart of it for the entire ride. Kind of sad to see it end but nothing ever truly lasts."{{cite:thread-237070|post #4, 13 Nov 2018}}

On 26 June 2022 came the post that closed the public record. Correcting [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] — "Don't mean to necro, but a majority of the alliance info is incorrect. here's a list in case you want to update it" — the post set out [[cucumber-company|Cucumber Company]]'s fourteen guilds: [[aequitas|Aequitas]], [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]], [[avicia|Avicia]], Blacklisted, KongoBoys, Empire of Sindria, Gang of Fools, [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], The Clowns, Nefarious Ravens, Sins of Seedia, [[the-aquarium|The Aquarium]], Wynn Legacy and [[profession-heaven|Profession Heaven]]{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}. Less than two weeks later [[sg-voltage|Sg_Voltage]] deleted the thread's alliance section{{cite:thread-278112-p09|p9 #161, 7 Jul 2022}}, and no alliance roster has been published publicly since. The same post recorded the retreat from the forums in miniature: "my guild has ceased recruiting through forums. We have an application process within our discord as many other guilds now do."{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}

She is also credited with the video "SMTN ELSE SLANDER" of 3 October 2022, made after the bloc renamed itself [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]]{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-tfcs3b6emlq|"SMTN ELSE SLANDER", TherapueticLiz, uploaded 3 Oct 2022}} — leaving her chronicler of both the roster and its successor's mockery. As of September 2026 the Wynncraft API records her as Sins of Seedia's owner{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3, guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}.

Thundderr was one of the two chiefs of [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] under [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]], styled "Prince of the Phoenixes" in the guild's monarchy-themed rank scheme, alongside "Princess Whimsy".{{cite:thread-204381|post #1 (OP), 24 Sep 2017}} The guild was established on 23 September 2017 and co-founded the [[Coalition]] with [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] weeks later.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L869}}

He held the guild itself for seven weeks. AurumKitsune stepped down on 22 November 2017 and passed him the crown, making him King of the Phoenixes{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|Kingdom of Phoenixes dated event log}}, and he passed it back on 12 January 2018 when she returned{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|"The History of the Kingdom of Phoenixes", monarch and viceroy table}}.

[[drew1011|Drew1011]] handed him [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] on 31 January 2018, posting on its new thread the same day: "Make me proud."{{cite:thread-217600|post #2, Drew1011, 31 Jan 2018}} Revived inside the Coalition, the guild was allotted 19 territories in the alliance's February 2018 division of the map,{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}} and its May 2018 thread lists Thundderr as leader with [[kuroi|Kur0i]] and [[pillowpet|PillowPet]] — the guild's creator — still among its chiefs.{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}

Drew1011 wrote that he gave the guild up on 1 April 2018{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1154–1155}}; the guild’s announcement channel has him still directing it afterwards, asking for bounty placements on 7 April and sharing a new forum signature on 28 April.{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|4/7/2018 and 4/28/2018}} Through that spring he ran the guild inside [[the-federation|the Federation]] — posting the alliance server on 17 February, announcing the [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] revival on 10 March, promoting officers, and surveying members’ playing hours to schedule events.{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|2/17/2018, 3/10/2018 and 3/18/2018}} Drew1011's Federation tribute thanks him "for allowing HoL to shine once more and for being there for us in the crucial beginning months".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

Writing in May 2018, Drew1011 credited him with "probably somewhere between 100-150 territories" across several guilds — an estimate offered before the rule against warring on multiple accounts existed.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}}

Titans Valor [ANO], created on 2 Jul 2017,{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-titans-20valor|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} belonged to more alliances than almost any other guild - and documented much of that history itself through its newsletter, the [[titan-times|Titan Times]].

## History

### A community guild that took up warring (2017–18)

The guild described itself in December 2017 as one that "began as a community guild, although we have gotten more into warring, although Titans Valor will always be part community", valuing "loyalty, courage and respect"{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}. Its published rules bound members to the guild's diplomacy — "do not attack any guild in the alliance we are affiliated with, or if we have a pact of good terms" — and removed anyone inactive for more than two weeks{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}. The hierarchy then ran [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] as leader with KnixFice and AnDr3i_FTW as chiefs and advisers; by February 2018 the same three were styled Emperor and Consuls{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}{{cite:thread-206094-p04|#73, 24 Feb 2018, quoting the opening post}}.

The guild's own history dates its entry into [[emperium-of-wynn|the Emperium of Wynn]] to early August 2017, on an invitation extended the month it was founded, and records that it was voted out of the alliance on 11 October 2017 — an expulsion it says caused other guilds to leave and brought the alliance down.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Jul 2017 – Oct 2017}} It was invited into [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] within days, recreated its guild thread on 14 October, took every island territory on the map, and opened the Titans Valor Shop on the 30th.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Oct 2017}} That November it replaced its hierarchy with an imperial one and began styling itself an empire.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Nov 2017}}

The December war left it isolated. Its history calls the Coalition's declaration of 21 December the start of the Gavellian Invasion, records three guilds leaving War Syndicate on the 23rd and the rest abandoning the defence of Gavel, and says that Titans Valor formed an alliance of its own, Aphelion, in the attempt to recover; Aphelion fell apart when the land it had taken was infiltrated.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Dec 2017}} Through January 2018 the guild fought the Coalition without an alliance, alongside the other War Syndicate remnants, "although it would not be considered an official alliance yet, although we were under the name of Illustratus".{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Jan 2018}} On 16 February 2018, the day the Coalition split, Titans Valor established a sub-guild called Illustratus [Ius]; IceResistance appointed Dark5010 its serving emperor the following month.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Feb 2018 and Mar 2018}} IceResistance announced the Winter Festival on the guild's own thread on 16 December 2017, and the applications he was accepting that month required a promise not to change username while in the guild — the double-name glitch that trapped players in dead guilds.{{cite:thread-206094-p03|p3 #42–49, 16–17 Dec 2017}} It adopted an eight-medal award system that February and held its first award ceremony on 24 March 2018.{{cite:gdoc-1fev2xrzlfbeo2ll|Feb 2018 and Mar 2018}}

Its leader gave a different account of Aphelion's end in July 2018. He said he had assembled it quickly out of what was left of the War Syndicate, that it had been doing well at regathering the Wynn province, and that the [[coalition|Coalition]] attacked it at night once it decided the province was not to be theirs.{{cite:war-syndicate-successors-discord-private|13 Jul 2018}} He added that two alliances had been made from those remains, that few people knew it, that Aphelion merged with the other and left the old bloc almost whole, and that [[illustratus|Illustratus]] came out of the merger — which nobody else said.{{cite:war-syndicate-successors-discord-private|13 Jul 2018}} By September 2018 the name belonged to a guild rather than an alliance, one he described as having been made to help new players and whose leader he was advising to lower its level requirement and recruit more broadly.{{cite:war-syndicate-successors-discord-private|23 Sep 2018}}

### Its leader, and the Senate

The guild was governed by a Senate that voted on its alliance membership and on its posture in wars, and its leader repeatedly put questions to that body rather than settling them himself.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|guild governance}} [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] appears across the period under three names — Ice, IceResistance and hot pink emperor — one account, with the rename recorded, and members and rivals used all three interchangeably.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|the leader's handles}} Guild and tag do not match either: Titans Valor under the tag ANO, also written Titans Valor Empire.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|naming}}

Within a month of the guild's admission to the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] in July 2017 he had taken an unofficial Speaker role for that alliance's High Council, campaigning to fill its understaffed seats.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|July–August 2017}} When the alliance voted the guild out that October over complaints that he was undermining its leadership, a second guild left in sympathy, and an old log quoted back into the channel later has the guild reinstated on the instruction of the alliance's former leader to his successor rather than by any vote.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|October 2017}} The removal was settled among four of the alliance's leaders on the evening of 11 October 2017, three to one with an abstention, and was never put to the membership.{{cite:emperium-of-wynn-membership-2017-discord-private|11 Oct 2017, the leadership vote}} The guild that left in sympathy was Tranquility [PaT], and within the hour one of the four was proposing to take Titans Valor back on condition that its leader was not made Speaker again.{{cite:emperium-of-wynn-membership-2017-discord-private|11 Oct 2017, the aftermath}}

He ran [[illustratus|Illustratus]] as a side-alliance built from the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] remnant, having suggested the name for that server once War Syndicate was finished, and described it as an alliance of equals that had targeted Hall of Fame and the Kingdom of Foxes before going inactive.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|Illustratus as a side-alliance}} He said outright in March 2018 that before the Federation existed he had deliberately worked to destroy the [[coalition|Coalition]] — one message, and the kind of claim made to take credit as readily as to confess.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|March 2018}} Members describe the Federation as the surviving half of that alliance combined with Illustratus, so the guild that worked to break the first supplied part of the ancestry of the second.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|guild accounts, 2018}}{{cite:coalition-fracture-2018-discord-private|February 2018}}

### Whose enemies (April 2018)

On the evening of 3 April 2018 the guild's leader asked the Federation's leadership channel whether there ought to be a rule that member guilds must attack any guild the alliance had listed as an enemy, with enemies designated by vote, and set out the three reactions to vote with. An officer restated the effect so nobody could miss it: if the yes vote passed, every Federation guild would be obliged to attack the guilds on that list.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the motion}} The alliance's founder gave the principle behind it — that to join the alliance was to take on every war it was engaged in as one's own.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the founder}}

The man who had raised it then said he could not comply. There were guilds he would have no difficulty attacking, he said, but he could guess perfectly well which guilds would end up listed; he had helped the alliance before and particularly in the last war, but could not take part in this one if he were obliged to attack any guild the Federation called an enemy. Pressed, he said he would keep warring where he was needed and would refuse to fight certain guilds by his own choice.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the objection}}

A member put the counter-argument in a line: if people were trying to take the alliance down that made them an enemy, and how could he belong to it and decline to fight the people trying to destroy it.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the counter-argument}} The rest of the channel was not arguing. Within seconds it was asking whether he had just revealed himself as the opposing leader's source of information, and whether he could simply be removed from the alliance.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the reaction}}

The vote carried. By early the following morning a member reported that it had reached two thirds; asked shortly afterwards whether it was settled, the leaders worked through the arithmetic. The alliance had twenty-one guilds, but the founder had directed that Kasai Shinrai not be counted, since counting it would have given the leader of Titans Valor a double vote.{{cite:federation-obligation-to-attack-2018-discord-private|4 Apr 2018, the count}} That is the one-vote-per-guild rule at its strongest: not a duplicate ballot voided after the fact, but a member guild struck from the roll in advance. The twenty-one is the leaders' own count, and it sits above the nineteen guilds on the alliance's published map of 24 March.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|3/24/2018}}

What the rule bound was every member guild, to attack any guild the alliance had voted onto its enemy list, and the [[the-federation|Federation]] was still revising that list in its leadership channel three months later.{{cite:federation-enemy-list-july-2018-discord-private|2 Jul 2018}}

Later the same evening an officer told the guild's leader that both of his guilds would be put to a vote on inactive guilds, and that it was not looking good for them; he answered that they were not inactive but had decided to help in a different war, and was told that Kasai Shinrai was inactive regardless.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|3 Apr 2018, the threat}} The inactivity motion went up the next morning against four other guilds, and neither of his was named on it.{{cite:federation-inactive-guilds-april-2018-discord-private|4 Apr 2018, the motion}} It is described at [[the-federation-april-2018|the Federation in April 2018]].

### Neutrality and expulsion (April–May 2018)

On 12 April 2018 the guild declared neutrality on behalf of its Senate, staying a nominal member of the Federation while withdrawing from its wars; a vote to expel it followed two days later, after its leader publicly criticised the alliance.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|April 2018}} It was expelled at the start of May 2018 for inactivity and its leader's perceived disloyalty. He left the guild from the alliance's own server before the vote concluded, and the alliance then voted to remove it, treated it as having abandoned its membership, and announced that other guilds were free to attack it.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|May 2018}}

What the guild did next sits awkwardly beside the reason given. Its recorded war participation runs 28 transitions in April 2018, 43 in May, 163 in June and 250 in July — roughly nine times as much warring in July as in the month it was judged on — though its holdings stayed small, moving between nothing and nineteen territories across those four months.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|war transitions by month, Apr–Jul 2018: 28, 43, 163, 250}}{{cite:territory-exchanges|Titans Valor holdings replayed from every exchange, 1 Apr – 1 Aug 2018 UTC: range 0–19, peak 19 at 04:21 on 29 Jul}} The alliance judged it on the months it had, and those were genuinely its quietest.

### Organization

Above the recruit rank sat the [ANO] Council, entered after a week in the guild by interview with the leader rather than by written application, with contribution to the guild — donated experience among other things — counting in the applicant's favour. Recruiters were council members recognised for bringing in new players; captains led in war or on the community side; advisers, under a Lead Adviser, oversaw the other officers and answered to the leader.{{cite:gdoc-1wypxzcjmw75lyww|"Titans Valor [ANO] Hierarchy"}}

The guild also concluded a bilateral non-aggression pact with the [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]], signed by IceResistance as Emperor of Titans Valor and [[drew1011|Drew1011]] as Viceroy of the Foxes. Neither guild was to attack the other or its lands under any circumstance; either side could end it by notifying the other's leadership, and any aggression ended it automatically. The pact bound only the two guilds: "neither are obliged to be at peace with parties they are allianced with."{{cite:gdoc-1tdkt4kvwsxy7hdv|Titans Valor / Kingdom of Foxes non-aggression pact}}

### Federation and the wars of 2019

The guild was admitted to the Federation on 17 February 2018 after a lengthy debate about whether it could be trusted, having left the grouping it had been fighting in.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|17 Feb 2018}} Its own subguild [[illustratus|Illustratus]] followed by a contested route: found holding alliance territory and roles without a vote, refused admission three to seven on 25 February, declared independent, and carried on a second vote in March whose counting rule was announced with the result.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|24 Feb – 17 Mar 2018}}

The guild's membership of the Federation was explicitly conditional on another guild's. In March 2018 [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] told the alliance's war channel that his own senate had voted to join on the strength of [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]]'s adherence to it, that Titans Valor meant to stand wherever that guild stood, and that a departure by it would trigger a vote in his senate which he expected would follow it out.{{cite:sins-of-seedia-guild-profile-discord-private|Federation war channel, March 2018}}

Titans Valor cycled through [[the-federation|the Federation]] three times in 2018 (February-May, June-July, and September to the collapse).{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In 2019 it fought with [[Terra]] against [[Luna]], attacking Luna's guilds 214 times in the fortnight between Terra's formation and its first free-for-all declaration,{{cite:territory-exchanges|attacks by Titans Valor on the guilds recorded as Luna members, 30 Aug – 13 Sep 2019 UTC: 214. No alliance had a free-for-all list in force between 12 Oct 2018 and 14 Sep 2019, so the raw count is also the contested count}} co-founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] on 15 Sep 2019, left on 21 Nov - two days before the alliance collapsed - and co-founded [[Horologium]] on 1 Dec 2019 with [[DiamondDeities]] and [[The Simple Ones]], which died with DiamondDeities' disbandment on 8 Jan 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Under its tag ANO the guild is named, with Immortals Light, as one of the two that did the attacking under [[alovilatious-treaty|the multi-guild targeting arrangement of January 2018]] against Hall of Fame, a [[coalition|Coalition]] member guild; a third guild was counted in the grouping without carrying the fighting.{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition war channel, 4 Feb 2018}} The arrangement had been assembled and named by the guild's own leader, [[iceresistance|IceResistance]], posting as Ice and later as hot pink emperor, who denied five weeks later that it had ever existed.{{cite:pasta-treaties-2018-discord-private|Coalition and Federation channels, January–February 2018}}{{cite:emperium-announcements|9/1/2017}} After the Federation collapsed it petitioned to affiliate with the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] on 12 November 2018, citing that collapse as its reason.{{cite:federation-collapse-2018-discord-private|12 Nov 2018}}

### Hestia, Artemis, and the blocs of 2020-2021

From around mid-2020 Titans Valor belonged to the community alliance [[Hestia]]. By 2 Dec 2020 it was in [[Artemis]]: its own member [[paladinsorcerer|Pally]] wrote on [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] that 'ANO is apart of the alliances Hestia (a community alliance between ANO, ESI, LXA, and PUN) and Artemis (war alliance) made up of all the current massive land holding guilds on the map'.{{cite:thread-278112|post #10, 2 Dec 2020}} The guild stayed through [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021 into [[Valhalla]] and [[Vanir]], and fought the ex-Valhalla side of [[valhalla-khaos-war|the Khaos war]] into 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Pally restated the Hestia roster on the megalist on 6 Jun 2021.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #140, 6 Jun 2021}}

### The realignment and Adonis (2022-2024)

Titans Valor joined [[Cucumber Company]] for Season 5, which ran from 3 Mar to 2 May 2022 - its newsletter's first volume (8 May 2022) records 'our first season being a part of the new Cucumber Company war alliance'{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} - and carried into [[smtn elf]] until that alliance's quiet death in mid-2023.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}} Around May 2022 its leaders and Empire of Sindria's founded [[Adonis]] as Hestia declined, 'a space for those of us who are still active to hang together';{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} Adonis was still active in March 2024.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Its newsletter records the guild's standing through the first seasons. Titans Valor finished Season 6 fifth, and entered Season 7 with a claim grown from twenty-seven territories to thirty by the addition of Jofash Docks, Aldorei Valley West Entrance and Light Forest West Lower.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol4|vol. 4, 24 Jul 2022}} It ended Season 7 sixth, on just over six million season-rating points.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol5|vol. 5, 27 Aug 2022}} War strategists were certified by an internal test, and each season the guild ran its own warring competition, Ocean Trials, paying liquid emeralds to its top warrers.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol4|vol. 4, 24 Jul 2022}}{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol5|vol. 5, 27 Aug 2022}} The [[adonis|Adonis]] alliance kept a shared vanilla Minecraft server for its members from about June 2022 and ran cross-guild events on its Discord.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol4|vol. 4, 24 Jul 2022}}

![Territory-map excerpt from Titan Times vol. 13 (22 March 2024) marking out Titans Valor's 'Jungle FFA' course through nine numbered ANO-held territories in Season 17; neighbouring holdings tagged TAq, AVO and DFS are visible around them.](/images/chronicles/media/titans-valor-1c6832fa.webp){{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol13|vol. 13, 22 Mar 2024}}

### Ownership

[[iceresistance|IceResistance]] founded the guild and opened its recruitment thread on 15 Oct 2017,{{cite:thread-206094|post #1, opened 15 Oct 2017}} and was still speaking for it politically in December 2020. By October 2022 he was on hiatus,{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}} and by March 2023 he was the guild's founder and previous owner{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}} - ownership changed hands at some point between those dates, and the successor was not named at the time.

In a November 2025 interview with Lamplesspost, the guild's leader Calluum - a Sage Council member back in vol. 1 - described his succession: 'No one else wanted it when pally was stepping down, so I realised I'd need to step up and take on the mantle.'{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol20|vol. 20, 23 Nov 2025}} Pally - apparently ANO's [[paladinsorcerer|PaladinSorcerer]] - led the guild before Calluum, who led it by November 2025. Whether Pally took over directly from IceResistance, and when either handover happened, was never recorded.

IceResistance remained a public voice for the guild long after leaving the ownership: his October 2025 forum remark that real diplomacy 'happens in private alliance chats' names the defining fact of [[private-diplomacy-era|the private-diplomacy era]].{{cite:thread-322643|post #1, 2 Oct 2025}}

### Later years (2024-2026)

Titan Times ran to vol. 21 on 18 May 2026,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol21|vol. 21, 18 May 2026}} but from vol. 14 onward it names no alliance at all, reporting only guild-internal affairs: the guild reached level 105 in mid-2024,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol15|vol. 15, 5 Aug 2024}} placed fifth on the Season 21 leaderboard and sixth in Season 22,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol17|vol. 17}}{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol18|vol. 18}} and continued its internal Ocean Trials war rankings through Season 29.{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol21|vol. 21, 18 May 2026}}

## Leaving the Federation (July 2018)

The guild turned a year old on 2 July 2018 and its leader marked it by asking that it not be expelled. Late on the 1st he told [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s leadership channel to expect inactivity from Titans Valor in wars, that he would be away for a little under a month, and that they should not kick it{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|1 Jul 2018, the request}}; the alliance's founder answered that he would not allow it.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|1 Jul 2018, the answer}}

By the 10th he had given the guild up. At 13:47 he asked the leadership channel why he still held a role there when he had disbanded his guild, and said he had not done it in the game only because he was away from home.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|10 Jul 2018, 13:47}} Twenty minutes later he said he might keep the guild alive on a second account and join a good one himself, that it had never been intended as a war guild, and that he had decided against carrying a dead guild into a second year.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|10 Jul 2018, the second account and the reasons}} That morning he had said what he wanted instead: to rebuild [[legio|Legio Praetoria]], which he thought should never have fallen and whose story had made him create a guild at all, and of which the Federation formed no part.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|10 Jul 2018, 06:35 to 07:28, Legio Praetoria}}

Nine days later a member moved that the alliance expel the guild for showing no sign of being able to take ground anywhere.{{cite:federation-kick-vote-19-july-2018-discord-private|19 Jul 2018, the motion}} At 14:34 the following afternoon, in the middle of an exchange of insults with that member, the leader announced that he was going: he would rebuild the old alliance, and he would be beyond the man's reach.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|20 Jul 2018, 14:34, the announcement}} His roles came off before the next morning, when a member asked the general channel whether the guild was still in the alliance given that its leader had none.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, 06:41, the roles noticed}}{{cite:federation-late-july-2018-discord-private|20 Jul 2018}} He had announced departures before, and this one came inside a run of insults, so it fixes what he said and the reasons he gave rather than when the decision was taken.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|20 Jul 2018, the setting of the statement}}

The removal reached the membership as somebody's copy-paste of the leadership channel, in which the founder said he had heard the leader might have applied to the opposing alliance, could not verify it, and had taken the roles away until he could speak to him.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, the paste}} Asked eight minutes later whether the man stood accused of treason, the member who had pasted it agreed that he broadly did — one member's word for it rather than the alliance's designation.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, the word treason}} By the afternoon members were asking whether there should be an announcement and being told that nobody knew the departure was confirmed.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, 15:19, unconfirmed}}

The captures began, and the leadership could not agree what they meant. The guild leader whose territories were being taken reported that Titans Valor's leader was telling him his captains were warring at random{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, the report of randomness}}; two other leaders answered that captains warring at random would not be chasing one guild's assigned ground in particular, and called the explanation false.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, the answer to it}} The last attempt at a settlement came from the guild that was leaving. At 18:17 the founder told the leadership channel that its leader wanted to come in under [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] as a subguild and that he might be able to arrange it{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, 18:17, the subguild proposal}}, and in the same minutes that the main reason the man was considering leaving at all was that he was harassed whenever he spoke in that channel; another leader replied that both sides were to blame.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, the reason given and the reply}}

A week out the guild held seventeen territories by a member's count in the war channel on 28 July, and two members remarked that it had warred outside the alliance when it had not warred inside it; a third answered that it had still done more damage while it was in the Federation than it ever would outside.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|28 Jul 2018, 21:30, seventeen territories}} That seventeen is read off the game's guild list, and the capture record agrees with it almost exactly: replaying every exchange puts the guild at sixteen territories at the minute the count was given, and at nineteen nine minutes earlier, which is the highest it reached between April and July.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Titans Valor holdings replayed from every exchange: 16 at 04:30 UTC on 29 Jul 2018, the minute of the 21:30 count on the export clock; peak 19 at 04:21 UTC}} The guild's holdings turned over fast enough that the two instruments could disagree by a good deal more than one without either being wrong.

A month later the alliance it had left was watching it rebuild. On 27 August 2018 a member told the Federation's war channel that Titans Valor was starting to build territory up and held thirteen at that moment; a guild leader answered that they were going after the lightly defended areas and sweeping them, another asked whether they were with the rival alliance, and a member of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] observed that they used to be allies.{{cite:federation-keeping-track-august-2018-discord-private|27 Aug 2018, the warning and the count}} The capture record puts the guild between nothing and seventeen territories across that day on the export's clock, so thirteen falls inside what the log will bear; the same day measured in UTC tops out at nine, and the difference is the seven hours between the two clocks rather than anything the guild did.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Titans Valor holdings replayed from every exchange: range 0–17 for 27 Aug 2018 on the export clock (07:00 UTC 27 Aug – 07:00 UTC 28 Aug), range 0–9 for the UTC day}}

The accusation that had cost him his roles was withdrawn by the alliance's founder nine days after the guild had gone. On 30 July the member who had moved the expulsion motion told the leadership channel that the leader had been affiliated with the opposing alliance even before the vote{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|30 Jul 2018, the assertion}}; the founder answered flatly that he had not been, said he had sources in every one of that alliance's chats, and that nothing short of a screenshot of the man working with them would settle it.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|30 Jul 2018, the disavowal}} The mover allowed that he might have been played.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|30 Jul 2018, the answer}}

Two months afterwards he gave a reason for the departure that he had given nobody in July. On 21 September 2018 he told the Federation's leadership channel that the description attached to his guild's own vote had stated there was nothing to show Titans Valor could take territory anywhere; that he thought the statement untrue and rude; that it had been a large part of what drove the guild out; and that taking a single territory would have shown it up.{{cite:titans-valor-family-of-guilds-2018-discord-private|21 Sep 2018, the reason given}} He called it an admission vote. The wording matches the ground stated on the motion of 19 July to expel the guild, and which of the two documents he meant was never settled.{{cite:federation-kick-vote-19-july-2018-discord-private|19 Jul 2018, the motion}} Setting the two beside each other is this article's.

## The treaty of 9 September 2018

The third readmission was preceded by a treaty, and the treaty by an application on unusual terms. On 4 September 2018 [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s founder put to the alliance's voting channel a statement he said the guild's leader had sent him: that Titans Valor had enjoyed fighting for the Federation and had found no unity in the Confederation, that it had lately not wanted territories at all and had been giving them to the alliance, and that its allies had made it what it was and it wished to serve them.{{cite:titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|4 Sep 2018, the application}} Ten minutes later he added a further line from the same source: the guild wanted no territories and wished only to serve the alliance it had helped to found, and its friends.{{cite:titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|4 Sep 2018}} In a month when the alliance's leaders argued about almost nothing but territory, a guild was applying on the footing that it wanted none.{{cite:federation-map-round-september-2018-discord-private|September 2018}}

Next door in the leadership channel they treated the vote as a joke while it ran. The result was already obvious at nine to nothing, one said; another voted yes and no at once and was told to remove the no; a third said that if enough of them voted ironically the motion would carry, and a fourth that the guild could then be in the alliance ironically. Two were asked to pick a side. Somebody counted it as the guild's third attempt, or fourth, and another asked what made its leader suppose he was wanted back.{{cite:titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|4 Sep 2018, the leadership channel}} In the middle of it one leader wrote that here at last was a guild that did not want territories.{{cite:titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|4 Sep 2018}} The vote failed on the threshold. Just over twenty-four hours after it went up a leader asked whether a motion that had not reached two thirds within the day had therefore failed, and was told that it had; the count was given in the channel as nine to five, which the leaders worked out at sixty-four per cent, short of the two thirds required.{{cite:federation-titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|5 Sep 2018, the count reported at the time}} No admission was announced that day, or for a fortnight.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|announcements channel, 4–19 Sep 2018}}

What the alliance produced instead was an instrument. On 8 September it asked its guild leaders whether to make a treaty under which Titans Valor would attack the Confederation and the Federation would leave its ground alone except when reclaiming assigned territories.{{cite:titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|8 Sep 2018, the motion}} On the ninth it told its war role that a treaty had been established on those terms: the guild would attack only the Confederation and would help the alliance regain its territories, and nobody was to attack it unless reclaiming their own assigned ground from it.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/9/2018 1:36 PM}} The weekly bulletin thirteen minutes later carried an exception the announcement had not, for free-for-all ground, and on the fifteenth the announcements channel had to remind the war role of the treaty again.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/9/2018 1:49 PM and 9/15/2018}}

On 18 September the founder put a fresh application from the guild to the voting channel. It opened by observing that two weeks had passed and that the guild's leader had been giving the alliance territory throughout the fortnight, apologised for the guild's past aggression towards the Federation, and asked to be taken back.{{cite:federation-titans-valor-treaty-september-2018-discord-private|18 Sep 2018, the application}} Fourteen days separated it from the motion that had refused the guild, which was the interval the alliance had voted itself on 1 September for applicants it turned down.{{cite:federation-admissions-rush-2018-discord-private|1 Sep 2018, the waiting-period vote}} Whether the alliance counted that fortnight from the posting of the refused motion or from its failure a day later was never stated. On 19 September, ten days after the treaty, the guild rejoined the Federation outright.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/19/2018}} Reading the treaty as a stage in the readmission rather than an alternative to it is this article's; the alliance connected none of the three.

The shape came back under this guild's name. On 1 October 2018 the Federation announced a treaty with Minerva [Min] and gave its terms by reference rather than setting them out: "Minerva [Min] has qualified for a treaty with Federation (Similar to what ANO had before)."{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|10/1/2018}} Twelve days after the guild's own treaty had been replaced by membership, the alliance was still using it as the name for a class of arrangement.

Its leader put what a guild was worth in emeralds in the middle of the summer before. On the morning of 10 July 2018 he told the Federation's leadership channel that he had once offered sixty stacks of emeralds for [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] outright, on condition that the guild kept its own leadership, and that the offer had been refused; founding a guild, he pointed out in the same conversation, cost five emeralds.{{cite:federation-member-guilds-july-2018-discord-private|10 Jul 2018, the offer and the price of founding one}} It is his account of himself, given in a conversation about how wealthy he was — [[federation-member-guilds-july-2018|the Federation's member guilds in July 2018]].

On 21 November 2018 the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] told its whole membership that Titans Valor was a friend of the alliance rather than a member: that it would be seen helping in the Canyon when needed, that it would be taking instructions from the pact's leader, and that it was to be treated well although it was not a full member.{{cite:aesir-membership-record-2018-discord-private|21 Nov 2018}} Setting that beside the Federation's treaty is this article's.

## Four movements in eight months

The guild's Federation membership was not a single span but four, inside five months. It was expelled at the start of May 2018 on a motion citing inactivity, antagonising other leaders and no effort to help the alliance; it rejoined on 13 June, announced in a single line; it left again on 22 July alongside [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] as Aphelion joined; and it was readmitted on 19 September by nine votes to three, welcomed back in the general channel the next day.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|4 May and 19 Sep 2018}}{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 6/13/2018 and 7/22/2018}}

The alliance found the pattern funny by then. On the day the readmission passed, a member joked that if the guild were kicked again they should leave its role in place on the Discord to save the trouble.{{cite:titans-valor-guild-profile-discord-private|19 Sep 2018}}

Looking back in October 2024, its leader said he had, arguably, had four guilds inside the Federation, and named them: Titans Valor and three others.{{cite:titans-valor-family-of-guilds-2018-discord-private|20 Oct 2024, the count of four}} It bears on how the alliance voted, because the Federation counted one vote per guild and set its admission threshold at two thirds of the member guilds.{{cite:federation-admissions-2018-discord-private|the admission threshold counted on member guilds}} Whether all four were members at the same time, or held by him while each of them was, was never set down.

## A claim of authority, September 2019

Ten months after [[the-federation-dies|the Federation dissolved]], the guild's leader claimed it. On the evening of 3 September 2019, in [[terra|Terra]]'s war channel, he told the Federation's founder that Titans Valor had never left that alliance, that the founder's own guild had, and that as the last guild still housed under the alliance's name he therefore held full authority over whatever remained of it; membership rights, he said, had lapsed with the guild that walked out.{{cite:federation-authority-claimed-september-2019-discord-private|3 Sep 2019, the claim}} The founder answered that [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] had left without him, and that his appointment to the imperial style put the question of the remnants beyond argument.{{cite:federation-authority-claimed-september-2019-discord-private|3 Sep 2019, the answer}} A third member watching said the point was evenly balanced.{{cite:federation-authority-claimed-september-2019-discord-private|3 Sep 2019, the bystander}}

The first of the two factual claims is contradicted by the alliance's own announcements channel, which recorded on 22 July 2018 that Titans Valor had left it alongside [[angels-of-eternal|Angels of Eternal]] as [[aphelion|Aphelion]] joined.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 7/22/2018}} The notice was written by the man being argued with, and neither of them cited it.{{cite:federation-authority-claimed-september-2019-discord-private|3 Sep 2019, the announcement uncited}} It settles July 2018 and nothing after it: the guild was readmitted on 19 September 2018 and was a member at the dissolution.{{cite:federation-alliance-announcements|Drew1011, 9/19/2018}} What the title he was answered with was worth is at [[federation-last-motions-2018|the Federation's last motions]].

Earlier the same evening he said that his guild had come close to becoming a subject guild of Kingdom Foxes about a year or more previously, and gave no date.{{cite:federation-authority-claimed-september-2019-discord-private|3 Sep 2019, the near-vassalage}} Fourteen months before, on 21 July 2018, the Federation's founder had told its leadership channel that the guild's leader wanted to come in under Kingdom Foxes as a subguild.{{cite:titans-valor-departure-july-2018-discord-private|21 Jul 2018, 18:17, the subguild proposal}} Nothing in either conversation joins the two.

