## Legacy
Valhalla headed the alliance line that ran Goose–Valhalla–Vanir and, after the winter war with Khaos, fed the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]] into [[Cucumber Company]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Its era also marks the closing of the public record: it was the first dominant alliance whose roster never appeared in public.

Founded by Kingdom of Foxes (later [[Kingdom Foxes]]) and [[Imperial]] "not established for the purpose of war" and governed by an Electorate of guild masters{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}}, it persisted as a social and political layer beneath — and once, briefly, above — every war bloc from the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]] to the eve of [[the-realignment-era|the realignment era]].

## The revival that was not attempted

On 16 February 2018 — the day the [[coalition|Coalition]] broke and [[the-federation|the Federation]] was founded — the Kingdom of Foxes' Viceroy recorded that he and another member had substantial changes prepared for Valkyrie and had wanted to bring it back to what it had been. They abandoned the idea because nothing remained in the alliance beyond [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] and one other guild, both by then finished.{{cite:valkyrie-revival-2018-discord-private|16 Feb 2018}}

Talks had been running for at least four days: on 12 February a Coalition leader noted that there was talk of reviving it, and in the same conversation traced its whole history from memory — [[imperial|Imperial]] and the Kingdom of Foxes, then those two with a third guild, then those three with a fourth, then Imperial with [[house-of-sentinels|House of Sentinels]], then nothing. She marked the third step as uncertain herself.{{cite:valkyrie-revival-2018-discord-private|12 Feb 2018}} The alliance's own relaunch of August 2016 is better evidence of its composition than a member's memory two years later, and where the two differ the relaunch should be preferred.

She also recorded that every member guild carried a small icon marking it as a Valkyrie guild.{{cite:valkyrie-revival-2018-discord-private|12 Feb 2018}} Membership was a visible thing rather than a private understanding, which matters for an alliance that later ran inside another one.

The Federation was the second option that day. The first was reviving Valkyrie, and what ruled it out was the state of the surviving membership rather than anything about the alliance itself. A revival was announced three weeks later all the same, and it was drafted before it was sent: in the guild's board channel a leader told the member who would post it to include the revival, then asked him to hold for a minute.{{cite:valkyrie-revival-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018}} On 10 March 2018 Holders of LE told its members twice within a quarter of an hour that Valkyrie was being brought back, with an invitation to join.{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|3/10/2018}}

## History

### Founding and the Electorate (2015)
Valkyrie's founding thread was opened on 10 September 2015 by [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]], Queen of the Foxes, and set out both the date and the purpose: "unlike many other alliances, Valkyrie was not established for the purpose of war. Rather, the partnership was created with the aim of solidifying and maintaining the already very good social relations between the two guilds." It was put into action on 2 June 2015, the Kingdom of Foxes' first anniversary.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}}{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.1) Our History}}

The alliance's own constitution gives the collapse of [[legio|Legio Praetoria]] as the reason it existed: "The guild community was devastated by the wake of Legio Praetoria. Competition between guilds was unhealthy and toxic, and this started to tear the community apart. Allegiances determined your friends, and they also determined your enemies."{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.1) Our History}} Four aims followed, among them "to keep member-guilds free from the scourge of hyper-competition" and to be "the beacon of maturity and professionalism for all guilds in the community".{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.2) Our Mission}}

Its constitution left internal government alone and pooled only foreign policy: "While guild governments may still maintain their powers with regards to their respective internal affairs, all powers regarding the conclusion of foreign affairs or policy will be forfeited to the Valkyrie Electorate. This administration comprises the guild leaders of each member-guild and functions using unanimous agreement in their decision-making process."{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}} A third guild followed that winter: at a joint award ceremony on 12 December 2015, LoveLusting announced that "the Lightly Toasted Heroes, lead by klove and Emily, will be joining the Valkyrie Alliance."{{cite:thread-89529|post #16, LoveLusting, 7 Jan 2016 (reporting the ceremony of 12 Dec 2015)}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2015: "12th Dec, Lightly Toasted Heroes [LTH] joins Valkyrie"}}

### The Ordo Malleus intake (March 2016)
Valkyrie's first expansion beyond its founding circle followed the collapse of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] on 9 March 2016. Holders Of LE [HoL] and HaHaUnited [HHU] joined on 18 March 2016{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entries}}, a date Valkyrie's constitution also gives.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.1) Our History}} The Kingdom of Foxes' handbook instead dates HaHaUnited's entry to 20 May 2016, under Ha_Ha_Redstone.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section IX: The Alliance}} [[drew1011|Drew1011]], who owned Holders of LE and negotiated the entry, described the occasion: the four guilds gathered at a ceremony in Llevigar on 18 March 2016, nine days after Ordo Malleus's collapse, and it was there that their joining was officially announced.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L472–473, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The town is given differently in the two typings of that instalment, and the reading above is the later one, which is the copy that left Discord{{cite:drew1011-storytime|instalment headings, 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}}; [[guild-community-and-institutions|the ceremony]] sets out why it is followed. By his account the opening had been arranged months earlier — he had been sent to recruit Kingdom of Foxes and Imperial into Ordo Malleus in November 2015, failed, and kept the friendship with LoveLusting that resulted{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L447–448, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} — and he describes the alliance in that period as having "no true leader", with LoveLusting its "unofficial leader"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L448, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}.

Holders of LE left on 5 June 2016 to found [[halcyon|Halcyon]] with ToastedPandas{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, opening post (Halcyon founded 5 Jun 2016 between ToastedPandas and Holders of LE)}}, and Drew1011 published a leaving message in which he called the guild "the first (and probably only) guild to ever leave Valkyrie" and undertook not to share alliance business{{cite:gdoc-18udeawtdyn6-sew|Drew1011's leaving message, preserved from Skype}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L499–501, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}. It rejoined on 3 September 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L554, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}.

![The message by which Holders of LE left Valkyrie on 5 June 2016 to found Halcyon; from Drew1011's account of the period. It also records that LoveLusting drew the guild's art.](/images/chronicles/storytime/17-image.webp)

### The Parliament and the 2016 relaunches
Valkyrie's thread was rebuilt twice in thirteen months. "ahri left so Kv had to make a new one, then Kv left so now I run this thing," Yuno F Gasai of Imperial wrote on 13 September 2016.{{cite:thread-147790|post #15, Yuno F Gasai, 13 Sep 2016}} Yuno's relaunch thread, opened 29 August 2016, reused the founding text with one substitution: the Electorate had become the "Valkyrie Parliament", now "the guild masters of each member-guild", still acting by unanimity. Its roster of four — Imperial, Kingdom of Foxes, House of Sentinels and Lightly Toasted Heroes [Lth] — was the alliance's largest recorded concurrent membership.{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}} "pretzule leads a Valkyrie guild tho," Yuno answered a rival's boast in the same thread.{{cite:thread-147790|post #8, Yuno F Gasai, 29 Aug 2016}}

Three rosters survive from a seven-week window and no two agree. The August thread lists Imperial, Kingdom of Foxes, House of Sentinels and Lightly Toasted Heroes{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}}; Drew1011, describing 3 September, wrote that "the alliance was now composed of Imp, HHU, LTH, and Snt"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L552, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}; and the October thread lists Kingdom of Foxes, Holders of LE and Ha Ha United{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}}. Drew1011's version explains the August list's Kingdom of Foxes entry as stale, since the guild had disbanded on 2 July 2016{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jul 2016: "2nd Jul, LoveLusting disbands Kingdom Foxes [Fox]"}}, but his own October thread lists Kingdom of Foxes again, while by his narrative it did not exist between 2 July and 24 November 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L600–604, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}. The likeliest reading is that the published rosters were kept loosely, with guilds carried on paper after they ceased to operate.

### The 2016 leadership change
The third relaunch, opened on 15 October 2016 by [[drew1011|Drew1011]], marks the point where the alliance had outlived its founders.{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}} Imperial had left in the intervening weeks — "Hey, we are pretty alive," its leadership replied to a mourner in the thread, "Just not in the alliance anymore"{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, Ascended Kitten, 15 Oct 2016}} — and Lightly Toasted Heroes had also gone "a few weeks ago"{{cite:thread-159734|post #11, Drew1011, 15 Oct 2016}}, "in order to try and revive the guild".{{cite:thread-159734|post #18, Yuno F Gasai, 21 Oct 2016}}

The sequence ran over three days: the Valkyrie guild leaders convened on 13 October 2016, Yuno F Gasai was asked to step down on the 14th, and Drew1011 became leader of the alliance on the 15th.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Oct 2016}} The narrative of what happened between the two threads is Drew1011's, written in February 2018; he is its principal actor and beneficiary. By his account [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] proposed the change: "she suddenly suggested that the other leaders and me should coup Yuno and make myself the leader of Valkyrie. The thought had barely crossed my mind until Ari suggested it."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L556–557, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} He describes canvassing Misty of House of Sentinels and Ha_Ha_Redstone of Ha Ha United, drafting each message himself and having Misty send it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L562–567, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}. The first message, signed "A Unanimous Declaration from the Leaders of Valkyrie", asked Yuno F Gasai to "step down from your position and focus your attention on leading Imperial, not Valkyrie", citing his inactivity and his creation of a war alliance and admission of the Wybel Kingdom to it without consultation{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L567 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}.

![The first ultimatum sent to Yuno F Gasai, drafted by Drew1011 and sent by Misty; from Drew1011's account of the period.](/images/chronicles/storytime/21-image.webp)

Yuno declined, asked for more time, asked who the others intended to install — which Drew1011 says he refused to answer — and said Imperial would leave if he were removed. "To be truthful, I thought he was bluffing. I think we all did," Drew1011 wrote{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L568–574, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. A third message answered that "if the price of this change is the loss of Imperial, then that is a price we are all willing to take"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L576 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. "Immediately after I sent this message, Yuno announced that Imperial would be leaving. He left all the chats and deleted his Valkyrie thread."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L577–578, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

![The message that preceded Imperial's withdrawal from Valkyrie, autumn 2016; from Drew1011's account of the period.](/images/chronicles/storytime/23-image.webp)

The October thread reproduced the August thread's constitutional text verbatim: "I obtained Yuno's permission to copy and paste his Valkyrie thread, and posted it myself," Drew1011 wrote.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L580, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}} The reaction in the new thread was elegiac: "R.I.P OG Valkyrie guilds", wrote DireFire{{cite:thread-159734|post #5, DireFire, 15 Oct 2016}}, and another reader observed "tmw the alliance originally made by Imp and Fox has neither Imp nor Fox in it"{{cite:thread-159734|post #2, Zahr, 15 Oct 2016}}. Drew1011 led the alliance from 15 October 2016 to 10 March 2018.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}}

The alliance did not revive under him. "I began revising the Valkyrie constitution, but only ever got about a fourth of the way through… I could not lead an alliance that did not have the ambition to rise," he wrote of the weeks after the relaunch{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L586–587, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}; and of February 2017, "a mere five days after the leadership change, the House of Sentinels left the alliance. Considering HoL and HHU, the only other guilds left in Valkyrie, were already dead, there seemed to be no point in trying to revive Valkyrie at that time."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L670–671, composed 16 Feb 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}} House of Sentinels' departure thus fell around 12 February 2017, leaving the revived Kingdom of Foxes as the alliance's only functioning member.

### The Federation years (2018)

The revival has a date and a voice. On 10 March 2018 Thundderr told the Holders of LE channel "We are also reviving an alliance known as Valkyrie", and gave a server to join{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|3/10/2018}} — three weeks after the same channel had carried the Federation’s own server, and while both alliances ran side by side.{{cite:holders-of-le-announcements|2/17/2018}}
Valkyrie persisted through the year of [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s total map dominance, several of its members simultaneously inside the war bloc. The Hive joined around March 2018, welcomed that April as having joined a month earlier, and [[Emorians]] joined on 23 May 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The memberships of Holders Of LE and HaHaUnited appear to have ended with a leadership restructure on 10 March 2018, the day Drew1011's Valkyrie leadership ended.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}} The alliance still ran an operational channel that spring: describing a warning he passed on in May 2018, Drew1011 names "the Valkyrie command channel" as one of three places he sent it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1159, composed 20 Jun 2019}}.

### What the revival consisted of

The alliance was assembled again rather than restored to anybody. On 7 October 2018 the leader of [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]] told the Federation's war channel what she had wanted from it: the original pairing of [[imperial|Imperial]] and her own guild back inside Valkyrie. At the time, she said, Valkyrie was Lightly Toasted Heroes, HaHaUnited and [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]], and the word revival described putting the two founders back in.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|7 Oct 2018, what the revival was}} The sitting guilds were not put out.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|7 Oct 2018, nobody removed}} Reading that beside the leadership restructure of 10 March is this article's, and it accounts for memberships that ended without a vote or a notice. Minutes earlier another member had said he remembered the period when Valkyrie was dead, and that a thing only needs reviving if it is dead.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|7 Oct 2018, the remark on reviving}}

The Federation's founder had posted the news to his own leadership channel on the evening of 10 March 2018, as a link to a thread on the game's public forums announcing the alliance's return, with three words of description; nobody answered him, and nothing in the channel says whether any Federation guild was involved.{{cite:federation-first-fortnight-of-march-2018-discord-private|10 Mar 2018, the link to the forum thread and the silence after it}}

Members put the alliance at its height at two thirds of the map. On 13 August 2018 an officer of Kingdom of Foxes told the Federation's advisory council that Valkyrie had once held that much, gave his working as 149 territories for his own guild and about fifty for Imperial, and placed it with another councillor at about three months earlier.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|13 Aug 2018, the two thirds and the figures behind it}} The figure was very nearly right and the date was not. Kingdom Foxes reached 148 territories at 13:55 UTC on 16 June 2018, its highest of the summer and two months before he spoke; Imperial held 61 at that minute, and the two together held 209 on a map of about 385.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Kingdom Foxes and Imperial holdings replayed from every exchange, 1 Apr – 1 Sep 2018 UTC: Fox peak 148 at 16 Jun 13:55:16, Imperial 61 at that instant, 209 combined, against 386 distinct territories seen by 1 Sep 2018}} A little over half, and his own two figures come to less than that again.

Holdings moved faster than a day, which is as much weight as a round number of this kind will bear: Kingdom Foxes ranged between 86 and 148 territories inside 16 June alone, and between 33 and 108 across the days of July.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Kingdom Foxes holdings replayed from every exchange, daily minimum and maximum, 1 Jun – 15 Aug 2018 UTC}} The same officer claimed a second expansion as his own work in the same conversation — from 55 to 106 territories in about a month, done almost alone, while five guilds were routed by the [[confederation|Confederation]] and his guild took the ground they lost.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|13 Aug 2018, the second expansion claimed}} That is July, and both of his figures fall inside a single ordinary July day for the guild. He was arguing about how much ground it should be allotted at the time.{{cite:valkyrie-remade-not-revived-2018-discord-private|13 Aug 2018, the argument he was in}}

### The interregnum (winter 2018–19)
After [[the-federation-dies|the Federation died]] in November 2018, the community timeline records that "all guilds keep to themselves with valk owning most of Gavel" — the closest the alliance ever came to territorial power in its own name.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Kingdom Foxes and Imperial were the interregnum's top territory gainers.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Drew1011 held Valkyrie officer titles through January 2019.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}}

### Luna and after (2019)
In 2019 the bloc warred publicly as [[Luna]], with Valkyrie remaining the social layer beneath the war alliance; the apparent Fox-versus-Imperial fighting of that spring was a war fought under Luna's banner.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Emorians' Valkyrie stint ended with its August 2019 Luna exit. Imperial and [[Paladins United]] were members by 14 September 2019.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}

A memoir written by [[arkada|Arkada]] of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] as the September 2019 fighting was still going on states: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians, have existed for longer than I've played Wynncraft."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} Imperial and Paladins United's recorded joins both fall on 14 September 2019{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, and Imperial had left the alliance in 2016.{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, Ascended Kitten, 15 Oct 2016}} The discrepancy is best read as a wartime observer assuming the bloc he was fighting was as old as its name; the years 2017–2019 are thinly documented, and a longer Imperial or Paladins United association cannot be excluded.

### Final years (2020–2022)
Valkyrie still described itself as a community alliance "built on friendship" in 2020{{cite:thread-263975-p04|post #63, Haisay, 9 Mar 2020}}, and a Paladins United member wrote simply "In Valk" in March 2020.{{cite:thread-135149|Wynncraft forums thread 135149, Mar 2020 (via Wayback Machine)}} Through the May 2021 realignment that produced [[Valhalla]] and [[Khaos]], a [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] contributor noted that "Valkyrie stayed the same" while the two major alliances renamed.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|post #136, Dream, 25 May 2021}} Paladins United's thread listed the guild as "in both Valkyrie, and [[Hestia]], which are both community alliances" from November 2021{{cite:thread-246617|opening post, Wayback capture 28 Nov 2021}} until 19 September 2022.{{cite:thread-246617-wb20220919|Wayback Machine capture of the Paladins United guild thread, 19 Sep 2022}} Nothing later mentions the alliance, and no dissolution was ever recorded. The satirical "Greater Valkyrie Alliance" thread of October 2022 involved unrelated guilds trading on the name.

## Organization

By its fourth edition the constitution split the alliance into three institutions. The Parliament, made up of the Electresses of every member-guild, was the deliberative assembly and held sole jurisdiction over admissions and over the foreign affairs of each member. A Directorate drawn from the senior guilds interpreted the constitution, could amend it unilaterally, and alone could expel a member. A Commission of Executrices appointed by the Parliament executed policy. Parliament and Directorate both decided by unanimity, which did not require unanimous participation: an agreement could bind only some members so long as every Elector approved it.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part II (2.2) Institutions}}

Surrendering foreign policy was the price of membership. A member-guild had to consult the Parliament before allying with another guild, supporting one, or hosting a public event.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part II, "Defining Foreign Affairs"}} Two further agreements were optional. The Shared Code of Conduct Agreement bound signatories to a common set of rules, including a duty to "Be respectful to all players, including our enemies" and to turn the other cheek rather than defend the alliance when it was insulted. The Shared Borders and Admission Process Agreement, modelled on the European Union's Schengen Area, let a member move between signatory guilds with both leaders' consent instead of reapplying, and set a shared admission bar of level 50, two hours online a day and a Skype account.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part III, the SCCA and SBAA notes}}

A note in the constitution signed by [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] set the alliance's manner: "It is demanded that there be a shroud of secrecy around the operations and intentions of the Valkyrie Alliance; we should maintain our image of being a 'shady alliance'."{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part II, "Notes on the Culture of the Valkyrie Government"}}

### The unremovable member (2019)
Two features of the constitution collided in the summer of 2019. Membership obliged a guild to consult the alliance before committing itself elsewhere, and one member held permanent, unremovable status under the alliance's own rules, so that it could not be disciplined or expelled whatever it did.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|Valkyrie rules, August 2019}} When [[emorians|Emorians]] left [[luna|Luna]] without first consulting the wider alliance, fellow members held that the move breached the requirement of unanimous agreement — and the alliance had no mechanism to answer it.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|August 2019}} The guilds that objected left and built [[terra|Terra]] instead.{{cite:terra-alliance-2019-discord-private|founding of Terra, 29–30 Aug 2019}}

## Membership
Valkyrie's full roster was never published in any era. The fourth edition of its constitution runs a Table of Policies across five member-guilds — Kingdom of Foxes, Imperial, Lightly Toasted Heroes, HaHaUnited and Holders Of LE — the largest membership any Valkyrie document names.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part III (3.1) Table of Policies}} Its largest recorded concurrent membership from a dated roster is the four guilds of the August 2016 relaunch — Imperial, Kingdom of Foxes, House of Sentinels and Lightly Toasted Heroes.{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}} Machine-recorded alliance data begins in January 2018 and shows at most three member guilds at once.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

{{alliance:Valkyrie}}

## Legacy
Valkyrie outlived every war alliance of its time — [[Coalition]], [[the-federation|Federation]], [[Luna]], [[Terra]], [[Artemis]], [[Valhalla]] — spanning seven years and every era of guild warfare from 2015 to 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Though it held territory in the interregnum, in each of its own self-descriptions across seven years it was a community alliance first.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}} Its constitutional formula — internal affairs to the guilds, foreign affairs to a unanimous council of guild masters — was reused almost verbatim by [[halcyon|Halcyon]] in 2016{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, opening post (Halcyon founded 5 Jun 2016 between ToastedPandas and Holders of LE)}} and was the earliest written model of alliance governance. Drew1011, describing Halcyon's founding, put the borrowing plainly: it was "a small two-guild alliance that totally wasn't a rip off of the original Valkyrie."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L496, composed 23 Jan 2018, re-posted 26 Feb 2018}}

## History
On 28 November 2021 ten [[Valhalla]] guilds — including [[The Aquarium]] — reorganized as Vanir. Guardian of Wynn and Nefarious Ravens were invited on 1 December.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The reorganization doubled as a purge: The Mage Legacy and TheNoLifes, whose friction with the bloc had been building since August, were excluded, and their war on their former allies erupted that December — 5,359 territory exchanges in the month.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Vanir inherited Valhalla's side of the ongoing [[valhalla-khaos-war|Valhalla-Khaos war]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

The alliance did not survive the month. On 18 December 2021 [[Emorians]], Nefarious Ravens, IceBlue Team and [[Avicia]] left, and Vanir collapsed. [[Niflheim]], the community alliance overlapping much of its world, officially dissolved the same day.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The causes of the collapse were never publicly recorded.

