## Legacy
Vanir was the last alliance of the Valhalla line, and its twenty-day life marks the moment the era's mega-blocs stopped holding together. The winter that followed — [[Khaos]]'s last war against the ex-Vanir guilds — ended in the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]] that produced [[Cucumber Company]], where most Vanir guilds reappeared alongside their former Khaos enemies.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## The consultation, 4 February 2018

On 4 February 2018 the developer writing the coming changes to guild warfare asked in the [[coalition|Coalition]]'s leadership channel whether a server existed anywhere that held all the major guild owners. Members answered that this was that server, and that most of the game's active guild owners were already in it.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|4 Feb 2018, the question and the answer}} They offered to build him a channel of his own inside it for the leaders of large guilds, to invite in leaders from outside the alliance, and — from one member — the alliance's own guild-leader rank, so that he could read its leadership chat.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|4 Feb 2018, the offers}} Whether he took the rank went unrecorded.

He named the difficulty himself in the same conversation. He said his worry was that anything he changed would be read as done to benefit that alliance, and that it would be read that way whatever he did.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|4 Feb 2018, the developer on his own position}} He had already tried holding the discussion in the game's own server and had been overwhelmed by replies from players with no experience of guild warfare.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|4 Feb 2018, the earlier attempt}}

## The test, 8 February 2018

Four days later he opened a server on which the system could be tried in public, and territory taken during the test took effect almost immediately.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, the test server}} The alliance's moderation set the arrangement out for its leader that afternoon: the server was open, captures made in it registered at once, and the alliance's opponents had made use of that while the test was still getting under way.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, the account given to the alliance's leader}}

The alliance had declared some ground open to anyone, but published it as a map image with those squares in black and never wrote the names out.{{cite:coalition-announcements|1/16/2018, the Gavel assignment; free-for-all ground marked on the image only}} No figure below has that ground taken out of it.

## The dispute over allied ground

[[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]] took Crater Descent from [[hackforums|HackForums]] at 20:33 UTC and Molten Heights Portal at 20:52.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Hall of Fame as attacker against HackForums, 8 Feb 2018 UTC}} Both guilds stood on the alliance's own membership card.{{cite:coalition-information|member list as revised 14 Feb 2018}} Minutes afterwards a HackForums representative asked in the guild leaders' channel why Hall of Fame was attacking his guild — 13:01 by the channel's clock, which ran eight hours behind UTC that winter.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, 13:01, the complaint}}

An officer of Hall of Fame answered that the developer had told participants to take territories, that a public test was running, and that his guild had not defended what it took.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, the answer}} Another member said the developer had asked participants not to attack allies; the officer replied that the mechanic needed testing and that he had taken the ground before the instruction reached him.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, the instruction and the reply}} A member of the alliance's moderation made the same defence of her own two captures, adding that the ground was going to [[imperial|Imperial]] at the end of the test in any case.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, the moderator's captures}}

## What the map did

Over the twenty-four hours from 08:00 UTC on 8 February — the day as the channel itself kept it — 478 territories changed hands between 37 attacking guilds.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures and distinct attackers per 08:00-08:00 UTC day, 8 Feb 2018}} That was more captures and more guilds than on any of the thirty-six days before it, which ran from 110 to 355 captures and 16 to 34 guilds.{{cite:territory-exchanges|same measure, 3 Jan - 7 Feb 2018 UTC; no enumerated free-for-all list exists for the window}} At 15:08 the alliance's leader told its war channel that he had not seen this many guilds fighting at once since what he called the Gavel invasion, which he did not date; a moderator answered that it would get much worse once the change was announced, and worse again after the update itself.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, 15:08}}

Fighting inside the alliance did not rise with it. Guilds named as members on the alliance's card took ninety-nine territories from one another over those same twenty-four hours, against forty-four to a hundred and eight on each of the seven days before.{{cite:territory-exchanges|captures where attacker and defender both appear on the Coalition member list, per 08:00-08:00 UTC day, 1-8 Feb 2018}}{{cite:coalition-information|member list as revised 14 Feb 2018}} Their share of the day's fighting fell rather than grew. Setting the two measures beside each other is this article's: the channel argued about whether allied ground could be taken at all, and never about how much of it was.

## Calling out the alliance

Between 03:15 and 05:50 UTC on 9 February [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] took eighteen territories from [[imperial|Imperial]] in an unbroken run through Cinfras and the Gylia lakes, none of them recovered while it lasted.{{cite:territory-exchanges|Sins of Seedia as attacker against Imperial, 9 Feb 2018 03:15-05:50 UTC}} At 22:20 by the channel's clock the alliance's leader asked its war channel whether the situation warranted tagging the whole alliance, two or three member guilds being badly damaged; a member answered that it did and named Sins of Seedia as the guild doing it.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|8 Feb 2018, 22:20}} The next morning members were still identifying attacking guilds to one another by full name, among them Heavy Metal Viking.{{cite:war-system-test-february-2018-discord-private|9 Feb 2018, the attacking guilds}}

The rewrite the test was for was released on 1–2 March 2018 and broke the system it replaced; its effects are described at [[territory-warfare|territory warfare]].{{cite:war-update-march-2018-discord-private|1-2 Mar 2018}}

Whimsicality — "Whimsy" — first appears in [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] in the summer of 2016, in a quarrel with Snowing and [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] that the guild’s own history records without explaining.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|"Guild History", the Kingdom of Foxes}}

## Prime Minister of the Foxes

The Foxes held their first guild election in April 2017 to give the gentry a voice in Parliament, and she won it against Antra by fifteen votes to three. The office was named Prime Minister shortly afterwards and settled into organising events rather than governing; [[drew1011|Drew1011]], who ran the election, noted that her re-election was the only entry the guild timeline carried for the three months that followed.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|the first guild election}} She took the post on 16 April 2017 and a second term on 4 July.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|"Guild History", the Kingdom of Foxes}}

The [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] made her one of its six trial judges on 22 April 2017, three of the six coming from Kingdom Foxes.{{cite:emperium-announcements|4/22/2017}} She stood again that August, in the poll of 31 August 2017 for the Emperium's Shadow Advisor, and came joint last of four candidates with four votes against Drew1011's nineteen.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L797–798 and the accompanying tally}}

## The Phoenixes

When Kingdom Foxes rejoined the Emperium on 23 September 2017, she was among the members who left over it and founded [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]].{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|"Guild History", the Kingdom of Foxes}} The new guild’s thread lists her as one of its two chiefs, styled "Princess Whimsy".{{cite:thread-204381|post #1 (OP), 24 Sep 2017}}

She was out of it inside six weeks. [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] made [[drew1011|Drew1011]] viceroy on 2 November 2017 over Alhecks, and the two women fell out badly enough that AurumKitsune removed her from the guild; Whimsicality and others then founded the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]].{{cite:thundderr-oral-history|on the November 2017 split}}

The guild’s own papers describe the two halves of that separately. Its event log dates the removal to 4 November and names Whimsicality, [[elegantdeath|ElegantDeath]] and Alhecks, struck off for "high treason, forever forbidden from coming back" after pressing the Queen to hand the guild over to them.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-4-17}} Its history table dates the break to the 3rd and records only that members left after failing to force her resignation, and founded the Serpentem Empire.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}} No other source repeats the charge of treason.

The ban did not hold. On 13 April 2018 she posted to the guild she had been forbidden to return to: "Some of you may know me, but I see a lot of new faces since I was last here! Well anyways, I’m Whimsy, the original co-creator of Phx. I have recently returned back home!" — and said she was "looking forward to joining back on as a co leader".{{cite:kingdomphoenixes-announcements|4/13/2018}} Nothing records what changed in the five months between.

April 2018 gave her both guilds at once. In the same month she posted her return to KingdomPhoenixes, she took ownership of [[hall-of-fame|Hall of Fame]], the Federation guild that had just been broken by the cost of holding Corkus; by the 24th she had stepped back from running it day to day and named another member to hold the office, and by early May members of other guilds were describing her and [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] as running one guild each.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|April–May 2018}} She announced she was stepping down from Hall of Fame on 1 July 2018 and left it for good on the 27th, without passing it to anyone in game.{{cite:hall-of-fame-guild-profile-discord-private|July 2018}}

The guild she founded in the meantime outlived the quarrel: the [[serpentem-empire|Serpentem Empire]] fought in the [[coalition|Coalition]] that December{{cite:drew1011-storytime|the rosters at the declaration of war, 21 Dec 2017}} and was still a [[the-federation|Federation]] member a year later.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

**yosteric5** owned [[libertas|Libertas]] [Lir], the second-largest territory holder on the Wynncraft map in 2016.

## Holders of LE (2015)

Before Libertas he ran Holders of LE on behalf of its absent owner SSEEBBYZ. In a 2015 forum post the guild's member Kuroi described him as "the stand-in leader of HoL, our guild" while petitioning Spham, the leader of Kangronomicon, to persuade SSEEBBYZ "to kick him out of the guild or demote him"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L24–26 and the accompanying screenshot of Kuroi's forum post, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] — named in the post as one of the members behind it — was a party to the dispute.

![The 2015 forum post by Kuroi asking Kangronomicon's leader to intervene against yosteric5's leadership of Holders of LE, reproduced in Drew1011's account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/02-a64d84b0a8360b896c510f3abac7132c.webp)

By Drew1011's account the approach failed and the members involved instead raised their grievances with yosteric5 directly, who made two of them Head Chiefs{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L28–30, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}; that later he demoted Drew1011 from co-leader to recruit on learning of the plot, and then removed him from the guild{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L43–46, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}; that the two reconciled and Drew1011 rejoined as co-leader on 13 September 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L55, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}; and that on 22 September 2015 SSEEBBYZ sold the guild, after which yosteric5 was demoted and left, taking a number of members with him first to Validus and later to Libertas{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L67–76, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}. yosteric5's own version of the quarrel was never recorded.

## Libertas (2016–17)

The guild's recruitment thread, which he opened on 30 March 2016 and kept for eighteen months, gives its leadership as three people: himself as owner, Amplitude as co-owner and Master_NinjasHD as head chief{{cite:thread-119596|post #3, 30 Mar 2016}} He posted its progress as it climbed — "Libertas is now Ranked #15! we hit level 43 today! I would like to think my active war members for all there hard work"{{cite:thread-119596|post #8, 10 Apr 2016}} — and by the thread's last revision, on 6 November 2016, its header read "Guild Rank: 2 / Guild Level: 62".{{cite:thread-119596|post #1, as revised 6 Nov 2016}} In September 2016 Libertas held 60 of the map's roughly 332 territories, behind only [[hackforums|HackForums]].{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}

Libertas joined [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] on 1 December 2015; Drew1011 says he sponsored the application after the two "made our amends"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L245–246, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}. It appears in the alliance's February 2016 roster{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}. Drew1011 also asserted that Ezura of Validus "had given Yosteric the funds to create the guild"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L247, composed 19 Jan 2018, re-posted 22 Feb 2018}}; how Libertas was funded was never otherwise recorded.

He was well connected across guild lines — "I do know that especially since I always talk to yost", a poster wrote in August 2016 when the [[hackforums|HackForums]] bloc came up{{cite:thread-143392|post #13, 9 Aug 2016}} — and his personal availability was read as a measure of the guild's strength: "Yosteric and Lir wont be too difficult, as their warring standards are usually based around yos being on", a rival wrote that October.{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #49, 16 Oct 2016}}

One request went unanswered. On 9 August 2016 a Libertas member addressed him in the thread: "I just wanted to know the name of our alliance and if I can make a guild shop."{{cite:thread-119596-p08|post #152, 9 Aug 2016}} No reply appears in the thread's twenty-six pages, and no name for the bloc was ever recorded. He is listed as Libertas' owner in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] roster of May 2017{{cite:thread-188024|post #4, Yuno F Gasai, 7 May 2017}}, and his last recorded post, accepting two applicants, is dated 21 September 2017.{{cite:thread-119596-p26|post #516, 21 Sep 2017}}
